<node id="ae44a78d-98ba-4a82-92fb-b9378124227b">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"Premiums, Reinstatement &amp; Death Benefit Terms","text":" policy may be reinstated within five (5) years of lapse by providing evidence of \ninsurability satisfactory to the Company and payment of all past due premiums with interest, \nas determined by the Company at the time of reinstatement. \n \n \nPREMIUMS AND PAYMENT TERMS  \nPremium Amount and Mode  \nThe premium amount and payment mode are shown in the Schedule of Benefits. Premiums \nare payable in advance and may be paid on a monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, or annual \nbasis, as elected by the Policy Owner and approved by the Company.  \nPremium Due Dates  \nThe first premium is due on the Effective Date of the policy. Subsequent premiums are \ndue on each premium due date according to the payment mode selected.  \nChange in Premium Mode  \nThe Policy Owner may request a change in the frequency or method of premium payment \nby written notice to the Company. Such change shall become effective upon approval by \nthe Company.  \nNon-Payment of Premium  \nFailure to pay the premium by the end of the grace period will cause the policy to lapse, and \ncoverage will terminate without value except as provided under the Reinstatement provision.  \nAutomatic Premium Loan (APL)  \nThis policy does not include an Automatic Premium Loan provision unless endorsed or \nadded by rider. If APL is in force, unpaid premiums due at the end of the grace period will be \npaid automatically by a policy loan, provided there is sufficient loan value available.\n\n===== Page 7 =====\nDEATH BENEFIT PROVISIONS  \nDeath Benefit Payment  \nUpon receipt of due proof of the Insured’s death while this policy is in force, the Company will \npay the Death Benefit to the designated Beneficiary, subject to the terms of this policy. \nPayment will be made in a lump sum unless an alternative settlement option is elected and \napproved by the Company.  \nProof of Death  \nProof of the Insured’s death must be provided in a form satisfactory to the Company. \nAcceptable proof includes a certified copy of the death certificate and any other \ndocumentation the Company may reasonably require.  \nTime of Payment  \nThe Company will pay the Death Benefit promptly upon receipt of satisfactory proof of death. \nInterest, as required by applicable law, will accrue from the date of death until the date of \npayment.  \nBeneficiary Designation  \nThe Beneficiary is the person or entity named in the application or most recent written \ndesignation on file with the Company","summary":"Premiums are payable in advance based on the chosen mode—monthly, quarterly, semi-annually, or annually—and are due on specific dates set by the policy schedule. Failure to pay within the grace period results in policy lapse, though reinstatement is possible within five years if insurability is proven and overdue premiums plus interest are paid. This policy lacks an automatic premium loan feature unless added via rider. Upon the insured's death during active coverage, the company pays the death benefit in a lump sum unless otherwise specified, contingent on submission of acceptable proof such as a certified death certificate.","topics":["Premium Payments","Policy Reinstatement","Death Benefit Claims","Insurance Provisions"],"facts":[{"name":"Policy Reinstatement Window","sentence":"A policy may be reinstated within five years of lapse.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["policy reinstatement","lapse duration","reinstatement eligibility"],"entities":[{"name":"Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurer authorized to approve changes","relational_anchors":["effective date","schedule of benefits","reinstatement provision"]},{"name":"Policy Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"payer responsible for premium decisions","relational_anchors":["written notice","approval by the Company"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"life insured under active coverage","relational_anchors":["death benefit","in force"]},{"name":"Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"recipient of death benefit payout","relational_anchors":["designated beneficiary","application","most recent written designation"]},{"name":"Premium","type":"CONCEPT","role":"financial obligation for ongoing coverage","relational_anchors":["first premium","subsequent premiums","past due premiums","grace period"]},{"name":"Effective Date","type":"DATE","role":"start date of initial policy coverage","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Grace Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"window after due date before lapse occurs","relational_anchors":["end of grace period","non-payment of premium"]},{"name":"Reinstatement Provision","type":"CONCEPT","role":"process restoring lapsed policy","relational_anchors":["five (5) years of lapse","evidence of insurability","all past due premiums with interest"]},{"name":"Automatic Premium Loan (APL)","type":"CONCEPT","role":"mechanism covering missed premiums via policy loans","relational_anchors":["unpaid premiums","loan value available"]},{"name":"Death Benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"payout triggered by insured's death","relational_anchors":["upon receipt of due proof","lump sum","alternative settlement option"]},{"name":"Schedule of Benefits","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"document specifying premium details","relational_anchors":["premium amount","payment mode"]}]},{"name":"Evidence of Insurability Required","sentence":"Reinstatement requires providing evidence of insurability satisfactory to the Company.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["reinstatement","evidence of insurability","policy lapse"],"entities":[{"name":"Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurer authorized to approve changes","relational_anchors":["effective date","schedule of benefits","reinstatement provision"]},{"name":"Policy Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"payer responsible for premium decisions","relational_anchors":["written notice","approval by the Company"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"life insured under active coverage","relational_anchors":["death benefit","in force"]},{"name":"Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"recipient of death benefit payout","relational_anchors":["designated beneficiary","application","most recent written designation"]},{"name":"Premium","type":"CONCEPT","role":"financial obligation for ongoing coverage","relational_anchors":["first premium","subsequent premiums","past due premiums","grace period"]},{"name":"Effective Date","type":"DATE","role":"start date of initial policy coverage","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Grace Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"window after due date before lapse occurs","relational_anchors":["end of grace period","non-payment of premium"]},{"name":"Reinstatement Provision","type":"CONCEPT","role":"process restoring lapsed policy","relational_anchors":["five (5) years of lapse","evidence of insurability","all past due premiums with interest"]},{"name":"Automatic Premium Loan (APL)","type":"CONCEPT","role":"mechanism covering missed premiums via policy loans","relational_anchors":["unpaid premiums","loan value available"]},{"name":"Death Benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"payout triggered by insured's death","relational_anchors":["upon receipt of due proof","lump sum","alternative settlement option"]},{"name":"Schedule of Benefits","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"document specifying premium details","relational_anchors":["premium amount","payment mode"]}]},{"name":"Reinstatement Requirements","sentence":"Reinstatement requires payment of all past due premiums with interest.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["policy reinstatement","past due premiums","interest on delinquent payments"],"entities":[{"name":"Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurer authorized to approve changes","relational_anchors":["effective date","schedule of benefits","reinstatement provision"]},{"name":"Policy Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"payer responsible for premium decisions","relational_anchors":["written notice","approval by the Company"]},{"name":"