  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="8553795c-a210-458d-bbd9-47de9966423a">
  <data key="d3">The presence of an accelerated death benefit rider enhances the original commitment to pay the death benefit by allowing earlier access to funds if specified health criteria are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="3c328b68-a332-4773-9c29-f646235f7d51">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider adds a specific provision that affects the payout mechanism of the death benefit, thereby qualifying and shaping the scope of the insurer’s obligation mentioned in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="4c454305-8df7-4f9a-b113-fd49d2e08142">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence identifies a specific component—an Accelerated Death Benefit Rider—that is explicitly mentioned as being part of the total contract described in the first sentence. Thus, it exemplifies one of the elements outlined in the broader contractual definition.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec">
  <data key="d3">The rule mandating written, officer-signed amendments ensures that additions like the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider are formally documented and legally binding under the policy's terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON_COMPLIANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="44a69e56-850d-4ea1-95b8-2226d8cfc678">
  <data key="d3">An accelerated death benefit rider enables partial access to the policy’s death benefit if the insured meets certain health criteria. Its existence does not affect or rely upon the terms of the contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="0d5e54d4-82aa-4712-9f7e-bdb99dc0e6ca">
  <data key="d3">The presence of an accelerated death benefit rider permits beneficiaries to receive funds earlier if the insured becomes terminally ill, independent of whether the suicide exclusion applies; however, the suicide exclusion could still prevent any payout regardless of the rider’s availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="3fabbb3c-c938-4f7a-ab4d-20e58b9e5b05">
  <data key="d3">The presence of an accelerated death benefit rider applies to the policy held by Jordan Everett Hughes, whose identity was established in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">FEATURE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="5e40f960-de3c-481f-98c1-874810eac969">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of an Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is part of the policy’s feature set, formally documented under the policy number SLAC-2025-001.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="835b03af-5fa4-431f-80f1-d702c4462036">
  <data key="d3">The presence of an accelerated death benefit rider indicates that the underlying policy supports optional add-ons; specifically, it confirms that the base policy is a 20-year level term life insurance product capable of being extended through such riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXTENDS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="c446b9c8-2ed6-4125-bd61-520aaa02f788">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of an accelerated death benefit rider reflects a feature designed for terminally ill individuals; its availability aligns with standard underwriting practices where age at issue (37) helps determine insurability and rider eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNDERWRITING_CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3" target="29dbe36f-fb96-403b-9aed-0b906b3fd9d1">
  <data key="d3">The existence of the accelerated death benefit rider has no bearing on the insured’s gender, as it is a standard optional feature available regardless of sex.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
