  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes the timeframe during which a lapsed policy may be reinstated, but it does not relate to the components that make up the policy itself.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period defines how long one has to reinstate coverage after a lapse, but whether renewal or conversion is possible depends on adherence to specified contract conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes the time window during which a lapsed policy may be reinstated, but it does not relate to who the insured person is or how that status affects the reinstatement process.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement period applies only if allowed under the policy’s governing terms and conditions, including any exclusions or requirements specified within them.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period being 5 years from lapse describes a time window during which coverage may be restored after termination due to missed payments. This detail relates to administrative procedures but does not directly inform or depend on the definitional scope of a "Policy."</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period refers to the timeframe during which a lapsed policy may be reinstated; however, this detail does not relate to the identity of the insurer, Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period refers to the timeframe during which a lapsed policy may be revived; it does not relate directly to who receives the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period specifies how long one has to reinstate a lapsed policy, though it does not directly involve the definition of ownership roles. This timing mechanism operates independently of who holds ownership rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
