  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period specifies when a lapsed policy may be revived, but it does not influence or relate directly to how the Death Benefit is determined or paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement window allows the policy to be revived after lapsing, ensuring continued coverage and enabling the Death Benefit to remain applicable if restored before certain limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period specifies when a lapsed policy may be revived, but it does not define what payments are necessary to sustain coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period begins after a policy lapse, allowing renewal if certain conditions are met. This follows potential failure to pay premiums during the grace period, though it operates independently once the lapse occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS_AFTER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year instatement period limits when reinstatement can occur, ensuring that restoration of a lapsed policy is only allowed within this timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period specifies how long one has to revive a lapsed policy, but it does not affect the operation of the grace period, which maintains coverage briefly after a premium default.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period defines how long one has to reinstate a lapsed policy, but it does not affect whether the insurer can later challenge coverage based on prior misstatements.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period allows revival of lapsed policies within five years, but does not affect the incontestability clause that limits challenges to claims for only two years after issue.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period defines how long one has to revive a lapsed policy, but it does not affect whether agents can change policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period allows revival of a lapsed policy within five years, but does not affect the timeframe during which the company can contest the policy's validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period refers to how long one has to reinstate a lapsed policy, but it does not define or influence the components that make up the legal contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period being five years from lapse relates to reactivating coverage after termination but does not connect directly to the policy’s issuance based on application content.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period's length does not influence the requirement for written authorization to alter or waive policy terms. The two concepts operate independently within policy administration.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period being 5 years from lapse relates to reinstating coverage after termination but does not explain how the policy was initially created or activated.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period defines how long one has to reinstate the policy after lapsing, but it does not determine or affect the effective date listed on the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year instatement period allows for policy revival after lapse, contingent upon fulfilling ongoing premium obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period allows the policyholder to revive a lapsed policy within five years, but this does not affect the ownership rights already held by the policy owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period defines how long one has to revive a lapsed policy, but it does not impact when coverage officially starts upon issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement period allows the policyholder to revive a lapsed policy, but it does not affect the assignment rights held by the policy owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period of 5 years after a lapse relates to restoring coverage but does not affect the policyholder’s ability to update beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The instatement period's length does not affect who owns the policy if no Owner is designated. This fact stands independently of ownership assignment rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period allows the policy to be revived after lapsing, independent of the owner’s ability to cancel the policy outright.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period being 5 years from lapse pertains to restoring coverage after a premium default. This does not directly relate to the owner’s right to examine the policy, which concerns initial review before commitment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement period allows the policyholder to revive a lapsed policy within five years, but it does not affect the 20-day window during which the policyholder may cancel the policy upon receipt.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes a 5-year reinstatement window from lapse, which directly supports and clarifies the condition stated in fact_sentence_2 about reinstating a lapsed policy within five years.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement period sets the timeframe within which past-due premiums accrue interest upon revival of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement window allows recovery from lapse only if the insured can prove insurability, linking temporal eligibility to underwriting criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement window sets the temporal boundary under which the requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest becomes applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement period ensures that the policy remains eligible for activation post-lapse, allowing the insurer to fulfill its obligation to pay the death benefit if the insured dies while the policy is subsequently restored to active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement window allows policyholders to restore coverage after lapse, which may lead to a death benefit payout if the insured passes away during that period. Acceptable proof of death ensures accurate processing when a claim arises under these conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement window depends on clear ownership; without a named owner, the insured defaults as owner, enabling them to initiate reinstatement by fulfilling conditions outlined in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement window allows recovery after lapse, whereas the 20-day refund option provides cancellation prior to binding; both offer safeguards but apply at distinct time points in the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">While the first fact allows reinstatement within 5 years of lapse, the second asserts that returning the policy makes it void from inception, effectively negating any chance of revival regardless of timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFLICTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement window complements the 20-day examination period by providing long-term recourse options; while one allows cancellation before commitment, the other enables revival after lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">If the policy is returned, it is treated as though never issued, which negates the possibility of reinstatement even within the allowed 5-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement window depends on formal compliance with written procedures, ensuring that policyholders cannot reinstate without documented approval per contractual rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement window described in fact_sentence_1 relies on proper documentation and authorization, as required by fact_sentence_2, ensuring only formally approved reinstatements are valid.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
