<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Level premiums throughout the guaranteed term ensure consistent payments regardless of age or health changes; however, this has no direct bearing on the duration available to reinstate the policy after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that premiums stay at a consistent rate over time; this directly supports fact_sentence_2 by providing evidence that increases are prohibited under the guarantee.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The stable premium rate during the guaranteed term ensures predictable costs, but renewal or conversion after the term depends entirely on clauses specified in the contract, independent of current premium levels.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The fixed nature of premiums ensures predictable cost over the term, but does not extend coverage beyond its expiration; thus, the policy’s termination upon term end is consistent with the temporary guarantee.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The stable premium rate during the guaranteed term ensures consistent cost predictability but does not influence how benefits are determined under the policy’s stated terms and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The fixed premium rate ensures predictable payments throughout the term, directly enabling the clear understanding that coverage will cease after five years if not extended.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums describes a financial feature of the policy but does not relate to the identity of the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums describes a financial characteristic of the policy, which is essential information once the reader understands what constitutes the policy itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums describes financial consistency during the term but does not explain or rely on the structural elements listed in the definition of a Policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums describes the consistent cost of the policy over time, while the definition of the Insured identifies who is protected by the policy’s benefits. These elements serve complementary roles but do not influence each other directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums during the guaranteed term describes financial consistency over time but does not relate directly to who receives the death benefit after the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums describes a financial feature ensuring consistent payment obligations during the term. This does not directly relate to the definition of the Owner, who holds legal control over the policy regardless of premium structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The stability of premiums over time relies on the foundational understanding that a premium is the periodic payment necessary to sustain coverage under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The fixed premium rate ensures predictable costs over the term, while the Death Benefit represents the primary financial protection offered by the policy. These elements operate independently but together define the policy’s economic framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Fixed premiums ensure consistent payment expectations, allowing the insurer to reliably implement a standardized 31-day grace period after any missed due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">Level premiums ensure consistent payment amounts over time, providing stability; however, if payments cease, reinstatement allows recovery of coverage through specific procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The consistent premium rate ensures predictable cost over the term, while the death benefit remains contingent on adherence to the policy’s stipulated rules and conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">Level premiums ensure consistent cost over the term, enabling uninterrupted coverage even if payments are delayed within the grace period. This consistency helps maintain the policy’s validity during transitional phases like the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes stable premium payments over time, while fact sentence 2 outlines a legal protection window limiting when insurers can contest death benefits. These elements coexist in the policy framework but do not directly influence each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The constancy of premiums during the guaranteed term does not influence the company’s ability to contest the policy over misrepresented information.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The constancy of premiums during the guaranteed term does not influence or relate to the insurer’s ability to contest the policy’s validity during the incontestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums describes pricing consistency over time, while the definition of the Entire Contract outlines the formal components of the binding agreement. These elements serve different functional roles within the policy framework but are independent in meaning.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The fixed nature of premiums ensures predictable payments, enabling the insured to reliably maintain coverage through consistent payment behavior.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The constancy of premiums over the guaranteed term ensures predictable costs, while the prohibition against altering policy provisions safeguards the permanence of those terms, including premium levels.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The consistency of premium payments over time does not affect the requirement for written authorization when altering policy terms. This ensures administrative integrity regardless of stable pricing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">Level premiums ensure consistent payment amounts during the guaranteed term, while the effective date marks when the policy becomes active. The effective date provides temporal context for when those stable premiums apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The fixed nature of premiums ensures predictability in the policy’s cost, enabling the insurer to issue the policy upon receipt of the first payment. This consistency allows the policy to become active based on a known, unchanging financial obligation.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The consistent premium rate ensures predictable cost over the term, supporting long-term affordability. This predictability relies on accurate initial disclosure through the application, which validates the insurer’s risk assessment and enables fair pricing.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The fixed nature of premiums ensures consistent payment obligations during the term, while coverage commences precisely at 12:01 A.M. on the Effective Date, marking the official onset of protection under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The fixed premium rate ensures predictable cost for the insured, enabling consistent coverage without increases. This stable financial commitment supports the owner’s ability to maintain control and exercise full rights over the policy without disruption from changing costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The premium stability during the guaranteed term ensures predictable costs for the insured, while the ability to change beneficiaries allows the policy owner flexibility in estate planning. Both reflect key aspects of policy management and design.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums during the guaranteed term relates to financial obligations over time but does not influence or relate to how ownership is determined if unassigned.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The fixed premium rate ensures predictable cost over the term but does not affect the policyowner’s legal authority to transfer ownership through assignment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">Level premiums ensure predictable costs over time, allowing the policy owner to make informed decisions about maintaining or terminating coverage based on consistent expense forecasts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The stable nature of premiums over the guaranteed term ensures predictable costs but does not influence or affect the owner’s statutory right to examine the policy before acceptance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that premiums remain constant throughout the guaranteed term, ensuring predictable costs. This feature operates independently of the 20-day right to examine, which allows cancellation without penalty after receiving the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of level premiums ensures financial predictability, enabling policyholders to maintain payments and avoid lapses; this increases the likelihood of successfully reinstating the policy within the allowed timeframe should it lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Stable premiums during the guaranteed term help maintain policy in-force status, ensuring eligibility for the death benefit upon the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of level premiums ensures predictable cost over time, but failure to maintain payments can lead to policy lapse; reinstating the policy later requires proving continued insurability, linking long-term affordability to future underwriting criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The fixed nature of premiums during the guaranteed term enables predictability in payments; should a payment fail, reinstatement becomes possible under clear conditions involving back premiums and interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The stability of premiums during the guaranteed term complements the later provision about interest charges upon reinstatement, as it establishes baseline expectations for payment consistency before any lapses occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The fixed premium guarantee ensures ongoing policy validity, allowing the beneficiary to receive the death benefit when the insured passes away, provided proper proof like a certified death certificate is submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
