<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Fixed premiums over the guaranteed term provide financial predictability regardless of when reinstatement might occur after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 confirms that premiums cannot rise during the term, which logically implies they remain unchanged—thus aligning with and validating the claim made in fact_sentence_1 about levels.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFIRMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums throughout the term provides financial certainty, which complements the understanding that coverage expires after five years if not extended.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums ensures predictable costs during the term, which aligns with the policy's finite duration described here. Coverage ceases after the term unless conversion occurs, making the fixed premium relevant only until termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won't increase during the term relates to financial obligations under the policy but does not provide information about the insurer's identity.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won't increase during the term relates to financial obligations but does not define or influence who the insured party is.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The fixed nature of premiums ensures predictable costs throughout the term, enabling the policyholder to plan financially when considering renewal or conversion options later.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won't increase during the term ensures financial predictability but does not influence or relate to who owns the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases applies throughout the term but does not define what constitutes the legal entity of the policy. This factual claim about pricing remains independent of the composition of policy documents.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The statement about stable premiums applies specifically to the type of contract referred to as a "Policy," reinforcing its stability features within the defined scope.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of unchanging premiums ensures predictable payment obligations, allowing the insured to maintain coverage without fear of rising costs. However, even with stable premiums, any death benefit payout remains contingent upon compliance with the policy’s stated conditions and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won’t increase during the term ensures financial predictability for the policyholder but does not influence who receives the death benefit after the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won’t increase ensures financial predictability for the policyholder over time. This stable cost does not directly affect how the Death Benefit is determined or paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases ensures stable cost over time, which supports consistent access to coverage. This stability indirectly enables the Death Benefit to be paid according to the agreed-upon terms without disruption from rising costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won’t increase relies on the definition of a premium as the necessary payment to sustain coverage. Without understanding what a premium is, the significance of it being fixed cannot be fully grasped.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won't increase ensures financial predictability during the term, but does not affect whether a lapsed policy can later be reinstated through formal procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The fixed nature of premiums ensures predictable costs over time, allowing the policyholder to rely on consistent funding. This consistency enables the grace period mechanism to function effectively, maintaining coverage despite temporary delays in payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that premiums remain constant throughout the guaranteed term, ensuring predictable costs. This information does not influence or relate to the duration of the incontestability period described in fact sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won't increase during the term ensures financial predictability for the policyholder but does not affect the insurer’s ability to contest the policy’s validity under the incontestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that premiums are fixed during the term, providing stability. Fact sentence 2 explains that if a premium is missed, there's a 31-day grace period before cancellation, offering temporary protection despite late payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won't increase during the term ensures financial predictability for the policyholder but does not affect the company’s ability to contest the policy based on prior misstatements.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases relies on the policy's immutability; without authorized alterations, the fixed rate remains intact.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums ensures predictable cost over time, while the definition of the Entire Contract clarifies the legal components forming the binding agreement. These statements operate independently but together support transparency about policy obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won't increase during the term ensures financial predictability but does not influence the requirement for written authorization to alter or waive policy provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums relies on the policyholder fulfilling the obligation to pay the first premium, which triggers the start of the guaranteed term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums ensures that policyholders can reliably meet their payment obligations, enabling continuous coverage if payments are made promptly.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won't increase during the term ensures financial predictability but does not influence the policyowner’s ability to designate or change beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases ensures stable costs over the term, while the policy’s issuance relies on accurate information provided at application. These elements operate independently within different aspects of policy formation—one concerns pricing consistency, the other underwriting integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases ensures stable costs during the term but does not affect when coverage starts or how it activates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">Fixed premiums ensure stable financial obligations, allowing the Policy Owner to reliably exercise full control over the policy without unexpected cost changes disrupting their rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases applies throughout the term but does not determine or influence the policy’s effective date, which is independently specified elsewhere.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases ensures stable costs over time, but does not influence or affect the policy owner’s ability to assign the policy to another party.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won't increase during the term relates to financial obligations but does not influence or relate to how ownership is determined if unassigned.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases ensures stable costs over time, allowing the policyholder confidence in ongoing affordability. This financial certainty supports the policyholder’s ability to exercise the right to cancel without unexpected cost burdens.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums won't increase ensures predictable costs over time, complementing the 20-day examination period, which allows the policyholder to review and potentially void the agreement if unsatisfied.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases ensures stable costs over time, while the examination right allows the Owner to review the policy before finalizing it. These are independent protections within the same policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The fixed premium guarantee ensures stability during the term, but if coverage lapses, reinstatement hinges on proving insurability—a factor that may undermine the original guarantee’s benefits if the insured becomes uninsurable later.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">A fixed premium guarantee ensures ongoing policy coverage, directly supporting the insurer’s ability to fulfill its commitment to pay the death benefit when the insured passes away during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The fixed premium guarantee ensures financial predictability over the term, enabling the policyholder to maintain coverage without cost shocks; this stability facilitates potential reinstatement later, especially since the five-year reinvestment window matches the guaranteed term duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums during the term supports continuous coverage, reducing risk of lapse; however, if a lapse does occur despite this guarantee, reinstatement becomes necessary and depends on paying backlogged premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of stable premiums during the term ensures predictable cost, whereas the interest charge on past-due amounts applies only if the policy lapses and is later reinstated, adding a potential extra expense outside the guaranteed term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against premium increases ensures stable cost during the term, enabling predictable funding of future benefits; however, it does not affect the requirement for submitting a certified death certificate when filing a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
