<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Termination at the end of the term means coverage ceases unless renewed; however, this outcome is independent of whether reinstatement was possible after prior lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Since coverage ends upon termination of the term, it underscores why premiums are set at a stable, level amount for the entire guarantee period—to maintain affordability across the known lifespan of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">Termination upon expiration of the term implies that ongoing premium payments beyond the initial period require renewal; thus, the stability of those future premiums depends on whether renewal occurs under new terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not influence or relate to the components that make up the policy document.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">If coverage ends at the term’s close, it may only be extended via renewal or conversion under conditions set forth in the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The statement about coverage terminating at the end of the term does not provide information related to the identity of the issuing company.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The statement about coverage terminating at the end of the term relies on prior definitions establishing what constitutes the policy itself, but does not directly build upon or modify the definition.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term limits the window during which benefits might be payable. However, even within that window, benefits remain contingent upon compliance with policy-specific terms and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that coverage ends unless renewed, implying continuation through reissuance under new terms. Fact_sentence_2 specifies that coverage ends unless converted into another type of policy, suggesting a structural change rather than simple extension. Both address post-term outcomes using alternative triggers.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The policy's coverage duration ends upon expiration of the term, but it only applies to the specific individual designated as the Insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not affect the definition of the Owner’s rights, which remain independent of the policy’s expiration timeline.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not affect how the death benefit is distributed; it only determines when benefits cease if the insured survives beyond the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is only available if the policy remains active; since coverage ends at the term's conclusion unless renewed, the benefit ceases to apply beyond that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINGENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">If the policyholder fails to pay the required premium, coverage will terminate at the end of the term. Therefore, timely premium payments are essential to sustain coverage through the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">If coverage expires at the end of the term without renewal, the Death Benefit ceases to apply because the policy is no longer in force. Therefore, the Death Benefit is contingent upon the policy remaining active throughout the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The policy continues in force during the grace period despite the upcoming end of the term, allowing time for renewal or premium payment without immediate lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows continued coverage for up to 31 days after a missed premium, preventing immediate lapse even if the term is nearing its end. This interim protection ensures flexibility without altering the final termination date.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not influence or relate to the length of the incontestability period, which applies regardless of when coverage ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">If coverage expires at the end of the term without renewal, the policy may become inactive, creating a scenario where reinstatement could apply to revive it.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The end of the term marks the conclusion of coverage regardless of any prior representations made during application. This outcome stands independently from whether the insurer later contests the policy based on misstatements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not influence the definition of the Entire Contract, nor is it derived from it.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term provides the temporal boundary within which the incontestability period operates, ensuring that challenges to policy validity occur only during its active phase.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not influence or relate to the requirement for written authorization to alter or waive policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term relies on the policy's immutable nature; since no one can change its provisions, the expiration date remains binding without exception.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term relies on the policy’s legal foundation, which is established through accurate representations in the application. Without truthful disclosure, the policy might not have been issued, affecting its duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">If coverage is not renewed by the end of the term, it ceases; however, renewal requires timely payment of all upcoming premiums, ensuring continuity only if obligations are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage after the five-year term relies on the prior establishment of the policy through the payment of the first premium. Without this initial payment, the coverage would never begin, rendering its expiration moot.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">Coverage begins precisely at 12:01 A.M. Standard Time on the Effective Date, setting the initial point from which the five-year term operates before terminating.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term does not affect the policyowner’s ability to designate or change beneficiaries during the active policy period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term may affect the exercise of rights by the Policy Owner, who controls the policy’s fate post-term through potential renewal or lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">Coverage expiration occurs after the five-year term concludes if renewal does not happen, marking the endpoint of protection. This outcome depends on knowing when the policy began, which is established by the Effective Date found on the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not influence who owns the policy if no Owner is designated. This statement concerns policy expiration rather than ownership rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The policy's coverage ends when the term expires, which sets a temporal boundary that could influence decisions about assigning the policy. However, the assignment right exists independently of the termination clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">Coverage ends automatically upon the conclusion of the 5-year term if renewal doesn't occur. This outcome is distinct from voluntary cancellation initiated by the policy owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term does not affect the owner’s statutory right to examine the policy before acceptance. This right is time-bound but separate from the policy’s active duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term occurs regardless of the examination period, but the 20-day right to examine allows the insured to assess and possibly void the policy before it becomes binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49010202-fde3-476d-98f4-d300347db155" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7e06d37d-cad7-4701-a273-ebee09a2478e" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is subject to</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84052e93-a85b-41c3-85bc-702b0ae1cd79" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">controls renewal of</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1f0e2e47-7866-4c38-bcb2-ca613268a55c" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on active coverage for receiving</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3419c034-c76f-4bc3-bcd6-40e5b1391198" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">requires active coverage to be payable</data>
</edge>
<edge source="995539a8-9266-4a45-81b8-d491652f25bf" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">defines-term-end</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="db720366-d4ff-4c4f-9494-415ae5421baf">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="14bd8fc5-2979-450c-8d28-919ff71217f1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="c35e4ed7-42b8-49eb-b3cd-1d111d56a39c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="bda98062-1489-4439-9c5b-9b04edde9a28">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="ca7f1d1b-b547-40f4-8bf9-98ceff788029">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="a8bac917-bd49-4888-8302-14e384ba31e7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="e4bc62be-e6f3-4fa3-8e16-4beb47ad2652">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="7606f871-61fd-4e7c-86d7-291160d50f7e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="5fffb847-ced0-4d3f-9df7-7e30f81c650b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="d6d28ce3-dd15-4e49-9685-1c16f1463abb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="8c083438-6b13-4996-810c-9dbe95e8d4eb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="618eb950-38ec-4ad8-a9cb-5fe38d222b4e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="977622e0-4f78-482b-b476-786588a70672">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Termination at the end of the term depends on whether conversion occurs; however, this endpoint has no direct impact on the duration of the reinstatement window post-lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Since coverage is only active during the guaranteed term, the permanence of fixed premiums aligns with the understanding that benefits cease after the term concludes without conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">Since coverage ends at the term’s conclusion unless converted, the permanence of fixed premiums becomes meaningful only up to that point. Without conversion, ongoing premium guarantees lose applicability beyond the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 notes that coverage expires unless converted, meaning it may transition into a permanent policy without further underwriting. Fact_sentence_1 emphasizes renewal as the means to continue protection, typically involving updated premium rates. While similar in intent, they differ in method—conversion versus renewal.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">If coverage ends at the term’s close unless converted, then conversion must occur according to specified contract rules to maintain protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not influence or relate to the components that make up the policy document.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term depends on whether the policy allows conversion, but any potential benefits upon termination remain bound by the policy's stated terms and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The statement about coverage terminating at the end of the term does not provide information related to the identity of the issuing company. The company name is independent of the policy's expiration conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage after the 5-year term depends on the existence of a formal policy agreement, which is explicitly defined in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not affect the definition of the Owner's rights. The Owner retains ownership regardless of when coverage ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence explains when coverage ends if not converted, but does not depend on knowing who the insured is. The second sentence defines the identity of the person covered, providing foundational information unrelated to the timing of termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term does not affect who receives the death benefit if the insured dies during the active term. The designation of the beneficiary remains relevant regardless of when coverage ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The policy ends when the term concludes unless it’s converted; however, maintaining coverage requires regular premium payments to prevent lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">If coverage expires at the end of the term without conversion, the Death Benefit becomes unavailable because the policy is no longer active. Therefore, the existence of the Death Benefit hinges on the continuation of coverage beyond the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">If coverage continues beyond the initial term without conversion, it ends, making the Death Benefit irrelevant thereafter. Thus, the existence of the Death Benefit hinges on the policy remaining active during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of the policy term leads to cessation of coverage unless action is taken. This outcome could potentially be mitigated by timely payments during the grace period, though the grace period itself does not extend the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage upon expiration of the term does not influence or relate to the length of the incontestability period, which applies regardless of when coverage ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">If coverage expires at the end of the term without conversion, the policy may become inactive; however, reinstatement allows it to be revived back into force within certain time limits and requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFTER_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term depends on whether the policyholder acts within the grace period to maintain coverage through timely payment. Without using the grace period effectively, the policy would lapse upon expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">DELAYS TERMINATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The end of the term leads to cessation of coverage, but this does not affect the insurer’s ability to challenge the policy’s validity post-issue if material misstatements were made during application.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term is determined by the policy’s agreed-upon terms, which are formally documented within the scope of the Entire Contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not influence or relate to the requirement for written authorization to alter or waive policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The end of the policy term results in automatic termination of coverage if conversion doesn't occur. This outcome occurs independently of whether the insurer exercises its right to contest the policy’s validity during the incontestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term relies on the policy's immutable nature; since no one can change its provisions, the expiration date remains binding and enforceable without exception.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The policy ends when the term expires unless conversion occurs, which relies on the initial accuracy of information submitted during application. Without truthful application data, the policy might not have been issued at all.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">If coverage is to persist past the initial term, it relies entirely on the insured making all required premium payments on time. Without consistent payment, termination is inevitable even if renewal were otherwise possible.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage after the five-year term relies on the policy having been lawfully initiated through the payment of the first premium. Without this foundational act, the coverage period—and thus its termination—would not exist.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term depends on the start time established by the effective date listed on the Schedule of Benefits. Without knowing the effective date, the exact end point of coverage cannot be determined.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">Coverage begins precisely at 12:01 A.M. Standard Time on the Effective Date, marking the initiation point of the insured period that lasts until the end of the five-year term.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term does not affect the policyowner’s ability to designate or change beneficiaries during the active policy period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">If coverage ends at the term's conclusion without conversion, the policy owner retains the ability to make decisions about renewal options, including conversion, due to their possession of all contractual rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not impact the policyowner’s right to assign the policy during its active lifetime.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at the end of the term does not affect how ownership is determined if no Owner is named. This statement stands independently regarding policy expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">If the policy is canceled by the owner during the term, it would terminate early rather than waiting until the end of the 5-year guarantee period. This shows how the owner’s action can preempt automatic termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term does not affect the owner’s statutory right to examine the policy before acceptance. This right exists independently of when coverage ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of coverage at the end of the term is unrelated to the timeframe during which the policyholder may examine and potentially cancel the policy upon receipt.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db720366-d4ff-4c4f-9494-415ae5421baf" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines rules for conversion eligibility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="14bd8fc5-2979-450c-8d28-919ff71217f1" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">may convert coverage before term end</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c35e4ed7-42b8-49eb-b3cd-1d111d56a39c" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has authority to initiate conversion</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ca7f1d1b-b547-40f4-8bf9-98ceff788029" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">remains payable only if policy is active post-term</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c083438-6b13-4996-810c-9dbe95e8d4eb" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is required for</data>
</edge>
<edge source="618eb950-38ec-4ad8-a9cb-5fe38d222b4e" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">defines timing of</data>
</edge>
<edge source="977622e0-4f78-482b-b476-786588a70672" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">may precede eligibility for</data>
</edge>
