<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Contractual stipulations govern renewal or conversion options; however, even if allowed by contract, those actions must still fall within the 5-year window following a lapse to be eligible for reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">While renewal or conversion requires adherence to contract-specified procedures, those requirements do not affect the guarantee of level premiums during the initial term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating or converting the policy requires adherence to contract-specified criteria, which may influence whether the insured continues benefiting from the originally guaranteed premium rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that renewal or conversion follow contract specifications ensures they are conditional upon actions taken before or at the end of the term when coverage would otherwise terminate.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_RENEWAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">To avoid termination upon expiration, the insured must convert the policy per the contract’s stipulated requirements, ensuring continuity of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for renewal or conversion under contract specifications depends on the broader rule that all benefits are bound by the policy’s stated terms and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBSUMED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The concept of renewal or conversion relies on the existence of a formal policy agreement, but the definition of “Policy” itself does not require information from the renewal clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for renewal or conversion to follow contract specifications depends on the comprehensive definition of the Policy, including documents like applications and endorsements, which collectively form the binding agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The statement regarding renewal or conversion procedures is governed by contract terms, but the identity of the insurer, Sentinel Life Assurance Company, does not influence or explain those procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">Renewal or conversion options depend on contract terms that apply only to those with ownership rights, including the designated Owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">Renewal or conversion procedures depend on contract terms that apply regardless of the insured’s identity. The definition of the Insured does not influence how renewal or conversion is governed by the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">Renewal or conversion options depend on contract terms but do not influence how the Death Benefit is determined or paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Renewal or conversion options are limited by the policy’s specified terms, which also determine the amount and availability of the Death Benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for renewal or conversion under contract terms does not depend on the existence of a grace period for late payments.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 addresses procedural rules for extending or changing coverage after the initial term, whereas fact_sentence_2 clarifies who receives the death benefit if the insured passes away. These statements cover different aspects of policy functionality—future flexibility versus payout distribution—and do not influence each other directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The ability to renew or convert the policy depends on meeting contractual requirements, including timely premium payments necessary to sustain the policy’s active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The ability to renew or convert the policy depends on contract rules but does not affect whether the policy remains in force during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to renew or convert a policy under contract terms does not directly influence or explain how a lapsed policy is reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">Renewal or conversion options depend strictly on contract-specified rules, but they do not affect the company’s ability to contest the policy based on prior misstatements during application.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The ability to renew or convert the policy under contract rules does not influence or relate to the insurer’s capacity to contest the policy’s validity during the incontestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines conditions under which the policy may be renewed or converted, independent of the second sentence’s definition of the incontestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">Renewal or conversion options depend on explicit terms within the official contract documents, including the policy, application, and any addenda. This ensures consistency with the legally binding components of the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for renewal or conversion to follow contract specs depends on the rule that no one—including agents—can change policy terms. This ensures consistency and legal protection of the original agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to renew or convert the policy is contingent upon fulfilling ongoing premium payment requirements. Without timely payments, renewal or conversion privileges become unattainable.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The ability to renew or convert the policy depends on contract-specified rules, which could be influenced by the truthfulness of prior declarations in the application process.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The ability to renew or convert the policy depends on meeting conditions specified in the contract, which only applies once the policy has been properly issued upon receipt of the first premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines conditions under which the policy may be renewed or converted, based on contract terms. Fact_sentence_2 identifies when the policy becomes active by referencing its scheduled effective date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines constraints on renewal or conversion processes, which are subject to change only through formally approved alterations. Fact_sentence_2 establishes that such changes cannot take effect without express written authorization from a company officer, reinforcing the need for official documentation before any adjustment to renewal or conversion terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for renewal or conversion to follow contract specifications depends on the policy owner having control over those decisions, as they hold all contractual rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">Renewal or conversion options are governed strictly by contract terms, independent of the owner’s ability to modify beneficiaries. The right to change beneficiaries does not affect or depend on renewal or conversion rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">Renewal or conversion options are governed by specific contract rules, but this does not affect the policyowner’s ability to assign the policy. The assignment right exists independently of renewal or conversion procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that renewal or conversion follow contract specifications pertains to potential future modifications of the policy, whereas the start of coverage at a precise moment on the Effective Date establishes the initial activation timeline. These statements describe separate operational phases without direct causal or sequential dependence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s renewal or conversion options are governed by specific contract terms, but this restriction does not affect the separate right of the policyowner to cancel the policy at any time during the initial review period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for renewal or conversion under contract terms does not rely on whether an Owner has been designated; instead, it applies regardless of ownership status.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The ability to renew or convert the policy depends on contract-specified conditions but is unrelated to the 20-day examination window during which the policyholder may cancel without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The ability to renew or convert the policy depends on contract-specified rules, which may only become relevant after the owner exercises their right to examine the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
