<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Policy terms and exclusions govern whether reinstatement is permitted after a lapse, thus constraining the applicability of the 5-year reinstatement period.</data>
  <data key="d4">GOVERNS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Benefit availability depends entirely on the policy’s specified terms and exclusions, regardless of whether premiums remain level over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">Although all benefits are bound by the policy’s terms and exclusions, the policy guarantees that premiums will not rise over the five-year term, providing assurance that continued access to benefits depends solely on meeting eligibility criteria rather than escalating costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">While benefits depend on adherence to policy terms and exclusions, those benefits only exist while the policy remains in force—which ends automatically at the conclusion of the 5-year term unless renewal occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">TEMPORALLY_DEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">Even though coverage ends at the conclusion of the term, any claim related to death before expiration would still be evaluated against the policy’s specified terms and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">GOVERNS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">Since all benefits are subject to policy terms and exclusions, any action like renewal or conversion must comply with the detailed specifications set forth in the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The clause about benefits being subject to policy terms relies on identifying who is insured, making the role of the Insured essential for applying benefit conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The statement about benefits being subject to policy terms relies on knowing which entity—Sentinel Life Assurance Company—is responsible for enforcing them. Without identifying the company, the scope of "the policy" lacks clear attribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The statement about benefits being subject to policy terms relies on the prior clarification that 'a Policy' refers specifically to this individual term life insurance contract, ensuring clear reference points.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The statement about benefits being subject to policy terms relies on understanding the scope of the policy itself, which is clarified by including documents like applications and riders. Without defining the full content of the policy, the applicability of its terms remains ambiguous.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">Benefits depend on compliance with policy terms; only the designated Owner possesses the legal standing to claim those benefits within the framework established by the policy’s conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is contingent upon the policy's stated terms and exclusions, ensuring that payment occurs only when conditions are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Beneficiary depends on the policy’s governing terms and exclusions, meaning only individuals meeting specified conditions may claim the Death Benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that all benefits are bound by policy terms, providing a broad principle. Fact_sentence_2 applies this principle directly to the Death Benefit, illustrating how it falls under the umbrella of the overarching condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums ensures continued validity of the policy, which is necessary for any benefits to be payable under the policy’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period ensures that failure to pay a premium promptly does not automatically void coverage, aligning with the conditionality of benefits stated in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The continued effectiveness of the policy during the grace period is contingent upon the conditions specified in the policy's terms and exclusions. Without reference to these governing rules, the grace period would lack legal or operational basis.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence sets a foundational condition that all benefits are governed by policy terms, including processes like reinstatement. Reinstatement allows restoration after lapse but remains constrained by those same governing conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period allows the company to verify the accuracy of information at issuance; if contested during this window, it could nullify benefits despite general adherence to policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The general principle that benefits depend on policy terms includes the incontestability period as a key contractual limitation affecting claim validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The clause stating that all benefits are subject to policy terms and exclusions sets the stage for exceptions like contestability. The company's right to contest based on misrepresentation is one such exception explicitly covered under those terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that benefits depend on policy terms; fact_sentence_2 reinforces this by ensuring those terms cannot be altered by agents, thus maintaining the conditionality of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 depends on the scope defined in fact_sentence_2 because it refers to “terms and exclusions” that are formally established within the Entire Contract, including the policy, application, and attachments.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The validity of benefits hinges on compliance with policy terms, including truthful disclosures during application, since the policy was issued based on those representations.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization to alter policy terms ensures that the limitations and exclusions defining benefits cannot be changed arbitrarily, reinforcing the binding nature of the original terms described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that all benefits follow policy terms relies on the policy being properly initiated through the payment of the first premium, establishing legal enforceability.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for timely premium payments ensures compliance with policy terms, directly enabling the continuation of benefits described in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of benefits depends on adherence to policy terms, including the specific date from which coverage starts—the Effective Date—as indicated on the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The clause stating that benefits depend on policy terms is reinforced because the policy owner controls all contractual rights, ensuring they can enforce or manage compliance with those terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The start of coverage at 12:01 A.M. on the Effective Date is governed by the policy’s terms, including any exclusions or limitations specified earlier. Without meeting the conditions set forth in the policy, coverage would not activate even if the date arrived.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries exists within the boundaries set by the policy's terms and exclusions, meaning any beneficiary changes must comply with established conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The policy's conditions govern all benefits, including the ability to transfer ownership via assignment. The right to assign the policy exists only under the constraints set forth in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The policy's benefit availability depends on compliance with its terms; however, the owner’s power to cancel allows them to terminate coverage before any claim arises, effectively preventing benefit payment regardless of eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that all benefits adhere to policy terms makes understanding those terms essential; thus, granting the Owner the right to examine the policy ensures they can assess whether benefits would apply under specified conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The conditionality of benefits based on policy terms depends on proper identification of the Owner; without one, the Insured assumes ownership, thereby gaining control over claim-related actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day examination period allows the policyholder to assess whether the policy’s terms and exclusions align with expectations before finalizing coverage, ensuring informed consent regarding future benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">The presence of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is subject to the general terms and exclusions specified in the policy, meaning its availability and use depend on the conditions laid out in the core agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is a specific benefit subject to the general policy terms and exclusions described in fact_sentence_1, particularly regarding eligibility, reduction of death benefit, and prohibited causes.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the foundational rule that all benefits are bound by policy terms; fact_sentence_2 describes one specific benefit (accelerated death benefit) whose eligibility hinges entirely on those terms, particularly regarding diagnosis and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the foundational rule that all benefits are bound by policy terms; this includes the requirement in fact_sentence_2 that a terminal illness diagnosis must meet a 12-month life expectancy threshold to qualify for an accelerated benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the overarching rule that all benefits follow policy terms; fact_sentence_2 exemplifies one such term—requiring physician certification—for accessing an accelerated death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the foundational rule that all benefits follow policy terms; fact_sentence_2 elaborates on one such benefit by specifying the required action—written submission—to access it, showing compliance with those terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the foundational rule that benefits are subject to policy terms; fact_sentence_2 provides a concrete example of such a term—an exclusion for self-inflicted injuries affecting accelerated death benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the foundational rule that all benefits adhere to policy terms; fact_sentence_2 illustrates this by showing how receiving an accelerated benefit triggers a reduction in the death benefit, demonstrating compliance with those terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the foundational rule that benefits are subject to policy terms; fact_sentence_2 exemplifies this by specifying a particular exclusion—felony-related terminal illnesses—from receiving accelerated benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the overarching principle that all benefits are bound by policy terms; fact_sentence_2 exemplifies this by specifying one such term—the insurer's right to demand a second medical opinion when processing accelerated death benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the foundational rule that benefits are subject to policy terms and exclusions; fact_sentence_2 exemplifies this by specifying that war-related terminal illnesses fall under those exclusions, thus limiting eligibility for accelerated benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the foundational rule that all benefits adhere to policy terms; fact_sentence_2 exemplifies this by showing that the process for accessing accelerated benefits includes a revocable step, reinforcing that even partial benefit claims are bound by specific contractual procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
