<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Defining a "Policy" as the Individual Term Life Insurance contract establishes the core legal entity under discussion. This definition sets the stage for understanding all other clauses, including those about reinstatement, but it is independent of timing specifics like the 5-year instatement period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Defining the policy as the individual term life insurance contract establishes the subject to which the claim about stable premiums applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">REFERS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a "Policy" encompasses the contractual arrangement where premium increases are explicitly prohibited during the guaranteed term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINITIONAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">Defining “Policy” as the individual term life insurance contract sets the stage for interpreting other clauses, including how long coverage lasts before expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The concept of a "Policy" as described here directly supports the interpretation of when coverage ends, making its definition essential for understanding the scope of the coverage clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">Defining “Policy” establishes essential terminology needed to interpret clauses about renewal and conversion, though those actions do not alter the core identity of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Defining ‘Policy’ as the individual term life insurance contract provides necessary context for understanding how benefit eligibility is constrained by contractual terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The Policy, defined as the individual term life insurance contract, comprises various supporting documents such as the application, policy schedule, riders, and endorsements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that "Policy" refers to the individual term life insurance contract described in the document. This definition sets up the scope of reference for understanding the contractual entity discussed throughout the text.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES_ENTITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The policy encompasses coverage for a specific individual—the Insured—whose life is protected under its terms. This establishes the core purpose of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Policy establishes the contractual framework under which ownership rights are granted. This enables the identification of the Owner as the legal holder of those rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES_ROLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence establishes that the policy is an individual term life insurance contract. The second sentence describes the beneficiary's role in receiving the death benefit under that policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 introduces the concept of the policy as the contractual agreement, setting context for understanding other elements. Fact_sentence_2 builds on this by specifying what happens under a particular condition (death of the insured), defining a central component of the policy's purpose.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The Policy is formally established as the individual term life insurance contract described in the document. The Death Benefit’s eligibility and amount are determined entirely by the rules outlined within this very policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a Policy establishes the core agreement, while the explanation of a Premium clarifies how the policy remains enforceable over time through periodic payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NEEDS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The concept of a "Policy" sets the foundational framework for understanding contractual elements like the grace period, which applies specifically to that policy’s premium obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The policy, defined as the individual term life insurance contract, includes specific protections such as remaining in force during the Grace Period.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a "Policy" establishes the foundational contractual entity, providing essential context for understanding procedures like reinstatement, which apply specifically to policies that have lapsed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The concept of a "Policy" serves as the central component of the "Entire Contract," which encompasses additional documentation such as applications and riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the policy establishes the subject matter upon which the incontestability clause operates. Without clarifying what the policy is, the timing and scope of contestability cannot be meaningfully understood.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The policy, defined as the individual term life insurance contract, serves as the subject matter upon which the company's right to contest based on misrepresentation operates.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes that 'Policy' refers to the individual term life insurance contract described in the document. Fact sentence 2 states that the incontestability period lasts two years but does not connect this detail back to the policy’s identity or nature.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The policy is formally defined as the individual term life insurance contract, and this definition is reinforced by the rule that no external party can change its terms, ensuring consistency and legal stability.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The policy is formally defined as the individual term life insurance contract, and its creation hinges on the truthful representations contained in the applicant’s submission.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a Policy establishes the core contractual entity to which modification rules apply. This sets the stage for understanding that any change to the policy’s terms must follow formal procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The policy, defined as the individual term life insurance contract, remains in force only if premiums are paid regularly; failure to pay results in termination of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The policy is defined as the individual term life insurance contract; its formal creation and validity depend on the initial premium payment, making the payment a prerequisite for the policy's activation.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the policy sets the foundation for understanding when its terms become active; therefore, knowledge of the policy's identity enables identification of its effective date via the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The policy, defined as the individual term life insurance contract, establishes the framework under which coverage becomes active. Coverage begins precisely at 12:01 A.M. Standard Time on the Effective Date, marking the start of protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES_TIMING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The Policy is defined as the individual term life insurance contract, establishing its legal framework. This foundational definition supports the assertion that the Policy Owner possesses control over beneficiary designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Policy sets the foundation for understanding who holds control over it; specifically, the Policy Owner possesses legal authority to transfer or assign the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The Policy is defined as the individual term life insurance contract, establishing the legal entity to which ownership rights apply. This foundational definition supports the claim that the Policy Owner has exclusive control over the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES_ENTITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Policy establishes the contractual framework that grants ownership rights, enabling the Policy Owner to exercise control over the policy, including requesting its cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The policy, defined as the individual term life insurance contract, includes a 20-day examination period during which the policyholder may review and potentially cancel the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">Knowing that a Policy refers to the individual term life insurance contract enables understanding why the Owner has the right to examine it during the 20-day examination period.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The concept of a "Policy" establishes the contractual framework; without this foundational definition, the role assignment in case of unnamed ownership would lack legal grounding. Thus, the existence of the policy enables the application of default ownership rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
