  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines what elements make up a policy, but it does not reference or depend on the name of the issuing company. The second sentence names the insurer without relating to the structural definition of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The policy comprises various documents including applications and riders, among which the designation of the Insured is formally recorded. This ensures clarity on who is protected under the coverage outlined in those documents.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The policy encompasses various formal documents, one of which governs the Death Benefit. Therefore, the Death Benefit is determined by the collective terms included within the policy framework outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
