</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence establishes that the insured is the person covered by the policy, which sets the stage for understanding what kind of event triggers death benefit payment—relevant to why coverage might terminate upon the insured’s passing. However, it doesn’t influence whether coverage continues beyond the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The existence of the Insured establishes the subject of coverage, which indirectly affects renewal or conversion eligibility; however, the specific conditions for those actions are determined independently by contract language.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
