  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="dad7abc1-3335-4510-87bf-f832bda34f72">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="93eccc1d-df68-4feb-a641-8a1e27e5d7b8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="8e34e303-a0b1-4be8-b4af-bbc4f5266af2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="0984cc4c-32c1-4c40-be5e-ccf8a646ca2c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="53c6f8da-42a9-4fd1-8602-b9d874479d33">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="4c897023-812d-4f19-bbc7-b33066e4d75d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="99a6d49b-c4e3-419e-87ec-d2dd970a81be">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="181dd229-5d1b-485a-aa0d-ad0137abbfb1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="0571a1f4-a9e4-435f-a1ee-9ba4578ac963">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is the recipient of the death benefit, but this definition has no direct connection to the length of the instatement period after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Defining the beneficiary as the recipient of the death benefit has no direct connection to whether premiums remain constant throughout the term.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">The designation of a beneficiary determines who inherits the death benefit, independent of whether premiums remain fixed throughout the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The designation of a beneficiary ensures that the death benefit is paid out appropriately regardless of whether the policy has terminated due to expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">Knowing that the beneficiary receives the death benefit provides context for why timely conversion might matter; however, it doesn't alter the rule that coverage simply ends at the term's conclusion without renewal.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the recipient of the death benefit based on designations made by the policyholder, independent of any renewal or conversion processes described in fact_sentence_1. The existence of a named beneficiary does not affect whether renewal or conversion may occur, nor vice versa.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Since the Death Benefit is subject to policy terms and exclusions, the designation of the Beneficiary must align with those constraints to ensure validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence specifies who benefits from the death benefit when the insured passes away. This information applies directly to the policy described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence identifies who receives the death benefit when the insured passes away. While relevant to overall policy function, it doesn't rely on nor clarify any component listed in the first sentence about policy composition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is designated to receive the Death Benefit after the Insured passes away. The identity of the insurer, Sentinel Life Assurance Company, has no bearing on who qualifies as the Beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is entitled to receive the Death Benefit only if the Insured dies, making the identity and status of the Insured essential for activating the benefit transfer process.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary receives the Death Benefit only upon the Insured’s passing and has no inherent authority over policy ownership; that responsibility lies exclusively with the Owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is entitled to receive the Death Benefit, but its availability and amount are constrained by the policy's governing terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is the recipient of the Death Benefit after the Insured's passing, which is paid out only if the policy remains active—requiring ongoing premium payments to sustain it.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary receives the Death Benefit when the Insured dies; this role only has meaning if the Death Benefit is established as a payable sum.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Beneficiary relates to post-death benefits but does not influence or depend on the existence of a grace period for premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Beneficiary pertains to who receives the Death Benefit after the insured's passing, but it does not influence or relate to whether the policy stays active during a grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence explains who receives the death benefit, but it does not relate directly to the length of the incontestability period described in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Beneficiary outlines who receives the payout after the insured's death, but it does not influence or relate to the company's ability to contest the policy during the incontestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is entitled to receive the death benefit if the insured passes away, but this payout only occurs if the policy remains in force. Reinstatement allows a previously lapsed policy to become active again, potentially enabling future benefits including those payable to the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary receives the death benefit upon the insured's passing, but this payout could be challenged if the company discovers material misrepresentations during underwriting.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Beneficiary does not influence or relate to the requirement for written authorization to alter or waive policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Beneficiary specifies who receives the death benefit, but does not influence or relate to restrictions on modifying policy terms by agents.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary's right to receive the Death Benefit is determined by the documents included in the Entire Contract, including the policy itself and any amendments.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary's entitlement to the Death Benefit relies on accurate disclosures during application, ensuring legitimacy and validity of claims. Without truthful application data, even properly named beneficiaries may face denial.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary's right to receive the Death Benefit is contingent upon the policy being properly issued, which requires the initial premium payment described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The designation of a Beneficiary relies on the policy remaining in force, which requires ongoing premium payments. Without timely payments, the policy lapses, nullifying the beneficiary's right to the Death Benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is determined by the insured party but requires authorization through the policy owner, who controls changes to beneficiary status.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence explains who receives the death benefit, but it does not relate to when the policy becomes effective. The second sentence identifies the source for determining the policy's effective date, independent of beneficiary designations.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is entitled to receive the Death Benefit when the Insured passes away, while the Policy Owner has control over the policy, including the ability to name or change beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is entitled to receive the Death Benefit after the insured passes away, but only if the policy was active at that time. Coverage beginning at 12:01 A.M. on the Effective Date ensures the policy is live before any potential payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The designation of a beneficiary determines who receives the death benefit after the insured passes away. This information is independent of the policy owner’s right to terminate the policy at any time during its term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Beneficiary specifies who receives the Death Benefit after the Insured's passing. This information does not rely on whether the Owner is named or assumed by default under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is entitled to receive the Death Benefit after the Insured's passing, and this entitlement remains unaffected by the Policy Owner’s decision to assign the policy, though assignments may require updating beneficiary designations if changes occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary receives the Death Benefit upon the Insured’s passing, while the Owner holds the authority to review the policy documents, potentially affecting decisions about beneficiaries during the examination window.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Beneficiary relates to posthumous payout distribution, whereas the 20-day examination period allows the policyholder to review and potentially cancel the policy before commitment. The two concepts operate independently in the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="80518b2d-1bb2-4fa2-93b9-79573d720a98">
  <data key="d3">The general definition of a beneficiary provided in fact_sentence_2 helps clarify the significance of the individuals listed in fact_sentence_1 who are set to receive the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="90ec6e29-a29c-4e3c-8d1b-c21dc571dc89">
  <data key="d3">The general definition of "Beneficiary" in fact_sentence_2 clarifies the role fulfilled by Elaine M. Hughes as specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="d13623e0-a45f-4060-82e1-dbdfcb46c827">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 offers foundational terminology that helps interpret the roles described in fact_sentence_1, particularly regarding the designation of Morgan L. Hughes as the contingent beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539" target="af0642b0-b73b-4d5a-941d-8b8a65fef5d4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 defines 'beneficiary'—a key element referenced in chunk_summary_1—and supports understanding of who receives benefits under policies like the one detailed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS_CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
