<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit’s availability hinges on compliance with policy terms, including timely reinstatement within the 5-year period after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is determined by the policy’s terms, which include stable premiums maintained at a fixed level throughout the guaranteed term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is determined by the policy’s contractual framework, including its duration and payment rules. Since premiums are locked in during the term, the insurer maintains sufficient reserves to fulfill the promised death benefit if claims occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON TERMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit only applies while the policy remains in effect; since coverage ends at the conclusion of the term unless renewed, the benefit cannot be paid if the insured dies beyond the term’s expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is only payable if the insured dies while the policy is still in effect, meaning it cannot apply once coverage has terminated under the stated term limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">Since the Death Benefit operates under the policy’s terms, any decision regarding its continuation via renewal or conversion must comply with those same terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the Death Benefit as a particular benefit affected by policy terms. This specificity supports and exemplifies the broader claim made in fact_sentence_1 about all benefits being subject to policy conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBSUMED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit exists only under the framework defined by the Policy, meaning its application and limitations depend explicitly on the contractual terms agreed upon in the policy document.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">Since the Death Benefit is bound by the policy’s conditions, it relies directly on the inclusion of supporting documentation—such as applications, schedules, and endorsements—as specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is determined and enforced under the framework established by Sentinel Life Assurance Company, reflecting the insurer’s role in upholding policy obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">GOVERNS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit's application relies on the Insured being clearly identified, so its validity hinges on the prior definition of the Insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">While the Death Benefit is determined by the policy’s stipulations, the Owner possesses full rights to govern the policy, ensuring compliance with or modification of terms during active coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit, which determines what the Beneficiary receives, is explicitly bound by the policy’s stipulated conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">GOVERNS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The policy's governing terms determine how and under what circumstances the Death Benefit is paid, making it dependent on those stipulations rather than being automatically enforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is contingent upon the policy remaining active, which relies on timely premium payments. Without consistent premiums, the benefit cannot be paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit depends on timely premium payments; if payment is delayed beyond the 31-day grace period, the policy could lapse, potentially voiding the Death Benefit. This creates a conditional link from the Death Benefit to the Grace Period mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit depends on maintaining policy validity; if the policy lapses due to missed payments without using the Grace Period, the death benefit may not be paid. Thus, the Grace Period supports the conditionality of the Death Benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is determined by the policy’s conditions, including potential changes due to reinstatement after lapse. However, the specific impact of reinstatement on the death benefit amount is not detailed here.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is contingent upon the policy remaining in force beyond the incontestability period, during which insurers cannot contest coverage based on misrepresentations.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit depends on the policy remaining valid; its payment is contingent upon the company not successfully challenging the policy during the incontestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit’s payment is contingent upon the absence of material misrepresentations made at policy inception; if such misrepresentations exist, the insurer may deny the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is determined by the terms within the Entire Contract, which encompasses the policy, application, and any addenda. This establishes that the scope of the Death Benefit is legally bounded by the documents comprising the Entire Contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is determined solely by the policy’s agreed-upon terms, which remain unchanged due to restrictions on unauthorized modifications by agents or representatives.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit’s applicability is contingent upon adherence to the policy’s conditions, including requiring official written consent for any changes. Without authorized modification, the benefit remains strictly under existing contractual terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is determined by the policy’s terms, which rely on truthful disclosures during application. Without accurate application data, the policy—along with its associated benefits—may not be enforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is contingent upon the policy being properly issued, which requires the first premium payment. Without this payment, the policy does not take effect, rendering the Death Benefit undefined under current conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is contingent upon the policy becoming effective, which is formally established by the date specified in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is only payable if the insured remains covered under the policy, which requires continuous premium payments. Without timely payments, coverage ends, rendering the Death Benefit unenforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is determined by the policy terms, including who receives it—this depends on changes made by the Policy Owner regarding beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is determined by the policy’s stipulations, which are fully controlled by the Policy Owner through their vested contractual rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit only applies once coverage has officially begun, which occurs at 12:01 A.M. Standard Time on the Effective Date. Therefore, the activation of the Death Benefit hinges entirely on the start time specified in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is governed by the policy’s stipulations, including any limitations or requirements related to changes in ownership. Ownership rights allow the holder to modify beneficiary designations, potentially affecting benefit distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit depends on the policy remaining active, which can be terminated if the Policy Owner exercises the right to cancel.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit’s applicability depends on policy-defined conditions, including who holds ownership. If no Owner is designated, the Insured becomes the Owner, thereby gaining authority over benefit distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is contingent on the policy terms, which the Owner may inspect during the examination period. This access enables the Owner to verify whether the benefit aligns with agreed-upon conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit’s validity depends on whether the policyholder exercises their right to examine within the specified 20-day window; if not exercised, the policy proceeds into effect, making the Death Benefit applicable under agreed terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The condition that the Death Benefit is subject to policy terms is reinforced by the possibility of reinstating the policy within five years of lapse, ensuring continued eligibility for benefits upon revival.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit depends on fulfilling policy conditions, including providing acceptable proof of death such as a certified death certificate, ensuring proper validation before payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit depends on maintaining active policy status, which can only occur if reinstatement occurs after lapse—requiring payment of overdue premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit depends on maintaining active policy status, which may require reinstatement after lapse; therefore, proving insurability—as required by fact_sentence_2—is essential to preserving eligibility for the Death Benefit described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit depends on timely premium payments; if premiums are late, reinstatement requires paying interest, preserving the beneficiary’s future entitlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit's applicability depends on meeting the policy's requirements, including timely payment of premiums and submission of proper documentation after the insured's death. This aligns directly with the procedural conditions detailed in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit, as outlined in the main policy, may be partially accessed earlier through the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider when certain health criteria are met, demonstrating a conditional extension of the original benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit, though generally subject to policy terms, can be partially accessed earlier through the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider when certain criteria are met, showing a conditional extension of its application.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit, as defined by policy terms, may be reduced when an accelerated benefit is paid out upon diagnosis of a terminal illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit, defined in the main policy, serves as the basis for the accelerated payment available under the Terminal Illness Rider when eligibility criteria are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for physician certification in determining life expectancy supports the conditions under which the Death Benefit may be accessed early via the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, aligning with the broader policy terms governing benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a written request for an accelerated benefit depends on the broader terms governing the Death Benefit, ensuring compliance with policy rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit's administration may involve a second medical opinion, particularly under riders enabling early payouts, linking it directly to the process governing benefits distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit, while initially defined by policy terms, is explicitly subject to reductions when an accelerated benefit is accessed, demonstrating a conditional modification based on rider provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit, as outlined in the main policy, includes limitations such as exclusions for benefits related to war, directly aligning with the restriction stated in fact_sentence_2 regarding accelerated payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit, while generally applicable per policy terms, excludes payment of accelerated benefits if the terminal illness arises from a felony, creating a limitation on access to part of the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_EXCLUSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit, while generally applicable per policy terms, excludes payment of accelerated benefits if the terminal illness arises from intentional self-harm—a limitation detailed in the rider provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_EXCLUSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit's treatment under the policy includes reductions due to accelerated payments, making its definition contingent upon actions like revoking a claim. This connection shows how procedural flexibility around accelerated benefits impacts the final death benefit outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
