<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">A grace period provides temporary coverage extension after a missed premium payment, preventing immediate lapse. It precedes any need for reinstatement, which only becomes relevant if the grace period expires without payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">The presence of a 31-day grace period provides temporary relief from forfeiture when a premium is late, reinforcing the reliability of level premiums over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 describes a 31-day grace period available when a premium is missed. This applies regardless of whether premiums are fixed or variable, so it doesn't rely on the guarantee stated in fact sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">If a premium is missed, the grace period extends coverage for 31 days past the due date, delaying termination until the end of the term regardless of the delay.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">A 31-day grace period provides temporary relief from cancellation due to late premiums, allowing time to pay before coverage ends—but only within the original term’s duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period for missed premiums operates independently of whether renewal or conversion options are exercised per contract rules.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The grace period serves as a procedural safeguard enabling continued benefit eligibility during temporary lapses, consistent with the overarching principle that benefits depend on adherence to policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period depends on the policy being active, reinforcing its role as part of the broader policy structure defined by the initial statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">A 31-day grace period allows time to pay a missed premium without lapsing coverage; however, it does not affect what documents make up the policy itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period allows policyholders time to pay overdue premiums without losing coverage, a feature implemented by insurers like Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The Grace Period ensures continued protection for the Insured even if a premium is late, thereby safeguarding the core benefit associated with the Insured’s status under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">PROTECTS_INSURED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">A 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payments without immediate lapse, though it does not affect the Owner’s established rights or responsibilities.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed premium payment without immediate policy lapse, but it has no bearing on who receives the death benefit when the insured passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day Grace Period supports ongoing policy validity, ensuring that the Death Benefit remains enforceable if the policyholder pays within the window.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures continued validity of the Death Benefit even if a premium is not paid on time, thereby protecting the beneficiary’s entitlement unless the delay exceeds the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period ensures continued protection after a missed premium payment, reinforcing the importance of timely premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provides a buffer after a missed premium, ensuring uninterrupted coverage during those 31 days.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period offers a buffer after a missed premium, allowing time to pay before the policy lapses. This creates the opportunity for reinstatement should the premium remain unpaid beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The Grace Period allows a 31-day window after a missed premium without immediate policy lapse, but it does not affect the duration or conditions of the Incontestability Period, which begins separately from the policy issue date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The Grace Period allows a delay in premium payment without immediate policy lapse, but it does not affect the company’s right to contest the policy’s validity during the Incontestability Period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The Grace Period allows continued coverage despite a late premium, but its existence is independent of the legal composition of the Entire Contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed premium payments without immediate loss of coverage, but it does not affect the insurer’s ability to later challenge the policy based on misrepresented information during application.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed payment without immediate policy lapse, but it does not affect the rule that only the formal policy documents govern terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows a temporary extension for paying overdue premiums without immediate policy lapse. This does not influence or relate to the requirement for written approval to alter or waive policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provides temporary relief from cancellation due to late payments, but does not affect the requirement that the policy was issued based on accurate application information.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provides temporary protection after a missed premium, but only applies if the policy has already been activated by the payment of the first premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period enables delayed premium payment while maintaining coverage temporarily; however, ongoing coverage ultimately relies on paying all upcoming premiums on time.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows additional time to pay a missed premium without lapsing coverage, but it does not affect when the policy becomes effective. The effective date is determined independently by the issuer and documented on the benefits schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The grace period offers a 31-day window post-missed premium during which coverage remains active, but it has no bearing on when coverage officially commences.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums without losing coverage, but it does not affect the policyowner’s ability to modify beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides temporary relief if the policyowner misses a premium payment, supporting their ability to maintain coverage. This aligns with the owner's right to manage the policy, reinforcing their control during lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provides a buffer for late premium payments without immediate loss of coverage. This does not affect the policy owner's ability to assign the policy, which remains independent of payment timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The grace period offers a 31-day buffer after a missed premium before the policy lapses, providing flexibility in payments. This does not directly affect the owner’s ability to cancel the policy, which remains a separate unilateral decision.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows continued coverage after a missed premium but does not affect the owner’s right to examine the policy prior to acceptance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows a 31-day window after a missed premium payment before coverage lapses, ensuring temporary protection despite late payments. This provision does not influence who owns the policy if no owner is explicitly named.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provides a 31-day window after a missed premium to maintain coverage, but it does not affect the 20-day examination period during which the policyholder may cancel the policy before finalizing commitment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The grace period serves as a buffer before reinstatement becomes necessary, enabling timely resolution of missed payments. Without it, policies would lapse immediately upon default, making reinstatement irrelevant.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides a critical window allowing policyholders to avoid lapse and qualify for reinstatement up to five years later, making it foundational to the possibility described in fact sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period gives the policyholder time to catch up on payments before the policy lapses, enabling eligibility for reinstatement later if needed.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed payments without immediate policy lapse; however, reinstating the policy later incurs interest on past-due premiums, which is assessed when reinstatement occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows temporary continuation of coverage after a missed premium, ensuring the policy remains in force long enough to qualify for death benefit payments if the insured passes away during this time.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows time to rectify late payments before policy lapse; if the insured dies during this period, proper proof of death—including a certified death certificate—is needed to claim the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures continued coverage despite late payment, but its application hinges on having a recognized Owner; thus, defining the Owner via the Insured’s default status enables proper implementation of this mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures continuous coverage even after a missed premium, while the 20-day examination window allows the owner to assess and potentially void the policy early; together, they provide layered protection for the policyholder during initial enrollment and ongoing maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">Fact Sentence 1 establishes a standard grace period mechanism that operates under the broader framework of policy rules requiring written documentation for modifications, reinforcing consistency in administrative procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows continuation of coverage after a missed premium, whereas the 20-day return option permits cancellation prior to acceptance. These timelines overlap temporally but apply to distinct stages: one addresses ongoing policy maintenance, the other initial buyer satisfaction.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes a 31-day grace period allowing late premium payments, enabling continued coverage; however, fact sentence 2 asserts that returning the policy renders it void from inception, negating any chance of continuation even under grace conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes a grace period allowing delayed premium payment without immediate lapse; this supports the idea that policies can remain active temporarily even after missing a payment, consistent with the broader framework under which returned policies may be voided only prior to final acceptance.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes the 31-day grace period for late premiums, while fact sentence 2 specifies that any modification to policy terms—including those affecting grace periods—requires written approval from an authorized company officer. Together, they highlight procedural rigor around policy flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
