</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The company’s right to contest the policy hinges on material misrepresentations made by the insured. Therefore, this provision relies on identifying who the insured is—the central figure in any claim-related dispute.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">While the Company has the right to contest the policy due to misrepresentations, this does not alter the fact that the Owner retains complete ownership rights unless otherwise invalidated through legal process.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">If the company contests the policy due to material misrepresentations, it may deny the claim even though the beneficiary was properly named to receive the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS_PAYOUT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">If the company discovers material misrepresentations in the application, it has the right to contest the claim, potentially preventing the Death Benefit from being paid to the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Material misrepresentations allow the company to contest the policy, potentially invalidating the Death Benefit even if otherwise payable under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">If material misrepresentations were made at application, the company may void the policy regardless of whether premiums have been paid consistently over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The insurer’s right to contest the policy over material misrepresentation exists independently of the grace period provision, which only pertains to late payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">Although the policy may be contested by the company over material misrepresentations, this potential action does not impact whether the policy remains active during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">If material misrepresentations exist, the insurer retains the right to contest the policy regardless of whether reinstatement was attempted or granted later.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">Material misrepresentations allow the company to contest the policy, but only within the legally defined two-year incontestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">Material misrepresentations provide the legal grounds upon which the company may contest the policy’s validity during the Incontestability Period, establishing the rationale for the insurer’s limited power.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The company's right to contest the policy relies on information contained within the application, which is explicitly included in the definition of the Entire Contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">If material misrepresentations exist, the company may contest the policy, but this right cannot be undermined by unauthorized actions from agents, ensuring that only official policy language determines eligibility for contestation.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the company to contest the policy hinges on the validity of the applicant’s representations during underwriting. Without accurate statements in the application, the basis for issuing the policy collapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the company to contest the policy due to misrepresentation does not depend on whether alterations require written authorization; it concerns factual accuracy at application. This statement stands independently regarding policy validation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the company to contest the policy due to misrepresentation does not affect the requirement for timely premium payments to maintain coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The company’s ability to contest the policy hinges on representations made prior to its issuance, while the policy only becomes active upon receipt of the first premium, linking contestability to the timing of payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the insurer to contest the policy due to misrepresentation does not influence or rely upon the determination of the policy’s effective date listed on the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the company to contest the policy due to misrepresentation does not affect when coverage begins. Coverage start time is determined by the Effective Date regardless of potential future disputes over accuracy of representations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The company's ability to contest the policy due to misrepresentation does not influence or relate to the policyowner's authority to change beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The company’s right to contest the policy due to misrepresentation does not affect or influence the policy owner’s ability to assign the policy. The assignment right remains independent of claims about accuracy during underwriting.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The company's ability to contest the policy due to misrepresentation does not directly affect the policy owner's possession of contractual rights, though it may impact those rights if the contest succeeds.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO DIRECT RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the company to contest the policy due to misrepresentation does not influence or relate to the rule that the insured becomes the owner if no owner is designated.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The insurer's ability to contest the policy due to misrepresentation does not influence the policyowner's right to cancel it. The two clauses address separate aspects of policy enforcement and termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The insurer's right to contest the policy due to misrepresentation is relevant because it underscores why the owner should exercise their examination right—to verify accuracy and identify any false statements that might later lead to denial of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the insurer to contest the policy due to misrepresentation operates independently of the policyholder’s right to examine and reject the policy within 20 days. The examination period allows the insured to withdraw without penalty, while contestation rights pertain to claims after death if fraud is discovered later.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
