<edge source="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Entire Contract includes documents forming the basis of the policy, but it does not specify or affect the length of time available for reinstatement post-lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Defining the Entire Contract establishes the authoritative documents forming the policy’s legal basis, whereas the claim about level premiums specifies financial terms. The former sets structural context; the latter addresses cost predictability—no mutual dependence exists.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">Defining the Entire Contract establishes the formal documentation basis of the policy, whereas the premium guarantee specifies financial commitments during the term. Neither statement relies on the other for meaning or validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Entire Contract does not determine when coverage ends; it only specifies the documents that form the binding agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The concept of the Entire Contract includes all binding documents governing the policy, among which is the provision specifying when coverage ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTAINS_TERM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the Entire Contract includes all formal elements governing policy actions like renewal or conversion, ensuring those processes adhere strictly to documented terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">GOVERNS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the components of the Entire Contract, one of which—policy terms—is directly relevant to determining the conditions under which benefits are paid, as noted in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
