<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Policy provisions cannot be altered by representatives regardless of reinstatement timelines or conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">The rule preventing agents from modifying policy terms preserves the fixed nature of premiums during the guaranteed period, ensuring that rate stability cannot be undermined externally.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on altering policy terms ensures that the promise of stable premiums cannot be undermined after issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The rule against altering policy terms ensures that the automatic termination upon expiry is preserved exactly as written, preventing unauthorized extensions or modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The rule against altering policy provisions ensures that the automatic termination clause at the end of the term stands unchanged, preserving the intended lifecycle of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against altering policy provisions underpins the necessity that renewal or conversion options remain strictly within the documented contract language.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 prohibits agents from changing policy terms, which directly enables the enforcement of the conditions described in fact_sentence_1 regarding benefit eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against altering policy provisions depends on the existence of a clearly defined policy; without defining what the policy is, the restriction would lack reference point.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy encompasses multiple documents including riders and endorsements, it follows that no agent may unilaterally alter them, preserving the integrity of the comprehensive contractual framework outlined in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The rule that no agent or representative may alter the policy implies that ultimate authority rests with Sentinel Life Assurance Company, whose identity validates the exclusivity of decision-making power within the organization.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES LIMITATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">Policy provisions cannot be altered by representatives, reinforcing the formal nature of the agreement; this includes protections related to the Insured’s coverage, maintaining consistency with the defined roles.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on altering policy terms ensures that the Owner’s full ownership rights remain unchallenged and legally protected from unauthorized interference.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">A prohibition against agents altering policy provisions ensures that formal changes require adherence to written procedures; this rule applies regardless of beneficiary designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against altering policy provisions ensures that the Death Benefit remains intact and legally binding as specified in the original agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PROTECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against altering policy provisions ensures that the Death Benefit remains fully consistent with the original terms set forth in the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The rule preventing agents from changing policy provisions ensures that the premium payments remain unchanged and consistently enforced over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">MAINTAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against unauthorized alterations ensures that even during a grace period, no party can modify core policy conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">Policy changes require formal procedures not subject to agent discretion, ensuring consistency; meanwhile, the grace period allows temporary flexibility without voiding coverage, operating under distinct rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against altering policy provisions ensures that even during reinstatement attempts, core terms remain unchanged and enforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against agents altering policy provisions ensures contractual integrity, independent of when the incontestability period begins or ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 ensures that no agent can change policy terms, thereby upholding the conditions under which the incontestability clause operates without interference.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">Any attempt by an agent to modify or waive policy terms would violate the principle that only the written contract governs, thereby preserving the conditions under which the company can legally contest the policy based on misrepresentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on agent alterations safeguards the integrity of the Entire Contract, ensuring that only authorized written materials—such as the policy, application, and endorsed riders—are legally recognized.</data>
  <data key="d4">PROTECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against altering policy provisions ensures that the accuracy of application statements remains binding, preserving the foundation upon which the policy was granted.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on unauthorized changes ensures that only formally authorized actions—specifically those approved in writing by a company officer—can legally alter the policy, preserving its contractual integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against altering policy terms relies on the policy having been properly issued, which occurs only upon receipt of the first premium. Without this payment, the contractual framework cannot take effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The rule that no one can change policy terms ensures that the requirement to pay premiums remains unchanged, directly supporting the continuation of coverage based on timely payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The rule against altering policy provisions ensures consistency in defining key elements like the effective date, which is formally documented in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against altering policy provisions ensures that the effective date and coverage start time remain binding and unchanged. This rule supports the precise activation timeline described in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on altering policy provisions ensures that the owner's exclusive rights remain intact and不受外部 interference. This protects the owner’s ability to fully control the policy without third-party modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The rule against unauthorized alterations ensures policy terms remain intact, supporting consistent application of ownership definitions like those in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIANCE_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against altering policy provisions ensures contractual stability, while the owner's assignment right reflects ownership autonomy. These statements support separate aspects of policy governance without direct causal linkage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The rule preventing agents from altering policy terms ensures that only authorized parties can make changes, preserving the integrity of the owner’s ability to manage beneficiary designations independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on altering policy provisions ensures that the policyowner’s right to cancel remains based on clear, unchanged terms. Without this protection, the cancellation process could be undermined by arbitrary changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on altering policy provisions ensures that the Owner’s examination right cannot be undermined by unauthorized changes, maintaining the validity of the inspection window.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against altering policy terms ensures that the 20-day examination period remains based on the original, unchanged agreement. This preserves the fairness and transparency of the inspection process.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES INTEGRITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="9e3cd4f3-d236-4040-a6c4-c46f3a22a611">
  <data key="d3">The claim that no representative may alter policy provisions conflicts with Eleanor B. Raynor’s status as an authorized figure implicated in fraudulent conduct, suggesting potential abuse of authority despite contractual safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="de0d67af-5b66-4374-8edd-cc82b199731b">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on agents waiving policy provisions may apply to individuals like Eleanor B. Raynor, whose leadership role could involve overseeing compliance; however, no direct link exists between her position and the specific policy clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="df9797d7-629e-4917-bc56-582d8cf4fe9d">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against agents altering policy terms in fact_sentence_1 stands in direct contradiction to the implication of unauthorized conduct in fact_sentence_2, suggesting potential breach of policy integrity through fraudulent behavior.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFLICTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37" target="57fafae6-d83d-473d-a0a2-e4e4d1824c40">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on altering policy provisions applies universally, including to representatives like Eleanor B. Raynor, whose role at Sentinel Life Assurance Company underscores potential administrative influence, though not authorization to override core terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
