  <data key="d3">Any change to policy terms, including those affecting premiums, must be formally authorized in writing; however, this rule applies independently of whether premiums are guaranteed not to rise.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">Requiring written authorization for alterations or waivers has no direct bearing on when coverage ends at the conclusion of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">Requiring written authorization for alterations or waivers has no direct bearing on when coverage ends; it governs change processes rather than expiration conditions.</data>
