  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">Any attempt to alter the rules around renewal or conversion—as specified in fact_sentence_1—must first receive express written authorization from a company officer, as stated in fact_sentence_2. Without such authorization, even if allowed by contract language, the change would not be legally binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Any attempt to modify the terms governing benefits—including exclusions—depends on adherence to the procedural safeguard specified in fact_sentence_2, directly linking it to the scope of benefits established in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">Any attempt to alter the Policy—as defined in the prior statement—requires explicit written approval from a company officer, ensuring control over contractual modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_AUTHORIZATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">Any change to parts of the policy—including its application, schedule, or riders—must be authorized through explicit written consent from a company officer, reflecting the boundaries established by the policy’s composition.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by a company officer implies institutional control over policy changes, reinforcing the legal entity responsible—Sentinel Life Assurance Company—as central to enforcement and modification procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">Any changes to the policy require explicit written approval from a company officer, ensuring legal integrity and accountability. This requirement applies regardless of the insured's status, meaning it governs modifications even after defining the insured party.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">Any change to the policy requires explicit written approval by the company, reflecting the limits on even fully owned rights to prevent unilateral actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The need for written approval to modify policy terms has no bearing on who is named as the Beneficiary or how they receive the Death Benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">Any modification to the policy, including changes affecting the Death Benefit, must be authorized in writing by a company officer. Such formal consent ensures that alterations align with contractual integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Any attempt to alter the Death Benefit must follow formal procedures involving written authorization from a company officer, ensuring compliance with the original policy framework governing the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">Formal changes to policy terms require written approval, independent of the regular premium payments needed to sustain the policy's active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Any change to the policy’s terms or waivers must be formally authorized by a company officer in writing. This rule stands independent of whether a grace period applies after a missed payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">Any change to the policy’s terms, including those potentially affecting grace period conditions, must be formally authorized in writing by company officials.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
