  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">Policy modifications or waivers must be formally authorized in writing by a company officer, ensuring control over contractual changes. This rule stands separately from the incontestability period, which governs when claims may be contested.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 establishes that alterations to the policy require formal written approval from a company officer. This requirement applies regardless of whether the change occurs during the incontestability period described in fact sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">Requiring written authorization for waivers or changes ensures that modifications are formally documented, but this process does not affect the company’s right to contest the policy over prior misrepresentations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">Since alterations to the Entire Contract require explicit written consent, this rule reinforces the boundaries established by defining what comprises the contract itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by a company officer enforces the rule that no one else—including agents—may change the policy, reinforcing the binding nature of the original agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization to alter the policy does not rely on the payment of the first premium, though both relate to policy administration. This statement stands independently regarding procedural compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization ensures that modifications to the policy cannot occur without official consent, preserving the integrity of the agreement grounded in the applicant’s original statements.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization to alter the policy ensures that changes are formally documented, but it does not affect whether continued coverage hinges on timely premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines procedural requirements for altering the policy, independent of its start date. Fact_sentence_2 specifies that the effective date appears on the benefits schedule, establishing when coverage begins.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization ensures that while the policy owner holds all contractual rights, they cannot unilaterally alter the policy without official approval, preserving the integrity of the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by a company officer ensures formal control over policy alterations, but it does not influence or depend on when coverage starts. Coverage commencement is determined independently based on the Effective Date and standard time rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to change beneficiaries is subject to the condition that any such change must be formally authorized in writing by the company, ensuring compliance with contractual procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization to alter or waive policy terms ensures control over modifications, while the owner’s right to cancel operates independently as a termination option under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by a company officer ensures that any official change to the policy—such as an assignment—is formally validated. This safeguards against unauthorized transfers even if the owner attempts to assign the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by a company officer applies universally to contractual changes but does not influence or rely upon who holds ownership under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The 20-day examination period allows the policyholder to review and reject the policy before any modifications take effect, providing a safeguard against unauthorized changes that require written authorization.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The Owner's right to examine the policy allows them to review its contents before making decisions about modifications. This inspection phase could inform whether an alteration is desired, though it does not trigger or enable such changes directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="de0d67af-5b66-4374-8edd-cc82b199731b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by a company officer in fact_sentence_1 is directly relevant to Eleanor B. Raynor’s role as CEO, making her a potential approver for waivers or alterations under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="57fafae6-d83d-473d-a0a2-e4e4d1824c40">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by a company officer aligns with Eleanor B. Raynor's role as CEO, making her a potential approver of any policy modifications mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
