  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="df9797d7-629e-4917-bc56-582d8cf4fe9d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by a company officer creates a safeguard against unauthorized changes; however, the occurrence of a fraudulent act raises concerns about whether such procedures were bypassed or compromised during the alleged misconduct.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNDERMINES_TRUST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a" target="9e3cd4f3-d236-4040-a6c4-c46f3a22a611">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization from a company officer (fact_sentence_1) could apply to actions taken by someone like Eleanor B. Raynor, who is designated as an authorized representative (fact_sentence_2). However, her association with fraud casts doubt on the validity of any purported authorizations she might issue.</data>
