<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The effective date marks when the policy becomes active, independent of the 5-year window available for reinstating a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">The effective date determines when the policy's benefits commence, including the initiation of the guaranteed term during which premiums are fixed at a level rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">SETS_CONTEXT_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">The effective date of the policy sets the start time for coverage, including the commencement of the guaranteed premium rate, though it doesn't affect whether premiums are locked in.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The Effective Date determines when the policy becomes active, setting the timeline from which the 5-year term and eventual termination are measured. Without this start date, it would be impossible to determine when coverage expires under the stated condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the effective date helps establish when the 5-year term began, thereby allowing calculation of when coverage will terminate if not extended or converted.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The effective date of the policy, listed on the Schedule of Benefits, marks the start of coverage. This timing is separate from the procedural requirements governing renewal or conversion, which depend solely on contract stipulations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the Effective Date enables determination of when the policy's terms, including those governing benefits, become enforceable and applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the effective date requires prior recognition of the policy itself, so the concept of the policy must exist before its effective date can be determined or referenced.</data>
  <data key="d4">IS_DETERMINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">Since the effective date is specified on the Schedule of Benefits, and the Schedule is part of the complete policy, the existence of the effective date relies on the inclusion of the schedule within the broader policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINED_IN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The effective date listed on the Schedule of Benefits signifies when the policy takes effect, relying on the existence of a responsible entity—Sentinel Life Assurance Company—to administer it.</data>
  <data key="d4">INSTITUTIONAL BASIS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The Effective Date marks when the policy's protections commence, including those for the Insured. While critical for timing, it does not alter or define the Insured’s status, which remains constant regardless of the start date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence identifies the policy's start date via the Schedule of Benefits, but it does not reference or rely on the concept of ownership held by the Owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence establishes the method for identifying the policy’s effective date through the Schedule of Benefits, which has no bearing on the definition of the Beneficiary described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The Effective Date established on the Schedule of Benefits marks when coverage—including the Death Benefit—is officially in force.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The Effective Date listed on the Schedule of Benefits sets the timeline from which the Death Benefit becomes applicable under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The Effective Date indicates when the policy's benefits commence, including any obligation to make future premium payments, but does not define what those payments entail.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The effective date marks when the policy's coverage begins, regardless of any subsequent grace period used after a late payment; thus, the timing of the grace period is unrelated to how or when the policy became effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The Effective Date defines when the policy's coverage commences, whereas the Grace Period allows temporary flexibility post-due date without losing coverage. They operate independently in defining temporal boundaries of the policy’s validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The effective date is established at policy issuance and recorded on the Schedule of Benefits; however, this date does not influence whether reinstatement is possible after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The Effective Date marks the beginning of the policy's coverage and serves as the reference point for initiating key protections like the Incontestability Period, making it foundational to understanding the timing of legal safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">ANCHORS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The effective date sets the timeline for key policy features, including the beginning of the incontestability period, under which the insurer may later challenge the policy’s validity if issues arise.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The effective date of the policy, as stated on the Schedule of Benefits, has no bearing on whether the company can later contest the policy based on prior misrepresentations.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The Effective Date specified in the Schedule of Benefits relies on the inclusion of the policy, application, and attachments—collectively known as the Entire Contract—for proper validation and enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The effective date's location in the Schedule of Benefits underscores its importance as a binding component of the policy, consistent with the principle that only authorized changes apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the effective date listed on the Schedule of Benefits, which determines when the policy takes effect. This does not depend on whether alterations require written authorization.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The effective date listed on the Schedule of Benefits marks when coverage starts, contingent upon prior acceptance of the applicant’s statements during the application phase.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The Effective Date, listed in the Schedule of Benefits, marks when the policy becomes active; this date is dependent on prior conditions, including the receipt of the first premium, which initiates the policy’s validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONED_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The Effective Date marks when coverage starts, setting the timeline from which future premium payments are expected, though it does not influence whether those payments are made.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The effective date listed on the Schedule of Benefits determines when the policy officially takes effect. Coverage begins precisely at 12:01 A.M. Standard Time on that day at the Owner's address.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The effective date determines when coverage begins but does not affect the policyowner's ability to assign the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The effective date of the policy is determined by the schedule of benefits but does not influence who owns the policy if no owner is designated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The effective date marks when the policy's coverage starts, but it does not influence the ownership rights held by the policyholder. Ownership remains consistent regardless of activation timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The effective date determines when the policy begins providing coverage, setting the stage for all subsequent rights and obligations, including those related to changing beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s effective date determines when coverage begins, which sets the timeframe within which the owner can exercise cancellation rights. Without an effective date, the basis for exercising those rights would be unclear.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The effective date determines when the policy begins, setting the timeline within which the owner may exercise their right to examine the policy. Without knowing the start date, the window for evaluation cannot be properly contextualized.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The effective date marks when coverage officially starts, but it occurs after the 20-day examination period ends, meaning the policyholder has time to evaluate the policy prior to its activation.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
