<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s right to change beneficiaries operates independently of the 5-year reinstatement window following a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to modify beneficiaries underscores their control over the death benefit distribution, which operates independently of how premiums are structured during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner's authority to change beneficiaries operates independently of premium guarantees, reflecting separate governance rights under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner's authority to change beneficiaries exists independently of when coverage ends, as it relates to ownership rights rather than coverage duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner's authority to change beneficiaries exists independently of when coverage ends, as it relates to ownership rights rather than coverage duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's authority to update beneficiaries operates independently of any requirements related to renewing or converting the policy under specified contract conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Benefit entitlements depend on adherence to the policy’s terms, including those governing who may be designated as a beneficiary and how designations can be altered.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES_CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">Since the Policy Owner has the right to change beneficiaries, this implies they hold significant decision-making power regarding the policy’s distribution terms, consistent with the role described by the Policy's formal definition.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to change beneficiaries implies the presence of a comprehensive policy structure, which encompasses forms, schedules, and other official documents as specified in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the policy owner to change beneficiaries depends on the policies administered by Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4">ADMINISTERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s authority to change beneficiaries stems from their legal standing in the policy, which includes managing key elements like beneficiary designation. The existence of the Insured establishes the subject of coverage that the Owner manages through contractual privileges.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries is a direct manifestation of the Owner’s comprehensive control over the policy, stemming from their full ownership status.</data>
  <data key="d4">DERIVES_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The ability to designate or modify beneficiaries stems from the policy owner’s legal authority under the policy agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to modify beneficiaries enables them to direct who will receive the Death Benefit. This power ensures that the intended recipient of the benefit aligns with the owner’s current wishes.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to change beneficiaries ensures flexibility in directing the Death Benefit according to current wishes, aligning with policy-defined rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries belongs solely to the policy owner and does not require any condition related to premium payments or financial obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s right to change beneficiaries operates independently of the grace period provision for late premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's ability to update beneficiaries reflects ownership control, which exists regardless of whether the policy is currently in a grace period or active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">Changing beneficiaries involves modifying benefit designations under the policy; this action is unrelated to the process of reinstating a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner's right to change beneficiaries reflects ownership control over beneficiary designation. This autonomy exists regardless of the incontestability period's duration or purpose.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s right to change beneficiaries exists regardless of whether the company can later contest the policy during the incontestability period; one does not impact the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s right to modify beneficiaries is independent of the insurer’s potential to contest the policy based on prior misrepresentations.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to change beneficiaries relies on the contractual framework established by the Entire Contract, which formally defines the boundaries of ownership and decision-making power.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The owner’s right to change beneficiaries operates within the constraints set by the policy, including the prohibition against unauthorized modifications by representatives, ensuring changes remain compliant with formal procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">Any attempt to modify beneficiary designations under the policy must follow the rule requiring explicit written consent from a company officer, reinforcing the legal framework governing amendments.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The Owner’s authority to change beneficiaries reflects full ownership rights granted by the policy. This autonomy operates independently of the condition that the policy was issued based on application statements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s authority to modify beneficiaries reflects ownership rights established once the policy is issued, contingent upon fulfilling conditions including paying the first premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to designate or update beneficiaries reflects their ownership privileges. This administrative power exists independently of whether premiums have been paid, though it only applies while the policy is in force.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to change beneficiaries exists from the moment the policy takes effect, making it contingent upon the policy having been issued and activated.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries stems directly from the Policy Owner holding all contractual rights under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to change beneficiaries presupposes that the policy is in force, meaning coverage must have already begun at the specified time on the Effective Date.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries depends on having ownership; without a designated Owner, the Insured automatically assumes that role and acquires the authority to make such changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries depends on first having access to the policy through the examination period, ensuring informed decisions about beneficiary assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to change beneficiaries reflects ongoing management control, which complements their power to assign the policy to another party, ensuring flexibility in transferring or modifying ownership-related decisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner's right to change beneficiaries reflects ongoing management authority, which supports their capacity to later initiate cancellation if desired. This autonomy enables proactive adjustments before deciding to terminate coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries relates to ongoing policy management by the owner, while the examination right allows the policyholder to assess and reject the policy within 20 days of receiving it. The two concepts operate independently across distinct temporal phases of the policy process.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states the broad right of the Policy Owner to modify beneficiaries, which is operationalized in fact_sentence_2 through a formal submission process. This provides clarity on how the right is exercised.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to change beneficiaries, established in fact_sentence_1, is made actionable through the timing rule specified in fact_sentence_2, which states that changes take effect on the date of signing.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to change beneficiaries (fact_sentence_1) is concretely realized through the rule that changes become effective on the date of signing (fact_sentence_2), ensuring immediate enforceability.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries complements the owner’s ability to assign the policy, as both reflect broad discretionary control over the policy’s disposition and benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to change beneficiaries, established in fact_sentence_1, is made actionable through the rule that such changes take immediate effect upon receipt, even if the insured has passed away, as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries complements the owner’s ability to cancel the policy, as both reflect broad discretionary powers granted to the Policy Owner regarding policy management and termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to change beneficiaries, as stated in fact_sentence_1, is operationally realized through the mechanism described in fact_sentence_2, where changes take immediate effect regardless of the insured’s current health status.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries depends on having access to accurate payment records, which ensures compliance and proper tracking during modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries depends on having access to the policy documentation, which supports informed decision-making. This ensures transparency and accountability when modifying key policy elements.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 grants the Policy Owner general authority to modify beneficiaries, which is concretely realized through the action described in fact_sentence_2—requesting new designations. This shows procedural implementation of a broader entitlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries complements the owner’s ability to request riders, as both empower the Policy Owner to tailor the policy’s benefits and distribution according to evolving needs.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8109d34e-387f-451f-abe9-fe721dabe42e" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_right_to_change</data>
</edge>
