  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="54cfd348-9340-4ece-b6af-4762df5f254a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="1c84614e-a442-4e1c-b430-f726c81cf404">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="9201622f-6f59-4351-a9e1-e7b16db47eb0">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s ability to assign the policy exists independently of the reinstatement window that follows a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s right to assign the policy reflects ownership control, which exists regardless of whether premiums are fixed or variable.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to assign the policy reflects ownership authority; however, this right operates independently of whether premiums are fixed or subject to change.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to assign the policy allows transfer of ownership prior to termination, potentially affecting how the death benefit is managed upon expiry of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner's right to assign the policy exists regardless of whether coverage continues beyond the term or terminates at its conclusion.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner's right to assign the policy is a standalone ownership privilege that operates regardless of whether renewal or conversion follows specified contract conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to assign the policy implies that such action is permissible but still bound by the policy’s governing terms and exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">Because the Policy is defined as the individual term life insurance contract, any rights associated with it—including assignment—are inherently linked to the designated Policy Owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">DERIVES_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The ability to assign the policy stems from the policy's status as a legally binding whole composed of multiple integrated parts, including applications and endorsements.</data>
  <data key="d4">DERIVES_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s right to assign the policy reflects ownership control, which exists independently of the specific identity of the insurer, though the insurer facilitates such actions through contractual procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner possesses the authority to assign the policy, independent of who the Insured is, though the Insured’s identity remains central to coverage eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The ability to assign the policy confirms that the Owner holds full ownership rights, reinforcing the foundational claim about ownership established earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner holds the authority to assign the policy, which could potentially impact future benefit distribution, including whether the originally named Beneficiary continues to receive the Death Benefit depending on how the assignment is executed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner holds the legal authority to assign the policy to another party. This right operates independently of how the Death Benefit is determined or paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s authority to assign the policy enables them to transfer ownership, possibly altering who receives the Death Benefit upon claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's authority to assign the policy reflects full ownership privileges. This right exists regardless of whether premiums have been paid, though failure to pay may result in lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to assign the policy reflects ownership control. This right exists regardless of whether a grace period applies or not, as it pertains to legal transfer rather than payment obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s right to assign the policy exists regardless of whether the policy is currently in a grace period or active status; the assignment right is unaffected by temporary coverage extensions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to assign the policy enables transfer of ownership, regardless of whether the policy was previously lapsed or could be reinstated. Reinstatement depends on eligibility criteria, independent of assignment rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner holds full ownership rights, including the legal capacity to assign the policy to someone else. This right exists regardless of whether the incontestability period applies or not.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">Ownership rights permit the policyholder to assign the policy, regardless of whether the insurer retains contestation power during the incontestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to assign the policy does not impact the company’s ability to contest it based on prior misrepresentations; these are separate legal mechanisms operating independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner's right to assign the policy is supported by its inclusion in the Entire Contract, ensuring that ownership powers are formally recognized and legally enforceable under the agreed-upon terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DERIVED_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s ability to assign the policy stems from full ownership rights, whereas the restriction on agents modifying terms preserves legal consistency. Neither statement depends on the other for validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s ability to assign the policy implies they hold significant control, though such an action would still require explicit written consent per company policy, ensuring compliance with governance rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s right to assignment exists independently of whether the policy was issued based on application statements.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s ability to assign the policy stems from full ownership rights, which are established after the policy is issued, contingent on the first premium payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to assign the policy stems from ownership rights, whereas maintaining coverage relies solely on consistent premium payments, without requiring assignment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s right to assign the policy exists regardless of the effective date, which only specifies when benefits become active.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The Owner’s ability to assign the policy presupposes that coverage is active, meaning the assignment only applies after the policy takes effect at 12:01 A.M. on the Effective Date.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">Because the Policy Owner holds all contractual rights, they inherently possess the ability to assign the policy, making this action a natural extension of their full ownership status.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy enables transfer of ownership interests, which includes the subsequent ability to designate new beneficiaries through the new owner, making it logically connected to changing beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to assign the policy demonstrates control over its transfer, which complements their power to initiate cancellation, reflecting comprehensive ownership autonomy.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy belongs to the designated Policy Owner; if no Owner is specified, the Insured automatically assumes that role.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_RIGHT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The Owner’s ability to assign the policy depends on first having access to its contents, which is enabled by the examination right. This ensures informed decisions before transferring ownership.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy pertains to ownership transfers after acquisition, whereas the right to examine allows cancellation during an initial 20-day window post-receipt. The former relates to ongoing ownership management; the latter concerns early-stage decision-making before commitment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports the owner’s broader authority to manage its transfer, which inherently includes changing the beneficiary, reinforcing the owner’s control over distribution of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports the owner’s broader capacity to manage ownership transfers, which complements the ability to change beneficiaries independently, ensuring consistent control over policy disposition.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to assign the policy supports their broader authority to manage ownership transfers, which includes changing beneficiaries independently through formal requests.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 grants the Policy Owner the broad right to assign the policy, which is further clarified in fact_sentence_2 through detailed procedures requiring a written assignment approved by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">ELABORATES_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy underscores the owner’s broad control, enabling them to transfer ownership entirely—a capability consistent with the authority to unilaterally change beneficiaries, even posthumously.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy underscores the policy owner’s broad control over its disposition, which complements the separate but related right to unilaterally change beneficiaries without requiring the insured’s consent or presence.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports the owner’s comprehensive control, enabling them to transfer it before cancellation; this complements the explicit right to cancel at any time.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy depends on having access to its documentation; thus, the ability to request a copy supports the enforcement of assignment rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports transparency needs, making it relevant that the owner can also request premium payment history to verify the policy’s financial standing before transfer.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports the owner’s broader capacity to manage beneficiary designations, as assignment may transfer these responsibilities to another party. This ensures continuity of intent even after ownership changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy supports the owner’s ability to transfer control, which can be exercised when adding riders like the Accelerated Death Benefit. This enhances flexibility in managing the policy post-transfer.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79d7c579-6c3e-45f4-9ba4-aa81ddab7b31" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_right_to_assign_policy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="e2782ab1-d8aa-4137-9b31-44c82f1c57a2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="107a3359-cf05-402d-a671-26060c296e4b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="58a1f434-89e3-48b6-8ba8-3e678dc074ed">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="403ff8b2-ea98-4eb2-9813-83789c485623">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="34931128-8e2e-46a3-9643-bff4bbfa7f14">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="b5692955-b879-4df3-a1ab-b5f77264b99e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="20cc386d-205e-4dde-9202-10ead16f4e11">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="541d99fd-9b6f-4f31-9cf4-9a62e3621538">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="49372d91-674a-48db-b085-d5c8dafe7461">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="89bbb71e-be07-45a0-bc6b-59f8bfccc166">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="9da2f3b6-8f69-41a5-956a-80ba356c1c36">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="2c36b247-af70-48e9-87c9-ad36bdadce54">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="9617b84a-5728-4558-900c-b3fc5a07e5e8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner may choose to cancel the policy at any time, regardless of whether it was previously reinstated or remains active.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to cancel enables them to exit the agreement at any point, potentially motivated by factors including the ongoing commitment required by fixed premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSIDERED_IN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">The policyholder’s right to cancel provides autonomy over policy retention. Knowing premiums won’t rise enhances the practical significance of this right by reducing risk associated with long-term commitments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="bf239f1e-143c-4033-9908-3fd3008ea579">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner possesses the unilateral power to terminate the policy early via cancellation. This action contrasts with the default termination occurring at the end of the term without renewal.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="b0b717e1-fe2d-4c8b-9cf6-9744f1fe04ce">
  <data key="d3">The option to cancel allows the owner to end coverage before the term concludes, thereby avoiding continuation beyond the intended duration, even though the default endpoint is at the end of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREEMPTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="691ac7f0-573b-4d26-abde-28f5eabaea4f">
  <data key="d3">Although the policyowner may cancel the policy, this right operates independently of whether renewal or conversion would otherwise be permitted under the contract’s specified conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">The owner’s right to cancel enables termination of the policy, thereby nullifying potential future claims even if the insured meets all conditions required for benefit payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="42f4b018-315c-49b6-a097-7db245ea5c4a">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to request cancellation implies the existence of a formalized policy entity, reinforcing the need for a precise definition of what constitutes the Policy itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="60830010-3081-43cc-889f-dacd9c3bee07">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to request cancellation implies the need for a formally documented Policy containing all relevant components, including applications and schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="7f99ae4d-301d-4e94-ac84-b8b363a2497d">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner holds the legal authority to initiate cancellation, a right exercised against Sentinel Life Assurance Company, the issuing insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESPONSIBLE_ENTITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="1d0d3536-a9fe-4662-85e5-dbb9cc333be7">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner possesses decision-making authority over the policy, including cancellation, independent of who the Insured is. This autonomy allows the Owner to manage the policy regardless of the Insured’s identity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_ROLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="bc216732-e99f-411e-a7bb-6d75de3cce94">
  <data key="d3">The right to request cancellation is a manifestation of the Owner’s comprehensive control over the policy, stemming directly from their full ownership status.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="35280027-764e-4dc6-8e92-4ecfb705c539">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner holds full ownership rights and may exercise control over the policy, including the option to cancel it. This autonomy exists regardless of who is named as the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may initiate cancellation at any time during the term, though doing so would prevent future claims based on the Death Benefit. Cancellation does not alter the original definition of the Death Benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner may cancel the policy at any time during the term, thereby preventing the Death Benefit from becoming payable upon death.</data>
  <data key="d4">TERMINATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="f57a074b-320b-46ff-87df-0bfd1ce1e327">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s power to terminate the policy means they can cease making premium payments at any time during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner holds full rights to terminate the policy at any time through cancellation. This right exists regardless of whether a grace period applies due to a missed premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may choose to cancel the policy at any time, irrespective of its status; this includes cancelling during the grace period when the policy remains in force.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">If the policy owner requests cancellation, the policy cannot be reinstated afterward, making reinstatement impossible once cancellation occurs. This highlights the finality of cancellation relative to reinstatement efforts.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="28d91714-766b-42cd-8559-cf76b7c97afa">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner holds the authority to terminate the policy through cancellation, regardless of whether the incontestability period has elapsed or not.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="40c847da-d90f-459a-9872-60f7ef19fd1f">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to cancel is independent of whether the insurer can contest the policy during the incontestability period. Cancellation is a unilateral action by the owner unrelated to the insurer’s review timeline.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="6fd46389-338e-4186-b747-65809a50a1ba">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner's right to request cancellation is independent of whether the company can later contest the policy based on misrepresentation. One pertains to voluntary withdrawal, the other to potential invalidation post-issue.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="726d6a54-75c6-4811-9e47-b9b938256a64">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to request cancellation relies on knowing exactly what documents make up the contract; thus, the concept of the Entire Contract enables meaningful exercise of cancellation rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="62b8f75b-d774-450e-ab8b-266f127aef37">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s ability to initiate cancellation is meaningful only if the policy terms remain intact; thus, the right to cancel presupposes that no one—including agents—can override those terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="e30bcb57-7999-45fd-95ab-1d5af8b3642a">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s ability to request cancellation stands separately from the need for written consent to modify the policy, reflecting distinct administrative procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="2916fbaf-1ddb-4b5c-b5a0-43f4f0d1cbbc">
  <data key="d3">Ownership includes the authority to terminate the policy via cancellation, regardless of the initial conditions based on application content used to issue it.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="b2604be3-8c9d-411a-9752-e7c408e44f8a">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner holds the authority to terminate the policy at any time. This right exists independently of whether the first premium was paid to initiate coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="5ed00eb3-5246-49ea-b4ac-9973d604854e">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to cancel allows them to end coverage at any time, even if premiums have been paid regularly and coverage would otherwise continue.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREEMPTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="b8a0acec-5bad-4385-aa38-b690f03f26b5">
  <data key="d3">The policyowner’s right to request cancellation implies that they have control over the policy once it is issued and effective, meaning the effective date must precede any potential cancellation action.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="d58b7734-e9a8-4ee8-84f1-1c5d18ebf4e8">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to request cancellation applies once coverage begins, meaning it takes effect after the specified commencement time of 12:01 A.M. on the Effective Date.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="5a5e7682-7da5-4049-b77a-16dfdd50aec3">
  <data key="d3">The right to request cancellation is a manifestation of the Policy Owner's comprehensive ownership and control over the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The right to request cancellation implies ultimate control over the policy, reinforcing that the owner retains the power to modify key elements like beneficiaries prior to termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner's right to request cancellation underscores their decision-making authority, which aligns with their capacity to assign the policy, reinforcing full ownership rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The right to cancel the policy depends on having previously exercised the option to examine it, ensuring informed consent before termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner's right to request cancellation is contingent upon exercising it within the 20-day examination period established after receiving the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="c500b2bb-cfaf-41ad-a305-33298ee4a81b">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the Policy Owner to request cancellation depends on who holds ownership; if no Owner is designated, the Insured automatically assumes that role and thereby acquires the right to cancel.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The right to cancel the policy complements the owner’s ability to change the beneficiary, as both reflect broad discretionary powers retained by the Policy Owner over policy administration and designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The right to cancel the policy complements the owner’s control over beneficiary designations, reinforcing overall ownership autonomy. While cancellation terminates coverage, changing beneficiaries modifies payout instructions without affecting policy validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The right to cancel the policy complements the ability to change the beneficiary, as both reflect the Policy Owner’s broad administrative control over the policy’s lifecycle and distribution outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The right to cancel the policy reinforces the policy owner’s authority over major decisions, consistent with their ability to change beneficiaries independently. Both actions reflect unilateral decision-making power under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">The right to cancel the policy complements the owner’s ability to assign it, as both reflect core ownership powers allowing control over the policy’s lifecycle and transfer.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">Fact Sentence 1 establishes the Policy Owner’s right to cancel; Fact Sentence 2 elaborates on how this right can be exercised through a written request at any time, providing procedural clarity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The right to cancel the policy reinforces the Policy Owner’s overarching control, which also includes changing beneficiaries independently of the insured’s status. This supports the idea that ownership entails broad administrative powers over policy decisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">The right to request cancellation is supported by the ability to review premium payment history, which helps assess financial obligations before terminating coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">The right to request cancellation complements the right to obtain a policy copy, as having access to the policy documentation enables the owner to make informed decisions about termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">The right to cancel the policy complements the owner’s authority to manage beneficiary designations, as both reflect core aspects of ownership control over the policy’s lifecycle and distribution outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">The right to cancel the policy complements the owner’s ability to add riders, as both reflect the owner’s control over policy scope and duration. Cancellation allows withdrawal from coverage entirely, whereas adding riders enhances benefits without terminating the base policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58a1f434-89e3-48b6-8ba8-3e678dc074ed" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_right_to_cancel</data>
</edge>
