  <data key="d3">The ability to cancel a policy early does not influence the conditions required to restore it after lapse. Reinstatement depends solely on future underwriting approval, independent of initial dissatisfaction.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the right to terminate the policy early due to dissatisfaction, while the second discusses the ability to restore a lapsed policy later through specific requirements. These pertain to distinct phases of policy lifecycle management.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO DIRECT RELATIONSHIP</data>
