  <data key="d3">The ability to return a policy within 20 days without penalty relates to initial dissatisfaction, whereas reinstating a lapsed policy involves paying backlogged premiums at a later stage. They address separate phases in the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
