  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy leads to it being void from inception, meaning any prior ownership—including automatic assignment to the insured—is invalidated due to the policy's termination at origin.</data>
  <data key="d4">REVERSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">The option to void the policy from inception exists only because the owner has been granted a 20-day examination period to evaluate and reject it.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy initiates a process where the contract becomes invalid effective from the start due to the owner’s dissatisfaction during the review window.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s voidance from inception occurs because it was returned within the 20-day examination window, qualifying the holder for a full refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the policy becomes void from its beginning upon return. This aligns directly with fact sentence 2, which clarifies that the policy should be considered as though it was never issued at any point.</data>
  <data key="d4">EQUIVALENT TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy results in its immediate nullification from the start date. This outcome does not rely on written modifications but rather on the act of return itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">If the policy is returned, it becomes void from the start, and this outcome cannot be altered because no agent or broker has authority to waive such a rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy results in its immediate invalidation from the start date. This outcome is independent of whether changes to the policy were formally approved.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">If the policy is returned, it becomes void from the start, meaning no legal effect exists; this outcome reinforces why only authorized personnel can make changes to prevent premature invalidation through improper handling.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy results in immediate nullification from inception, preventing any accumulation of rights such as incontestability. In contrast, incontestability only arises after sustained compliance over two years without lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="64edfdb5-aded-401b-bbe7-55880fad2b56">
  <data key="d3">The first statement concerns invalidation of the policy upon return, while the second addresses limitations on claims due to suicide within two years. They pertain to separate events and outcomes unrelated in sequence or causality.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="6cde3bd7-3a57-480f-b1f9-561875fd48f4">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns policy termination due to return prior to acceptance, while the second addresses limitations on claims when death occurs via suicide within two years. They pertain to separate risk events and do not influence each other directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08">
  <data key="d3">If the insured returns the policy, it is voided retroactively. This action differs from voidance due to misrepresentation, though both result in loss of coverage before maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="fffa6d30-0053-4c00-b207-2a77ad194bd2">
  <data key="d3">The first statement concerns immediate cancellation of the policy upon return, rendering it null from its start date. This scenario does not influence the second statement about suicide-related claims, which applies regardless of whether the policy was returned.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="f1888ece-7434-4b7e-aebc-5434189a9e7a">
  <data key="d3">The voidance of a policy upon return pertains to cancellation before acceptance, while adjusting coverage due to incorrect age applies post-issue during claim evaluation. They operate under separate scenarios and do not influence each other’s validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">If the policyholder returns the policy, it becomes void retroactively. This condition operates independently of whether the policy is still active during its grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="52a31aaf-1af7-416b-8b31-a19b2a5a1510">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes the consequence of returning the policy, rendering it invalid from the start. This scenario does not relate directly to how coverage should be corrected when gender was incorrectly stated during application.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy results in immediate voidance from inception, regardless of subsequent events like missed payments. This statement does not relate to the grace period provision for later premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">The first statement describes immediate invalidation of the policy upon return, regardless of timing. The second explains claim settlement rules when death occurs during the grace period, independent of prior returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">If the policy is returned, it becomes void from the start, preventing it from ever reaching the two-year mark required for incontestability under fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy results in immediate voidance from inception, independent of premium status. This action terminates coverage regardless of whether the grace period applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy results in immediate voidance from inception, independent of any missed payments. This action terminates the contract retroactively regardless of prior compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">If the policy is returned, it becomes void from inception; however, this termination may be overridden by the Reinstatement provision, which allows restoration of benefits under specific conditions such as timely application and proof of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">If a policy is returned, it becomes void from the start, preventing any future reinstatement. This contrasts with the provision allowing reinstatement only if the policy lapses within five years, assuming eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy nullifies its validity retroactively, meaning no benefits apply. This aligns with the consequence of failing to maintain timely premium payments beyond the grace period, resulting in forfeiture of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">If a policy is returned and declared void from inception, it may still be reinstated later by providing acceptable evidence of insurability to the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy results in its immediate cancellation from the start, nullifying any future claims or benefits. Reinstating a lapsed policy requires paying outstanding premiums but assumes prior lapse occurred under specific terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">VOIDS REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">If the policy is returned and deemed void from inception, reinstatement may still occur under limited circumstances, requiring repayment of past-due premiums plus applicable interest set by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="3319e60e-025b-4b9a-bb2f-a275aa449bb0">
  <data key="d3">Returning the policy terminates it from inception, which aligns with the purpose of the 20-day examination window by ensuring that any decision to withdraw invalidates the policy entirely once returned.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 declares that returning the policy voids it retroactively, undermining the purpose of the 31-day grace period mentioned in fact sentence 1, which assumes ongoing eligibility for renewal despite delayed payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="5e10d7d2-9369-45f7-b96c-869e9315411d">
  <data key="d3">While the first fact supports the idea that a lapsed policy can be revived through reinstatement, the second claim invalidates the policy entirely from inception upon return, making reinstatement impossible under these conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFLICTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The claim that returning the policy voids it from inception undermines the validity of the 5-year reinstatement window mentioned earlier, rendering the reinstatement provision meaningless if the policy is returned.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fad2d24f-8146-4ac8-95f2-9e301d6c974b" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
