  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 mandates that all policy modifications must be documented in writing; fact_sentence_2 reinforces this by explicitly prohibiting agents or brokers from waiving provisions, ensuring only authorized personnel can act under the written requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242" target="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written amendments ensures procedural integrity, while the incontestability rule provides long-term protection against challenges to claims after two years. These rules serve complementary but distinct purposes in maintaining policy reliability.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
