  <data key="d3">The requirement for written modifications ensures proper documentation of changes, which helps prevent disputes over misrepresented information that could trigger the policy's potential voidance within two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242" target="6cde3bd7-3a57-480f-b1f9-561875fd48f4">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written amendments ensures that exceptions like the suicide clause cannot be altered informally, preserving its enforceability through proper channels.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242" target="f1888ece-7434-4b7e-aebc-5434189a9e7a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization ensures that adjustments like those based on incorrect age information are formally documented and legally binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_WRITTEN_AUTHORIZATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
