<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision activates after two years of continuous coverage, a rule that operates independently of whether the insured is designated as owner or not.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">After two years of being in force, the policy gains incontestability status regardless of the owner’s prior actions during the 20-day examination period.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681">
  <data key="d3">After two years, the policy becomes incontestable, meaning the insurer cannot dispute its validity due to misrepresentation—this occurs irrespective of whether the owner exercised the 20-day right to cancel.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">The second fact outlines a long-term protective provision ensuring the insurer cannot contest claims after two years, regardless of earlier actions such as returning the policy for a refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">After two years of uninterrupted existence, the policy gains incontestability, making it immune to challenges by insurers unless fraud or non-payment occurred. This protects against invalidation even if the policy was returned earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTERIORS TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause takes effect after two years of active policy status, but it does not override the rule that returning the policy results in treatment as if never issued.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">After two years, the insurer cannot contest the policy's validity except for non-payment, reinforcing its permanence. This does not affect the need for written consent when altering terms, which remains mandatory regardless of duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">After two years of continuous coverage, the policy becomes legally unchallengeable under normal circumstances, reinforcing its enforceability; however, this does not affect the need for authorized sign-offs when modifying terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_DIRECT_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision after two years relies on consistent application of rules, such as requiring written authorization for changes, to maintain policy validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision after two years relies on the rule that only authorized representatives may alter policy terms, preventing unauthorized modifications that could undermine its application.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">The first statement establishes a standard incontestability period of two years, while the second clarifies that this protection does not extend to cases involving unpaid premiums, thereby narrowing the applicability of the initial claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision protects the policyholder after two years unless fraud or misrepresentation invalidates it. This means that any material misstatement made at application could still allow the insurer to deny claims within the initial two-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="6cde3bd7-3a57-480f-b1f9-561875fd48f4">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot challenge the policy's validity except for non-payment, whereas the suicide clause specifically limits payouts if death occurs by suicide within the first two years, creating a notable exception to general coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="fffa6d30-0053-4c00-b207-2a77ad194bd2">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures policy validity after two years, except where exceptions like suicide apply. Suicide within two years triggers a limitation on benefits, reducing liability to refunded premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="64edfdb5-aded-401b-bbe7-55880fad2b56">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures long-term stability of claims eligibility after two years, while the suicide clause imposes a restriction specifically applicable before that same timeframe, creating a conditional safeguard against early death-related claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="52a31aaf-1af7-416b-8b31-a19b2a5a1510">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures long-term stability of the policy after two years, while the gender-adjustment rule allows corrective action for initial inaccuracies, maintaining fairness regardless of when such issues arise.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="f1888ece-7434-4b7e-aebc-5434189a9e7a">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures long-term stability of the policy terms after two years, allowing any inaccuracies like misstated age to still trigger corrective actions such as benefit adjustments without contestation by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTERIORITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot challenge the policy's validity due to misrepresentation, but this does not affect how long the policy remains effective during a grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot challenge the policy's validity due to misrepresentation, while the 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payments without immediate lapse. These features operate independently but contribute collectively to long-term policy protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot dispute the validity of the policy unless due to non-payment. This does not affect how unpaid premiums are handled during the grace period upon death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision becomes effective after two years of uninterrupted policy existence, contingent on continued compliance with premium obligations such as those outlined in the grace period rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot challenge the policy's validity except for non-payment. This stands independently of whether coverage terminates due to unpaid premiums after the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision applies only if the policy remains active; failing to pay premiums within the grace period terminates benefits and prevents the policyholder from benefiting from the two-year incontestability rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot challenge the policy's validity due to misrepresentation, but this does not affect whether a lapsed policy can later be reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause ensures the insurer cannot challenge claims after two years, while the reinstatement exception allows recovery of benefits despite lapses, providing complementary safeguards for policyholders' rights over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot dispute the policy's validity, but this does not affect the process of reinstating a lapsed policy through premium repayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot contest the policy’s validity, but this does not affect the requirement to pay interest on past-due premiums when reinstating the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot challenge the validity of the policy due to misrepresentation, while reinstatement requires demonstrating current insurability, reflecting separate safeguards for claim integrity and policy continuity.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="4c454305-8df7-4f9a-b113-fd49d2e08142">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces the incontestability provision effective after two years, which complements fact_sentence_1 by ensuring the contractual obligations—including those involving riders and beneficiaries—are legally enforceable once the waiting period passes.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114" target="0d5e54d4-82aa-4712-9f7e-bdb99dc0e6ca">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2's assertion of incontestability after two years depends on the presence of the suicide exclusion clause described in fact_sentence_1, as such exclusions are standard exceptions to incontestability, particularly concerning suicide-related deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
