<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">A policy's validity can be challenged due to material misrepresentation within two years, regardless of who owns it. Ownership status does not alter the consequences of such misrepresentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">If a material misrepresentation was made at application, the insurer may void the policy within two years regardless of the owner having exercised their 20-day right to examine and potentially cancel it.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681">
  <data key="d3">A policy may be voided for material misrepresentation within two years regardless of the owner’s satisfaction or use of the 20-day review option.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">Even if a policy is returned within 20 days for a refund, any material misrepresentation made during application could still lead to the policy being declared void if detected within two years—this applies irrespective of the refund process.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">A policy can be voided within two years if material misrepresentations are found. This contrasts with cancellation via return, where the insurer does not assess accuracy but accepts withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">Material misrepresentation affecting risk assessment can lead to policy voidance within two years of issuance. However, this only applies once the policy has been accepted—not when returned prior to formal issue, which triggers different treatment per fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">A policy may be voided due to material misrepresentation within two years, emphasizing the importance of ensuring all changes are formally documented in writing to maintain enforceability.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes a time-limited condition under which false information can void the policy; this justifies the requirement in fact_sentence_1 that any modification must be officially documented, ensuring such changes cannot circumvent liability tied to initial representations.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">If a material misrepresentation occurs, it underscores why only officially authorized individuals should handle policy changes—to prevent fraudulent or erroneous alterations that might compromise the insurer’s ability to assess risk accurately.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Material misrepresentations can nullify the policy within two years; this provision relies on unwaivable rules enforced by the insurer, such as the one preventing agents from overriding policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114">
  <data key="d3">If a material misrepresentation was made at application, the insurer retains the right to contest the policy's validity even after two years have passed, thereby overriding the standard incontestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies circumstances—material misrepresentation or omission—that permit the insurer to challenge the policy within two years; this directly limits the scope of fact_sentence_1’s blanket incontestability provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="6cde3bd7-3a57-480f-b1f9-561875fd48f4">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes how material misrepresentation can nullify the policy within two years; this sets a broader legal condition under which the insurer avoids liability. Fact sentence 2 specifies one such scenario—suicide—as a distinct but parallel exception where the insurer limits its obligation to returning premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="64edfdb5-aded-401b-bbe7-55880fad2b56">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines conditions under which a policy may be voided due to fraud, specifically related to misrepresented risks. This condition operates independently but shares a time-bound limitation (two years) with the suicide clause described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">TEMPORAL_OVERLAP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="fffa6d30-0053-4c00-b207-2a77ad194bd2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 discusses how false statements about risk can invalidate the policy early on; fact_sentence_2 limits payouts when death results from suicide during the same initial period. While both apply within the first two years, one deals with fraud and the other with intent.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="52a31aaf-1af7-416b-8b31-a19b2a5a1510">
  <data key="d3">Misrepresentation of gender constitutes a material misstatement that could void the policy within two years; however, instead of cancellation, the insurer adjusts coverage proportionally to reflect the correct gender-based premium rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="f1888ece-7434-4b7e-aebc-5434189a9e7a">
  <data key="d3">Misstatements about age fall under broader categories of material misrepresentations that could invalidate a policy within two years. However, instead of voiding the contract outright, the policy adjusts benefits proportionally based on corrected age data.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns the validity of the policy due to truthful disclosure during underwriting, whereas the second outlines a leniency window for paying premiums. They operate independently within different phases of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period ensures continued coverage even when premiums are late, independent of initial underwriting accuracy. This does not affect whether misrepresentations invalidate the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns policy invalidation due to fraud within two years, while the second explains deduction of overdue premiums from death benefits if death occurs during the grace period. They address separate legal conditions affecting claim outcomes but do not logically depend on each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">Misrepresentation affecting risk assessment could lead to policy invalidation early on, but this does not directly influence whether a missed premium causes a lapse during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The presence of material misrepresentation affecting risk assessment could impact policy validity, but it does not alter the requirement to pay premiums during the grace period. Coverage termination due to late payment remains independent of whether misrepresentations were made.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">The first statement concerns policy invalidation due to fraud within two years, whereas the second describes conditions allowing revival of a canceled policy up to five years later. They address distinct aspects of policy integrity and continuity without direct interaction.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder misrepresented information affecting risk assessment, it might result in the policy being voided; however, should the policy have already lapsed due to such issues, reinstatement would still depend on providing acceptable evidence of current insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_PRECEDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">Misrepresentation impacting risk assessment could lead to policy invalidation early on, whereas failure to pay premiums after the grace period results in loss of benefits regardless of prior accuracy. Both events terminate protection, though through different mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_VALID</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">If a policy is voided due to material misrepresentation within two years, it generally terminates benefits. However, the Reinstatement provision allows exceptions where benefits can still be restored under certain conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">If a policy was invalidated due to misrepresentation within two years, it cannot be reinstated unless specific conditions like unpaid premiums are resolved. Reinstatement requires fulfilling outstanding financial obligations such as back premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">If a material misrepresentation is found within two years, the policy may become void. This does not affect the requirement to pay interest on past-due premiums when reinstating the policy later.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
