  <data key="d3">The second sentence limits insurer liability in cases of suicide within two years, whereas the first applies to policies returned before being accepted. Neither condition affects the validity or outcome described in the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6cde3bd7-3a57-480f-b1f9-561875fd48f4" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">The second statement applies only after the policy is effectively issued and covers suicide-related payouts, whereas the first deals with pre-acceptance returns where the policy is nullified. Their contexts differ fundamentally—one involves termination before validity, the other during active coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
