  <data key="d3">The suicide clause restricts the company’s liability to refund premiums if the insured dies by suicide within two years, irrespective of whether the owner exercised the 20-day right to cancel. These clauses function independently regarding policyholder dissatisfaction and claim eligibility.</data>
