<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides leeway for timely premium payment after the initial term, allowing continued coverage even if payment is late. It operates independently of the earlier 20-day examination phase, serving a later stage of policy maintenance rather than pre-commitment review.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures continued coverage despite late payments, whereas the 20-day review window enables early termination without penalty. Neither condition affects the validity or operation of the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 establishes a 31-day grace period for paying subsequent premiums. This does not depend on or relate directly to the 20-day refund option described in fact sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay premiums without losing coverage, but it applies only when the policy is already in force. It does not override the rule that returning the policy makes it void from the start.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">A 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payments without immediate lapse, regardless of whether the policy might later be returned.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period allows flexibility in premium timing, though such adjustments would still need to comply with the rule requiring written approval for any policy modification.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period enables delayed premium payments, whereas the need for an authorized signature prevents unauthorized changes to policy terms. Both contribute to policy integrity but function separately in governance and compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period enables timely premium payments, reducing risk of lapses, whereas the restriction on unauthorized modification preserves the legal validity and consistency of policy terms set by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period depends on the policy’s formal structure, which prevents unauthorized alterations by agents or brokers.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides temporary relief for missed premium payments, helping maintain active coverage, whereas the incontestability clause protects against future disputes over policy terms after two years. Neither condition depends on the other for activation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay premiums without lapsing, helping maintain continuous coverage necessary to eventually meet the two-year threshold required for incontestability.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
