</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay premiums before the policy lapses, enabling future reinstatement within five years if required. Without the grace period, policies would lapse immediately, making reinstatement impossible.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides temporary relief for late premium payments, enabling policyholders to avoid lapses; however, if that window is missed, reinstatement becomes necessary, requiring payment of all delinquent premiums plus interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to make late premium payments without immediate consequence; failing to do so triggers policy lapse, directly linking the two facts.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period maintains policy in-force status beyond the due date, enabling the insurer to fulfill its obligation to pay the death benefit when proof of death is provided.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures that the policy remains active long enough to allow proper processing of a death claim, thereby enabling the requirement for proof of death to be met when needed.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
