<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">The policy stays active during the grace period regardless of who owns it. Ownership assignment by default occurs independently of the grace period’s functionality.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period ensures continued coverage even if a premium is delayed; however, this does not impact the owner’s separate 20-day right to cancel and receive a full refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage despite delayed payment, whereas the 20-day review window enables early termination before commitment. Neither condition affects the operation of the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">The grace period maintains policy validity post-due date, separate from the initial 20-day window where refunds are allowed without conditions. No overlap or dependency exists between them.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">The policy stays in effect during the grace period even if a premium is overdue. However, returning the policy nullifies it entirely from the start, regardless of ongoing grace periods.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows continued policy validity even when a premium is late, but this only applies once the policy is already issued. It cannot override the effect of returning the policy before acceptance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of policy effectiveness during the grace period underscores why written authorizations are necessary—any extension or action affecting coverage must follow formal processes to maintain legal standing.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Even though the policy remains in force during the grace period, any changes to its terms still require written consent from an authorized company officer, ensuring compliance even while coverage continues post-due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">NEEDS_AUTHORIZATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">Even though the policy remains effective during the grace period, this does not override the requirement that only official representatives may make formal changes to the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of policy validity during the grace period depends on maintaining contractual integrity, which aligns with the restriction that only official representatives may authorize changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
