  <data key="d3">The rule about deducting unpaid premiums from the death benefit applies only when the policy remains active during the grace period, whereas reinstatement hinges on future proof of insurability after lapsing. These clauses operate at different points in time and serve separate purposes—one for claims processing, the other for restoring coverage.</data>
