<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses, resulting in termination of coverage. This means the policy's active state ends precisely when the grace period expires.</data>
  <data key="d4">EQUIVALENT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to missed premium payment beyond the grace period, it triggers the condition that requires reinstatement through evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is missed past the grace period, the policy lapses, creating a state where reinstatement becomes necessary. Within five years of this lapse, the policyholder may restore coverage through proper procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period results in policy lapse, necessitating repayment of delinquent premiums to regain coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay a premium within the grace period results in policy lapse, but this termination of benefits can be overridden via the reinstatement provision, allowing restoration under specific terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses. To restore the policy later, the insurer requires that any accrued interest on the delinquent premium be repaid according to its terms at the time of reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The lapse caused by missing a premium payment allows for potential reinstatement within five years, provided terms like overdue payments and insurability are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The inability to pay a premium before the grace period ends leads to policy lapse, but reinstatement remains possible if the applicant can demonstrate insurability to the company’s standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
