<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">Exceptions to benefit termination through reinstatement imply that someone (like the owner) must act to restore coverage; thus, having a defined owner ensures accountability in triggering such processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement exceptions permit restoring benefits after lapse, which could follow from exercising the initial 20-day examination right by canceling and later seeking renewal.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence concerns restoring a terminated policy via reinstitution procedures, whereas the first addresses immediate cancellation rights before any commitment. They operate independently across different timeframes and scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO DIRECT RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement rights allow revival of a lapsed policy under certain conditions, independent of the initial 20-day refund window.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">The Reinstatement provision creates an exception to the automatic voidance caused by returning the policy, enabling revival of benefits even after termination, subject to compliance with time limits and medical requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">QUALIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of reinstating a lapsed policy allows beneficiaries to regain benefits even after the policy was previously treated as if never issued due to return.</data>
  <data key="d4">REVERSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">Exceptions to benefit termination through reinstatement rely on documented procedures; however, such processes still require written approval per general policy rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Exceptions to termination through reinstatement depend on proper documentation and authorization, aligning with the rule that changes need official written consent, ensuring controlled reactivation of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement exceptions depend on formal processes requiring written authorization, consistent with the rule that only official representatives may alter policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Although the reinstatement provision permits revival of benefits after lapse, it does not override the rule that only official representatives can authorize changes, maintaining control over policy modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement exceptions allow revival of lost coverage, which operates independently but complements the incontestability rule that protects claim validity after two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">Exceptions to benefit termination allow for reinstatement even after lapses, reinforcing the importance of the two-year incontestability window during which insurers cannot contest claims due to misrepresentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08">
  <data key="d3">The Reinstatement provision permits restoring benefits even when policies might otherwise terminate, such as in cases involving misrepresentations, providing relief from some outcomes outlined in earlier clauses about voidance.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="6cde3bd7-3a57-480f-b1f9-561875fd48f4">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement allows restoration of benefits after lapse, independent of the suicide clause's restrictions during the initial two-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="64edfdb5-aded-401b-bbe7-55880fad2b56">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement enables resumption of benefits after lapse under specific terms, whereas the suicide clause restricts claims due to suicide within two years regardless of reinstatement status. They apply to separate circumstances and do not influence each other directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="fffa6d30-0053-4c00-b207-2a77ad194bd2">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence mentions exceptions allowing reinstatement of benefits, but this does not directly affect or clarify the suicide clause described in the first sentence, which remains independent in scope and application.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="f1888ece-7434-4b7e-aebc-5434189a9e7a">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence notes exceptions enabling reinstatement after lapse, which could indirectly involve corrected information like age. However, it doesn't reference or rely on age misstatement adjustments described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="52a31aaf-1af7-416b-8b31-a19b2a5a1510">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence outlines conditions under which benefits may continue despite termination, particularly through reinstatement rules. The first sentence explains how coverage adjusts when gender was incorrectly stated initially, unrelated to post-termination revivals.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement exceptions permit restoring coverage after lapses, relying on conditions like proof of insurability; this depends on prior compliance such as using the grace period to avoid automatic termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">Exceptions to benefit termination under the Reinstatement provision allow policies to be restored after lapse, which complements the grace period’s role in sustaining coverage briefly beyond due dates, together forming layered mechanisms to preserve policyholder protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence discusses reinstatement rights enabling benefit restoration after lapse, whereas the first outlines claim settlement rules during the grace period. They operate independently but share thematic concern over benefit preservation amid payment issues.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement provision allows for recovery of benefits after a policy lapse caused by missed premium payments during the grace period, offering a remedy to the consequences outlined in the prior statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">REMEDY_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The Reinstatement provision provides an exception to the automatic termination of coverage due to missed premium payments, enabling recovery of benefits after lapse under defined conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a Reinstatement provision provides a mechanism to restore benefits even after they would have been terminated due to missed premium payments during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">QUALIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">The existence of exceptions to benefit termination allows for reinstatement of a lapsed policy, contingent upon providing acceptable proof of insurability to the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years serves as a key exception allowing continued benefits after termination, supporting the claim made in fact_sentence_1 about exceptions under the Reinstatement provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">The existence of exceptions to termination allows for reinstatement, which requires paying accrued interest on overdue premiums as set by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">The existence of exceptions to benefit termination allows for reinstatement even after lapsation, but such reinstatement requires fulfillment of specific conditions like paying all delinquent premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The first statement highlights exceptions allowing benefit continuation through reinstatement, while the second confirms the five-year window for reinstating a lapsed policy, reinforcing the feasibility of those exceptions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The existence of exceptions to benefit termination under the Reinstatement provision relies on satisfying requirements like demonstrated insurability, which ensures eligibility despite prior lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a reinstatement provision depends on the occurrence of a policy lapse due to unpaid premiums beyond the grace period, making this fact foundational to the exception mentioned.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The existence of exceptions to termination under the Reinstatement provision suggests that even if standard terms like paying overdue premiums with interest are met, additional leniencies might apply depending on circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a reinstatement provision allows a lapsed policy to regain validity, ensuring it can still be 'in force' at the time of the insured's death, thus enabling the payment of the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy does not affect the requirement to provide proof of death for claiming benefits; reinstatement restores coverage prior to death, whereas proof of death validates a claim afterward.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
