<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years relies on fulfilling specific terms like health verification and missed payments; it does not affect or rely on who was designated as the original owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="b2835f9b-be1f-42a0-910e-c6e995ace28d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years provides a second chance to maintain coverage after failure to pay premiums, but it operates independently of the initial 20-day inspection period, which occurs prior to any lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="d31837ea-1599-48d9-acef-f6708a189681">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 discusses the option to reinstate a lapsed policy up to five years after lapse, contingent on fulfilling requirements like paying overdue premiums and proving insurability. Fact_sentence_1 refers to returning the policy within 20 days of receipt for a full refund if dissatisfaction occurs. While both involve recovery options, they apply to distinct phases of the policy timeline and do not rely on each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="69580977-8680-4303-b27e-16864466b8e8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the option to reinstate a lapsed policy up to five years after it lapses, subject to approval and fulfillment of requirements like paying overdue premiums and proving insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="65938361-ed69-4ef2-88b7-4494b82bd742">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement of a lapsed policy within five years is possible under certain terms, but returning the policy results in immediate voidance from inception, making reinstatement impossible regardless of timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">OPPOSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="12ebf888-5542-48cf-a3ae-6bbbc3b648b6">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years implies ongoing eligibility despite interruption. However, if the policy is returned instead of merely lapsing, it is treated as though never issued, negating any chance of reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTED BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy depends on fulfilling conditions such as paying overdue premiums and obtaining medical review; these actions must be documented in writing as required by policy rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_CONDITIONAL_CHANGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement of a lapsed policy within five years depends on fulfilling specific requirements, including obtaining necessary approvals; thus, it relies on the formal validation mandated by authorized personnel.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years relies on formal approval processes, which aligns with the rule that only official representatives can alter the policy, ensuring integrity during revival.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years requires adherence to formal rules, consistent with the rule that no unauthorized party can alter policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS_PROCEDURE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="8828a9e7-6ada-4747-9993-0ab39713e114">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years depends on fulfilling conditions like health requirements and missed payments, independent of the incontestability clause that applies after two years of continuous existence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="2b144ac4-5731-4e59-b5d4-9c1044113d9e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy within five years provides a pathway to restore benefits even after failure to pay premiums. This complements the incontestability rule by ensuring policies remain viable beyond initial lapses, reinforcing long-term reliability.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="35b294dc-e18b-451a-85f0-043e5a2acc08">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement of a lapsed policy within five years does not affect the enforceability of clauses related to misrepresentation during initial issuance. The timing of lapses and potential revivals is independent of early contestability rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="6cde3bd7-3a57-480f-b1f9-561875fd48f4">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 explains that a lapsed policy can be revived within five years under certain conditions. This provision operates independently of the suicide clause described in sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="64edfdb5-aded-401b-bbe7-55880fad2b56">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that a lapsed policy can be restored up to five years after lapse, contingent on fulfilling certain conditions. This provision stands independent of the suicide clause described in fact_sentence_1, which pertains solely to claim settlement limits during a defined initial period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="fffa6d30-0053-4c00-b207-2a77ad194bd2">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 describes the opportunity to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years under certain conditions. This provision operates separately from the suicide clause that affects claim settlements during the initial two-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="f1888ece-7434-4b7e-aebc-5434189a9e7a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 explains that a lapsed policy can be revived within five years if certain requirements are met. This process is independent of prior inaccuracies in age reporting, though it could involve recalculations like those described in sentence 1 during reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="52a31aaf-1af7-416b-8b31-a19b2a5a1510">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence outlines the window for reinstating a lapsed policy, contingent on health and payment requirements. This process is independent of any prior correction related to gender-based premium miscalculations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement within five years depends on timely action post-lapse; the prior availability of a 31-day grace period provides a critical window to avoid lapse and preserve reinstatement rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility up to five years after lapse provides a recovery path for policies that have expired due to missed payments. This depends on fulfilling requirements like proof of insurability and paying overdue amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence states that a lapsed policy can be reinstated within five years if certain requirements are met. This provides context for why maintaining timely payments matters, such as avoiding lapsation altogether—a concern addressed in the first sentence regarding deductions from the death benefit during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years depends on the occurrence of a lapse caused by failure to pay a premium after the grace period ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years depends on it having been terminated due to unpaid premiums after the grace period expires.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years implies that lapses occur when premiums are missed beyond the grace period, reinforcing the finality of benefit cessation at that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES RECOVERY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">Since a lapsed policy can be reinstated within five years, this creates a specific condition where benefits are not permanently terminated—thereby exemplifying one of the stated exceptions to termination under the Reinstatement provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years depends on providing acceptable proof of insurability to the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years depends on satisfying specific requirements, notably paying all outstanding premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years creates a context where additional conditions, such as paying accrued interest on past-due premiums, become applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies that reinstatement within five years requires meeting health and payment criteria, which supports and elaborates on the more general claim made in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years hinges on satisfying the insurer’s requirements regarding insurability, which ensures the risk remains manageable at reactivation.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The inability to pay the premium beyond the grace period directly causes the policy to lapse, creating the condition that allows for later reinstatement within five years.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES_LAPSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The first fact enables reinstatement within five years, which relies on the second fact’s condition of repaying overdue premiums with interest to complete the process.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy ensures it remains in force, enabling the beneficiary to receive the death benefit upon the insured's passing, assuming required proof is submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy enables eligibility for a death benefit, but payment requires submitting acceptable proof of the insured’s death, linking policy status recovery to claims compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
