<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Proving insurability is essential for reinstating a lapsed policy within the allowable five-year timeframe. It serves as a critical condition enabling the restoration of coverage under the original terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that proving insurability is required before reinstatement. This condition must be met prior to fulfilling any financial obligations like paying overdue premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability must first be established before reinstatement occurs; only after this step does the insurer determine the applicable interest on unpaid premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after a policy lapse depends on demonstrating insurability to the insurer’s satisfaction, but this condition does not relate directly to how premiums are detailed in the benefits schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The need to prove insurability applies when seeking to reinstate a lapsed policy after missing payments; however, this condition is independent of the frequency of premium payments like monthly installments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after a lapse depends on proving insurability, which follows from failure to meet prior premium payments. However, this requirement is independent of when premiums are scheduled to be paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The need to prove insurability applies when reinstating a lapsed policy after missed payments, regardless of the original payment frequency like annual premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement involves demonstrating insurability to the insurer, which is unrelated to the choice of premium payment mode selected at enrollment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The need to provide evidence of insurability applies when reinstating a lapsed policy after missed payments. Payment frequency options like quarterly do not affect the insurability requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The need to prove insurability for reinstatement does not rely on the frequency of premium payments like semi-annual billing. These are independent aspects of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement hinges on demonstrating insurability to the company, independent of the approved premium payment method. The decision to approve a payment mode does not influence or depend on whether insurability has been verified.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after policy lapse depends on proving insurability, but this condition does not influence or relate to the timing of the first premium payment, which occurs at policy inception regardless of future lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability allows the policyholder to reinstate coverage, enabling the resumption of scheduled premium payments under the originally chosen payment mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after a policy lapse necessitates demonstrating insurability to the insurer, but this condition does not influence or relate to requests for changing premium payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement necessitates proving insurability to the company, but this requirement does not influence or depend on changes to the premium payment mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after a lapse requires demonstrating continued insurability to the insurer, but this condition does not influence or relate to changing the frequency of premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement necessitates demonstrating insurability to the insurer, but this condition does not affect the timing or validity of changes to the premium payment mode, which require separate approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is necessary when seeking to reinstate a policy after it has lapsed due to missed payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement is conditional on demonstrating insurability, which applies only after the policy has already lapsed and terminated without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability allows the policyholder to reinstate coverage after it has terminated, thereby preventing loss of value. Without meeting this requirement, the policy remains permanently terminated.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The need to prove insurability for reinstatement applies regardless of whether an automatic premium loan exists. The absence of such a feature means policyholders cannot use it to avoid lapsing, making reinstitution more reliant on external payment methods.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement hinges on demonstrating insurability to the insurer, but this condition does not affect whether an Automatic Premium Loan can be added. The need for insurability verification is unrelated to adding riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required to reinstate a lapsed policy, independent of whether a loan covers outstanding premiums. The availability of a loan depends solely on accumulated cash value, regardless of health status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy necessitates demonstrating insurability, which may become relevant only if alternative protections like an automatic premium loan are absent. Without such a loan, lapses lead to termination requiring reinstatement efforts.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement involves proving insurability to restore coverage after it has lapsed; however, this process does not affect how the death benefit is distributed when the insured dies under active coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement requires proving insurability, but this does not affect how or when the death benefit is paid. The payment of the death benefit depends solely on the policy being in force at the time of death and submitting proper documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement hinges on proving insurability, while the death benefit is governed by policy-specific provisions; one does not influence or rely on the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after policy lapse depends on proving insurability, but this condition has no bearing on whether the death benefit is paid in a lump sum. The payment method is determined independently by the beneficiary’s election.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after a policy lapse depends on proving insurability to the insurer’s satisfaction, while alternative settlement options require prior approval from the same entity; however, these processes operate independently in distinct phases of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes requirements for reinstating a lapsed policy through demonstrated insurability. Fact_sentence_2 outlines documentation needed when claiming the death benefit. Though both require approval from the insurer, they apply to distinct stages of policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement involves proving insurability, while payment of benefits depends on submitting proper death documentation. The two processes occur at separate points in time and involve different requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is necessary for reinstatement, but the insurer may request extra documentation to support the application.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement necessitates proving insurability, and the required evidence stems from the insurer’s reasonable judgment regarding necessary documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after policy lapse requires proving insurability to the insurer, but this condition has no direct connection to how quickly or under what terms the death benefit is paid after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement involves proving insurability after a policy lapses, while interest on the death benefit begins accruing only after the insured’s passing. The two processes occur under distinct circumstances and timelines.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">This statement outlines the requirement to prove insurability when seeking to reinstate a lapsed policy. It does not relate to the identity or role of the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability ensures the applicant remains eligible for coverage after a lapse, but it does not affect whether interest is legally required on overdue payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after policy lapse involves proving insurability to the insurer’s satisfaction, but this process does not determine who receives the death benefit upon the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">While premiums are fixed during the guaranteed term, missing payments may trigger lapse, necessitating reinstatement through evidence of current insurability—an outcome that indirectly challenges the assumption of uninterrupted coverage despite consistent pricing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">While the policy guarantees no premium increases during the term, reinstating it after lapse requires showing insurability, meaning the initial protection can be lost if health deteriorates post-lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy depends on proving insurability, which becomes necessary because failure to pay within the 31-day grace period leads to lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required to reinstate a lapsed policy, which only applies when the grace period has expired and coverage has terminated—making the grace period a prerequisite condition for avoiding the need for reinstatement altogether.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS_LAPSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability is required to reinstate the policy within the 5-year post-lapse period established by the initial term provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">Proving insurability for reinstatement ensures continued validity of the policy, preserving the right to receive the Death Benefit upon the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Proving insurability for reinstatement ensures continued coverage, allowing the Death Benefit—defined by policy terms—to remain enforceable, making it dependent on compliance with reinstatement requirements detailed in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="ad1cb066-961b-4cae-bf88-48a316e04583">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder fails to make timely payments due to issues with the bank draft system, reinstatement might become necessary; therefore, the requirement for evidence of insurability depends on maintaining reliable payment methods like Monthly Bank Draft.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="a337b41c-27fd-4c74-8c49-2a45657cee74">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability is required to reinstate a lapsed policy, making it essential only outside the protected 20-year guaranteed period where continuous payment maintains validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability is necessary to qualify for reinstatement within the 5-year timeframe allowed by the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="8553795c-a210-458d-bbd9-47de9966423a">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability is necessary to reinstate the policy, thereby preserving the ability to fulfill the commitment to pay the death benefit as stated in the initial agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="3c328b68-a332-4773-9c29-f646235f7d51">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability required for reinstatement ensures that the individual remains eligible for the death benefit, which is itself governed by the terms described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_CONDITIONAL_COVERAGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a policy after lapse depends on proving insurability and paying dues, while changing a beneficiary takes effect immediately upon signing. These processes operate independently—one restores coverage eligibility, the other alters benefit distribution without affecting reinstatement criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement requirements focus on proving insurability after a lapse, while beneficiary changes take effect independently of the insured’s current health or life status. The two processes operate separately within policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after lapse depends on proving insurability and paying arrears, which is unrelated to changing the beneficiary. The two processes operate independently within different aspects of policy maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy depends on proving insurability, which is unrelated to changing the beneficiary. However, both processes involve administrative actions initiated by the policy owner and require formal submissions to the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required to reinstate a lapsed policy, which may occur when a premium is not paid within the 31-day grace period established earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required to reinstate a lapsed policy, but only becomes relevant after the grace period expires and the policy no longer remains in force.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required to reinstate a lapsed policy, which may occur after missing payments beyond the grace period. However, if death occurs during the grace period, no reinstatement is needed—the death benefit is adjusted by subtracting outstanding premiums regardless of insurability status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">Proving insurability is necessary to reinstate a policy that has lapsed due to nonpayment of a premium beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_RECOVERY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to prove insurability for reinstatement directly addresses the risk posed by lapses caused by missed premium payments during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The need to prove insurability for reinstatement arises specifically because unpaid premiums beyond the grace period terminate benefits, making reactivation conditional on new underwriting approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">Proving insurability is a prerequisite for reinstating a lapsed policy, aligning with the broader framework allowing exceptions to termination of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">Proving insurability is a necessary precondition for reinstating a lapsed policy, which is only permitted within a five-year timeframe under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITION_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that reinstatement depends on proving insurability; fact_sentence_1 expands on this by specifying that such evidence must meet the company’s satisfaction, reinforcing the same condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 emphasizes the need to prove insurability before reinstatement can occur, which complements fact_sentence_1’s focus on settling unpaid premiums; both conditions must be met simultaneously.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability ensures the insurer’s risk assessment is met before reinstatement, which directly enables the application of interest charges on overdue premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
