</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">Payment of past-due premiums with interest is necessary to reinstate a policy that has lapsed due to nonpayment beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement depends on the prior occurrence of coverage termination caused by missing the grace period deadline, making it a corrective action following the event described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay past-due premiums with interest enables recovery from policy lapse caused by missing the grace period deadline.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_RECOVERY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">Meeting the requirement to pay past due premiums with interest is likely part of the process enabling reinstatement, yet exceptions may permit relief from this obligation under special conditions outlined in the provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">The second fact outlines a necessary precondition for reinstatement—the repayment of delinquent premiums—which supports the feasibility of the time-bound reinstatement option described in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">Payment of delinquent premiums with interest satisfies the financial condition required to reactivate the policy, which complements the need to demonstrate current insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that reinstatement involves not only unpaid premiums but also accrued interest, which supports and expands upon the basic condition outlined in fact_sentence_1 regarding repayment obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 mandates payment of past-due premiums with interest for reinstatement, which operationalizes the provision described in fact_sentence_1 about interest being applied under company determination.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="642af3f4-30c7-401f-809e-b10dd7d614fc" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">requires payment of past due premiums</data>
</edge>
<edge source="811594d3-7009-4d9b-b3d4-3b79a4f7f911" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is responsible for paying</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6ec823ad-3b95-4628-8360-2008b12ebe48" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">must be paid with interest</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5d80a29c-b00a-47af-b500-5512f557cf57" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">requires</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="0b7f99de-0307-43aa-92a2-343af9bb8d66">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="1e6fbef1-c28d-40aa-b239-bdaae6d1afbb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="02a1c351-4c58-4635-ba24-18535fb55346">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="3bd5ec7f-b632-487e-8a6d-6c078f86be38">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="31c7ee67-6efa-4d3c-9866-de05b9d546b7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="74d37793-fcd8-4dc0-89db-15548b662dae">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="94ac6999-5df9-4197-81f9-347610fb63f5">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="207d5b64-5f9e-4ace-ba55-69fb98748e1d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="133a682a-cc74-442b-9067-90eba35d9360">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="dfc1a544-8dc0-4fe4-b3cc-07b0c73f0604">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="4abded86-6777-463f-aa25-b5edb6b31503">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on overdue premiums when reinstating a policy ensures compliance with the reinstatement terms outlined after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The determination of interest on overdue premiums happens post-reinstatement eligibility, which itself depends on satisfying the insurability requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The determination of interest on overdue premiums occurs at the moment of reinstatement, directly influencing the total amount required to restore the policy’s active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">The calculation of interest on overdue premiums relies on prior knowledge of the scheduled premium amount and payment terms, which are defined in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The obligation to pay premiums in advance sets the stage for potential delinquency, making it relevant to the calculation of interest on overdue amounts at reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on overdue premiums applies regardless of the payment frequency selected; thus, even if premiums are paid monthly, failure to meet those obligations triggers interest charges upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The interest charged on unpaid premiums upon reinstatement applies regardless of the payment frequency selected, including semi-annual payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The statement about interest on past-due premiums applies when a policyholder fails to make timely payments, including those made quarterly. It does not depend on the choice of quarterly payments specifically.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on overdue premiums applies regardless of the payment frequency selected, including annual payments. Thus, choosing annual billing increases the potential amount owed if not paid on time.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The determination of interest on overdue premiums occurs upon reinstatement and does not depend on the prior approval of the payment mode. The approved payment mode sets the schedule but doesn't affect how interest is computed later.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">The selection of a premium payment mode by the policy owner determines the timing of payments, which may lead to overdue amounts requiring interest at reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Interest on overdue premiums applies only if a lapsed policy is reinstated, not related to the timing of the first premium’s due date. The first premium being due on the effective date sets up the initial commitment but does not influence how interest is calculated later.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The calculation of interest on unpaid premiums occurs when a lapsed policy is reinstated, setting up conditions under which subsequent payments become due again according to the original schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Interest on unpaid premiums is assessed when a lapsed policy is reinstated, regardless of prior changes to payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The calculation of interest on unpaid premiums upon reinstatement does not depend on whether the premium mode has been changed. The need for written notice regarding a mode change is independent of interest determination.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Interest on unpaid premiums applies when reinstating a lapsed policy, but this does not directly influence the policy owner’s right to alter the payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for interest on overdue premiums at reinstatement does not affect when a change in premium mode takes effect. The latter depends solely on insurer approval, regardless of outstanding interest charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder fails to pay the premium by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses. This lapse initiates the process requiring reinstatement, after which the insurer determines interest on past-due amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on overdue premiums enables reinstatement, which prevents full coverage termination. Without paying accrued interest, reinstatement cannot occur, reinforcing why coverage typically terminates without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The calculation of interest on unpaid premiums at reinstatement is independent of whether an automatic premium loan is available through a rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on overdue premiums at reinstatement becomes more significant because the policy lacks an automatic premium loan option, meaning policyholders have fewer alternatives to avoid lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">If premiums remain unpaid beyond the grace period, the policy lapses and coverage terminates without value. However, reinstatement remains possible within five years if overdue amounts—including interest—are paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_RESTORE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The interest rate applied when reinstating a lapsed policy is determined by the insurer at the time of reinstatement, independent of any automatic loan used to prevent lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The amount of interest charged upon reinstatement relies on whether a policy loan can be used to settle outstanding premiums, which itself depends on having enough accumulated loan value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">This statement concerns interest charges applied when reinstating a lapsed policy, unrelated to how benefits are distributed post-death. It does not influence or relate to who receives the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how interest on unpaid premiums is calculated when a lapsed policy is reinstated. It does not influence or depend on the process of paying the death benefit upon proof of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Interest on unpaid premiums applies only when reinstating a lapsed policy, whereas the death benefit is paid according to the overall policy provisions upon the insured’s passing. The two statements concern distinct events in the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The determination of interest on overdue premiums at reinstatement does not influence or relate to the requirement that alternative settlement options need Company approval.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">This sentence explains how interest is applied when reinstating a lapsed policy, but does not influence or relate to the method of death benefit disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for interest on overdue premiums at reinstatement does not influence the type of proof needed for a death claim. The two facts concern separate administrative processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for interest calculation on overdue premiums applies when reinstating a lapsed policy, but it does not influence or depend on the type of death proof required for a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for additional documentation supports the administrative process involved when calculating interest upon reinstatement, ensuring accurate verification before applying charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Interest on unpaid premiums is assessed upon reinstatement, and the amount depends on the company’s discretion. Additional documents may also be requested based on the company’s judgment regarding the reinstatement request.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how interest on unpaid premiums is calculated when a policy is reinstated. It does not relate to who is designated as the recipient of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Interest on unpaid premiums applies only when reinstating a lapsed policy, whereas the death benefit is disbursed once proof of death is verified. The two events occur under different circumstances and do not influence each other directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for charging interest on overdue premiums arises because applicable laws mandate it, providing the legal foundation for the insurer’s action when reinstating a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">MANDATED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how interest on unpaid premiums is calculated when a policy is reinstated. It does not relate to the identification of the party entitled to receive benefits upon the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes how interest is calculated when a lapsed policy is reinstated, depending on the insurer’s determination at that time. Fact sentence 2 explains that interest accumulates on the death benefit from the moment of death until payout, regardless of prior lapses or reinstatements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires paying overdue premiums with interest, which contrasts with the initial guarantee of level premiums, highlighting a shift from predictable cost to variable financial obligation when coverage fails.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">While the first fact emphasizes no premium increases during the term, the second highlights that failure to maintain timely payments can lead to reinstatement fees including interest, thus indirectly reinforcing the importance of consistent payment under the guaranteed terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after a missed premium depends on surviving the grace period, during which interest begins accruing on overdue amounts once the grace period ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after lapse depends on timely payment of overdue premiums and accumulated interest, making the grace period critical for avoiding the need for reinstatement altogether.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATED_BY_GRACE_PERIOD</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement within 5 years allows for payment of overdue premiums with interest, making the timeline critical for triggering the interest calculation.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires paying overdue premiums plus interest, whereas the Death Benefit remains unaffected by prior lapses provided the policy was revived before death—indicating separate operational stages.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy involves paying interest on overdue premiums, enabling continued eligibility for the Death Benefit as outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The rule about interest on past-due premiums applies to reinstating lapsed policies but does not affect the timing or validity of beneficiary changes, which depend solely on the signing date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The rule about interest on past-due premiums pertains to financial compliance for reinstating lapsed policies, while the beneficiary change rule concerns administrative authority over policy designations; these topics do not intersect directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on past-due premiums ensures policy reinstatement eligibility, while the ability to change beneficiaries allows ongoing control over death benefit disbursement. These clauses operate independently but together support comprehensive policy governance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on past-due premiums relates to restoring policy coverage but has no bearing on the policyowner’s authority to designate or change beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0b7f99de-0307-43aa-92a2-343af9bb8d66" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines_interest_on</data>
</edge>
<edge source="31c7ee67-6efa-4d3c-9866-de05b9d546b7" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_past_due_interest_determined_by</data>
</edge>
<edge source="207d5b64-5f9e-4ace-ba55-69fb98748e1d" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines interest on past due premiums</data>
</edge>
