  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="a7cf8660-bc76-457d-a656-701faa190468">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The display of premium details in the Schedule of Benefits has no bearing on whether a policy can be reinstated after lapsing, which depends on separate conditions like time frame and insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The premium amount and payment mode are defined in the Schedule of Benefits, which provides foundational terms unrelated to the separate process of proving insurability for reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment frequency, which directly informs how much must be paid to reinstate a policy after lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">While the Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment mode, the actual financial consequence of failing to meet those payments—including accrued interest upon reinstatement—is governed separately by the insurer’s policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment options; one such option is quarterly payments, which is explicitly stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment options; one such option is monthly payments, which is explicitly stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits contains detailed premium terms, including allowable payment frequencies like semi-annual billing, making it the source where such options are documented.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment frequency, which directly informs the timing and structure of payments. Since premiums are payable in advance, knowing the payment mode from the schedule ensures timely compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium amount and payment options, including the ability to pay annually. Therefore, the option to pay premiums annually is explicitly included in the documented terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">The payment mode selected by the Policy Owner is reflected in the Schedule of Benefits, ensuring alignment between choices and official records.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The premium amount and payment mode are documented in the Schedule of Benefits, which establishes the basis for determining when future premiums are due under the selected payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The premium amount and payment mode are initially outlined in the Schedule of Benefits, providing the basis for the insurer’s subsequent approval of the chosen mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the current premium mode; altering it requires submitting written notice to the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits specifies the current premium amount and mode, which may be altered only after obtaining formal approval from the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines the premium terms, including the payment frequency, which determines when the initial payment becomes due. Thus, the first premium’s due date relies on the scheduled payment mode defined earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits specifies the current premium payment mode, enabling the Policy Owner to understand existing terms before requesting a change in frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits specifies the current premium amount and payment frequency, providing essential context for any potential changes requested by the Policy Owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The payment terms outlined in the Schedule of Benefits help determine when premiums must be paid, directly influencing whether they are missed beyond the grace period, leading to policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The payment details in the Schedule of Benefits help determine whether a policy may lapse due to missed payments, contributing indirectly to the risk of coverage termination without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The payment terms outlined in the Schedule of Benefits determine whether premiums are met timely, which affects whether the policy remains active. If premiums aren't paid per the schedule, the policy may lapse, resulting in termination without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence identifies where premium information appears in the policy documentation. The second sentence clarifies that certain additional benefits, like an automatic premium loan, require supplemental provisions beyond the base policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 identifies the location of premium-related data, while fact_sentence_2 specifies a missing feature related to premium handling. The absence of an automatic premium loan is independent of how premium amounts and modes are displayed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence specifies where premium information is located in the policy document. The second describes who receives the death benefit when a claim occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the premium amount and payment mode from the Schedule of Benefits ensures timely payments, maintaining the policy in force so that the death benefit becomes payable upon the insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">The premium amount and payment mode are detailed in the Schedule of Benefits, providing foundational financial terms. However, this does not directly influence how the Death Benefit is processed under policy conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence explains where premium details appear in the policy documentation. The second describes the standard payout method for the death benefit when no alternate choice is made.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits specifies the premium amount and payment frequency, setting expectations for what needs to be paid. Unpaid premiums may be addressed through a policy loan, but only if sufficient loan value exists, linking repayment options to accumulated cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 identifies where premium terms are documented, but fact_sentence_2 discusses a hypothetical repayment method reliant on an add-on rider not mentioned in the original context. There is no direct causal link since the automatic loan feature is optional and not inherent to the standard policy described.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence specifies that premium information appears in the Schedule of Benefits, but it does not relate to how death benefits may be settled. The second sentence concerns procedural approval for alternate settlement methods, independent of premium display.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The location of premium details in the Schedule of Benefits is unrelated to the type of documentation required after the insured's death. One concerns pre-death financial obligations; the other addresses post-death claims processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The location of premium and payment information in the Schedule of Benefits may lead to the need for supplementary documentation to verify eligibility or compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The payment details outlined in the Schedule of Benefits relate to premium obligations, whereas the requirement for a certified death certificate pertains to claims processing after the insured’s passing. The two statements operate independently within different stages of the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence identifies where premium-related data is documented, but it does not influence or relate to how quickly the death benefit is processed after proof of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies that premium information appears in the Schedule of Benefits. Fact_sentence_2 indicates that required documents vary depending on the company’s discretion, but it does not relate directly to how premium details are presented.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence specifies how premiums are determined and scheduled, while the second identifies the individual or organization designated to receive benefits after the insured’s death. The information pertains to different components of the policy without overlapping content.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence specifies how premiums are determined and scheduled, while the second describes interest applied to the death benefit after the insured's passing. The topics are distinct: one concerns payments made before death, the other about payouts after death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The Schedule of Benefits outlines premium amounts and modes, which inform when and how much must be paid. Interest becomes relevant only if those payments are delayed beyond the grace period, triggering financial obligations under law.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence specifies where premium information is located in the policy documentation. The second sentence identifies the individual entitled to receive benefits upon the insured’s death. These topics pertain to different components of the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ef6ad179-0716-412b-b227-10baa8bdff2f" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">related_to_premium_details</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a7cf8660-bc76-457d-a656-701faa190468" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">contains</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="07bccaa9-6bdd-4f3b-b810-12ddd447afe9">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="8d7701df-a103-44ca-a82a-f95239f0674d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="d84f384e-1fbf-40b0-b7a5-eb7d06148f9e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="3bb5ef62-1315-446b-a3bb-d0db08599f98">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="7f92607e-a713-48f9-865a-d9f4ea885848">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="00d8e21f-94b9-4f26-b70a-ede09054ac9b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="0972c5e3-1172-4a30-a797-b8ef7cd65133">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="371a8cb0-63df-412b-bb75-94f04a090994">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="a0836879-e6ab-4bf6-a838-fb1b6575e9f0">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="4ac77a72-8a2d-4a33-84d2-fa07c9be8856">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="9b9b35dd-ea2a-4e8d-813a-001c36629aeb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance ensures continuous coverage, preventing lapse and thus preserving eligibility for reinstatement within five years should the policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The obligation to pay premiums in advance sets the foundation for potential lapses, which may trigger the need for reinstatement requiring proof of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Since premiums are payable in advance, any nonpayment creates arrears, making it essential to settle those outstanding amounts—including interest—to reinstate the policy after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Because premiums must be paid in advance, any failure to do so leads to arrears, necessitating interest charges upon later reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Knowing that premiums are payable in advance establishes why the payment mode and amount detailed in the Schedule of Benefits matter—they determine exactly when and how much must be paid upfront.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance sets the foundational timing rule, enabling specific payment schedules like monthly payments to be implemented effectively.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance allows for flexible scheduling options like quarterly payments, ensuring timely fulfillment of financial obligations tied to policy maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance allows for various payment schedules, including semi-annual billing. Thus, paying premiums semi-annually aligns with the overarching rule of advance payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance includes the option of paying them annually, making annual payment a concrete example of advance payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">Premiums being payable in advance depends on the payment mode selected by the policy owner, who has control over how frequently they are due.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The statement that premiums are payable in advance depends on the insurer approving the chosen payment frequency, ensuring the selected method aligns with policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance sets the foundation for scheduling future payments. Subsequent premiums are due on fixed dates aligned with the selected payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">The statement that premiums are payable in advance sets the foundational timing principle, underpinning why the first premium must be paid at the start of coverage. Without this condition, the concept of paying before the coverage begins would not apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Since premiums are required in advance, the policyholder has flexibility to adjust how often they make those advance payments through a formal request.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance sets the baseline for payment obligations, while the policyholder’s right to change the payment method provides administrative flexibility within those constraints.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The rule that premiums are payable in advance sets the stage for managing payment schedules, including changes in frequency. A formal request via written notice ensures proper administrative control when altering the premium mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Since premiums are required to be paid in advance, missing the deadline—including beyond the grace period—results in the policy lapsing due to non-payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid in advance as required, the policy may lapse, resulting in termination of coverage without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The statement that premiums are payable in advance sets the foundational rule for payments, while the effectiveness of any change in payment mode depends on prior approval by the insurer, adding a layer of administrative control over how those payments may be adjusted.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Payment in advance is required to maintain active coverage; failure to do so may result in termination without value, except through reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance sets the foundation for understanding how payment obligations are structured, which contextualizes why the lack of an automatic premium loan feature may impact policyholders who miss payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance sets the baseline for policy maintenance, while the need for a rider to add an automatic premium loan highlights a supplementary option beyond basic terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Payment of premiums in advance maintains the policy’s active status, which is required for the insurer to disburse the death benefit when the insured passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The rule that premiums are payable in advance sets the stage for scenarios where payment may be delayed. If an Automatic Premium Loan provision were activated, unpaid premiums beyond the grace period would be covered automatically through a loan against the policy’s cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_COVER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Payment of premiums in advance ensures ongoing policy validity but does not directly affect when or how the death benefit is paid. The death benefit is triggered solely by the occurrence of the insured’s death under active coverage conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance sets the stage for potential reliance on alternative funding methods like policy loans when payments are missed. However, such a loan option is only viable if the policy includes a loan provision and has accumulated sufficient cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Premiums being payable in advance ensure ongoing policy validity, which is a prerequisite for triggering the death benefit under the policy’s terms. Without proper premium payments, the policy may lapse, affecting eligibility for the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The statement about premiums being payable in advance concerns the timing of premium payments. It does not relate to the process of approving alternative settlement options upon claim.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Premature payment of premiums ensures ongoing policy validity, which enables the eventual disbursement of the death benefit. Without sustained premium payments, the policy could lapse, preventing any future claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for advance premium payments ensures ongoing policy validity but does not directly influence the need to submit proof of death upon the insured's demise.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for prepaid premiums relates to maintaining policy validity, while acceptance of a certified death certificate pertains to validating a claim after the insured’s passing. These statements concern separate stages of the insurance lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for advanced premium payments sets up financial obligations under the policy, while additional documentation may be requested later during claims processing or compliance checks. These elements operate in different procedural phases without direct interdependence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Payment of premiums in advance pertains to timing and frequency of payments. The need for additional documentation depends solely on the insurer’s reasonable judgment and does not logically follow from or affect premium payment terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">This statement outlines when premiums are due but does not relate to the identity or role of the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Payment of premiums in advance ensures ongoing policy validity, which enables eligibility for future benefits like the death benefit. Without timely payments, coverage could lapse, preventing any claim settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The first statement concerns pre-death premium payment requirements, while the second describes post-death financial adjustments involving interest on the death benefit. They operate independently across distinct temporal stages of the insurance contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Payment timing for premiums does not influence or relate to the identity of the beneficiary. The two concepts pertain to separate administrative components of the policy—one financial, the other procedural regarding claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for premiums to be paid in advance sets the stage for potential financial consequences like interest charges if payments are delayed. Interest being mandated by law could relate to outstanding balances but isn't explicitly triggered by the advance-payment rule itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_DIRECT_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="ad1cb066-961b-4cae-bf88-48a316e04583">
  <data key="d3">The use of a Monthly Bank Draft as the premium mode exemplifies one implementation of the broader requirement that premiums be paid in advance.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="a337b41c-27fd-4c74-8c49-2a45657cee74">
  <data key="d3">The rule that premiums are payable in advance supports the stability of the 20-year guaranteed premium period, enabling consistent billing and preventing unexpected increases during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4">
  <data key="d3">The 5-year reinstatement period depends on timely payment of overdue premiums and interest, which is only meaningful because premiums are required to be paid in advance per the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="8553795c-a210-458d-bbd9-47de9966423a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance ensures the fulfillment of the insurer’s commitment to deliver the death benefit, making it essential for the validity of the promised payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d" target="3c328b68-a332-4773-9c29-f646235f7d51">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid in advance according to the schedule, the policy may lapse, thereby preventing the insurer from fulfilling its obligation to pay the death benefit despite the existence of favorable terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07bccaa9-6bdd-4f3b-b810-12ddd447afe9" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">receives</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8d7701df-a103-44ca-a82a-f95239f0674d" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">pays</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f92607e-a713-48f9-865a-d9f4ea885848" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is payable in advance</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00d8e21f-94b9-4f26-b70a-ede09054ac9b" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">premiums must be paid before</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0972c5e3-1172-4a30-a797-b8ef7cd65133" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">applies after failure to pay in advance</data>
</edge>
<edge source="371a8cb0-63df-412b-bb75-94f04a090994" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">enables restoration of coverage after lapse caused by unpaid premiums</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0836879-e6ab-4bf6-a838-fb1b6575e9f0" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">can satisfy advance payment requirement using policy loans</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ac77a72-8a2d-4a33-84d2-fa07c9be8856" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on maintaining active status ensured by advance premium payments</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9b9b35dd-ea2a-4e8d-813a-001c36629aeb" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">payment_timing</data>
</edge>
