<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are one available option for maintaining coverage, but this choice has no bearing on whether a lapsed policy can later be reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">While premiums can be paid monthly, this payment option does not influence or determine whether proof of insurability is required for reinstatement after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The availability of monthly premium payments provides flexibility in fulfilling financial obligations, including those needed for policy reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are one of several available modes under the policy, and although they contribute to potential delinquency, the method of calculating interest on overdue amounts remains independent of the chosen payment interval.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Since monthly payment is a recognized mode in the policy terms, its inclusion supports the presence of detailed payment information in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Monthly payment frequency exemplifies one method through which the obligation to pay premiums in advance can be fulfilled.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that premiums can be paid monthly, while fact sentence 2 specifies quarterly payments. These represent distinct but parallel payment intervals allowed under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_MODE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that monthly payments are allowed, while fact sentence 2 specifies that semi-annual payments are also permitted. Both represent alternative payment schedules available under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_MODES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that monthly payments are allowed, while fact sentence 2 specifies annual payments as another available option. Both are distinct but equally valid payment methods under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_MODES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payment is only possible because the policy owner has selected it as their preferred payment mode. The availability of the monthly option is contingent upon the owner’s election.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are only permissible if the insurance company has approved the chosen payment mode, including monthly billing.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums monthly establishes the frequency of payments, which directly determines when future installments are due under the policy’s schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are permitted under the policy terms, and the first such payment is required on the Effective Date, establishing the start point for ongoing premium obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are permitted under the policy, and the policyholder has the right to adjust how often they pay premiums, including changing from other intervals to monthly.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums monthly establishes a payment option available under the policy. Changing from this mode—or any other—requires formal notification to the insurer, ensuring administrative control over billing arrangements.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums monthly provides a payment option, while any modification to this mode depends on prior approval from the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Monthly payments are one of the available premium payment modes, providing a foundation for why a policyholder might want to adjust their payment plan. The ability to change the payment method accommodates different financial preferences, including switching to or from monthly billing.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are one of the available options under the policy terms; failure to meet any scheduled payment—including those made monthly—by the grace period’s end leads directly to policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are one method of maintaining active coverage; failure to adhere to this payment schedule can result in policy lapse, leading to termination of benefits without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums monthly relates to payment flexibility but does not affect whether an automatic premium loan is available. The absence of such a loan is independent of the chosen payment interval.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are allowed under the policy’s payment options, but failure to maintain them leads to coverage termination unless reinstated per the stated provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums monthly does not influence whether an automatic premium loan can be added. The latter depends solely on adding a rider, independent of payment frequency choices.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums monthly provides flexibility in scheduling payments, but does not guarantee any form of financial backup should those payments fail.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_DIRECT_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments relate to ongoing policy maintenance but have no bearing on how the death benefit is distributed post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are one of several options available for maintaining policy coverage, but the actual payout of the death benefit depends on separate contractual terms that govern its release.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments ensure ongoing policy validity, which is required for the insurer to honor the death benefit obligation upon the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums monthly provides flexibility in scheduling payments, but it does not inherently trigger any automatic financial remedy if missed. The second sentence describes a potential solution—automatic loans—for late payments, but only applies if the rider is added, which is outside the scope of the core policy described here.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are one of several available modes under the policy terms. The death benefit is generally distributed as a lump sum unless an alternate payout method is chosen.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines flexible premium payment schedules, including monthly options. The second addresses that any non-standard death benefit distribution requires prior authorization from the insurer, unrelated to payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are part of the policyholder's obligation during active coverage, but do not directly affect the requirement to submit proof of death when filing a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The statement about monthly premium payments relates to ongoing policy maintenance, while the requirement for a certified death certificate pertains to post-death claim procedures. The two statements address unrelated aspects of the policy process.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums monthly is one of the available payment options under the policy terms. Additional documentation may be requested later during claim processing, but it is unrelated to the choice of payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Payment frequency options like monthly installments are independent of the documentation standards imposed by the insurance provider. No connection exists between how often premiums are paid and what documents are needed for claims processing.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments are one of several available modes for maintaining policy coverage, but this detail does not influence when the death benefit is paid. The payout occurs independently once proper documentation is received.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The statement about monthly premium payments does not directly explain or imply why interest is legally required. There is no indication that the payment frequency triggers or relates to statutory interest obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">Payment frequency options like monthly billing do not relate to the identity or role of the beneficiary. The information about how premiums are paid does not influence or explain who the beneficiary is.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines how often premiums can be paid, while the second describes when interest begins accruing on the death benefit. The topics are unrelated—one concerns pre-death obligations, the other post-death benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Payment frequency options like monthly installments do not influence or relate to the identity of the beneficiary named in the policy. The details about how premiums are paid are independent of who receives the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
