  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments are part of the available payment modes under the policy. However, they are unrelated to the condition requiring proof of insurability for reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments are allowed under the policy, providing flexibility in how often premiums are made, regardless of reinstatement requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments are one of several options available for paying premiums in advance, regardless of whether interest accrues later upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly payment is a valid payment mode included in the Schedule of Benefits, where premium details—including frequency—are documented.</data>
  <data key="d4">IS_PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments exemplify the rule that premiums must be paid in advance, aligning with the overall payment structure defined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 describes quarterly premium payments, whereas fact sentence 1 outlines monthly payments. Both are independent payment options included in the broader range of payment frequencies permitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_MODE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that quarterly payments are allowed, while fact sentence 2 indicates that semi-annual payments are also permitted. Both represent distinct but equally valid payment intervals available under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_MODE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that quarterly payments are allowed; this is one of several available payment intervals, including annual payments described in sentence 2. Both reflect alternative choices within the same payment structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments are permitted under the policy terms, but only if selected by the policy owner through their election of the payment mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments are only permissible if the insurance company has approved that payment mode as part of the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments are part of the available payment options; the first such payment under this mode would occur on the effective date of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums quarterly establishes a recurring payment pattern that determines when subsequent premiums are due under the policy’s schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums quarterly establishes a payment option that can be changed only through formal notification to the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments are one of the available options outlined in the policy terms, providing a concrete example of how the frequency of payments can be adjusted. This makes it feasible for the policyholder to request a change to this particular frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 illustrates a permissible payment frequency under the policy terms, providing context for why the policy owner’s ability to modify the payment method (as stated in fact_sentence_2) is meaningful and applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums quarterly is subject to the insurer’s approval before becoming effective. Without official authorization, even if quarterly payments are allowed under general terms, they cannot be implemented.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums quarterly is one method of maintaining active coverage; failure to do so consistently may result in policy lapse, causing coverage to terminate without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRIBUTES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums quarterly is one of the available payment modes; failure to meet any scheduled payment—including those made quarterly—within the grace period leads to policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums quarterly helps maintain active coverage and prevents the risk of policy termination without value, as stipulated when payments are missed beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums quarterly relates to the timing of payments but does not affect whether an automatic premium loan is available. The lack of this feature is a standalone policy limitation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums quarterly relates to payment scheduling flexibility, whereas the need for a rider to add an automatic premium loan highlights how certain benefits require additional endorsements. There is no direct interaction between these concepts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums quarterly provides one of several available payment options; however, it does not inherently trigger or relate to the use of an automatic premium loan, which depends on a separate rider being attached.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments relate to ongoing policy maintenance but have no bearing on how the death benefit is distributed. The timing of premium payments does not affect who receives the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The statement about quarterly premium payments relates to how premiums are scheduled but does not influence or relate to the requirement that alternative settlement options need company approval.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums quarterly relates to regular payment scheduling, whereas the use of a policy loan for unpaid premiums relies on accumulated loan value, independent of the frequency selected.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments relate to ongoing policy maintenance, whereas the lump-sum death benefit pertains to post-death claims processing. The two statements address different phases of the insurance lifecycle without overlapping logic.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments maintain active policy status, enabling eligibility for the death benefit upon the insured’s passing, assuming other requirements like proof of death are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">Quarterly premium payments maintain active coverage, enabling eligibility for the death benefit. Proof of death is required to trigger the payout under active policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums quarterly relates to maintaining active policy status, while submitting a certified death certificate pertains to validating a claim after the insured’s passing. The two statements address separate procedural aspects of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums quarterly relates to payment scheduling but does not influence or relate to the documentation required by the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums quarterly is one of several available payment options outlined in the policy terms. Additional documentation might be requested later during claim processing or compliance checks, but it is not directly tied to the choice of quarterly payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Payment frequency options like quarterly premiums are unrelated to how quickly the death benefit is issued after proof of death is received.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The statement about quarterly premium payments does not relate to the legal obligation requiring interest. No connection exists between payment frequency and statutory interest mandates.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The statement about quarterly premium payments relates to policyholder contributions before death, while the accumulation of interest on the death benefit occurs only after the insured’s passing. The two events occur at different stages of the policy lifecycle and are unrelated in function.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Payment timing options like quarterly premiums do not influence or relate to the identity of the designated beneficiary. The information in fact_sentence_1 pertains to financial obligations, while fact_sentence_2 concerns post-death benefit distribution rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes how premiums can be paid quarterly, relating to payment scheduling. Fact_sentence_2 explains who qualifies as the beneficiary under the policy. The two statements cover distinct topics without interaction.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines that premiums can be paid quarterly, one of several available payment frequencies. This relates to maintaining active coverage, which is a prerequisite for the death benefit described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
