<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums semi-annually is independent of the ability to reinstate a lapsed policy, which hinges on timely payments and compliance with post-lapse requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Semi-annual premium payments are unrelated to the condition of demonstrating insurability required after a policy lapse; one does not influence or follow from the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The availability of semi-annual premium payments offers flexibility in scheduled payments, while reinstatement depends on repaying delinquent amounts with interest regardless of original payment intervals.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">While premiums may be paid semi-annually, failure to do so triggers potential lapses and subsequent interest charges when reinstating the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Since semi-annual payments are a permitted mode, they must be explicitly stated in the Schedule of Benefits, which outlines all premium-related conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCLUDED_IN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Semi-annual premium payments exemplify the general principle that premiums must be paid in advance, demonstrating a specific instance of the broader payment obligation.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 mentions semi-annual payments as an option, and fact sentence 1 confirms that monthly payments are similarly accepted. These are mutually exclusive but coexisting choices within the policy’s payment structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_MODES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies that premiums can be paid every six months, whereas fact sentence 1 confirms they can also be paid every three months. These are independent payment frequency choices offered under the same policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_MODE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that semi-annual payments are allowed; this complements fact sentence 2, which confirms annual payments are also permitted, showing multiple available intervals within the same system.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_MODE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">The availability of semi-annual premium payments is made possible because the policy owner has the right to choose the payment mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The statement that premiums may be paid semi-annually is validated by the insurer’s approval of the chosen payment mode, ensuring its acceptability within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums semi-annually establishes a recurring payment pattern, leading directly to the requirement that future premiums align with the established due dates under that mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Semi-annual premium payments are one of the available options under the policy’s payment schedule, and the first such payment is required on the Effective Date, establishing the initial deadline for this installment.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums semi-annually is one instance of the flexibility offered when the policy owner requests a change in payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums semi-annually depends on obtaining prior approval from the insurance company, ensuring administrative control over changes in payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums semi-annually establishes a regular payment obligation that must be met; failure to do so within the grace period leads to policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The availability of semi-annual premium payments relies on the ability to modify the payment mode through official communication with the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Semi-annual premium payment is one of the options available under the policy’s payment modes, making it a viable choice when the policy owner requests a change in payment method.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums on a semi-annual basis is one of the available modes; failure to maintain such payments leads to policy lapse, resulting in termination of coverage without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRIBUTES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums semi-annually increases the risk of lapsing if not done timely, potentially triggering coverage termination unless reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums semi-annually pertains to the payment schedule flexibility offered under the policy. The lack of an automatic premium loan feature indicates a limitation in financial safeguards against missed payments, but it does not depend on or influence the availability of semi-annual payment choices.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums semi-annually creates a scenario where missed payments could trigger the need for alternative funding mechanisms like policy loans, assuming sufficient loan value exists.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums semi-annually is one of several available payment options outlined in the policy terms. The need to use a rider to activate an automatic premium loan reflects how certain benefits require explicit addition beyond standard plan features.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums semi-annually does not inherently trigger or rely on an automatic premium loan. The presence of such a loan depends solely on whether a rider was added, independent of the selected payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Semi-annual premium payments relate to ongoing policy maintenance, whereas the death benefit being paid to the beneficiary occurs only after the insured’s death under active coverage conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Semi-annual premium payments maintain active policy status, enabling eligibility for the death benefit payout described in the second sentence. Without ongoing premium payments, the death benefit would not be available.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Semi-annual premium payments maintain policy validity, ensuring eligibility for the death benefit when claimed after the insured's passing under active coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES ELIGIBILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The statement about semi-annual premium payments relates to how policyholders fund their coverage but does not influence or relate to the need for company approval of alternative death benefit settlement options.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums semi-annually pertains to the timing and method of premium payments, while the death benefit being subject to policy terms concerns post-mortem claims processing. These topics operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums semi-annually does not influence the requirement to submit proof of death. The two facts relate to separate administrative processes within the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums semi-annually relates to ongoing policy maintenance, whereas providing a certified death certificate pertains to post-death claims processing. The two facts address separate procedural aspects without mutual dependency.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Payment frequency options like semi-annual billing do not influence the documentation required from the policyholder. The need for supporting documents remains independent of how often premiums are paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">This statement outlines the available payment intervals for premiums, including semi-annual billing. It does not relate to the identity or role of the beneficiary under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
