<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments provide a method for fulfilling the financial obligation required to reinstate a lapsed policy within the allowed timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payment is one of several available modes and does not influence the requirement to demonstrate insurability for reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums annually provides a timing framework for when payments are due, but it does not alter the condition that unpaid premiums must still be settled with interest upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments increase the risk of accumulating significant unpaid amounts over time, potentially leading to higher interest charges upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASES_RISK_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Since the Schedule of Benefits lists the available payment modes, the possibility of paying premiums annually is derived from and confirmed by that document.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums annually aligns with the overarching rule that premiums must be paid in advance, demonstrating how a specific method fits into the general framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 indicates annual payment is permitted, and fact sentence 1 confirms monthly payment is also accepted. These represent alternative choices within the same set of payment frequency options.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_MODES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 indicates annual payments are permitted; this complements sentence 1 by providing another valid frequency option among those listed in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 indicates annual payments are accepted; this aligns with fact sentence 1’s mention of semi-annual payments, illustrating different but compatible payment schedules offered under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_MODE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums annually depends on the Policy Owner’s decision regarding the payment mode. Without the owner’s election, the annual option would not apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums annually relies on the insurance company approving the selected payment mode. Without formal approval, the annual payment method cannot be implemented despite being listed as a possibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments are permitted under the policy terms, and the first such payment is required on the Effective Date, establishing the initial obligation tied to the chosen payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums annually establishes a payment frequency that determines when future premiums are due. Subsequent premiums align with the periodicity defined by the chosen mode, including annual cycles.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums annually depends on obtaining prior approval from the insurance company before the new payment mode takes effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_APPROVAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payment is one of the available payment frequencies allowed under the policy terms. The policy owner can initiate changes to adjust how often they pay premiums, including choosing annual payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums annually is one of the options available when changing the payment method. The ability to switch methods allows the policyholder to choose annual payments among other intervals.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments help sustain active coverage; failing to make them timely causes the policy to lapse, resulting in termination without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The availability of annual premium payments sets the context for when a change in payment mode might occur, necessitating written notice to implement such a shift.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums annually is part of the available payment options, while failure to pay within the grace period leads to policy lapse. These statements describe separate conditions related to premium handling.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are paid annually but not maintained, it could lead to coverage termination after the grace period expires, unless reinstated per the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums annually relates to the flexibility of payment schedules outlined in the chunk summary. The lack of an automatic premium loan feature pertains to alternative financial provisions available under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums annually provides flexibility in payment scheduling, while the need to add an automatic premium loan via rider highlights that certain financial safeguards require explicit enrollment.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Payment frequency options like annual premiums relate to ongoing policy maintenance but do not influence how the death benefit is settled after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments ensure ongoing policy coverage, enabling the insurer to maintain financial obligations. When the insured dies under active coverage, the death benefit becomes payable to the named beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments increase the likelihood of cash-flow gaps; if unpaid, they could trigger a need for a policy loan—but only if sufficient loan value exists and the rider is in place.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments help maintain active policy status, which is required for the insurer to disburse the death benefit upon verified claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Payment frequency options like annual premiums are unrelated to how the death benefit is disbursed; one concerns ongoing obligations while the other addresses post-death payout conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums annually ensures ongoing policy coverage, which is prerequisite for triggering the requirement to submit proof of death when claiming benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes a standard payment option available under the policy, while the second discusses a supplementary feature (automatic loan) that only applies if specifically added. The existence of the loan feature does not affect the validity of paying premiums annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums annually is a method of fulfilling financial obligations under the policy. However, this does not influence or relate to the requirement that alternative death benefit settlement options need prior approval from the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines how premiums can be paid annually, focusing on payment scheduling. The second describes what documentation is needed when filing a death claim, emphasizing official verification of demise.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The option to pay premiums annually is part of the standard payment terms outlined in the policy. However, this choice does not inherently require additional documentation beyond what’s already mandated by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Payment frequency options include annual billing, but this does not influence or relate to the documentation standards imposed by the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">Payment frequency options like annual billing do not influence or relate to the identity of the beneficiary designated in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The first statement outlines the option to pay premiums annually, while the second describes interest accumulation on the death benefit after the insured's passing. The topics are unrelated, covering distinct phases of the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The statement about annual premium payments does not directly influence or depend on the requirement for interest under applicable law. The two statements pertain to separate procedural elements of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payment maintains policy continuity, ensuring the insured remains covered so the death benefit becomes applicable upon death. Without current coverage, the death benefit would not be payable regardless of payment method.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Payment frequency options like annual premiums do not influence or relate to the identity of the designated beneficiary. The information in fact_sentence_1 pertains to financial obligations, while fact_sentence_2 concerns post-death claims administration.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03817c8e-a663-462a-b1a4-467220250bd9" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">receives</data>
</edge>
<edge source="564548a6-84ae-471a-a97e-fc88377dd25d" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">pays</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ccfff5d0-e98c-49e7-8700-3338b557aa1e" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">Starts Payment Schedule</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c13969e3-5a49-4af4-a6ea-9ce4bd43c32c" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">Allows Late Annual Payment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdcfc085-1412-4fa0-84f9-675602ca089e" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">Applies After Failure to Make Annual Payment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9b568278-ea0e-485a-8cfb-3491f046f973" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">Fulfills Annual Payment Obligation Automatically</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4bba9058-2298-4def-bfd4-eb207368881f" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">Depends on Maintenance of Annual Premium Payments</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7290ca67-d4b8-4bcf-8f07-0a300be98b3e" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">includes_payment_terms</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="acb6c82b-3111-4181-a53b-470a8df095ed">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="0a10d848-4c13-4eef-94ab-3d2b5f4dd3dc">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="95c60aa4-c1b4-47dd-ab82-ee03eab3000d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="a7417922-eafe-4245-867e-ea25179b4ab1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="105d3e5f-d02f-40bd-b73d-83cb973e2013">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="ffef57f0-edb8-43d6-a38b-67c7e106a950">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="30c0c2db-5f80-4c39-b73f-f28f5489ef17">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="76f1703f-4aa8-4c8a-90f2-5e7efb3fff5b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="e5fb0e33-62f0-4269-8bf0-00e68ea00be4">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="1d4d89e0-287b-415b-a4ac-bbda59535fd9">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="a36fed2b-19da-47bd-b6f0-3924fabc8db7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Choosing the premium payment mode affects when payments are due but has no direct impact on whether a policy can be reinstated after lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The decision on how often to pay premiums does not affect the need to prove insurability upon reinstatement after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner selects the premium payment mode, which determines when premiums are due; however, failure to meet any deadline triggers the need to repay arrears with interest should the policy later require reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The calculation of interest on past-due premiums occurs after reinstatement and is affected by how frequently premiums were originally scheduled, which was decided by the policy owner’s election.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">The information displayed in the Schedule of Benefits depends on the premium payment mode elected by the Policy Owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s election of a payment mode dictates the timing and frequency of advance premium payments required under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">DETERMINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner selects the payment mode, enabling options like monthly payments; without this selection, monthly payments would not apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to choose the premium payment frequency, enabling them to select quarterly payments when applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">CHOOSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner selects the payment frequency, including the ability to opt for semi-annual payments when choosing the mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The ability to choose annual premium payments arises directly from the Policy Owner’s authority to select the payment mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner selects a preferred premium payment frequency, initiating the process. The Company reviews and formally accepts this selected mode, confirming its validity under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INITIATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner selects the preferred premium payment interval, which directly determines when future premiums are scheduled to be paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">ELECTS_MODE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s election of a premium payment mode sets the framework for when payments are due, including the first one. Therefore, selecting the mode inherently defines the timeline for the first premium being due on the effective date.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s election of a premium payment mode enables future adjustments to its frequency. Subsequent changes depend on the original choice being made.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s initial election of a premium payment mode enables future flexibility to adjust it. This decision sets the foundation for subsequent changes to the payment method.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s ability to choose the premium payment mode sets the stage for any future changes. Any modification to this selection requires official notification to the insurer, ensuring proper documentation and administrative processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner selects the preferred premium payment mode, but any modification to this selection only takes effect after receiving official approval from the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">INITIATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s selection of a premium payment mode determines the timing of each payment, which affects whether the premium is paid within the grace period; failure to do so triggers policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner selects the premium payment mode, but this decision does not affect whether an automatic premium loan can be added. The addition of that feature requires a separate contractual amendment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Choosing the premium payment mode determines timing and frequency of payments, affecting compliance with deadlines; failure to meet them leads to coverage termination unless reinstated per policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The selection of a premium payment mode pertains to how often payments are made but does not influence whether an automatic premium loan is available. The lack of this feature is independent of the chosen payment interval.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Choosing the premium payment mode determines how frequently payments are due, influencing the likelihood of timely payment. If payments are delayed beyond the grace period, the policy lapses, resulting in termination of coverage without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner selects how often premiums are paid, but this decision has no direct impact on whether an automatic premium loan covers missed payments, since that feature requires a separate rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The election of a premium payment mode ensures ongoing policy validity, which is a prerequisite for the death benefit to become payable upon the insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">The choice of premium payment mode affects ongoing policy maintenance but does not determine eligibility or timing for death benefit disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner selects the premium payment mode, influencing ongoing financial commitments but not affecting how the death benefit is settled at maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's election of a premium payment mode determines when payments are made but has no bearing on whether the death benefit will be paid according to policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The election of a premium payment mode does not influence the need for company approval of alternative settlement options. The two decisions operate independently within policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's decision on payment mode influences when premiums are due, potentially affecting whether loan funds accumulate over time. However, using a loan to cover unpaid premiums requires existing loan value, independent of the selected payment interval.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The election of a premium payment mode pertains to ongoing policy maintenance and financial obligations. It has no bearing on the procedural requirements for submitting proof of death when filing a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The choice of premium payment mode does not influence the requirement for submitting a certified death certificate upon claim filing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">Selecting a premium payment mode does not directly necessitate additional documentation, but the insurer may request further information depending on underwriting or compliance policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">The choice of premium payment mode does not influence the documentation required by the insurer. The need for additional documents remains independent of how frequently premiums are paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's decision on premium payment frequency has no impact on when the insurance company processes the death benefit claim, which depends solely on documentation and policy terms at time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner selects how often to pay premiums, but this decision does not influence or relate to statutory requirements about interest rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">The choice of premium payment mode does not influence who is named as the beneficiary. The beneficiary designation is independent of how premiums are paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The election of a premium payment mode determines when and how often premiums are paid but has no bearing on the interest accrued on the death benefit after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Selecting the premium payment mode has no bearing on determining the designated beneficiary under the policy. The decision about how often to pay premiums is independent of who receives the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0a10d848-4c13-4eef-94ab-3d2b5f4dd3dc" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">chooses_payment_mode</data>
</edge>
<edge source="105d3e5f-d02f-40bd-b73d-83cb973e2013" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_payment_mode_selected_by</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="3fa90973-a661-4fcf-8f55-00e515c371f8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="20742c52-cc87-4025-bc8a-8a66fdd5a6f1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="6c96457d-c5b8-4b20-bca2-5af55ed7ab6b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="b3e16b65-fe02-4fbe-b476-65adf1217162">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="45f93c77-5ac1-4606-b760-302c2f0f4174">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="fd1655a8-a2bc-4647-9aec-efaff79d2b38">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="8431eff5-905c-4da0-ac7e-c75217428806">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="b592dcdb-f9e6-44a8-816f-35063519148d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="3235a360-6eb7-4873-9265-640af7bab28f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="f0272cc1-c41c-4c5c-8dd4-627708a8c4d6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="30de1124-2423-42be-b5b0-e152c3a5b547">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Choosing a premium payment mode has no bearing on whether a policy can later be reinstated after lapsing. Reinstatement eligibility depends solely on time elapsed, proof of insurability, and repayment terms—not the originally approved payment method.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode occurs independently of the need to provide evidence of insurability for reinstatement. One process does not affect or rely upon the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of the premium payment mode sets the timing for payments, but it does not affect the requirements for reinstating a lapsed policy after failure to pay.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode establishes the billing cycle but has no bearing on how interest is assessed when reinstating a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">The Company’s approval of the payment mode relies on the details previously specified in the Schedule of Benefits, ensuring alignment with the agreed terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPROVES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of the premium payment mode allows for the enforcement of the rule that premiums must be paid in advance according to the agreed-upon schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The company's approval of the premium payment mode allows the policyholder to select options like monthly payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of the premium payment mode allows the policyholder to select options like quarterly payments, ensuring compliance with the agreed-upon schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of the premium payment mode enables the feasibility of paying premiums on a semi-annual basis, making it a permissible option under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">VALIDATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of the premium payment mode enables the policyholder to legally use the annual payment option, making it actionable under the terms of the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">After the Policy Owner chooses a payment mode, the Company confirms acceptance of that choice through formal approval, ensuring alignment with policy requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFIRMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">Once the insurance company approves the selected premium payment mode, future installments become enforceable on predetermined due dates aligned with that mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">The approved premium payment mode sets the framework for scheduling payments, including determining that the first installment is due on the policy’s effective date.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">The insurer’s approval of a premium payment mode follows from a formal request submitted by the policy owner seeking to modify how payments are made.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of the initial payment mode sets the stage for future adjustments. The policy owner can later seek modifications to the payment frequency, subject to the insurer’s review and consent.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The company’s approval of a premium payment mode sets the stage for any future modifications, making it necessary to formally notify them when altering the mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">Approval by the Company is required before any change in premium payment mode can take effect. Without formal approval, changes remain inactive.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The approved payment mode sets the due date timeline; failure to meet those deadlines—even after the grace period—results in policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode ensures continuous coverage, preventing premature termination. Without timely payments, even with approved modes, coverage may lapse and terminate without value unless reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">Approval of a premium payment mode does not influence or depend on whether an Automatic Premium Loan can be added via rider. These are independent administrative decisions regarding different aspects of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode sets the terms under which coverage remains active. If those terms are not met through timely payments, the policy lapses, resulting in loss of coverage and no cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES LAPSING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The approval of a premium payment mode pertains to when and how often premiums are paid, while the lack of an automatic premium loan feature concerns alternative funding options upon missed payments. The two facts describe separate policy features without mutual dependency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode ensures continuous policy status, enabling eligibility for the death benefit when claimed after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode establishes the timing of required payments, which may influence when a policyholder might need a loan to avoid lapsing. However, the availability of a loan depends solely on accumulated cash value, independent of the approved payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The approval of a premium payment mode establishes the timing and frequency of payments but does not directly trigger or enable an automatic premium loan. Such a loan would require a separate rider, so its availability is independent of the initial payment mode selection.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode ensures the policy remains financially viable over time, enabling continued coverage necessary for the eventual triggering of the death benefit claim. Without proper payment arrangements, the policy could lapse before death occurs, preventing any payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode ensures ongoing policy validity through timely payments, which indirectly supports continued eligibility for the death benefit. However, the actual payment of the death benefit remains governed solely by policy terms regardless of the payment method approved.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode determines when and how frequently premiums are paid, but it has no bearing on whether the death benefit is paid in a lump sum or through another settlement option.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The approval of a premium payment mode sets up ongoing financial obligations but does not influence the requirement to submit proof of death after the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">After approving the chosen premium payment mode, the insurer may require additional documentation to verify the selection’s validity or ensure compliance with underwriting standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode pertains to ongoing policy funding arrangements. Acceptable proof of death concerns post-mortem claim verification procedures. The two statements operate independently within different phases of the policy life cycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes the Company’s role in approving how premiums are paid, which occurs early in the policy term. Fact sentence 2 refers to the need for Company approval when selecting non-lump-sum death benefit settlements, which applies only after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">The approval of a premium payment mode does not influence or depend on the company’s discretion regarding additional documentation needs. These are independent administrative processes governed by separate criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The approval of the premium payment mode governs when payments are made but does not influence whether interest accumulates on the death benefit after the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode ensures the policy remains active through timely payments but has no bearing on the timing or conditions of death benefit disbursement once proof is submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">The approval of the premium payment mode pertains to financial obligations under the policy but does not define or influence who receives benefits after the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">Approval of a premium payment mode sets the timing for payments, but does not influence whether interest is mandated by law. Interest requirements exist independently of the selected payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Approval of the premium payment mode pertains to how and when the policyholder fulfills financial obligations. The beneficiary definition concerns who is entitled to receive the death benefit upon the insured’s passing. These topics operate independently in the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3fa90973-a661-4fcf-8f55-00e515c371f8" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">approves</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f93c77-5ac1-4606-b760-302c2f0f4174" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">approved_payment_mode</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3235a360-6eb7-4873-9265-640af7bab28f" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">approved_payment_mode</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="536f7f88-c333-4a42-8113-dd01b5eafe96">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="92b034df-df0e-4fb1-84c8-69688d25fe6b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="b2f932c1-e3f8-416a-8900-bd410248a4e6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="a1415b9a-294f-4951-af48-bf575a68b745">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="564eec8c-b4e4-43d0-bbac-dc5fe23295f2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="2a2e2984-677c-4182-8a59-df9cde2a3828">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="e577b67b-2ffc-43bf-bbc1-59d53500de71">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="e8393122-35fb-4121-9088-89e9bdf675e3">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="146eec48-481d-449d-897c-de6f734ed187">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="64a9c15b-12b5-4965-91fd-c576260b3ce2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="769c0170-7ffa-4039-9d41-fdc92d2e6019">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be due on the Effective Date sets the start point for payments, regardless of whether the policy later lapses and gets reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid on the Effective Date establishes the initiation of coverage, independent of later reinstatement procedures tied to insurability verification.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The first premium’s due date is established at policy inception, independent of later requirements like reinstating a lapsed policy through payment of arrearages and interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid on the effective date initiates the policy term but has no bearing on how interest is computed at reinstitution, which occurs under separate conditions unrelated to the original start date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the Effective Date helps establish the timeline for the first premium; however, the actual amount and payment method were previously determined by the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the Effective Date exemplifies how premiums are paid in advance; it illustrates the practical application of the general rule established in the prior sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid on the Effective Date enables the implementation of periodic payment options like monthly installments, ensuring timely initiation of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be due on the effective date sets the initial deadline for any payment frequency, including quarterly installments.</data>
  <data key="d4">SETS_TIMING_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be due on the Effective Date applies regardless of the selected payment frequency, meaning it also governs the timing of the first semi-annual payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">SETS_TIMING_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid on the Effective Date applies regardless of the selected payment mode, including the option to pay annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">SETS_TIMING_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be due on the effective date necessitates prior decision-making about the payment mode. Thus, choosing the payment frequency enables scheduling the first payment accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be due on the Effective Date necessitates that the payment mode has already been formally accepted by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The first premium’s due date sets the foundation for the recurring payment cycle. Subsequent premiums follow consistently according to the selected payment interval, maintaining alignment with the original effective date framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the Effective Date sets the initiation point for payment obligations, independent of any later changes to payment frequency that the policy owner might request.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the Effective Date sets the foundational timeline for payment obligations. Changing the premium mode later requires formal notification, ensuring administrative control over ongoing billing arrangements.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the Effective Date sets a foundational requirement for policy activation. The ability to later change the payment method allows flexibility but does not alter the initial due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The first premium’s due date is fixed at the policy’s Effective Date, independent of any future changes to the premium mode. Changes to how premiums are paid only take effect after formal approval from the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the Effective Date sets the timeline for compliance; failing to pay it within the grace period triggers policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">If the first premium is not paid on the Effective Date, it may trigger a lapse, resulting in termination of coverage without any value being retained.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid on the effective date pertains to payment initiation, whereas the absence of an automatic premium loan relates to available financial options. The two facts describe independent policy conditions without mutual influence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">If the first premium is not paid on the Effective Date, it could lead to early coverage termination, especially if not resolved within the grace period, resulting in loss of benefits unless reinstated later.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for the first premium to be due on the effective date sets the initiation point for payment obligations, but does not influence whether an automatic premium loan can be added later through a rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the effective date sets the timeline for initial payment obligations; however, this does not affect whether an automatic loan covers future missed payments unless specifically enabled through a rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the effective date ensures policy activation but does not affect how the death benefit is processed upon the insured’s passing. The death benefit remains conditional solely on fulfilling policy requirements regardless of early payment timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the effective date ensures the policy remains active, enabling future benefits including the death benefit. Without timely payment, the policy could lapse, preventing any death benefit from being paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be due on the effective date sets the start of financial obligation, which may later trigger reliance on a policy loan if not met. However, the availability of a loan depends solely on accumulated cash value, independent of the first payment’s due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for the first premium to be paid on the Effective Date ensures the policy becomes active, enabling it to remain in force long enough for the death benefit to become payable under subsequent circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the effective date ensures policy activation, while the death benefit payment method applies only after the insured’s passing under active coverage. These statements address separate aspects of policy mechanics—initial funding versus final disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the effective date relates to policy initiation, whereas approving an alternative settlement option occurs post-death under separate conditions. The two statements concern unrelated administrative steps in different phases of the policy’s life cycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid on the effective date pertains to policy activation, whereas providing proof of death relates to claims processing after the insured’s passing. They operate independently across different phases of the policy life cycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for the first premium to be paid on the effective date sets the initiation point for policy activation. Additional documentation might be needed to verify eligibility or process that initial payment, but it does not directly depend on the timing of the first premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be due on the effective date pertains to policy activation, whereas acceptable proof of death relates to claims processing post-mortem. The two events occur at different points in time and involve separate procedural requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the effective date sets the start of financial obligation, but does not determine the need for supplementary documents required later by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the Effective Date ensures timely initiation of coverage but does not influence who is designated as the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The first premium’s due date relates to policy initiation and does not influence how interest accumulates on the death benefit after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the effective date sets the start of financial obligation, which could trigger interest accrual under applicable laws if delayed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINGENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the Effective Date ensures policy activation but does not influence when the death benefit is paid. The payment of the death benefit depends solely on verification of the insured’s passing and submission of required documents.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">The first premium being due on the Effective Date establishes a key milestone for policy activation but does not influence or relate to how beneficiaries are designated.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
