<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for subsequent premiums to be paid on designated due dates arises directly from the ability to reinstate a lapsed policy, making timely payment essential post-reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums on designated due dates arises only after successfully meeting the insurability criteria needed for reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">After a policy has been reinstated, it becomes subject to the same recurring premium deadlines established at inception, requiring timely payment including any arrears with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">After a policy is reinstated, future premiums must be paid on designated due dates, triggering the application of interest charges on any previously overdue amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Since premiums are due on specific dates tied to the chosen payment mode, those dates are defined in the Schedule of Benefits, where the payment terms are initially outlined.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Because premiums are required to be paid in advance, it necessitates a clear timeline for upcoming payments, ensuring continuity of coverage through regular due dates.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for subsequent premiums to be paid on designated due dates depends on the initially selected payment mode, including the possibility of monthly payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that subsequent premiums align with the selected payment mode explains why quarterly payments are permissible and consistent with the overall billing cycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The rule that subsequent premiums are due on fixed dates depends on selecting a payment frequency like semi-annual, making it contingent upon the choice described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for subsequent premiums to be due on specific dates depends on selecting a payment mode like annual, which directly enables predictable scheduling of those obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">Once the payment mode is selected, all future premiums become due on fixed dates aligned with that chosen frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for subsequent premiums to be due on specific dates relies on prior approval of the chosen payment mode by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Each subsequent premium is scheduled relative to the initial due date defined at policy inception. Thus, the sequence depends directly on when the first premium was required.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the ongoing duty to pay premiums on designated dates under the current payment plan. Fact_sentence_2 allows the policyholder to adjust how frequently those payments occur, thereby influencing when future due dates fall.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for subsequent premiums to be paid on scheduled due dates creates the obligation that, if unmet beyond the grace period, triggers policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the fixed timing of premium payments based on the selected mode. Fact_sentence_2 allows the policyholder to modify how those payments are made, potentially altering future due dates.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for subsequent premiums to be paid on designated dates relies on the established payment mode, which only becomes altered after official company approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The rule requiring subsequent premiums to be paid on due dates establishes the standard payment pattern. Changing this pattern necessitates formal notification, ensuring administrative control over modifications to the established cycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid on the designated due dates, the policy may lapse, resulting in termination of coverage without any cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay subsequent premiums on time leads to coverage termination without value, unless the policyholder qualifies for reinstatement within five years.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for timely premium payments under the chosen mode operates independently of whether an automatic premium loan is included. The absence of this feature means policyholders cannot rely on it to prevent lapses when payments are delayed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for timely premium payments does not affect whether an automatic premium loan can be added, which depends solely on adding a rider. The two concepts operate independently within the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence establishes regular premium due dates based on the payment mode. The second suggests an automated solution for missed payments through a loan, but only applies if the rider is present—which is not indicated here.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">This statement outlines the recurring obligation to pay premiums on scheduled dates depending on the chosen payment frequency. It does not relate to how or when the death benefit is distributed after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for timely premium payments sets up the scenario where unpaid amounts might need alternative funding. Unpaid premiums could potentially be addressed through a policy loan, but only if the necessary loan balance exists and the rider enabling loans is present.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_COVER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">This statement outlines when future premiums must be paid based on the selected frequency. It does not influence or relate directly to how the death benefit is settled.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Timely payment of subsequent premiums ensures the policy remains active, which is a prerequisite for the insurer to fulfill its obligation to pay the death benefit upon proof of the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines when future premiums are due based on the payment frequency. The second sentence concerns conditions for approving alternate ways to receive the death benefit, unrelated to premium timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for subsequent premiums to be paid on scheduled dates ensures continued policy validity, which indirectly supports eligibility for future benefits like the death benefit. However, the actual disbursement of the death benefit is governed by separate contractual provisions unrelated to payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for timely premium payments ensures continued policy validity but does not directly affect the need to submit proof of death after the insured's passing. The second fact pertains solely to claim settlement conditions unrelated to payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines when future premiums must be paid based on the selected frequency. The second sentence specifies what documentation is needed to validate a death claim, unrelated to premium payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for future premiums on designated dates does not inherently necessitate additional documentation from the insurer. While documentation might be needed later for claims or reinstatement, it is not logically dependent on the recurring nature of premium due dates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines when future premiums are due based on the payment frequency. The second sentence states that the company may request further documents as needed, without specifying any connection to premium deadlines.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">This statement outlines when future premiums are required based on the payment frequency. It does not relate to the identity or role of the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">This statement concerns ongoing premium payments tied to the payment schedule. It has no direct impact on when the death benefit is paid, which depends solely on claim verification post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines when future premiums are due based on the payment frequency. The second sentence explains that interest begins accruing on the death benefit only after the insured passes away, regardless of prior premium schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">This sentence outlines when future premiums are required based on the payment frequency. It does not relate to the identity or role of the beneficiary designated to receive benefits upon the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for future premiums to be paid on scheduled dates does not directly depend on whether interest is mandated by law. Interest laws apply broadly but are not triggered solely by the recurrence of premium due dates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ed1bec0d-1fc7-4dcd-a76d-ff034921450c" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">sets</data>
</edge>
