</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="16ea7d81-660b-4d31-af38-80a43b1e4bb2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments affects how often premiums are made but does not influence whether a lapsed policy can be reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">A policy owner may request adjustments to how often they pay premiums, independent of whether they need to prove insurability upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">While the policyholder can adjust the frequency of premium payments, doing so does not eliminate the need to pay overdue premiums with interest when seeking reinstatement after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments has no effect on how interest is computed when reinstating a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">A request to alter the premium payment frequency depends on knowing the currently scheduled payment mode, which is detailed in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The availability of changing payment frequency depends on the underlying requirement that premiums be paid in advance, ensuring consistency across payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The policy allows changes to the frequency of premium payments, enabling the policyowner to select monthly payments among available options.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The ability to request a change in payment frequency allows the policyowner to select from various modes including quarterly payments, thereby enabling them to align their premium schedule with their financial planning needs.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXAMPLE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The ability to adjust payment frequency includes choosing semi-annual billing as a viable option.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The ability to request a change in payment frequency allows the policy owner to select annual billing, making it feasible to pay premiums once per year.</data>
  <data key="d4">IS_ENABLED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">A request to alter the payment frequency presupposes that a prior payment mode was already elected by the Policy Owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">A request to alter the payment frequency depends on the company’s willingness to approve it. Without formal approval, any proposed change cannot take effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">A policy owner’s ability to request a change in premium payment frequency does not affect the requirement that the first premium must be paid on the Effective Date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 grants the policyowner authority to modify the frequency of premium payments. This change directly impacts the timing described in fact_sentence_1, determining when subsequent premiums become due.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The ability to adjust premium payment frequency depends on submitting official written notification to the insurance company, ensuring proper documentation and authorization.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_NOTICE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to propose altering the premium payment frequency, but the requested change only becomes binding after receiving official approval from the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments involves adjusting how often payments occur, which may influence the preferred method used. Conversely, selecting a different payment method might require aligning with available frequencies.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments may impact the timing of when payments are made, potentially affecting whether the premium is paid before the grace period ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency may help prevent lapse, thereby indirectly helping maintain coverage. However, once a policy has already lapsed, changing payment terms cannot restore its value.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS LAPSING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments relates to how often premiums are made, whereas the lack of an automatic premium loan feature concerns backup funding options. The two concepts operate independently regarding policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments influences when premiums are due but does not affect the condition that coverage terminates without value unless reinstated per the stated provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments does not affect the availability of an automatic premium loan, which requires a separate rider addition regardless of payment scheduling preferences.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency affects when premiums are due, potentially influencing whether the grace period is exceeded and triggering reliance on an automatic premium loan if one exists.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_TRIGGER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments affects how often the policyholder makes contributions but has no bearing on the conditions under which the death benefit is paid after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments affects how often the policyholder contributes but does not alter the conditions under which the death benefit is paid upon the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments involves administrative adjustments related to ongoing policy funding but has no impact on the method or timing of death benefit disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments affects future payment obligations but does not influence whether a policy loan covers unpaid premiums. Loan availability depends solely on existing loan value, independent of payment scheduling changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments affects ongoing policy maintenance but does not influence how the death benefit is settled upon claim. The two concepts operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments does not inherently affect the need for company approval of alternative settlement options, as they relate to distinct stages of policy administration.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments relates to ongoing policy maintenance but does not affect the requirement to submit proof of death when filing a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency may prompt the insurer to request further documentation to verify eligibility or update records.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments affects how often the policyholder makes contributions but does not influence the type of documentation needed when submitting a claim after death.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments relates to ongoing policy maintenance but does not affect how quickly the death benefit is processed after a claim is submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments could prompt the insurer to request supplementary documentation to verify eligibility or compliance, depending on internal policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments pertains to the policyholder’s financial arrangements. The beneficiary designation is separate, relating to post-death distribution of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments affects how often the policyholder contributes funds but does not influence when interest begins accruing on the death benefit after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments does not directly affect the legal requirement for interest, but any delay in payment under a new frequency might trigger interest obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Changing the frequency of premium payments affects how often the policyholder fulfills financial obligations but does not influence who is designated as the beneficiary. The beneficiary remains independent of payment scheduling decisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="198ab335-c096-4f36-b808-396d9cc6b79c" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">requests_change_in_frequency_of</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e86c9cdb-3aaa-462f-9117-82b5c94c148c" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_changed_frequency_due_to_request_by</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8eddd560-de93-4b49-9149-433aa1a9b50d" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines_effective_timing_of_change</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="749cb803-590a-41cd-aad0-7ccd6484e65e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="41da1d70-0b28-4382-8c00-913229c760ba">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="1f0f271c-0e1b-44d6-a217-c980444fd1cf">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="9d3eb64e-d898-427b-b994-80063415402a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="894ad489-aeee-4a40-80da-55fe5e5fb864">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="bb81706e-ebc8-4ec9-a8b7-f0387bfcb828">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="ce179d6f-9d6b-4e4a-99b9-58de296e48b2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="a5e7e82d-3327-4afe-85bc-d39c286b9bfe">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="98962a5a-846f-4c70-89eb-5228ab922761">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="98c3e555-6592-495a-a8d1-20be90914806">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="e1f001e0-1cec-417f-a072-0c27209ace81">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method may reduce the risk of missing payments, thereby decreasing the likelihood of needing to reinstate the policy after it has lapsed.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS_LAPSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">A policy owner can request adjustments to their premium payment method independently; however, this action has no bearing on the requirements needed to reinstate a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method affects future installments but has no bearing on the obligation to pay back-due amounts when reinstating a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">A policy owner can choose a new premium payment method, potentially affecting future compliance and risk of lapses that might trigger interest charges upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s ability to request a change in payment method relies on having access to accurate information from the Schedule of Benefits regarding existing terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">While the rule that premiums are payable in advance defines the core obligation, it allows room for variation through the policyowner’s ability to adjust the payment method, maintaining compliance with the advance-payment principle.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALLOWED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">A policyowner’s right to alter the premium payment method implies they can choose any eligible frequency, such as monthly, supporting the feasibility of monthly payments described in the prior statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">IS_PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to alter the payment method enables them to choose quarterly payments, making fact_sentence_1 a potential outcome of the flexibility granted in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXAMPLE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">A policy owner who wishes to switch to semi-annual premium payments can do so through a formal request to modify the payment method, aligning with the allowed payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to alter the payment method includes selecting annual billing, making it a permissible choice under the flexible payment system.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">The capacity to request a change in the premium payment method depends on having previously elected a mode. Without an initial selection, modification would not be applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">A policy owner may initiate a change in premium payment method, which triggers the need for the insurer to review and approve the new selection.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">While the policy owner has the right to modify how premiums are paid, this choice does not affect the mandatory first payment deadline established at policy inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The option to change the payment method (fact_sentence_2) enables adjustments to when premiums are due, which directly affects the scheduling described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Choosing a new method of payment typically requires compatibility with existing payment frequencies; thus, modifying the method depends on whether it supports desired intervals like monthly or annual cycles.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to alter how premiums are paid, but any modification requires submitting a written notification to the insurance company to be processed.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_NOTICE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to propose altering the premium payment method, but the proposed change cannot take effect until it is formally approved by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_APPROVAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method may help avoid policy lapse, thereby preventing termination of coverage without value. However, it does not guarantee continued coverage if other conditions aren't met.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS LAPSING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method affects when payments are due, potentially influencing whether the premium is paid before the grace period ends. Thus, altering the method could impact the likelihood of falling into default.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method does not affect whether an automatic premium loan can be added, which remains dependent on a separate rider. The ability to alter payment modes exists independently of features like loan provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method relates to scheduling payments, whereas the lack of an automatic premium loan refers to the unavailability of a built-in financing option for missed payments. The two concepts operate in separate functional domains.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method might impact timely payment compliance, possibly increasing the risk of lapsing coverage if the new method leads to missed deadlines. Thus, it relates to potential failure to maintain active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY INCREASES RISK OF TERMINATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method affects how funds are allocated over time, potentially influencing whether sufficient loan value accumulates to cover unpaid premiums later.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method does not inherently trigger or affect the use of an automatic premium loan, but it could influence whether a loan becomes necessary depending on timing and payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method affects ongoing policy funding but does not influence the process or timing of death benefit distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method ensures continuous policy coverage, which is a prerequisite for the insurer to fulfill its obligation to pay the death benefit upon verified death.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method affects how consistently the policy stays in force, which influences eligibility for the death benefit. Thus, it has indirect bearing on the fulfillment of death benefit terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method affects ongoing policy maintenance but does not impact how the death benefit is settled at maturity. The two concepts operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method relates to ongoing policy maintenance but does not affect the requirement to submit proof of death when filing a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method requires formal processing, during which the insurer may demand extra documents to verify eligibility or compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method involves initiating a request, but any resulting alteration in how benefits are settled must still undergo formal review and acceptance by the insurance company before implementation.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_APPROVAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method may necessitate submitting additional documentation, depending on the insurer’s reasonable requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">Changing the method of premium payment pertains to ongoing policy maintenance before any claims occur. It does not influence or relate to the requirements for proving death when filing a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method involves administrative adjustments related to policy funding but has no bearing on how quickly or under what conditions the death benefit is issued.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method affects how premiums are submitted but does not influence when or how interest accumulates on the death benefit after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment method does not inherently affect the legal obligation to charge interest. Interest requirements exist independently of payment method selection.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">Changing the method of premium payment pertains to how the policyholder fulfills financial obligations. This has no bearing on identifying the individual or entity designated to receive benefits upon the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Changing the method of premium payment pertains to how the policyholder fulfills financial obligations. The beneficiary definition concerns who receives proceeds after the insured’s death, independent of payment mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="41da1d70-0b28-4382-8c00-913229c760ba" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">requests_change_in_payment_method_for</data>
</edge>
