  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode necessitates formal notification to the insurer, regardless of whether the policy has been previously reinstated or remains active.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires formal notification to the company, regardless of whether reinstatement procedures apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode demands written communication with the insurer and has no bearing on whether previously delinquent premiums must be repaid upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires formal notification but does not affect how interest is computed when reinstating a lapsed policy; those processes operate separately.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">To modify the premium mode, one must provide written notice, which implies awareness of the existing mode detailed in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode necessitates official communication through written notice, which aligns with the requirement that premiums be paid in advance to maintain coverage continuity.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode, including moving away from monthly payments, demands written communication with the company. This rule applies regardless of whether the current method is monthly, reflecting standardized procedures for modifying payment plans.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Changing from a quarterly premium payment mode requires submitting written notice, implying that quarterly payments are a valid and modifiable choice under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency, such as selecting semi-annual billing, necessitates submitting written notice to the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode, including selecting annual payments, requires prior written communication with the insurer, making it contingent on official documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_NOTICE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy owner selects the premium payment mode initially, any subsequent adjustment to it must be formally communicated through written notice to maintain compliance and validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">Any request to switch premium modes depends on prior approval of the original mode by the company, highlighting the need for official communication upon change.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency necessitates written communication with the insurer, which operates independently of when the first premium is due, although it affects subsequent payments after the effective date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires written notice, meaning any deviation from the default schedule governed by the initial payment plan must be formally initiated before affecting future due dates.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">To alter the premium payment frequency, the policy owner must provide written notice, making compliance essential before any change takes effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_CHANGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">To initiate a change in the premium payment method, the policy owner must provide written notice to the company, ensuring proper documentation of the requested adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_CHANGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium mode begins with submitting written notice to the insurer, which initiates the process leading to formal approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode necessitates formal notification; however, failure to meet any payment deadline—including those under a new mode—within the grace period leads to policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires formal notification to the insurer, separate from whether the policy includes an automatic premium loan feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode involves notifying the insurer but has no bearing on whether coverage ends without value upon lapse. The outcome described in fact_sentence_2 depends solely on payment status, not on changes to payment timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode necessitates official notification to the insurer, similar to how adding advanced features like an automatic premium loan requires a formal rider. Both involve documented requests to modify policy conditions beyond standard defaults.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_DOCUMENTATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency requires formal notification but does not directly impact whether coverage ends without value. Coverage only terminates without value when renewal fails and reinstatement isn't pursued.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_DIRECT_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires formal notification to the insurer, but this action has no bearing on whether an automatic premium loan covers missed payments beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode involves notifying the insurer formally, whereas covering unpaid premiums via loan depends solely on available loan balance—not related to prior changes in payment timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode involves submitting written notification to the insurer but has no bearing on the process of claiming the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency does not affect how the death benefit is determined or disbursed; it remains governed solely by policy terms regardless of payment method.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode involves submitting written notification to the insurer but has no bearing on the distribution of the death benefit to the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode involves notifying the insurer but does not affect how the death benefit is settled. The timing or method of premium payments has no bearing on whether the death benefit is issued as a lump sum.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode involves notifying the insurer but does not affect the requirement to submit proof of death when filing a claim. The two processes operate independently within different phases of the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency necessitates submitting written notification to the insurer, while selecting an alternative death benefit payout method also demands prior approval. Both processes reflect control mechanisms imposed by the company over key policy changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_APPROVAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode involves submitting written notice to the insurer, but this has no bearing on the type of proof required when filing a death claim. The two facts pertain to separate stages of policy lifecycle management.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode necessitates notifying the company in writing; subsequently, the company may require extra documentation to process the change.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode involves notifying the insurer but does not affect how quickly the death benefit is processed after a claim is submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode involves notifying the insurer but does not affect how interest accumulates on the death benefit after the insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode involves submitting written notice to the insurer but does not affect the legal requirement that interest must be charged where applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode involves submitting written notice to the insurer; this action does not affect who is designated as the beneficiary under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
