<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency requires company approval and only applies prospectively; however, this administrative step has no bearing on whether a previously lapsed policy can be revived under the five-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency only takes effect after company approval, regardless of whether the policy was previously reinstated or requires proof of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode takes effect only after company approval and has no bearing on whether previously missed premiums need to be paid for reinstatement purposes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Approval of a new premium mode has no bearing on how interest is computed on unpaid premiums at the time of reinstatement, which remains under separate company discretion.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Approval by the Company is required before any change in premium mode takes effect, even if the new mode was previously indicated in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_APPROVAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">While the timing of premium payments being in advance defines when obligations arise, changes to the payment frequency require formal approval before taking effect, ensuring compliance regardless of the original payment terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency, including switching to monthly payments, requires official approval from the insurer, making it contingent on administrative confirmation.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Company approval is required prior to changing to a quarterly premium payment mode, ensuring compliance with policy rules despite its availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">Company approval is required before switching to a semi-annual premium payment mode, making it a prerequisite for enacting this payment choice.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">Company approval is required before any change in premium payment frequency, including opting for annual payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">An approved change in the premium payment mode implies that the original decision was made by the Policy Owner, who initiated the request for adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_APPROVAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a changed premium payment mode hinges entirely on prior approval from the Company, making approval a prerequisite.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">While the first premium must be paid on the Effective Date, altering the payment frequency requires prior approval from the company and does not affect the original due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">Any adjustment to the premium payment mode must occur prior to altering the sequence of upcoming premium due dates outlined in the original payment plan.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Approval from the company is required for any adjustment to the premium payment frequency, making the change dependent on administrative confirmation.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_APPROVAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Approval by the company is required before any requested change in premium payment mode becomes legally binding, ensuring administrative control over policy modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON_REQUEST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">Approval from the Company is required before any change in premium mode becomes effective, making it dependent on prior written notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval but does not affect the requirement to pay premiums on time. The failure to meet payment deadlines leads to policy lapse regardless of the selected payment mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval but does not affect the circumstances under which coverage terminates without value, which only allows reinstatement after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium mode requires company approval and affects future payments, but does not guarantee continued coverage. Coverage only terminates without value if the policy lapses due to missed payments beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval but has no bearing on whether an automatic premium loan is included. The absence of such a feature is unrelated to adjustments in payment timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval and does not affect the availability of an automatic premium loan, which remains dependent solely on adding a rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval and does not affect how unpaid premiums might be handled through loans. The availability of loan funds remains independent of any mode adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval but does not affect the conditions under which the death benefit is paid. The timing or method of premium payments has no bearing on the insurer’s obligation to disburse benefits post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval but does not affect how the death benefit is distributed upon the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval and takes effect thereafter; however, if an automatic premium loan exists, it may cover missed payments even after a mode change, preventing lapses during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval but does not affect how the death benefit is processed. The death benefit remains governed solely by policy terms regardless of payment frequency changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 discusses the process for changing premium payment frequency, requiring company approval. Fact sentence 2 specifies what documents are accepted to verify death for claim purposes. These topics pertain to different stages of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency requires company approval and affects ongoing premium obligations; however, this has no bearing on how the death benefit is settled upon claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval, which may involve providing extra documentation to support the request.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_DOCUMENTATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval and does not affect the requirement to submit proof of death for claim settlement. The two processes occur at separate points in time and involve different administrative procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes that changing the premium payment frequency requires Company approval. Fact sentence 2 states that any alternate method of settling the death benefit also needs prior approval from the Company. Both reflect centralized decision-making but apply to unrelated policy components.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_APPROVAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency requires company approval, and any associated documentation needed depends on the insurer’s discretion.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval but does not relate to statutory interest obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval but does not affect the process of claiming the death benefit. The death benefit payout depends solely on submitting proper documentation, regardless of prior premium mode adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency requires company approval but does not affect how interest is calculated on the death benefit after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment frequency requires company approval and does not affect the identity or designation of the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Changing the premium payment mode requires company approval but does not affect who is designated as the beneficiary. The beneficiary’s identity depends solely on the most current written designation filed with the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
