<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The occurrence of a policy lapse from missed payments enables the potential for future reinstatement under defined conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapses if the premium isn't paid by the end of the grace period, potentially requiring future proof of insurability for reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest arises from the consequence of missing payments—the policy lapses when the grace period ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The determination of interest on past-due premiums occurs only when a lapsed policy is being reinstated, which happens specifically after the policy has failed to receive payment by the end of the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">If a premium isn't paid by the grace period’s end, the policy lapses—a risk that underscores why knowing the exact premium amount and payment mode from the Schedule of Benefits is critical.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The risk of policy lapse arises because premiums must be paid in advance; without timely payment, even within the grace period, the policy cannot remain active.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder fails to pay the premium by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses regardless of the selected payment frequency, including monthly installments.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">If a premium isn't paid by the end of the grace period, regardless of whether it was due monthly, quarterly, or another interval, the policy lapses, making regular payment schedules like quarterly ones critical to maintaining coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS_LAPSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder fails to pay the semi-annual premium by the grace period’s deadline, the policy lapses despite having selected semi-annual billing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapses when premiums aren't paid within the grace period, regardless of whether the payment was intended to be annual. The timing of payment does not affect the lapse condition described here.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to missed payments beyond the grace period, it implies that the initial decision on the payment mode may have contributed to non-compliance, highlighting its role in maintaining coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed payments beyond the grace period, it implies that the originally approved payment mode was not followed consistently.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">If the premium isn't paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses—a direct outcome of not meeting the initial due date requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses—a direct result of failing to meet the payment obligations established in the prior statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">If a premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, it implies that the current payment frequency may have contributed to missed deadlines, suggesting a need to reconsider the payment schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder fails to pay within the grace period, the policy lapses regardless of previously selected payment frequency, meaning that even a changed payment method cannot prevent lapse once deadlines pass.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">If a premium isn't paid by the grace period’s end, the policy lapses, even if a prior request to switch modes was submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The risk of policy lapse due to missed payments exists irrespective of any planned changes to the premium mode. Approval of a new payment mode cannot override the need to comply with existing payment terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">If the premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses, leading to immediate termination of coverage with no residual value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">If the premium isn't paid by the grace period’s end, the policy lapses, resulting in immediate loss of coverage with no cash value, unless reinstated per the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">If the premium isn't paid by the grace period’s end, the policy lapses. However, if an Automatic Premium Loan is activated, the system covers the missed payment automatically, avoiding lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">If a premium isn't paid by the grace period's end, the policy lapses. Since this policy has no automatic premium loan, there is no fallback option to keep it active after a missed payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO DIRECT LINK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">If a premium isn't paid by the grace period's end, the policy lapses. Since the base policy doesn’t include an automatic premium loan, the policyholder has fewer options to avoid lapse without additional cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">If a premium payment is missed beyond the grace period, the policy lapses; however, reinstatement may occur through a loan only if sufficient loan value exists and the rider enabling loans was previously added.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REMEDY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">If the premium is not paid within the grace period, the policy lapses, meaning it is no longer active. As a result, the insurer would not be obligated to pay the death benefit when the insured dies, since the policy was inactive.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS PAYMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">If the premium is not paid by the grace period’s end, the policy lapses, meaning it ceases to provide benefits including the death benefit. Therefore, the death benefit becomes unavailable unless the policy is reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to failure to pay within the grace period, it ceases to provide benefits, including the death benefit. However, if the insured dies while the policy remains active, the death benefit becomes payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay a premium leads to policy lapse, but this does not inherently affect the need for company approval of an alternative settlement option upon death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to missed payments, it may no longer provide benefits, including the death benefit. Therefore, timely premium payments ensure that the death benefit remains available.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The lapse of the policy due to missed payments creates a scenario where a death claim may still be processed if the policy was active at time of death. Proof of death remains necessary regardless of whether the policy lapsed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The consequence of failing to pay a premium triggers policy lapse, but the insurer may require extra documents later for processing claims or reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTERIOR_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse, but this does not affect the requirement for submitting proof of death when filing a claim. The need for a certified death certificate remains regardless of prior lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse, but this does not affect how interest accumulates on the death benefit after the insured’s passing. The two events occur at separate stages of the policy timeline.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The consequence of missing a premium payment beyond the grace period is policy lapse, but the statement about legally mandated interest does not directly explain or follow from this outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period leads to policy lapse, but this does not affect the definition or role of the beneficiary. The beneficiary remains defined regardless of policy status.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed payments beyond the grace period, it ceases to provide coverage. However, should the insured die while the policy was still active, the company remains obligated to disburse the death benefit after verifying documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium within the grace period leads to policy lapse, terminating coverage. The beneficiary is defined separately as the individual designated in writing to receive benefits upon the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that failing to pay within the grace period leads to policy lapse. Fact_sentence_2 states that required documents depend on the company’s reasonable discretion, which applies generally but not specifically to lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The failure to maintain premium payment leads to policy lapse, but does not impact when a beneficiary change becomes effective; beneficiary designations remain enforceable even after lapsation if properly documented before termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse, which affects whether a death benefit can be paid; however, changing the beneficiary has no impact on premium obligations or policy validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The failure to maintain premium payments leads to policy lapse, which could impact future benefits but does not prevent a beneficiary change from taking effect once submitted. The effectiveness of a beneficiary update is independent of the policy’s financial standing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to maintain premium payments ensures ongoing policy coverage, which is necessary for the beneficiary designation to remain effective. However, changing the beneficiary has no impact on premium payment obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">Policy lapse occurs when the premium remains unpaid beyond the 31-day grace period, which underscores the importance and function of that grace period established earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">The second fact describes what happens when the grace period expires—policy lapse—which directly follows from the first fact’s assertion that the policy remains in force only until the grace period ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapses when the premium isn’t paid by the end of the grace period, but if death occurs earlier during the grace period, the insurer still pays the death benefit less any unpaid premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 summarizes the effect of missing a premium payment beyond the grace period, which aligns precisely with the more detailed timeline provided in fact_sentence_1 regarding when the lapse occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 indicates that missing the grace period deadline results in policy lapse, reinforcing fact_sentence_1’s claim that coverage ends when the premium isn’t paid on time; thus, the two facts mutually support one another regarding policy consequences.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that missing the grace period leads to policy lapse, which supports fact_sentence_1’s assertion that no future benefits can be claimed once the grace period ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">A policy can lapse when premiums aren't paid by the end of the grace period, but it may still be restored later under the Reinstatement provision, showing continuity despite initial termination risk.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">Policy lapse resulting from missed premium payments sets the stage for the opportunity to reinstate the policy within five years, provided eligibility requirements are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy resulting from missed premium payments can only be restored if the applicant provides sufficient evidence of insurability, linking the cause of lapse to the requirement for reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay all past-due premiums for reinstatement depends directly on the policy having lapsed due to failure to meet the grace period deadline, linking the second fact to the first.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES_LAPSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">Policy lapse resulting from missing the grace period triggers the need to repay overdue premiums with interest to reinstate coverage, directly linking back to the stipulation in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">LEADS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="113c8be3-705c-4873-94a5-5727299a217f" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">sets conditions for policy maintenance</data>
</edge>
