  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="78d118fe-837d-451f-b5ac-51256bde2b7b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">When coverage terminates without value upon lapse, the policyholder still retains the option to reinstate it within five years, provided requirements like payment of overdue amounts and proof of insurability are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">A policy’s termination without value creates the scenario where reinstatement becomes necessary, requiring proof of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage without value after lapse creates the need to repay overdue premiums with interest to restore the policy’s status.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage upon lapse creates the need for reinstatement procedures, including paying overdue premiums along with interest determined by the company at the time of reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, it ends without any cash value, meaning that prior knowledge of the required premium amounts and modes—as detailed in the Schedule of Benefits—is essential to avoid such outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The risk of losing coverage without value arises because premiums must be paid in advance; failure to do so leads to policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed payments—even those made monthly—it loses all value, meaning the option to pay premiums regularly becomes irrelevant once coverage has terminated.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value upon policy lapse, it implies that missed payments—even those scheduled quarterly—are sufficient triggers for loss of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed payments—even those scheduled semi-annually—the coverage ceases entirely and has no residual value.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value upon lapse, it implies that maintaining regular premium payments—including annual ones—is essential to prevent such outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to failure to pay premiums within the grace period, coverage terminates without value. The initial decision to select a particular payment mode impacts the timing and frequency of those required payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to non-payment beyond the grace period, it implies that prior arrangements like approved payment modes were not followed, rendering them ineffective.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT OF NONCOMPLIANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Termination of coverage without value occurs when the policy lapses, often due to failure to pay the required first premium on the Effective Date.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay subsequent premiums on time ensures continued coverage; failing to do so triggers the end of benefits upon policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed payments, it loses all value regardless of any prior intent to adjust payment frequency. Thus, even if the owner wanted to change the frequency later, the damage is irreversible after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE OF LAPSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value due to lapse, any attempt to change the payment method becomes irrelevant after the policy has already expired.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE OF LAPSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, it terminates without value regardless of prior actions like switching premium modes. The requirement to provide written notice for a mode change is unrelated to the loss of cash value at lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, coverage ends without value regardless of prior premium mode choices. Any planned change in premium mode would become irrelevant once the policy has lapsed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">When coverage terminates without value after a lapse, it indicates that the policyholder failed to meet the payment requirement before the grace period ended.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage without value upon lapse is qualified by the possibility of reinstatement, meaning it doesn't apply universally.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTS_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The absence of an automatic premium loan reduces financial flexibility, increasing the likelihood of policy lapse, which leads to termination without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">If an Automatic Premium Loan is activated, it prevents policy lapse by paying overdue premiums after the grace period, thereby preserving coverage and avoiding termination without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS_LAPSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage upon lapse highlights the consequence of failing to maintain payments, which could have been avoided had an automatic premium loan been available. However, this feature requires a separate rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed payments, it terminates without any cash value. The death benefit is only available if the insured dies while the policy remains active.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to non-payment, coverage ends with no cash value. Unpaid premiums might be settled via a policy loan only if sufficient loan balance exists, potentially preventing lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS LAPSING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, coverage ceases without value, meaning the death benefit cannot be claimed. Therefore, the death benefit remains subject to the condition that the policy was active at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, coverage ends without value, making the death benefit unpayable regardless of the insured's death. Thus, the ability to receive the death benefit hinges on maintaining active coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS PAYMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses, coverage ends with no cash value, but if an alternative payment method is desired after lapse, it must be formally accepted by the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, coverage ends without value, meaning no death benefit would be payable. Therefore, the payment of the death benefit in a lump sum only applies if the policy remains active until the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, it ceases to provide benefits, but the insurer may still require documentation proving the insured’s death to process any potential claims related to the lapse event.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The statement about coverage terminating without value at lapse does not influence nor rely on the requirement for a certified death certificate to process claims. They pertain to separate events in the policy’s life cycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage upon lapse implies potential administrative steps post-lapse, possibly including document submission for reinstatement, although this is not explicitly stated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Policy lapse leads to termination of coverage with no cash value, independent of document submission rules. The second statement concerns procedural requirements for submitting documents, unrelated to the outcome of lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse leads to termination without value, but this outcome does not depend on who is designated as the beneficiary. The beneficiary remains defined regardless of policy status.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses, coverage ends without any cash value. The beneficiary is determined solely by the latest official designation on record, regardless of the policy’s status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The lapse of coverage does not affect how interest accumulates on the death benefit after the insured’s passing. The timing of the policy lapse is unrelated to the calculation of interest from the date of death onward.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The statement about coverage terminating upon lapse does not depend on whether interest is required by law. The requirement for interest applies independently to late payments but doesn't affect the outcome of lapse-related termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, it has no value, meaning any potential claim—including a death benefit—is forfeited. Therefore, the death benefit cannot be paid unless the policy was still active at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2db099c6-7010-4ab1-aa02-1a07ff214dc5" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces termination</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc8d1549-2921-4572-bf35-5aa0fc5d2ebd" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">fails to pay</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b01b5c4a-f3e3-4182-ac62-88c29686a4eb" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">loses protection</data>
</edge>
<edge source="868f08e9-36d3-467e-b294-c7c444fbdbc0" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">loses entitlement</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd7d50b-ec2e-42ed-bb35-916b83a07be9" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is required to maintain coverage</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1600a265-26fa-443c-b324-cdc15537292c" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines start of coverage window</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e8a156dc-495d-4f55-9e95-a9df3556afed" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">provides temporary protection against lapse due to late payment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f179b3a8-d715-4622-b45a-7e29066e1276" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">allows recovery of coverage after lapse, otherwise termination occurs</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6c28f10-97c9-4be8-8305-863d2b28de80" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse by covering overdue premiums automatically</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c500be2a-cddf-454f-a0d8-4c9ebd02b021" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">terminates without value when policy lapses</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78d118fe-837d-451f-b5ac-51256bde2b7b" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">loses applicability upon policy lapse</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="6b6da7e8-b838-44ed-8d6a-03169f3ad388">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="d0152e31-5163-412c-a3e2-de8dbfca4418">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="aa097870-5421-4aaf-ae4e-b1c61291568d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="91143741-6d29-48e6-88b8-10a66dd95cdd">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="b9aee283-4cd3-4cf3-88a8-9902dfead9cb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="d46bbf9f-7ef3-408c-8008-7be83f915bd9">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="1cf7d930-e834-490b-8277-e2cc376aebd5">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="f365e6ea-e31d-4ce0-886c-00af8f2b3451">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="9208d514-c5ab-4ae7-b5df-50cb16d66e3a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="481620ed-1c47-4688-ac91-3c78c7549c9a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="5b78b315-e08c-4645-bef5-667102878ab9">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility within five years explains why coverage does not terminate without value in all cases; it serves as a safeguard against permanent loss of coverage after lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The absence of reinstatement eligibility leads to permanent termination without value; however, proving insurability restores the possibility of revival.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON_INSURABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">If reinstatement does not occur, coverage terminates without value; however, this outcome can be avoided by fulfilling the reinstatement conditions, including paying overdue premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value, reinstatement becomes necessary; however, reinstatement requires payment of overdue premiums including interest, which is determined at the time of reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES INTEREST PAYMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value, it implies failure to maintain required premiums, which were originally defined in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Termination without value typically follows from unpaid premiums, which stems from not paying them in advance as required.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums regularly can result in coverage termination without value, although reinstatement remains possible within five years, even if monthly payments were originally selected.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make quarterly premium payments leads to potential loss of coverage without value, underscoring the importance of consistent quarterly payments to sustain benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">Failure to maintain regular semi-annual premium payments may result in coverage termination, underscoring the importance of consistent payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make timely annual payments, including those required under the annual payment option, risks triggering coverage termination unless reinstated within the allowed timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates due to non-payment beyond the grace period, it underscores why selecting a feasible premium payment mode is critical to maintaining continuous protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">Termination without value occurs when coverage lapses due to non-payment, but only after the initial approval of a payment mode has enabled the policy’s existence and operation.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make timely payments—including the first premium—can result in coverage termination without value, making prompt payment essential to maintain active status before any potential reinstatement window closes.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid on the designated due dates, the policy may terminate without value, despite ongoing obligations outlined in the payment schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value, changes to premium payment frequency become irrelevant because the policy is already inactive; however, reinstatement remains possible only under specific conditions regardless of prior payment scheduling choices.</data>
  <data key="d4">IRRELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Failure to meet payment obligations leads to coverage termination unless reinstated, making any attempt to alter payment timing risky. Therefore, modifying the payment method requires caution to avoid triggering termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES PAYMENT COMPLIANCE TO AVOID</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">If coverage lapses due to unpaid premiums and is not reinstated, it terminates without value regardless of prior premium mode choices. Changing the mode later would not restore lost benefits once termination has occurred.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_DIRECT_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">Coverage may terminate without value unless reinstated per the provisions, independent of any prior change in premium mode that required company approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The absence of any payout upon policy lapse—except when reinstated—is directly caused by failing to meet the premium payment deadline within the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility allows coverage to continue despite lapse, thereby preventing termination without value in those cases.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The absence of an automatic premium loan reduces options for maintaining coverage after a missed payment, potentially leading to termination unless reinstated. This highlights why the reinstatement clause exists as a safety net.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a default automatic premium loan feature means policyholders have fewer options to avoid lapse after missed payments, reinforcing why reinstatement becomes critical when coverage ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The risk of coverage termination without value is mitigated if an automatic premium loan is in effect, as it ensures payment of overdue premiums post-grace period, thereby preventing lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">If premiums remain unpaid beyond the grace period, the policy lapses unless reinstated; however, this lapse can potentially be avoided if there is enough accumulated loan value to cover the delinquent payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS LAPSING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses without reinstatement, the death benefit is not payable because coverage has terminated. However, if the policy remains in force at time of death, the death benefit is triggered upon proper documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses without reinstatement, it terminates without value, meaning no death benefit would be payable. Therefore, maintaining active coverage through timely payments ensures eligibility for the death benefit payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value, the death benefit may not be payable unless the policyholder meets reinstatement requirements. Therefore, the death benefit remains dependent on adherence to policy terms, especially regarding active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates without value outside reinstatement terms, it may affect how claims are settled, potentially requiring formal approval for alternative payment methods.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses without being reinstated, no surrender value is returned. However, if the insured dies while covered, the death benefit is paid out, usually as a lump sum unless changed by election.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to provide proof of death ensures proper validation before any claim settlement, even when coverage has terminated. Without submitting acceptable documentation like a certified death certificate, the insurer cannot disburse the death benefit despite the policy being active at time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for acceptable proof of death ensures eligibility for benefits after policy termination, supporting potential reinstatement actions when applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Policy cancellation without cash value applies unless reinstated per terms, while the need for extra documents rests on the insurer’s reasonable discretion.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The statement that coverage ends without value unless reinstated does not directly depend on whether additional documents are requested. Document requests pertain to validation processes, while coverage termination relates to payment failure.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to non-payment and isn't reinstated, no death benefit is payable. However, if the insured dies while the policy remains active, the company will pay the death benefit upon receiving proper documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The first statement outlines circumstances leading to loss of coverage value, while the second describes financial terms related to payout timing after death. They do not influence each other directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The statement about coverage termination without value does not directly involve or explain the legal requirement for interest payments.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">This statement outlines when coverage terminates without financial value, excluding reinstatement scenarios. It does not relate directly to identifying beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Policy termination without value applies when reinstatement isn't feasible, but this does not influence how beneficiaries are designated. The identity of the beneficiary remains independent of whether the policy lapses or is reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b6da7e8-b838-44ed-8d6a-03169f3ad388" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d0152e31-5163-412c-a3e2-de8dbfca4418" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">pays</data>
</edge>
