<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The ability to add an Automatic Premium Loan feature via rider applies regardless of reinstatement rules, meaning it’s a separate option that doesn’t impact or rely upon the timing or feasibility of bringing back a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The ability to add an Automatic Premium Loan via rider has no bearing on the insurability requirements needed for reinstatement after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The inability to access an automatic premium loan without adding a rider means policyholders lack a built-in mechanism to cover missed payments. As a result, failure to pay leads directly to lapse, increasing the need to reinstate the policy by paying back premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASES RISK OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Adding an automatic premium loan via rider does not affect how interest on past-due premiums is determined at reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">While the second sentence discusses adding special riders for premium loans, the first emphasizes that basic premium terms are already detailed in the official schedule, independent of any add-ons.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">While the availability of an automatic premium loan depends on adding a rider, this does not alter the fundamental obligation to pay premiums in advance, which remains mandatory regardless of riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">IS_DEPENDENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Adding an automatic premium loan via rider has no bearing on the option to pay premiums monthly. Payment modes remain available regardless of additional riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Adding an automatic premium loan requires a rider, independent of the chosen payment frequency like quarterly billing. Payment method choice does not influence eligibility for this feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">Adding an automatic premium loan requires a rider, highlighting that supplementary protections like this are not included by default. Meanwhile, paying premiums semi-annually is a standard option permitted under the policy’s payment flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">While the ability to pay premiums annually supports ongoing policy maintenance, adding features like automatic premium loans requires separate riders, emphasizing that enhanced protections are not default but opt-in.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">While the policy owner chooses the premium payment method, the ability to add an automatic premium loan depends solely on including a rider—not on any payment mode selected.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">Adding an Automatic Premium Loan via rider has no bearing on the approval of a premium payment mode; they pertain to separate policy enhancements and scheduling mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">Adding an automatic premium loan via rider is a separate contractual option unrelated to the timing of the first premium’s due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">Adding an automatic premium loan via rider has no impact on when future premiums are due; those remain governed strictly by the selected payment frequency and scheduled dates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">While the ability to adjust premium payment frequency offers administrative flexibility, it does not influence whether an automatic premium loan can be enabled, which depends solely on adding a rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">While an automatic premium loan cannot be added without a rider, the option to change the payment method stands separately and does not require any additional endorsements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The need to add an automatic premium loan through a rider parallels the requirement for written notice when switching premium modes, highlighting that non-standard adjustments to policies demand explicit approval processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_DOCUMENTATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The ability to add an automatic premium loan depends exclusively on a rider, regardless of any changes made to the premium payment mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The lack of an automatic premium loan feature means policyholders cannot use borrowed funds to cover missed premiums. Without this safety net, failing to pay within the grace period increases the likelihood of policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASES RISK OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Adding an Automatic Premium Loan via rider might prevent policy lapse, thereby preserving coverage value. Without it, failure to pay leads to immediate loss of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Adding an automatic premium loan via rider offers a mechanism to maintain coverage post-lapse, thereby reducing the risk of permanent termination despite failure to pay premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy does not automatically include an Automatic Premium Loan, its inclusion depends entirely on adding a rider or endorsement, making the requirement explicit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The addition of an Automatic Premium Loan via rider enables the system to cover unpaid premiums automatically after the grace period ends, ensuring continued policy validity without immediate lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cover unpaid premiums via a policy loan hinges on whether the Automatic Premium Loan provision has been added via rider. Without this addition, the loan option cannot activate even if loan value exists.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Adding an Automatic Premium Loan provision requires a rider, but this does not affect how the Death Benefit is distributed after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
