  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">An automatic premium loan prevents policy lapse and thus avoids coverage termination without value, serving as a safeguard against the condition outlined in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">Had the policy included an Automatic Premium Loan, it would have allowed unpaid premiums to be settled automatically; however, its exclusion makes this possibility irrelevant.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">Without adding the Automatic Premium Loan provision via rider, the policy cannot trigger automatic payments for overdue premiums, meaning the policyholder must manually address delinquency to avoid lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The automatic payment of unpaid premiums via policy loan relies on having enough accumulated loan value; without it, the system cannot execute the loan even if the feature is enabled.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">This sentence explains how unpaid premiums may be covered via a policy loan if the automatic premium loan feature is activated. It does not relate directly to the distribution of the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">An automatic premium loan covers unpaid premiums post-grace period, maintaining policy validity. This ensures that the policy remains active, enabling the potential future payment of the death benefit upon the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains that unpaid premiums may be covered by a policy loan if the automatic premium loan feature is activated. It does not affect how the death benefit is distributed when the insured passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The presence of an automatic premium loan does not affect the requirement for submitting a certified death certificate to process a claim. The two statements address separate procedural elements of insurance administration.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes how unpaid premiums may be covered via an automatic loan if the rider is present. The second sentence concerns the need for company approval before selecting certain death benefit payout alternatives. There is no direct connection between automatic premium loans and settlement option approvals.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes how unpaid premiums may be covered via an automatic loan if enabled, preventing lapse. Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that the death benefit is determined by policy terms, including any riders like the automatic premium loan. These elements together influence claim outcomes but do not directly depend on each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The presence of an automatic premium loan does not affect the need to provide proof of death for claiming benefits. The loan mechanism ensures continued coverage after missed payments, while proof of death remains a separate prerequisite for disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The presence of an automatic premium loan does not inherently require additional documentation beyond standard procedures. While loans affect policy status, the need for further paperwork mentioned in fact_sentence_2 appears unrelated to the loan’s operation.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains how unpaid premiums are handled via an automatic loan mechanism if the rider is present. Fact_sentence_2 describes the flexibility insurers have in requiring supplementary documents, independent of payment mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">When an Automatic Premium Loan is active, unpaid premiums after the grace period are covered by a loan; however, interest on such loans is mandated by law.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes how unpaid premiums may be covered via an automatic loan feature, ensuring continued coverage. Fact_sentence_2 explains that the death benefit is issued quickly once proper documentation is submitted. The two statements concern separate aspects of policy functionality: premium continuity versus post-death claims processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The presence of an automatic premium loan ensures that delinquent premiums are covered without lapsing the policy, but it does not affect how interest accumulates on the death benefit after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes how unpaid premiums may be covered via an automatic policy loan during the grace period. Fact_sentence_2 identifies who receives the death benefit under the policy. The two statements do not interact logically.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">This sentence explains how unpaid premiums may be covered using a policy loan if the rider is activated. It does not relate to the identity or role of the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
