  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="82323a75-1aa4-46a8-bd50-51c2778b6818">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a policy loan depends on accumulated cash value, but even if used, it doesn’t guarantee that a lapsed policy can be reinstated without meeting additional requirements like proof of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">A policy loan can cover unpaid premiums only if sufficient loan value exists; however, even with a loan, reinstatement still requires demonstrating insurability to the insurer’s satisfaction.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cover unpaid premiums through a policy loan depends on having sufficient loan value, offering a potential pathway to meet the reinstatement requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">If there is insufficient loan value to cover unpaid premiums, the insurer may still charge interest at reinstatement, but repayment would require alternative funds instead of relying on loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">If a premium remains unpaid, it might be covered using a policy loan when available. This possibility relies on prior accumulation of loan value, which is unrelated to how premiums are initially displayed in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">If a policy does not have a built-in loan feature, even advanced payment requirements cannot trigger automatic loan coverage; thus, failure to pay may lead directly to lapse without recourse.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY_PREMISE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Even if premiums are scheduled monthly, failure to pay them cannot automatically trigger a policy loan unless prior loan value exists, regardless of payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_DIRECT_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">While unpaid premiums could potentially be covered by a policy loan if funds exist, choosing a quarterly payment schedule does not inherently affect the availability of such loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_FACTOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder fails to make a semi-annual premium payment, they might rely on a policy loan—if available—to avoid lapsing, highlighting the interplay between payment frequency and financial safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a policy loan depends on accumulated loan value, which influences whether delayed annual premiums can be covered without lapsing the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLING_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">While the availability of a policy loan to cover unpaid premiums relies on built-up loan value, the initial election of a payment mode does not determine loan eligibility—it merely affects cash flow timing and accumulation patterns indirectly.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">A policy loan can only cover unpaid premiums if sufficient loan value exists, regardless of the approved payment mode. Therefore, the choice of payment interval does not affect the feasibility of using a loan.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">While the first premium being due on the effective date initiates the payment cycle, its failure does not automatically lead to a policy loan—it requires pre-existing loan value. Thus, the second fact conditions any remedy on prior accumulation rather than the timing of the first payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES_WITH_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">If premiums remain unpaid beyond the grace period, they may be settled using any existing policy loan value—but only if the policy includes a loan provision, which requires a separate rider; thus, this option relies on prior arrangements not guaranteed by default.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON_LOAN_AVAILABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Whether unpaid premiums are covered by a policy loan relies on available loan value, regardless of any prior decision to adjust the payment frequency. Payment frequency adjustments have no direct impact on loan eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">If a policy has enough accumulated loan value, it can cover unpaid premiums; however, this capability is independent of whether the payment method was changed.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a policy loan to cover missed premiums relies on accumulated cash value, independent of whether a change in premium mode has been requested or processed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">Even if unpaid premiums could be covered by a policy loan when sufficient loan value exists, that mechanism has no bearing on whether a new premium mode takes effect after company approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a policy loan to cover unpaid premiums hinges on having enough accumulated loan value, but since the policy does not include automatic loans without a rider, this option cannot prevent lapse unless specifically enabled.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON_LOAN_AVAILABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cover unpaid premiums with a policy loan relies on having enough accumulated loan value; however, even if used, failure to maintain payments still leads to lapse and loss of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON LOAN VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to use a policy loan to cover unpaid premiums depends on having sufficient loan value, which helps avoid coverage termination under the reinstatement provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lacks an automatic premium loan provision, then unpaid premiums cannot be covered automatically; instead, reliance shifts entirely to whether sufficient loan value already exists.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">A policy loan can only apply to unpaid premiums if the Automatic Premium Loan provision was specifically included through a rider; otherwise, no loan functionality is enabled regardless of available funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient loan value is required before an automatic premium loan can be applied to settle delinquent premiums, making it a prerequisite for the process described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how unpaid premiums may be addressed using a policy loan when funds are available. It does not relate directly to who receives the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">If premiums remain unpaid, a policy loan may cover them only when sufficient loan value exists; however, the eventual death benefit remains contingent upon overall policy compliance, including financial obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">If a premium remains unpaid, it may be covered by a policy loan when funds are available, helping maintain coverage status. This sustained coverage enables the insurer to fulfill its obligation to pay the death benefit upon proper documentation of the insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">If a premium remains unpaid, it may be covered using a policy loan when funds exist, but this does not affect how the death benefit is distributed after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a policy loan for unpaid premiums depends on accumulated cash value but does not influence the requirement for submitting a certified death certificate when filing a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a policy loan to cover unpaid premiums depends on accumulated loan value, while additional documentation might be needed later during claim settlement or underwriting review. These statements pertain to separate procedural stages.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a policy loan to cover unpaid premiums depends on accumulated cash value, while proof of death is required regardless of how premiums were settled. These elements serve distinct roles in the claims process.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains how unpaid premiums might be settled using a policy loan if funds exist. Fact_sentence_2 states that required documents depend on the company’s discretion. The two statements concern separate operational elements without mutual influence.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">This statement concerns financial mechanisms for maintaining policy status through loans when premiums are unpaid. It has no direct bearing on how quickly or conditionally the death benefit is disbursed post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a policy loan to cover unpaid premiums does not affect how interest accumulates on the death benefit after the insured's passing. The two concepts relate to separate stages of policy lifecycle management.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a policy loan to cover unpaid premiums depends on accumulated loan value, while alternative settlement options require prior company approval. The two concepts operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder uses a loan to cover unpaid premiums, interest must be charged according to applicable laws. The presence of a loan implies ongoing interest accrual.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
