<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Payment of the death benefit requires the policy to be in force at the time of death, regardless of whether the policy was previously reinstated after lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Payment of the death benefit occurs only if the policy was active at the time of death; however, this has no bearing on whether reinstatement is possible after a lapse, which hinges on separate criteria like insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid upon verified death of the insured under active coverage, regardless of prior lapses or reinstatements, so it does not rely on reinstatement procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">This statement outlines the condition under which the insurer disburses the death benefit—the presentation of proper documentation proving the insured’s death while the policy was active. It has no bearing on the computation of interest for late payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit when proof is submitted depends on the policy remaining active, which requires adherence to the premium payment terms detailed in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the death benefit depends on the policy being kept active through timely premium payments, making premium payment a necessary precondition.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a death benefit depends on maintaining active coverage, which requires regular premium payments—including those made monthly—as outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that the death benefit is paid when the insured dies while the policy is in force, assuming proper documentation is submitted. Active status depends on timely premium payments, such as those made quarterly as noted in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">A death benefit is only payable if the policy remains in force, which requires consistent premium payments—including those made semi-annually—as stipulated in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES COVERAGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">A valid death benefit payout depends on the policy being active, which requires regular premium payments—including those made annually—as stipulated in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a death benefit depends on maintaining active coverage, which requires that premiums be paid according to the selected payment mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">Receiving the death benefit depends on the policy being active, which requires prior approval of the premium payment mode and adherence to payment terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit upon verified death depends on the policy being actively maintained through timely premium payments, including the initial one due on the Effective Date.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit upon verification of the insured’s death depends on the policy being in force, which requires consistent premium payments as outlined in the premium due schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit upon verified death occurs regardless of any prior adjustments to premium payment frequency, making it unaffected by such administrative choices.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a death benefit depends on maintaining active coverage, which requires consistent premium payments that can be adjusted through changes requested under the payment method provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">Receiving the death benefit depends solely on providing proper documentation after the insured's death; it is unrelated to any prior changes in premium payment modes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is payable only when the policy is active at the time of death and proper documentation is submitted. This outcome remains unaffected by prior decisions about premium payment frequency or mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">For the insurance company to pay the death benefit, the policy must remain in force at the time of the insured’s death. Therefore, timely payment of premiums—even within the grace period—is essential to maintain coverage and eligibility for the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED FOR PAYOUT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable if the insured dies while the policy remains in force, implying that any lapse invalidates eligibility for payout, thereby rendering the benefit unavailable even posthumously.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON_ACTIVE_COVERAGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit depends on the policy being active at the time of death, which requires avoiding lapse through timely payments or successful reinstatement after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The obligation to pay the death benefit upon verified death occurs independently of whether an automatic premium loan was included; it depends solely on the policy being active at time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that the death benefit is issued when the insured dies while covered. Fact_sentence_1 clarifies that some features, including automatic premium loans, need separate endorsements to be included.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid only if the policy is still in force at the time of death. Active status depends on timely payments, including those covered by an automatic premium loan under a rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Upon receiving valid proof of the insured's death while the policy is active, the company disburses the death benefit. This outcome depends on the policy remaining in force, which could be influenced by whether unpaid premiums were settled via loan or other means.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON_COVERAGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Upon confirmation of the insured's death while the policy is active, the insurer disburses the death benefit, which is subsequently transferred to the individual designated as the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">PAYMENT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid only after verification of the insured's death, but this obligation is conditioned on meeting the policy’s stipulated requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is triggered when proof of the insured's death is submitted while the policy remains in force, and it is typically disbursed as a lump sum unless an alternate arrangement has been chosen.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINGENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to provide acceptable proof of death is essential before the company disburses the death benefit under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence establishes the default payment of the death benefit when proper documentation is submitted. The second sentence adds that any deviation from the standard lump-sum payout requires prior authorization from the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the obligation to pay the death benefit when proof of death is received. Fact_sentence_2 explains that this proof may require supplementary materials, ensuring compliance before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit requires proof of death, and the nature of acceptable proof is subject to the insurer's reasonable requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">Upon confirmed death during active coverage, the insurer disburses the death benefit, triggering the start of interest accumulation from the date of death onward.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the basic condition for death benefit payout: receipt of due proof. Fact_sentence_2 enhances this by specifying prompt payment and using "satisfactory proof," refining the timing and quality threshold of the required documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes when the death benefit is paid after proper documentation. The second sentence notes a legal requirement for interest, but does not clarify its application in relation to the death benefit claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid only after verification of the insured's death, and it is disbursed to the individual or organization legally designated as the beneficiary through official records.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINGENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid only after proper documentation confirms the insured's death while the policy remains active. The recipient of that benefit is determined by the individual or organization formally named as the beneficiary in the original application.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINGENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 depends on receiving proper documentation; fact_sentence_2 defines one key form of acceptable evidence—the certified death certificate—that satisfies this requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="73d6a0f7-3a12-49ab-8197-b9ddcf6268d3">
  <data key="d3">A guaranteed death benefit depends on the policy remaining active, which relies on consistent premium payments maintained through level premiums over the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="ffa8734c-36ec-49dc-aca1-efd25349e88a">
  <data key="d3">The assurance of a death benefit payout depends on continuous policy validity, which is maintained by unchanging premiums throughout the guaranteed term, making the two facts mutually reinforcing.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="61f37a31-547e-4c2f-8bb7-5fcbc201a22f">
  <data key="d3">The promise of death benefit payment depends on the policy remaining in force; the grace period safeguards against immediate lapse due to late payment, thereby enabling claim fulfillment even after a delayed premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="73bb717f-ccc3-4d83-a6ca-8ece25be0884">
  <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit depends on the policy remaining in force; therefore, the existence of the grace period—which maintains coverage—is necessary for the fulfillment of this commitment.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="32cc14dc-f185-40a1-b8fb-0ad86cc4416e">
  <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit upon verified death depends on the policy being in force; the 5-year reinstatement clause enables the policy to regain validity after lapsing, thus preserving eligibility for the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="6c97dbd6-9f74-4d6a-8dfc-ae292108fb75">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that the Death Benefit is paid upon confirmed death during policy validity, reinforcing the conditions under which the definition provided in fact_sentence_1 applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the Death Benefit follow the policy terms ensures that its payout occurs only when conditions like active coverage and submitted proof are satisfied, reinforcing the contractual framework established in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="ad1cb066-961b-4cae-bf88-48a316e04583">
  <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit upon proof of death depends on maintaining active coverage, which requires regular premium payments like those made via monthly bank draft.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="a337b41c-27fd-4c74-8c49-2a45657cee74">
  <data key="d3">The commitment to pay the death benefit upon proof of death depends on the policy being in force; the 20-year guarantee confirms the policy’s longevity and thus enables the fulfillment of this payment obligation.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="cdb0fe5e-2332-46bf-8e3c-ce3e60450bd4">
  <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit hinges on the policy being in force at time of death; thus, the possibility of reinstating the policy within 5 years preserves the pathway through which the death benefit becomes payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="8553795c-a210-458d-bbd9-47de9966423a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 requires proof of death to initiate the death benefit payment, which is explicitly promised in fact_sentence_1 once the policy terms—including premium payments—are satisfied.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="3c328b68-a332-4773-9c29-f646235f7d51">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes the process for triggering the Death Benefit through submitted proof, which operates within the framework established by fact_sentence_1 regarding policy terms and limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit depends on the policy being in force at the time of death, which is preserved through the 31-day grace period for premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit provision depends on the policy being in force at time of death, which includes cases where the policy was maintained through timely use of the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">Provided the policy is still in force when the insured dies, the death benefit is issued after verification; however, any outstanding premiums owed during the grace period reduce the total payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be payable per fact_sentence_2, the policy must remain in force, meaning premiums must be paid before the grace period expires, as stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable if the policy remains in force at the time of death; therefore, timely premium payment—even within the grace period—is necessary to maintain eligibility under the terms described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit can only be paid if the policy remains in force at the time of death; failing to pay within the grace period nullifies this entitlement, making the payment conditional on maintaining current status through timely premium payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the policy be in force at the time of death means that reinstatement options become critical; without them, beneficiaries would not qualify for the death benefit despite potential claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses but is successfully reinstated within five years, its continued validity allows the death benefit to be claimed, making reinstatement critical for maintaining payout eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable if the policy is in force at time of death, making reinstatement through demonstrated insurability a prerequisite for claim eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">A validly reinstated policy becomes eligible for death benefit claims, making timely repayment of past dues critical to maintaining coverage continuity and future benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
