<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The ability to receive the death benefit depends on maintaining active coverage, which requires timely reinstatement within five years if the policy has lapsed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Policy terms govern death benefit payments, but they don't dictate requirements for reinstating a lapsed policy, which instead relies on demonstrating current insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Policy terms govern how the death benefit is paid upon the insured’s passing, whereas reinstating a lapsed policy requires settling overdue amounts with interest. There is no direct logical link between the mechanisms governing claims and those enabling revival of inactive policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
