  <data key="d3">The death benefit is subject to policy terms, including potential requirements like submitting documentation, but it does not influence how interest on overdue premiums is calculated at reinstitution.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit is determined by the policy’s governing terms, which may include provisions related to payments. Yet, this clause stands independently from the location of premium details in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only available if the policy remains active, which depends on premiums being paid in advance as required; thus, adherence to payment schedules enables fulfillment of the death benefit terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit’s eligibility hinges on compliance with policy terms, including timely premium payments like those made monthly, although the payment method itself does not directly determine benefit availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The ability to receive the death benefit depends on maintaining active coverage, which requires consistent premium payments—including those made quarterly—as outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The condition that the death benefit is subject to policy terms does not depend on whether premiums are paid semi-annually; it applies regardless of payment frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The terms governing the death benefit do not depend on whether premiums are paid annually; instead, they apply regardless of payment frequency once coverage is active.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit be paid per policy terms applies regardless of the selected premium payment mode, making it independent of the initial payment choice.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit’s compliance with policy terms does not affect the selection or approval of the premium payment mode; it operates as a separate contractual obligation independent of payment scheduling decisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit payout depends only on meeting policy-specified criteria; it is independent of whether the first premium was timely paid, assuming the policy remained active after that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">While the death benefit is subject to policy terms—including required documentation—the obligation to make timely premium payments does not directly determine whether the benefit is paid, only whether the policy remains active at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">The terms governing the death benefit payment remain unchanged regardless of whether the premium payment frequency has been modified by the policy owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit be paid according to policy terms implies that any changes to premium payment methods must not compromise the policy’s active status to ensure claim validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for submitting proof and adherence to policy terms for death benefits has no bearing on whether a change in premium mode needs to be formally notified to the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit payout depends only on meeting policy-specified requirements, irrespective of any prior changes to the premium payment mode approved by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable under active policy conditions; thus, its availability depends on timely premium payments and avoiding lapse, making the timing of payment critical.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable under active policy conditions; hence, its availability hinges on avoiding lapse. Since lapse leads to termination without value, the existence of the death benefit claim depends on sustaining coverage through timely payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit follow policy terms includes provisions like reinstatement after lapse; thus, failure to reinstate means no death benefit despite claims, aligning with coverage terminating without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit be paid according to policy terms includes stipulations like non-inclusion of certain features (such as automatic premium loans), meaning the absence of such a feature aligns with the general contractual constraints affecting payout eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">While the Death Benefit is subject to policy terms, including potential delays or requirements, it is unaffected by whether an Automatic Premium Loan was added via rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines that the death benefit follows policy provisions, which could include features like automatic premium loans. Fact_sentence_1 explains how those same features might prevent lapses, ensuring continued eligibility for future death benefit payments. Thus, the presence of such a rider affects whether the policy remains active long enough to trigger the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit’s disbursement depends on adherence to policy rules, one of which involves paying premiums—potentially through a loan—if not settled promptly.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_UPON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">While the insurer agrees to pay the death benefit when proof of death is submitted, the actual disbursement hinges on whether the claim complies with the policy’s defined terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">While the death benefit is intended for the beneficiary, its release is contingent on meeting the policy’s stipulated requirements, ensuring proper verification before payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the Death Benefit follows policy terms includes the provision that it is typically paid as a lump sum unless an alternate settlement method is chosen.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINGENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate ensures compliance with the policy’s conditions governing the death benefit payment, making it essential documentation for claiming benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit’s disbursement method is governed by policy rules, and any deviation from standard lump-sum payments requires prior authorization from the insurer. This ensures compliance with contractual obligations and risk management protocols.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for acceptable proof of death ensures compliance with the policy terms governing the death benefit payment. Without documented evidence, the payment cannot proceed despite being subject to those terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit payout depends on compliance with policy conditions, including providing any necessary supplemental documentation requested by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit payout depends on meeting policy-specified conditions, including providing necessary documentation requested by the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit payout timeline and process depend on fulfilling the policy’s requirements, including providing acceptable proof of death. This ensures compliance with contractual obligations before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is distributed according to the policy’s conditions, including the designated recipient identified in the application. Without a properly named beneficiary, the payout process cannot proceed as intended.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit being subject to policy terms does not inherently depend on whether interest is mandated by law. Interest requirements pertain more broadly to financial obligations like unpaid premiums rather than direct death benefit rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The Death Benefit being subject to policy terms creates the foundation for when and how payments occur, including potential interest accrual post-death. Interest accumulates only if the claim is validated and processed per those terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">The amount and timing of the death benefit depend on policy terms, including proper identification of the rightful recipient through official documentation. Without a clearly designated beneficiary, even if the policy terms allow payment, distribution cannot proceed correctly.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS BENEFICIARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
