  <data key="d3">Approval of alternative settlement options involves administrative oversight after death, whereas the lack of an automatic premium loan affects pre-death financial flexibility. No mutual dependence exists between these clauses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">While the insurer approves alternative settlement options, this process is unrelated to whether an Automatic Premium Loan provision has been added via rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence outlines that alternative settlement choices require prior company consent. The first sentence explains how unpaid premiums might be settled using a policy loan if the rider exists. These topics relate to separate stages of policy administration and have no inherent causal or sequential link.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Approval from the company is required for any alternative settlement option, regardless of whether a policy loan exists to cover unpaid premiums. There is no direct causal link between the two conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for company approval of alternative settlement options implies oversight over how benefits are distributed after death. This complements the first statement by ensuring that even if the death benefit is triggered, its distribution method may need formal consent.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES_RESTRICTION</data>
