<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of death is necessary only when claiming benefits after the insured’s passing, regardless of whether the policy was previously reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that proof of death must meet the company’s standards to trigger a death benefit payment. Fact_sentence_1 details what is needed to reinstate a policy post-lapse. These are independent procedural steps tied to separate outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is necessary to receive the death benefit, regardless of whether the policy was previously reinstated. Reinstatement depends on financial obligations being met, while proof of death is independent of that process.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Providing acceptable proof of death is necessary to process a death benefit claim, regardless of whether interest was charged on unpaid premiums during reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death according to company standards has no bearing on how premiums are displayed or determined in the benefits schedule. The two facts pertain to separate stages of policy lifecycle management.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of death is necessary for claiming benefits, regardless of whether premiums were paid in advance, making it independent of prior payment conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
