  <data key="d3">Submitting acceptable proof of death is necessary to trigger the payout process; however, this step occurs after premiums have been paid and does not depend on the choice of payment frequency like monthly billing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Submitting acceptable proof of death allows the insurer to process the death benefit, but only if the policy was actively maintained through timely premium payments like those made quarterly.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_PAYOUT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is required when filing a claim but has no bearing on how premiums were previously paid, including whether they were paid semi-annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of death is required only if the insured dies while the policy remains active, which depends on consistent premium payments—including those made annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
