  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of death is necessary for claiming benefits after the insured’s passing, regardless of prior changes to premium payment arrangements.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of death is necessary only after the insured passes away; it has no bearing on whether a premium mode change was requested or processed earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">Submitting acceptable proof of death is necessary for receiving the death benefit, regardless of any prior changes made to the premium payment mode. Changes in premium mode do not influence the validity or necessity of providing death verification documents.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death enables the processing of a death benefit claim, even if the policy had previously lapsed due to unpaid premiums, assuming reinstatement conditions were met.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_PRESENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death satisfies a condition necessary for claiming benefits after the policy has lapsed, ensuring the claimant meets requirements despite termination of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Failure to submit required proof of death prevents the payment of the death benefit, reinforcing why coverage effectively terminates without value unless reinstated prior to death. Proof is essential to trigger the payout mechanism tied to active coverage status.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death ensures proper payout eligibility under the policy, regardless of whether an automatic premium loan was available. The requirement for documentation stands independent of any loan provisions tied to premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is necessary regardless of whether an Automatic Premium Loan provision has been added via rider; it is part of the claims process and unrelated to premium financing features.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is unrelated to whether an automatic premium loan was used to cover delinquent premiums. Death benefit claims require documentation regardless of how prior premiums were settled.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is necessary before any benefits are released, including cases where a policy loan might have been used to maintain coverage. The requirement does not depend on whether a loan was utilized.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death in a form satisfactory to the company enables the disbursement of the death benefit when the insured dies during active coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Providing acceptable proof of death is required before the death benefit can be issued to the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death in a satisfactory form enables the fulfillment of conditions necessary for the death benefit to be paid under the policy’s stipulations.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">Providing acceptable proof of death enables the disbursement of the death benefit, including the default lump-sum payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of the insured’s death is essential because it enables the company to evaluate and approve any requested settlement options, including alternatives.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 requires proof of death to be satisfactory to the company; fact_sentence_2 clarifies that a certified death certificate meets this standard.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for acceptable proof of death sets the baseline; however, the insurer reserves the right to request further documentation to verify claims fully.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 mandates submission of acceptable proof of death, while fact_sentence_2 indicates that the specific requirements depend on what the company considers reasonable under its judgment.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Satisfactory proof of death must be submitted before the company processes the death benefit payout. Without proper documentation, the claim remains unfulfilled.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit acceptable proof of death must be fulfilled before any processing of the death benefit occurs, including the calculation of accrued interest from the date of death onward.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit proof of death does not influence or relate to the legal mandate that interest must be charged. The two statements operate independently within the claims process.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is needed to validate the event triggering the payout, but the need for such proof does not alter or define who the designated beneficiary is.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death ensures eligibility verification, enabling the insurer to confirm the event triggering payout rights. This step precedes any disbursement to the identified beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="c4bbdfe5-b5f2-4f13-b7cd-d0bf51cdb854">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is only relevant if the policy was still active at the time of death, which depends on whether premiums were paid either on time or within the 31-day grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="6986ceb2-2463-4c38-aa31-8d40d06d7fe1">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is necessary to trigger the death benefit, but this requirement applies only if the policy remained in force—such as during the grace period—after a late premium payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="2126e6b2-1c1d-4993-96c9-8ad59b24c657">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is necessary before determining whether unpaid premiums should be deducted from the death benefit when the insured passes during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="865d01d3-900e-4d17-895c-7dbb4f659dbc">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is necessary to trigger a death benefit, but it cannot succeed if the policy has already lapsed due to missed premium payments beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="a8b806b3-5c59-4a05-a6ee-47c4708daa3c">
  <data key="d3">Failure to maintain coverage through timely premium payment—as described in fact_sentence_1—renders the requirement for proof of death irrelevant, since benefits are not payable once coverage terminates.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="f4a76f59-2b1c-453b-84bd-81156f57d01c">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is a prerequisite for receiving any benefit, but it cannot result in a payout if the policy has already lapsed due to unpaid premiums beyond the grace period, making timely payment a foundational condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="67eb9e29-b9c1-4902-8d0e-af0c9b75202b">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death enables the beneficiary to collect the death benefit, regardless of whether the policy was previously reinstated after lapse, meaning reinstatement status doesn't alter the necessity of submitting documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="432e1a1f-f7e9-4036-bcfa-49b2340827f2">
  <data key="d3">Providing acceptable proof of death allows the beneficiary to collect the death benefit, assuming the policy was either active at time of death or successfully reinstated within the allowable timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="65acf9bc-e764-4677-987e-baf89f2e6822">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is necessary to process a death benefit claim, even if the policy had been reinstated earlier through demonstrated insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">SEQUENTIAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="330543a9-5d64-4d96-89b1-f5991ca096b7">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death is mandatory for claiming the death benefit, regardless of whether the policy was previously reinstated. Reinstatement ensures ongoing coverage, which enables the claim process to proceed once proper documentation is submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5" target="fd1c6721-618b-442b-8c55-692936c13298">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of death enables the insurer to process a death benefit claim, which may occur even if the policy was previously reinstated under terms that included paying overdue premiums and interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
