  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="509f7ae6-0608-4b2c-8662-8dcbe0280a20">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">To reinstate a lapsed policy within five years, applicants must satisfy the insurer’s documented evidence expectations, which vary depending on reasonableness.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The level of documentation demanded for reinstatement is determined by the Company’s assessment of reasonableness, directly influencing what constitutes acceptable proof of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Additional documentation may be needed when reinstating a policy, which includes fulfilling the obligation to pay all past due premiums along with accrued interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The company has discretion over requiring extra documentation for reinstatement, which could include supporting materials related to payment history or eligibility. Interest charges on overdue premiums are similarly determined by the company when reinstatement occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines that document demands are at the company’s discretion. Fact_sentence_1 states that premium amounts and modes are displayed in the Schedule of Benefits, which is unrelated to documentation policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The flexibility in requiring additional documentation is independent of when premiums are paid. Whether premiums are paid in advance has no bearing on the company’s right to request further evidence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">Documentation requirements vary based on the company’s discretion and are not influenced by whether premiums are paid monthly or through another method. Payment mode does not affect evidentiary needs.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for additional documentation, determined at the company’s discretion, has no connection to the choice of quarterly premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The flexibility in documentation demands does not affect the available modes of premium payment, including semi-annual installments, which remain unchanged regardless of evidence requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The company may request various documents based on its discretion; however, this flexibility in documentation has no connection to how often premiums are paid.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">Documentation requirements are determined solely by the company’s discretion and do not depend on the selected premium payment mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">Requirements for extra documentation do not affect the selection or approval of a premium payment mode, as each involves distinct underwriting or operational considerations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">While additional documentation may be requested at any time, it does not affect the fixed due date of the first premium established upon policy inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence indicates that the insurer has discretion over required documentation. The first sentence specifies fixed due dates for premiums, which are unrelated to the conditions under which documentation might be requested.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">Additional documentation may be required when modifying premium payment frequency, reflecting the insurer’s discretion in validating changes to policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Additional documentation may be required when requesting a change in premium payment method, reflecting administrative oversight.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The company has the authority to request additional documentation when a premium mode change is requested, ensuring compliance with its internal standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">Documentation required for changes in premium mode varies depending on what the company deems necessary, including potential delays until approval is granted.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines that document needs are determined by the company’s reasonable standards. Fact_sentence_1 describes the outcome of non-payment, which does not directly relate to documentation requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">Documentation demands vary depending on what the insurer deems reasonable, regardless of whether the policy has lapsed or remains active. The first statement does not influence or rely on these documentation standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">Additional documentation may be required at the insurer’s discretion, potentially relevant when attempting to reinstate a lapsed policy that would otherwise terminate without value.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_REINSTATEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">The need for additional documentation depends on the insurer’s discretion and applies broadly across claim scenarios, regardless of whether a premium loan feature exists. It has no bearing on the presence or absence of that particular policy add-on.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">While the company has discretion over required documentation, including that for endorsements like an Automatic Premium Loan rider, the addition itself depends solely on formal agreement via rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the variable nature of document requests from the insurance company. Fact_sentence_1 details a technical provision for covering missed payments using loans, unrelated to documentation policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines that document demands vary based on the company’s judgment. Fact_sentence_1 describes reliance on policy loan availability for covering missed payments. No connection exists between procedural documentation and loan-based payment solutions.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The insurer has discretion to define what constitutes adequate proof of death, which determines whether the death benefit will be paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">Documentation requirements exist to verify eligibility for receiving the death benefit, ensuring proper validation before disbursement to the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Documentation requirements exist to ensure eligibility for the death benefit, aligning with the policy’s governing terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">While the company has discretion over document requirements, this does not affect whether the death benefit is paid in a lump sum or under another option.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The need for extra documentation arises because the company retains control over approving alternative settlement options, ensuring compliance with internal standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The reasonableness of the documentation requested by the company forms the foundation for determining whether the submitted proof satisfies the requirement outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">BASED_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 introduces flexibility for extra documentation, it relies on the existence of at least one mandatory document—such as the certified death certificate mentioned in fact_sentence_1—as part of the overall claim process.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The Company’s right to request additional documentation is grounded in its ability to act reasonably; thus, the condition in fact_sentence_2 defines the scope and legitimacy of the action described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">The need for additional documentation stems from the insurer’s discretion, unrelated to statutory interest obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for additional documentation relates to verifying claim eligibility but does not influence how interest accumulates on the death benefit after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">The Company has discretion over required documents, ensuring it receives sufficient evidence before disbursing benefits. This enables timely payment only after meeting its documented verification standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for additional documentation stems from the insurer’s discretion but does not relate to identifying the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">The need for additional documentation stems from the insurer’s discretion but does not influence who is designated as the beneficiary. The beneficiary status depends solely on the latest official designation filed with the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
