  <data key="d3">The death benefit accumulates interest from the date of death onward, independent of whether the policy was previously reinstated or remains active. Reinstatement requirements are unrelated to how interest is calculated post-mortem.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Interest on the death benefit begins accruing from the date of death until payout, regardless of whether the policy was previously reinstated or remains active. Reinstatement requirements do not influence this post-death interest mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 outlines the accrual of interest on the death benefit from the date of death onward, which occurs only upon claim processing. Fact sentence 1 addresses interest applied specifically to unpaid premiums during reinstatement, unrelated to claims or death benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
