  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">Interest accruing on the death benefit begins upon the insured’s death and continues until payout; this process has no connection to the timing or method of premium payments like quarterly installments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence explains that interest begins accruing on the death benefit from the date of death onward, whereas the first sentence specifies that premiums can be paid semi-annually. These points relate to distinct stages of the policy—premium collection and claim disbursement—with no functional interdependence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
