</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">This identifies the individual or organization designated to receive benefits upon the insured’s death. It has no bearing on the scheduling or conditions of premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is designated in the application and has no relation to adjustments in premium payment timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">Defining the beneficiary involves specifying who receives the death benefit. This role does not influence or depend on the method used to pay premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is defined as the individual or organization named in the application; this definition has no bearing on procedures related to altering premium payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary’s identity, defined at application, has no bearing on the process or timing of premium mode changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is designated in the application, independent of whether premiums are paid or the policy lapses due to non-payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is the individual or organization named in the application, independent of whether the policy has lapsed or terminated.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">This sentence defines the beneficiary as the individual or organization named in the application. It has no connection to how or when coverage may terminate.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">Knowing that the beneficiary is the person named in the application provides no information regarding whether the policy includes an automatic premium loan feature.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">The second statement defines the beneficiary, the recipient of the death benefit. The first statement concerns adding optional features like a premium loan. Neither depends on nor influences the other.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that the beneficiary is the individual or organization designated in the application to receive proceeds. Fact_sentence_1 outlines a mechanism for covering missed payments using a policy loan. No causal or contextual link exists between the roles of the beneficiary and premium repayment systems.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">This sentence identifies the individual or organization entitled to receive the death benefit. Its content does not relate to whether premiums are covered by loans or any financial provisions tied to delinquency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary, defined as the party named in the application, is entitled to receive the death benefit once the insurer verifies the insured's death occurred during active policy coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">RECIPIENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">The designation of the beneficiary determines who is entitled to receive the death benefit when the insured passes away under active coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">The individual or organization named as beneficiary in the application becomes entitled to receive the death benefit upon the insured’s passing, assuming all claim requirements are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENTITLES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is the party entitled to receive the death benefit upon the insured’s passing, which is generally disbursed as a lump sum unless an alternate arrangement has been agreed upon.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">Knowing that the beneficiary is the person named in the application does not influence whether alternative settlement options require company approval. Approval depends on policy terms, not beneficiary status.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is defined independently as the recipient, but without proper proof of death, even the rightful beneficiary cannot receive the payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is legally entitled to receive the death benefit upon proving the insured’s death through official documents such as a certified death certificate.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary, defined as the person or entity named in the application, might need to provide further documents if requested by the company during claim processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="5e097a82-f754-43e4-905d-5d147b217df4">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary as named in the application has no bearing on the documentation required by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="827c6995-f0dd-4669-b3cd-e64364930b24">
  <data key="d3">Knowing who the beneficiary is helps determine whom the insurer should pay the death benefit to once sufficient proof of death is received.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENTITLEMENT_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="aa4414ad-2a6e-42ca-8162-e018fe5fd62e">
  <data key="d3">This statement identifies the recipient of the death benefit but provides no information about interest requirements imposed by law.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="9a0ec08d-cc0c-4623-90af-479513e70439">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary must be clearly designated before the death benefit—including accrued interest—is eligible for distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db12acf6-7ef1-442a-a0b0-0ebe2981d3c4" target="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the baseline definition of the beneficiary from the original application, but fact_sentence_2 supersedes it by specifying that the most up-to-date formal designation takes precedence.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
