<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The identity of the beneficiary has no bearing on whether a lapsed policy can be reinstated within five years, which depends solely on underwriting and payment conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">The identity of the beneficiary is determined by the latest written designation on record; however, this has no bearing on whether a lapsed policy can be reinstated through proof of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">The identity of the beneficiary has no bearing on the requirements for reinstating a lapsed policy after missed payments.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">This statement identifies the individual or organization designated to receive the death benefit under the policy. It has no bearing on the financial terms related to reinstating a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="65a43e84-d268-46ce-900c-06f4538f2516">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence explains how beneficiaries are determined through official designations. The first sentence outlines the presentation of premium terms in the Schedule of Benefits. Neither statement influences nor depends on the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="d3aeb4da-98f5-49aa-9680-88328bc6317d">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary has no bearing on when premiums are required to be paid. It relates solely to post-death benefit disbursement, independent of payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="a81e586d-f4c9-49fe-827d-4bb85cdc14e2">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary has no bearing on the available modes of premium payment, including monthly billing. These elements operate separately within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="06c6864a-8a1b-46ee-bb2f-99522c008d8a">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary has no bearing on how often premiums are paid, including quarterly installments. One describes eligibility for payout; the other outlines payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="ae290ac1-57d5-418a-aeff-3020cd16c2e5">
  <data key="d3">This sentence identifies the beneficiary as the individual or organization formally designated in writing to receive proceeds. It has no bearing on how premiums are scheduled or paid.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="fc47d11a-7ce2-4140-9e5d-84adfba6efd3">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary has no bearing on how often premiums are paid. The role of the beneficiary is independent of premium payment modes outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="67535076-c012-4f51-9fca-3da547334acf">
  <data key="d3">Naming a beneficiary does not influence the selection of the premium payment mode; they are separate administrative choices made at different stages of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="2fe7c477-3ff3-4964-8334-5bce147c512e">
  <data key="d3">Defining the beneficiary involves specifying the recipient of the death benefit under proper documentation. This has no bearing on the selection or approval of premium payment modes, which relate solely to funding the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="f501fcfb-9924-4880-8895-de800216cc6b">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary as per the latest written designation has no bearing on when the first premium is due; it pertains solely to claim distribution after death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="d0a3204c-79af-4db3-91c3-0206bb2cd580">
  <data key="d3">This sentence identifies the individual or organization entitled to receive the death benefit under the policy. It has no bearing on the scheduling or conditions of premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="a88904d4-aa6d-4deb-9bf5-50550bbc075d">
  <data key="d3">The identity of the beneficiary, determined by formal designation, has no bearing on the ability to modify premium payment frequencies, which are governed by separate administrative procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="c9080843-8376-4174-a9be-27f5cfe85dc2">
  <data key="d3">The identity of the beneficiary determines who collects the death benefit. This does not depend on or influence the choice of premium payment method selected by the policy owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="7dd274eb-79fa-4549-9a30-e662efe45594">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is determined solely by the latest written designation on record, independent of any changes made to premium payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="c8766159-f2f1-4980-a4f4-30a5ac151e22">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is determined by the latest official designation on record and remains unaffected by any adjustments to the premium payment mode.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is the party entitled to claim the death benefit after the insured passes away. This entitlement depends on having an active policy, which requires timely premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="b160aaee-2bb3-42d4-99f1-e1274612ebc3">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is defined as the individual or organization formally designated in writing. Their right to receive benefits depends on the policy remaining active at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="2355dc3f-af2e-4eda-b96d-fd3204fa6b8e">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary has no bearing on whether coverage ends without value, as it pertains solely to claims distribution rather than policy continuation or termination criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="2d6cd2a6-4a3a-44fe-aa4e-912059d4a996">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the identity of the beneficiary does not affect whether the policy includes an automatic premium loan; the two concepts pertain to different components of insurance administration.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="cf255e83-6bf3-43a7-a0f5-ffa85d8f1f6d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies the identity of the recipient of the death benefit under normal circumstances. Fact_sentence_1 outlines conditions for adding financial provisions like automatic loans. Neither statement influences nor depends on the other; they pertain to distinct administrative elements.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="3ac57c69-3ec6-47e1-9a1c-8e288edc1b2b">
  <data key="d3">This sentence identifies the individual or organization entitled to receive the death benefit upon the insured’s passing. It has no bearing on whether premiums are paid via loan or any related financial mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="0e6c34e9-34ee-4684-a4db-b8f932cd319e">
  <data key="d3">This sentence identifies the beneficiary as the individual or organization formally designated in writing to receive the death benefit. It has no connection to whether premiums are covered by loans.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="defb9349-5ec2-419c-99cf-a721b93806df">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary, defined as the person or entity listed in the latest written designation, receives the death benefit once the insurer confirms the insured’s death while the policy remains in effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">ELIGIBLE_RECIPIENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="401085bd-ec9b-4194-a332-d312acf2f556">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary is defined as the party formally designated in writing to receive the death benefit upon the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="b9f4573a-344d-4bda-a387-f3c32ffcf8c5">
  <data key="d3">Only individuals or entities officially named as beneficiaries in writing may receive the death benefit, ensuring compliance with the policy’s stipulations governing payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENTITLES TO PAYMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="2030c442-4fb0-495a-995b-bc3c20a392ff">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary, defined as the party named in the most current written form on record, is eligible to receive the death benefit, which is generally disbursed as a lump sum unless another settlement choice has been selected.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="e7ae6851-fbec-41a1-96fb-55af6ecf7ebc">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary must be formally designated in writing with the insurer before any settlement option—including alternatives—can be processed, ensuring only authorized parties receive proceeds.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="c8957594-3af6-486f-91f2-abe9eabc42e5">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary must be clearly designated in writing before a claim can proceed. Their identity determines whom the death benefit is paid to once required proof has been validated.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="e15e7155-24f9-4078-bb5f-26d32c0baa61">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary must provide acceptable proof like a certified death certificate to collect the death benefit, meaning their entitlement depends on fulfilling evidentiary conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="adfc5e3f-7b76-4e27-9e64-1e3c4108cc29" target="38feed0f-4953-4e2f-a66c-0c3a2fbe012d">
  <data key="d3">The Beneficiary is determined by the most current written designation held by the Company, regardless of any additional documentation that may later be requested. Document requests do not alter how the Beneficiary is identified.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
