  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes the basis for whom the policy owner can designate or modify through formal submission.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes the basis for eligibility, enabling the enforcement of automatic生效 of beneficiary changes even if the insured has passed away.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes the subject of any potential change; therefore, it provides essential context for understanding how and when a change becomes effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary specifies who receives benefits under the policy. This role could potentially be altered via an assignment of the policy, though the clause does not explicitly link assignment to changing beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence identifies the designated beneficiary according to formal records. The second sentence clarifies that the insurance company does not assume responsibility for potential tax outcomes arising from assigning the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary does not influence or relate to the outcome of policy cancellation. The two concepts operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes the legal basis for changing designations. Since changes take effect upon receipt regardless of the insured's condition, the initial identification of the beneficiary is essential for determining the scope of such modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary establishes eligibility, but their actual rights are contingent upon whether an assignment has been made, meaning the beneficiary’s authority may be restricted under such circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence identifies how beneficiaries are formally designated through applications or written designations. The second sentence clarifies that the insurance company does not verify or guarantee the legality of policy assignments, which relates to ownership transfers but not beneficiary identification.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary establishes eligibility criteria for receiving benefits but does not influence or depend on the policy owner’s ability to cancel coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes entitlement under the policy, but does not influence the outcome of cancellation, where no benefits are paid thereafter.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence identifies the designated beneficiary through formal documentation. The second sentence addresses potential refunds of unearned premiums, which is unrelated to beneficiary definition or selection.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary establishes eligibility criteria but does not influence or rely on the policy owner’s right to access policy documents.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
