  <data key="d3">The first sentence identifies the legal recipient of benefits under the policy. The second sentence concerns the policy owner’s access to financial transaction data related to premiums paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes eligibility criteria but does not influence the requirement for company approval when altering settlement options.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary relies on formal designations made through proper channels, which are initiated by the policy owner’s authorized actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">The definition of a beneficiary establishes eligibility criteria but does not influence or require the policy owner’s ability to request riders. The two concepts operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
