<edge source="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">When the named beneficiary does not survive the insured, the rule reverts to the policy owner as the alternate recipient, relying on the prior specification of beneficiary eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">When no beneficiary survives the insured and the policy owner is alive, the death benefit is paid to them; otherwise, it passes to the owner’s estate. This reflects a sequential contingency plan based on who remains after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_FALLBACK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The rule about paying the death benefit to the policy owner if no beneficiary survives relies on the policy owner having authority to designate or update beneficiaries. This ensures the ownership role remains relevant even after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
