  <data key="d3">This sentence defines the outcome if no beneficiary survives, while the second explains when a beneficiary update becomes active. The first sets a fallback condition, whereas the second establishes the mechanism for updating it.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">This statement defines what happens if no beneficiary survives the insured and the owner is deceased, resulting in the death benefit going to the estate. This outcome depends on prior beneficiary designation but does not rely on the act of changing beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains what happens to the death benefit if no beneficiary survives and the owner is deceased, focusing on final disbursement. The second sentence details the mechanism by which the owner can legally transfer rights under the policy through formal documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how the death benefit is distributed if no beneficiary survives and the policy owner is deceased, focusing on estate disbursement. This information does not relate to the validity of policy assignments discussed in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how the death benefit is distributed if no beneficiary outlives the insured and the policy owner is deceased, directing funds to the estate. This does not relate directly to the tax liabilities associated with assigning the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how the death benefit is distributed if neither the insured nor the policy owner survives, directing funds to the owner’s estate. This scenario does not relate to the policy owner’s authority to cancel coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how the death benefit is distributed if no beneficiary or owner survives; it does not relate to accessing policy documents.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">This statement concerns the default payout destination if no beneficiary survives; it does not relate directly to the cessation of coverage due to cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">When no surviving beneficiary exists and the policy owner has also passed away, the death benefit defaults to the owner’s estate. This outcome may be affected if the policy was previously assigned, as such assignments can restrict or alter ownership rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how the death benefit is distributed when no beneficiary survives the insured and the policy owner is also deceased, leading to payout to the estate. This scenario does not involve cancellation or refund of premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">This sentence concerns the default recipient of the death benefit if no beneficiary or owner survives. This sentence relates to administrative access rights held by the policy owner but does not influence or depend on the outcome described in sentence one.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">The outcome described in fact_sentence_1 pertains to post-mortem disbursement when no eligible beneficiary remains, while fact_sentence_2 concerns termination of the policy prior to death, preventing any payouts. They address different scenarios involving benefit eligibility but do not influence each other directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">The rule about paying the death benefit to the estate relies on whether the policy owner exercised their right to name beneficiaries. Without any designation by the owner, the default occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the default recipient of the death benefit when no surviving beneficiary exists and the policy owner has also passed away. This does not relate to the company's duty to respond to information requests.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">Sentence 1 defines the default payout scenario if no beneficiaries survive; it does not relate to the provision of information by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains the outcome if no beneficiary survives the insured and the owner is also deceased, leading to payment to the estate. This situation is unrelated to the policy owner's ability to request riders, which pertains to proactive modifications rather than post-death procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">This statement specifies the default distribution path of the death benefit if no eligible beneficiary remains, while the second statement explains that any modification to how the benefit is distributed requires insurer consent. The first does not influence or rely on the second.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">This statement defines the fallback distribution path if no beneficiary survives and the owner is deceased, focusing on estate inheritance. The second sentence explains the policy owner’s authority to determine the form of disbursement once a beneficiary is designated.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">This statement specifies the default recipient of the death benefit if no beneficiary survives and the policy owner is deceased. The second sentence explains that any chosen settlement option must comply with the insurer’s defined settlement terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
