<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="8173134a-e29e-4aa3-9deb-7944def59471">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains the policy owner’s unilateral power to amend beneficiary details via written notice. This action has no bearing on how interest accumulates post-mortem, as defined in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to alter the beneficiary designation relies on having a clear definition of who constitutes a beneficiary under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s ability to change beneficiaries anytime provides them with control over who receives the death benefit, ensuring alignment with current intentions, especially important given the contingent payout scenario outlined in the other statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner can update beneficiaries at any time, but if none survive and the owner is deceased, the benefit goes to the estate—a separate contingency unrelated to the act of changing beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to initiate a beneficiary change through a written request, and this action triggers immediate生效 (effectiveness) once signed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to initiate a beneficiary change through a written request, and this action automatically takes legal effect once received by the insurer, even if the insured has passed away prior to processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES_EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the general right to change beneficiaries anytime. Fact_sentence_2 refines this by specifying that such changes are permitted throughout the insured’s life, reinforcing temporal applicability without contradiction.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to initiate a beneficiary change through a written request, and this action triggers immediate生效 (effectiveness) once signed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to initiate a beneficiary change through a written request, and this change becomes legally binding once received by the insurer, even if the insured has passed away before processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary does not affect the policy owner’s right to assign the policy. This right remains intact regardless of who is named as beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence explains the process for changing beneficiaries, while the second clarifies the insurer's limited liability concerning assignments. There is no direct connection between updating beneficiaries and the legal validity of an assignment.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary is a unilateral action by the policy owner, independent of tax considerations tied to assigning the policy. The act of changing beneficiaries does not inherently involve or trigger tax responsibilities managed by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to change beneficiaries is contingent upon compliance with any existing assignment agreements, meaning such changes may not proceed independently if an assignment has been made.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary involves updating personal designations without affecting the existence of the policy itself. This action stands independently from the decision to cancel the entire policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary does not affect the conditions under which coverage terminates; cancellation ends coverage independently of beneficiary designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary does not affect the validity or continuation of the policy itself. Cancellation results in the end of all benefits, irrespective of prior beneficiary designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary designation is a separate administrative action from handling unearned premiums. The process described in sentence 1 does not affect or relate to the financial provisions outlined in sentence 2 regarding refunds.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change a beneficiary does not influence or rely on the right to obtain a policy copy. These are independent administrative privileges available to the policy owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary designation allows the policy owner to update who receives benefits upon death. This action is unrelated to accessing historical premium data, which supports financial transparency rather than beneficiary management.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">Changing beneficiaries through a written request is a concrete manifestation of the broader right to request beneficiary designations held by the policy owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries is one specific exercise of ownership control, while requesting riders represents another form of customization available to the policy owner. These rights operate independently within the framework of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">After the policy owner submits a written request to change a beneficiary, the company is obligated to provide the necessary information regarding the process or outcome within a reasonable period.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESPONDS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary requires a formal request, enabling the policy owner to update who will receive the death benefit; once designated, the owner can then select how that benefit is disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to submit a written request to change beneficiaries. In turn, the company is obligated to respond by providing relevant information under legal requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESPONDS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">Changing beneficiaries is a unilateral action by the policy owner requiring only a written request, whereas altering settlement options requires prior company approval. The two processes operate independently under separate procedural requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary is a separate administrative action from selecting a settlement option. The ability to designate a beneficiary does not influence or constrain how settlement options are elected.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains the method by which the Policy Owner can fulfill the right described in fact_sentence_1—changing beneficiaries via a written request—making it actionable under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change the beneficiary demonstrates one practical application of the owner’s power to assign the policy, showing how specific actions stem from overarching ownership rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to designate or change beneficiaries underscores the Policy Owner’s comprehensive control, which includes the concurrent right to terminate the policy entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The Owner’s power to change the Beneficiary underscores their autonomy over key policy elements, consistent with having the right to thoroughly review the policy initially.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries requires having legal ownership; therefore, fact_sentence_2 depends on the ownership framework established in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary via written request complies with the broader policy requirement that all amendments must be properly executed and signed by an authorized company representative.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">Although policy changes generally require official approval, the specific act of changing a beneficiary is permitted directly by the policy owner via written submission, consistent with the requirement for documented authorization.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The ability to update beneficiary designations via written request complements the rule requiring official authorization for policy changes, demonstrating adherence to procedural integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary has no impact on whether a lapsed policy can be reinstated; these actions relate to different aspects of policy management—beneficiary designations versus renewal eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary does not affect eligibility for policy reinstatement, nor does it influence whether insurability can be demonstrated later. These actions serve separate administrative functions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary has no bearing on premium payment requirements or reinstatement eligibility. Reinstating a lapsed policy depends solely on financial compliance, unrelated to beneficiary assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">While changing beneficiaries grants flexibility in estate planning, it does not affect the conditions under which past-due premiums incur interest upon reinstatement. The two provisions address different facets of policy administration.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">The ability to designate or change a beneficiary does not affect the requirement to maintain premium payments to keep the policy active.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
