</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="8173134a-e29e-4aa3-9deb-7944def59471">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains when a beneficiary change becomes active—upon signing—but it has no bearing on whether interest accrues from the date of death, which is governed by separate legal provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change hinges on proper identification of the designated individual, making the initial definition critical to interpreting the timing clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">Sentence 2 sets the activation timeline for beneficiary changes, which could influence whether the designated individual qualifies under the conditions outlined in Sentence 1 regarding surviving beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIMING_INFLUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary changes become effective at signing, independent of future events like the insured’s survival. This contrasts with the first sentence, which applies only when no survivorship occurs, making it a contingency rather than an action-triggered event.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIMING_DEPENDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The moment a beneficiary change is signed determines its effectiveness, relying on the prior right granted to the policy owner to make such a change.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that a beneficiary change takes effect upon signing is strengthened by the condition that the insured’s survival status at receipt is irrelevant, ensuring continuity of intent regardless of timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that a beneficiary change takes effect upon signing relies on the policy owner having the authority to initiate such a change through a written request while the insured is alive.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">This sentence reiterates the exact same condition regarding the effectiveness of a beneficiary change, confirming consistency in timing from the moment of signature.</data>
  <data key="d4">REITERATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The change of beneficiary takes effect from the signing date, and this rule applies even if the insured has passed away before the company receives the request.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect on the signature date, but this does not address potential tax impacts associated with assigning the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary is an action taken by the policy owner that occurs upon signature, independent of the policy’s assignment capability. This reflects one aspect of control over benefits distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect on the date it is signed, but this does not imply anything about the legal enforceability or validation of assignments made under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect upon signature, independent of the policy being canceled later. The ability to cancel the policy exists separately from beneficiary designation procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">A beneficiary change becomes effective upon signing, but if the policy has been assigned, those rights may be restricted by the terms of the assignment agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect on the date it is signed, independent of other policy events like cancellation. This action does not influence or depend on whether coverage is later canceled.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change upon signing does not influence or relate to the policy owner’s right to request a copy of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect at the time of signing, independent of any later cancellation event. Cancellation terminates all future benefits but does not affect prior beneficiary designations unless explicitly revised.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect upon signing, independent of other policy events like cancellations or settlements. This action does not influence whether unearned premiums are refunded.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">Change of beneficiary effectiveness is governed by the signing date, independent of accessing historical premiums. This detail relates to administrative procedures rather than data retrieval.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">A beneficiary change requires prior authorization from the policy owner, who holds the legal right to make such requests. Without this right, the change could not occur at all.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The timing of a beneficiary change taking effect upon signing does not impact the insurer’s duty to provide requested information within a reasonable period.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary becomes effective upon signature, but selecting or altering a settlement option requires prior approval from the insurance company, making it an administrative step separate from beneficiary updates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect upon signature, enabling the policy owner to control who receives benefits; this decision supports the subsequent choice of how those benefits are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change upon signing is independent of the company’s duty to provide information under law. This statement concerns procedural validity rather than data disclosure.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect on the date it is signed, reflecting procedural authority under the policy. This aligns with the broader right of the policy owner to manage and modify policy terms, including requesting additional riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect at the time of signing, independent of settlement choices. The availability of specific settlement options does not influence the timing or validity of beneficiary changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="90ec6e29-a29c-4e3c-8d1b-c21dc571dc89">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s provision allowing immediate effectiveness of beneficiary changes supports the current beneficiary setup but also implies flexibility, enabling adjustments to Elaine M. Hughes’ status as primary beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="d13623e0-a45f-4060-82e1-dbdfcb46c827">
  <data key="d3">The rule that beneficiary changes take effect when signed supports the legitimacy and enforceability of naming Morgan L. Hughes as the contingent beneficiary in the original policy setup.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary changes taking effect at signing could impact who receives proceeds from an accelerated death benefit payment, making the timing of such requests relevant even though the rider itself does not require beneficiary approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64" target="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec">
  <data key="d3">While beneficiary changes take effect upon signing, they remain invalid unless formally documented and approved by an authorized representative of Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
