  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change regardless of the insured’s survival, noted in fact_sentence_2, depends on the policy owner having the legal authority to initiate such a change, which is confirmed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries independently of the insured’s survival supports the notion that the policy owner retains significant autonomy, reinforcing their capacity to assign the policy without restriction.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The capacity to change the beneficiary underscores the Owner’s independence from the Insured’s condition, which aligns with the Owner’s broader right to initiate cancellation at any time during the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">Knowing that beneficiary changes take immediate effect—even posthumously—underscores why the Owner should exercise their examination right to confirm understanding of these irreversible actions prior to any modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_UNDERSTANDING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries independently of the insured’s survival depends on clear ownership; without a designated owner, the insured automatically assumes this role per the provision in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Although beneficiary changes become effective upon company receipt regardless of the insured’s condition, they remain subject to the overarching rule that only authorized officers may validate such changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary changes taking effect independently of the insured’s survival status do not violate the prohibition against unapproved alterations, as these changes follow established procedures through the designated policy owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIES_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 shows that beneficiary changes take effect upon submission, aligning with fact_sentence_1’s rule requiring written authorization from officials, thereby validating the process under controlled oversight.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary changes take immediate effect upon receipt by the insurer even if the insured has passed away, which does not impact the conditions under which a lapsed policy can be reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary changes are effective upon receipt by the company irrespective of the insured’s condition, whereas reinstating a policy depends on demonstrating future insurability. These mechanisms serve distinct administrative purposes without overlapping logic.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary changes take effect immediately upon receipt, regardless of the insured’s condition, and do not affect the requirement to repay delinquent premiums for policy reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary designation changes take effect immediately upon receipt, irrespective of the insured’s condition, whereas interest on unpaid premiums applies only at reinstatement—these processes relate to different stages and functions of policy administration.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary becomes effective upon the insurer receiving the request, even if the insured has passed away, irrespective of whether the policy remains active due to unpaid premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49cec9ab-dc45-4017-9fbb-73158dbcac91" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">does not affect effectiveness of change</data>
</edge>
