</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="8173134a-e29e-4aa3-9deb-7944def59471">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains the policy owner's authority to update beneficiaries prior to the insured's passing, independent of how or when funds are paid out afterward.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to change the beneficiary relies on having a clear understanding of who the current beneficiary is, as defined in the initial statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner can change the beneficiary at any time while the insured is alive. This authority ensures that the intended recipient aligns with current wishes, particularly relevant in cases where the original beneficiary does not survive the insured—making it possible for the policy owner to receive the benefit under such circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner can update the beneficiary anytime while the insured is alive through a formal written request. This action influences future distribution outcomes but does not affect the default rule described in the first sentence regarding estate payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that beneficiary changes are allowed during the insured’s lifetime, providing contextual limitation. Fact_sentence_1 affirms the broader authority to make such changes via written request, encompassing the scenario described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to change the beneficiary at any time during the insured’s lifetime provides the basis for the rule that such changes become effective once signed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONED_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a written request allows the beneficiary change to become effective upon receipt by the company, regardless of the insured’s current health or survival status.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to initiate a beneficiary change through a written request, and this action triggers immediate生效 (effectiveness) once signed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to initiate a beneficiary change through a written request, and this action automatically becomes effective once received by the insurer, even if the insured has passed away before or after submission.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries allows the policy owner to update who receives benefits upon the insured's death. This action operates independently from the power to assign the entire policy to another party.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_RIGHT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary involves a written request from the policy owner but does not relate to the legal validity of an assignment, which falls outside the company's accountability.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary involves a written request from the policy owner but does not involve tax responsibilities tied to assigning the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's ability to change the beneficiary is contingent on whether an assignment has been made; such assignments impose limitations on the owner's rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary is an action related to estate planning and does not affect the overall validity or continuation of the policy itself. The right to cancel the policy exists independently of beneficiary modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary does not affect the conditions under which coverage terminates; cancellation leads to termination independently of beneficiary designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary does not impact the outcome of policy cancellation; the ability to update beneficiaries exists independently of whether the policy is later cancelled.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary involves a procedural update initiated by the policy owner; it does not affect or trigger any refund of unearned premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary involves updating designation details, whereas obtaining a policy copy allows review of existing terms; one does not logically depend on the other but supports independent administrative control.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries is unrelated to requesting premium payment history. These are independent administrative rights under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary is a specific manifestation of the broader right to request beneficiary designations, illustrating how the policy owner exercises control over beneficiary assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary is one specific action within the range of rights held by the policy owner, who also possesses the general power to request additional riders such as an Accelerated Death Benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to initiate a beneficiary change through a written request; in turn, the company commits to responding promptly by supplying necessary information.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESPONDS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to submit a written request to update beneficiaries. In response, the company provides relevant information compliant with legal requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESPONDS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary requires a written request from the policy owner, establishing who receives benefits; once designated, the policy owner can then select how those benefits are distributed.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary requires a written request but does not affect how benefits are settled later. The availability of settlement options depends on predefined company terms, independent of beneficiary changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary requires only a written request from the policy owner, while altering the settlement option necessitates prior approval from the insurance company. These processes are independent but similarly governed by formal procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="b12e9b16-bbb5-4f46-b60c-3a7549f861c6">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the policy owner to change the beneficiary relies on being legally recognized as the owner, which occurs automatically if no name is provided, per fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written authorization by an authorized officer ensures that beneficiary changes—like those permitted in fact_sentence_2—are formally documented and legally binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">While the policy allows owners to initiate beneficiary changes freely, these actions still require submission through official channels per the restriction that no unauthorized agent or broker may alter the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">While the first statement restricts waiver of policy provisions, the second allows beneficiary changes through proper documentation, demonstrating that such modifications fall under permitted administrative processes rather than provision waivers.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="fb72e3f0-f7b4-42f1-8874-ebac56171d8b">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries at any time remains unaffected by whether the policy has been reinstated after lapse or not.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="e6dc59e3-a8f4-4f56-940d-46199cdc1c83">
  <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary has no impact on reinstatement requirements, as it does not alter financial obligations like unpaid premiums or interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="3aea6d6e-6546-4579-b452-cbd38accf2bf">
  <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary does not affect the need to prove insurability for reinstatement after a lapse. While one involves updating beneficiary designations, the other pertains to restoring coverage eligibility through medical evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="afe75990-53e6-4092-8595-3ddaed9d18bc">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change the beneficiary independently of payment history ensures flexibility in estate planning, even when premiums are delinquent and reinstatement conditions apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386" target="18dba2f2-8e4f-4bcc-9c25-79f3830d6409">
  <data key="d3">While the policy can lapse due to missed premiums, the ability to designate or change a beneficiary remains intact as long as the policy is active. The existence of a beneficiary clause does not influence the financial conditions required to keep the policy in force.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9cc58ef0-8ed1-4b41-8d1a-14afaa2d5669" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">controls_record_of</data>
</edge>
