  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="fea8b3d7-129b-43b4-91da-ed2dea15f4a2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">RIDER</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="8173134a-e29e-4aa3-9deb-7944def59471">
  <data key="d3">This statement specifies that beneficiary changes become effective upon signing, independent of any subsequent events like death or interest accruals.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">The timing rule for beneficiary changes relies on knowing who currently holds the role, making the initial definition foundational to applying the effectiveness condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">Sentence 2 states that beneficiary changes become effective on the signing date, enabling prompt adjustments. This timeliness supports the enforcement of policies like the one described in sentence 1, where the policy owner inherits benefits only if designated and still alive after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect at signing, ensuring timely implementation. This contrasts with the default case described in the first sentence where no beneficiary survives, highlighting how proactive changes prevent estate distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The moment a beneficiary change is signed determines its effectiveness, relying on the prior right granted to the policy owner to make such changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">This sentence repeats the prior statement verbatim, reinforcing that the change takes effect on the date of signing, maintaining internal coherence within the chunk.</data>
  <data key="d4">REITERATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 identifies the signing of the request as the triggering event for a beneficiary change. This aligns with fact sentence 1, which confirms the change takes effect even if the insured has passed away, validating the significance of the signature date over survival status.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">The moment a beneficiary change is signed determines its effectiveness, relying on the prior authorization granted to the policy owner to make such changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The change of beneficiary takes effect from the signing date, and this rule applies even if the insured has passed away before the company receives the request.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary is an action taken by the policy owner that occurs upon signature, independent of the policy’s assignment capability. This reflects one aspect of control over benefits distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect on the date it is signed, but this does not imply anything about the legal enforceability or validation of assignments made under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect on the signature date, but this does not address potential tax impacts associated with assigning the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">A beneficiary change becomes effective upon signing, but if the policy has been assigned, those rights may be restricted by the terms of the assignment agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect upon signature, independent of the policy being canceled later. The ability to cancel the policy exists separately from beneficiary designation procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect on the date it is signed, independent of other policy events like cancellation. This action does not influence or depend on whether coverage is later canceled.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect at the time of signing, independent of any later cancellation event. Cancellation terminates all future benefits but does not affect prior beneficiary designations unless explicitly revised.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect upon signing, independent of other policy events like cancellations or settlements. This action does not influence whether unearned premiums are refunded.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change upon signing does not influence or relate to the policy owner’s right to request a copy of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">Change of beneficiary effectiveness is governed by the signing date, independent of accessing historical premiums. This detail relates to administrative procedures rather than data retrieval.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">A beneficiary change requires prior authorization from the policy owner, who holds the legal right to make such requests. Without this right, the change could not occur at all.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect on the date it is signed, reflecting procedural authority under the policy. This aligns with the broader right of the policy owner to manage and modify policy terms, including requesting additional riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The timing of a beneficiary change taking effect upon signing does not impact the insurer’s duty to provide requested information within a reasonable period.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change upon signing is independent of the company’s duty to provide information under law. This statement concerns procedural validity rather than data disclosure.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect upon signature, enabling the policy owner to control who receives benefits; this decision supports the subsequent choice of how those benefits are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary becomes effective upon signature, but selecting or altering a settlement option requires prior approval from the insurance company, making it an administrative step separate from beneficiary updates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary takes effect at the time of signing, independent of settlement choices. The availability of specific settlement options does not influence the timing or validity of beneficiary changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="90ec6e29-a29c-4e3c-8d1b-c21dc571dc89">
  <data key="d3">The rule that beneficiary changes take effect upon signature allows for potential modification of Elaine M. Hughes’ role as primary beneficiary, meaning her entitlement is conditional on no subsequent change being made.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_CHANGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="d13623e0-a45f-4060-82e1-dbdfcb46c827">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of changing beneficiaries—such as naming Morgan L. Hughes as contingent—is governed by the requirement that the change be signed, making the process described in fact_sentence_2 essential to establishing the beneficiary hierarchy mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary designation changes take immediate effect upon signing, meaning any future claims—such as those triggered by the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider—will go to the most recently designated beneficiary, even if prior designations were different.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="1d72c661-13a0-42a4-ac28-933c7e831eec">
  <data key="d3">Any alteration to the beneficiary designation must comply with the written-and-signed requirement set forth in the original contract terms, ensuring legal enforceability despite immediate生效 upon signature.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change upon signing (fact_sentence_2) depends on the policy owner having the legal authority to make such changes, which is affirmed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries upon signing reinforces the policy owner’s autonomy, aligning with their explicit right to assign the policy and exercise full ownership privileges.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries underscores the policy owner’s autonomy, which includes the related right to cancel the policy at any time during the initial review period.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The immediate effectiveness of beneficiary changes underscores the importance of the owner’s examination right, ensuring accurate and timely modifications based on understanding.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS_DECISION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="83582c0a-3af4-481f-98d3-0102afbf3328" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">signs_request_for_change_of_beneficiary</data>
</edge>
