</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">This statement grants the policy owner authority to assign the policy; this power exists independently of how the death benefit is distributed after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner holds the authority to assign the policy via written consent, enabling third-party transfers of interest. This capability does not affect the outcome described in the first sentence regarding estate payouts after multiple deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Assigning the policy does not alter the policy owner’s ongoing ability to update beneficiary designations unless explicitly restricted by the assignment agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">Assigning the policy allows transfer of interests under the contract; however, this does not affect how or when beneficiary changes become effective, which depends solely on the signing date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 grants the policy owner the right to assign the policy through formal documentation. This right complements the flexibility shown in fact_sentence_1, where beneficiary changes take immediate effect, illustrating the extent of the owner’s decision-making powers.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">The ability to assign the policy grants the owner control over transferring legal interests in the contract. This right exists alongside—yet separately from—the authority to modify beneficiary designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_RIGHT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">Assigning the policy allows transfer of interests under the contract; however, this does not affect how or when beneficiary changes become effective, which depends solely on the signing date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 grants the policy owner the right to assign the policy through formal documentation. This right complements the flexibility shown in fact_sentence_1, where beneficiary changes take immediate effect, illustrating the extent of the owner’s decision-making powers.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to assign the policy via written request; however, the company disclaims responsibility for any resulting tax outcomes associated with that action.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to assign the policy through a written request, though the company explicitly avoids assuming liability for confirming whether the assignment meets legal standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to transfer ownership through a formal written assignment. This action restricts the future exercise of rights by both the owner and the original beneficiary according to the assigned terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy allows the owner to transfer ownership interests, whereas the right to cancel permits termination of coverage. These are separate administrative options available to the policy owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to transfer ownership interests via written assignment, independent of whether coverage is later cancelled.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to assign the policy, but this does not affect the outcome of cancellation, which results in termination of future benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s ability to assign the policy is unrelated to the handling of unearned premiums. Refunds occur based on legal provisions independent of assignment actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states the Policy Owner’s authority to assign the policy, while fact_sentence_2 highlights their right to obtain a copy of the policy documents. These reflect separate but complementary aspects of ownership control.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner can assign the policy to another party through a formal written submission. This action does not affect their independent right to obtain historical premium data from the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">The ability to assign the policy reflects transfer of ownership interests, while the right to request riders allows customization of coverage terms. Both empower the policy owner but operate independently within the framework of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to assign the policy through a formal written request. The company complies with such requests by providing necessary documentation or confirmation, ensuring adherence to regulatory standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to assign the policy via written request, but the company’s obligation to respond with information does not depend on such an action. This statement reflects a general service commitment unrelated to assignment procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">The ability to assign the policy allows the owner to transfer legal interest, which could influence how beneficiary designations are managed or enforced. This reflects broader control over the policy’s disposition beyond just selecting recipients.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the policy owner can assign the policy through a written request approved by the company. This implies procedural compliance similar to other formal requests like changing settlement options, which also requires company approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO_APPROVAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy allows the owner to transfer ownership interests, which could indirectly affect how benefits are distributed later. This action does not alter the chosen settlement method unless explicitly changed afterward.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to assign the policy, but such an action does not affect the availability or modification of settlement options, which remain governed by separate contractual terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The capacity to assign the policy supports the flexibility implied in changing beneficiaries, illustrating the comprehensive nature of the owner’s control over the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the method for exercising the assignment right mentioned in fact_sentence_1, detailing that a written assignment accepted by the company is required to transfer ownership interests.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The capacity to assign the policy underscores the breadth of ownership rights, which includes the authority to terminate the policy through cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The Owner’s power to assign the policy depends on having first examined it; without the initial examination right, meaningful exercise of assignment would lack proper foundation.</data>
