  <data key="d3">This sentence explains that beneficiary and owner rights are limited by assignment agreements, but it does not address when or how interest accumulates post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">If an assignment exists, it overrides or limits the beneficiary’s rights; thus, the beneficiary’s role is dependent on prior administrative actions involving ownership transfer.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">The rights of the policy owner and beneficiary are constrained by the terms of any assignment, meaning even if the owner would normally inherit the death benefit, an assignment might prevent this outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">The rights of both the policy owner and beneficiary are limited by the existence of a policy assignment. In cases where the owner dies without a survivor, the assigned terms might determine whether the estate inherits the death benefit instead.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS_OUTCOME</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Any attempt by the policy owner to change beneficiaries may be restricted or governed by prior assignments, making the ownership right subordinate to assigned contractual conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The rights of the owner and beneficiary are constrained by assignment terms, meaning even a properly signed beneficiary change might not override binding assignment conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">Ownership rights, including the right to change beneficiaries, are constrained by prior assignments. This limitation applies regardless of whether the change occurs while the insured is alive or after death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">Assignment agreements restrict the policy owner’s authority to modify beneficiaries, thereby limiting the practical exercise of the right described in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The rights of the owner and beneficiary are constrained by assignment terms, meaning even a properly signed beneficiary change might not override binding assignment conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">Ownership rights, including the right to change beneficiaries, are constrained by prior assignments. This limitation applies regardless of whether the change occurs while the insured is alive or after death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy owner can legally assign the policy, the resulting transfer limits the scope of rights available to both the owner and the beneficiary under the new arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">The rights of the owner and beneficiary are limited by the terms of the assignment, which implies that the company cannot ensure such assignments' legal standing or enforceability.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">Assignment terms govern the rights of the owner and beneficiary, making it necessary to consider potential tax impacts even if the company does not assume responsibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence highlights that ownership and beneficiary rights are constrained by prior assignments. The second sentence asserts the owner’s independent power to terminate the policy through written notice, irrespective of such constraints.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">The right of the owner and beneficiary may be limited if the policy has been assigned, but this does not affect the outcome of cancellation, which independently terminates coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">The ownership right to obtain a policy copy may be restricted if the policy has been assigned, as assignments can limit certain owner privileges.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns restrictions on owner and beneficiary rights when a policy is assigned. The second sentence explains how unearned premiums are handled if refunded, based on legal requirements. There is no direct connection between the two topics.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">The right of the owner and beneficiary may be limited by an assignment, but if the policy is canceled, those rights cease altogether since no further benefits are paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">TERMINATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence limits rights based on assignment terms, but does not influence the second sentence about timely provision of information by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence limits ownership rights when an assignment exists; the second asserts the Owner’s authority to seek supplemental benefits. These ideas relate to different aspects of policy control but do not logically depend on each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns restrictions on ownership and beneficiary rights when an assignment exists. The second sentence pertains to the company’s duty to release information compliant with law. There is no direct causal or sequential link between them.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence limits the rights of the owner and beneficiary based on any existing assignment, whereas the second sentence asserts a separate administrative right of the owner to obtain premium payment details. These statements address different aspects of ownership without mutual dependence.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">The right to request beneficiary designations is one of the core privileges held by the policy owner, though it may be limited if the policy has been assigned. Assignment introduces constraints on how those rights can be exercised.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to determine the death benefit payout method is contingent upon not being restricted by prior assignments, which govern the distribution of benefits under certain conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">The right of the owner regarding assignments may limit how benefits are distributed, but it does not affect whether a settlement option change needs company approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">The right of the policy owner and beneficiary may be restricted by prior assignments, which could affect how settlement choices are exercised. This constraint indirectly influences the implementation of any elected settlement method.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
