  <data key="d4">RIDER</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="8173134a-e29e-4aa3-9deb-7944def59471">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner can cancel the policy anytime via written notice, but this action has no bearing on how interest accumulates after the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to cancel the policy independently does not alter or rely on how beneficiaries are designated under the terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">This statement grants the policy owner the unilateral authority to end the insurance coverage at any time via written notice. The existence of this right has no bearing on how the death benefit is distributed after the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">This statement grants the policy owner the unilateral right to cancel the policy at any time through a written request. This action would affect future benefits but does not impact the conditions under which the death benefit is paid to an estate.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Canceling the policy terminates coverage and ends all associated rights, including future beneficiary changes. However, such cancellation does not inherently affect prior beneficiary designations unless explicitly stated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">Canceling the policy at any time is an option available to the policy owner, but it does not affect how or when beneficiary changes become effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to cancel the policy at any moment by providing written notice. This right operates independently of beneficiary designation changes, which also become effective without regard to the insured’s survival.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">Canceling the policy terminates its existence entirely, rendering subsequent beneficiary changes irrelevant since the policy would no longer exist. However, such a decision is made independently of whether beneficiaries have been changed previously.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">Canceling the policy at any time is an option available to the policy owner, but it does not affect how or when beneficiary changes become effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to cancel the policy at any moment by providing written notice. This right operates independently of beneficiary designation changes, which also become effective without regard to the insured’s survival.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Cancelling the policy terminates coverage entirely, while assigning it transfers control to another party—these are mutually exclusive actions that do not rely on each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to cancel the policy has no bearing on whether the company assumes responsibility for assignments. Each clause governs independent aspects of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence states the policy owner’s unilateral right to terminate coverage through a written notice, independent of any tax-related responsibilities tied to assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence confirms the policy owner’s authority to cancel coverage anytime via written request. This autonomy could potentially override or limit the impact of earlier assignments affecting beneficiary rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREEMPTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to end the policy through a written request, resulting in the immediate cessation of insurance coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to terminate coverage anytime through a formal request, resulting in the cessation of all future benefit payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">When the policy owner cancels the policy, it initiates a process that results in refunds of unearned premiums according to applicable laws.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 details the policy owner’s authority to terminate coverage unilaterally. This stands independently from the right described in fact sentence 2, which allows access to policy documents.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cancel the policy reflects broad control over its existence, enabling the owner to terminate coverage whenever desired. This autonomy supports the broader capacity to manage beneficiary designations, ensuring alignment with current intentions.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states the Policy Owner’s authority to terminate the policy, while fact_sentence_2 highlights their right to obtain historical premium data. These reflect separate aspects of control over the policy but do not logically depend on one another.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states the policy owner’s power to terminate coverage unilaterally. This autonomy supports the broader capacity described in fact_sentence_2, where the owner can seek supplemental provisions such as riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to terminate coverage at any time through a written request. In response to such requests, the company commits to providing necessary information promptly.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the unilateral right to terminate coverage at any time through a formal request. This action does not affect the company’s duty to comply with regulatory mandates regarding disclosure and record availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">The right to cancel the policy has no direct impact on how the death benefit is settled. These are separate administrative choices available to the policy owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to terminate coverage unilaterally, but changing the settlement method remains constrained by available options defined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the unilateral authority to terminate coverage at any time through written notice. This action stands independently from decisions regarding how benefits are settled after death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cancel the policy underscores the Policy Owner’s ultimate control, which includes modifying beneficiaries, ensuring alignment with the owner’s autonomy over the policy’s structure and benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cancel the policy underscores the owner’s authority over its lifecycle, making the power to assign it more meaningful, as assignments require active ownership.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">Fact Sentence 2 specifies the mechanism and timing for cancellation—submitting a written request anytime—which directly supports and operationalizes the broader right described in Fact Sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPANDS_UPON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The power to cancel the policy anytime reinforces the significance of the initial examination right, allowing the Owner to review terms thoroughly before deciding to retain or terminate coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37b99e89-7ad8-49e1-bb5a-cb10a92ac37a" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_cancellation_right</data>
</edge>
