<edge source="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601" target="8173134a-e29e-4aa3-9deb-7944def59471">
  <data key="d3">Cancelling the policy stops future benefits, independent of any interest calculations tied to the date of death. There is no direct influence of cancellation on how interest accumulates post-mortem.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">Cancellation results in cessation of all benefits, rendering the prior designation of a beneficiary irrelevant since no payouts occur after termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">Cancellation ends all future benefits, meaning even if the policy owner qualifies under survivorship conditions, no death benefit will be issued after cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
