  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the Policy Owner can obtain historical premium data, while fact sentence 2 indicates they can retrieve details about designated beneficiaries. Both pertain to access rights over different aspects of policy administration.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 involves the Policy Owner’s right to obtain financial transaction data from the policy, while fact sentence 2 extends this access to contractual additions like riders. Together, they reflect comprehensive transparency rights over different types of policy documents.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
