  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to request beneficiary designations allows them to influence who receives the death benefit, thereby potentially preventing the need for payment to themselves under the contingency specified in the other statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to designate beneficiaries directly affects the conditions under which the death benefit may go to the estate instead of an individual beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">The right to request beneficiary designations encompasses the specific action of changing them via a formal submission, making it foundational to the process described in the other statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENCOMPASSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
