</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">Requesting beneficiary designations requires knowledge of policy details, which the Policy Owner can obtain by requesting a copy of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 highlights the Policy Owner’s authority to view beneficiary designations, whereas fact sentence 1 refers to retrieving past premium payment records. These are independent yet complementary rights concerning policy transparency.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's right to request beneficiary designations triggers the insurer's responsibility to provide the necessary information in a timely manner.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESPONDS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 highlights the Policy Owner’s authority over beneficiary assignments, while fact sentence 2 extends this autonomy to include selecting supplementary benefits such as riders. Together, they reflect the breadth of decision-making power vested in the Policy Owner regarding policy customization.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner exercises their right to request beneficiary designations, prompting the company to comply by providing the necessary information according to law.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">The right to designate beneficiaries allows the Policy Owner to determine who receives benefits; this foundational choice directly informs subsequent decisions about how those benefits are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to designate beneficiaries does not affect the process or eligibility for changing settlement options, which are governed by separate contractual terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may initiate beneficiary designations, but changes to settlement options require prior approval from the insurance company, highlighting separate procedural requirements within policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 highlights the specific capability to request beneficiary changes, reinforcing the foundational right stated in fact_sentence_1. Without this actionable power, the right would lack practical application.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">The ability to designate beneficiaries complements the right to assign the policy, since assigning it often involves transferring future benefit distribution decisions to a new owner who can update those designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to designate beneficiaries supports the overall autonomy of the policy owner, which includes the separate right to terminate the policy at any time during its term.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The owner’s power to request beneficiary designations relies on having access to the policy through the examination right, enabling proper management of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a19fbee-0bb7-4333-8eac-e0593595e009" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is subject to request by Policy Owner</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e004deaa-f35f-4425-b892-091fd97ef581" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">requests beneficiary designation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49fed75e-8771-495e-9340-ae879782973d" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is used to request</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="de39d0bc-13a4-4b42-bc94-711f6ed8e1ad">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="a042da88-f269-414d-80e2-2327fc39ab05">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="d4aab2fa-3ae0-40b8-803b-7908a2d5cefb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="91d25b60-f533-46da-9fe8-b15e0ba87488">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="bd427507-c3ac-4735-84df-785e05614b45">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="4460026a-1b4d-48d0-89c2-ece2774a818f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="c4c59cc0-e959-4aec-9e93-b7e03f1112a2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="73f40b38-bbb9-44ed-995f-9c5441912af4">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="3213f233-8bb0-4769-958f-7da716bae2b2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">RIDER</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="8173134a-e29e-4aa3-9deb-7944def59471">
  <data key="d3">The right to request riders allows customization of policy benefits before death, but it does not influence how interest accumulates post-mortem. There is no logical dependence between accessing rider options and interest calculation timelines.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to request riders does not affect how beneficiaries are defined; it pertains to modifying policy terms rather than identifying recipients of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">This statement highlights the policy owner’s right to obtain supplementary benefits through riders, but it does not influence or explain the conditions under which the death benefit is distributed.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states the policy owner may request riders such as an Accelerated Death Benefit, allowing flexibility in benefit access during life. However, this capability does not affect the conditions under which the death benefit is distributed to the estate, as outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Requesting riders allows the policy owner to expand benefits, such as accessing accelerated death benefits, whereas changing beneficiaries involves updating recipient details without altering core policy terms. Both reflect discretionary powers of the owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may request riders or endorsements, demonstrating their control over policy enhancements. This includes modifying beneficiary designations indirectly via new provisions, though not affecting the immediate effectiveness of existing changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may request additional riders such as an Accelerated Death Benefit, which allows early payout upon terminal illness. This right operates independently of beneficiary change procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may request riders or endorsements, demonstrating their control over policy enhancements. This includes modifying beneficiary designations indirectly via new provisions, though not affecting the immediate effectiveness of existing changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may request additional riders such as an Accelerated Death Benefit, which allows early payout upon terminal illness. This right operates independently of beneficiary change procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">The right to request riders includes potential modifications like adding benefits tied to beneficiary designations, but changing a beneficiary itself does not require a rider and operates independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Requesting riders gives the policy owner flexibility to enhance coverage, such as adding an accelerated death benefit, which could later influence decisions about assigning the policy if future financial needs arise.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's right to request riders or endorsements is independent of whether the company assumes responsibility for assignment validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may request additional riders or endorsements, but this right is independent of whether the company assumes responsibility for tax consequences related to assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence highlights the Owner’s power to request riders, while the first notes that such powers may be restricted by prior assignments. The presence of an assignment could potentially limit the exercise of this right.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 highlights the policy owner’s authority to obtain additional features like riders. This right complements the flexibility implied in fact_sentence_1, where the owner can end the policy entirely if desired.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may request riders or endorsements at any time, even after cancellation, though such requests would not restore terminated coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">Requesting riders allows customization of policy benefits, whereas cancellation ends all future payouts. The two concepts relate to different stages of policy control without mutual dependence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to request riders or endorsements is independent of whether unearned premiums are refunded under applicable law.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 enhances the scope of information available to the policy owner beyond just the main policy, reinforcing the right established in fact_sentence_1 by ensuring full transparency about attached provisions such as riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 addresses the Policy Owner’s entitlement to know about additional policy features such as riders, which complements fact sentence 1 by expanding the scope of accessible policy information beyond just premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 addresses the Policy Owner’s ability to add riders, which may influence how beneficiaries receive proceeds; thus, it indirectly supports the context of beneficiary management described in fact sentence 1, though not directly dependent on it.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may initiate requests for additional riders or endorsements, and the insurance company commits to providing the necessary information in a timely manner after receiving such a request.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESPONDS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner may initiate a request for additional riders or endorsements, and the company is obligated to fulfill this request by providing the necessary documentation in compliance with law.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESPONDS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner can request additional benefits like riders, though such actions do not automatically affect settlement method changes, which require separate company approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s right to request riders includes potential access to benefits like an Accelerated Death Benefit, which directly relates to how the death benefit is settled—supporting flexibility in choosing payment methods.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to request riders includes potential access to features affecting settlement options, making it relevant to changes in those options. However, actual implementation depends on predefined terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="67ea902a-000e-45d2-99dd-8a832a20afc4">
  <data key="d3">Requesting riders enhances the functionality of beneficiary designation, allowing the owner to customize payout conditions beyond standard arrangements, thus supporting more flexible beneficiary management.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="4f290f5d-0af6-4495-b93a-b82ca8a810cd">
  <data key="d3">Requesting riders allows the owner to customize the policy, potentially influencing future assignment decisions by altering benefits or conditions associated with the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="3cb3e4ad-67f0-491d-beb0-fbdc5114922d">
  <data key="d3">Requesting riders expands the policy’s functionality, which may influence decisions about cancellation; however, the right to cancel remains intact regardless of rider inclusion, ensuring ultimate flexibility for the owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4" target="07e46b3d-c885-48ba-b6cc-e766aa7d258b">
  <data key="d3">The owner’s ability to request riders depends on having prior access to the policy content; thus, the examination right facilitates meaningful engagement with supplemental options offered under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="91d25b60-f533-46da-9fe8-b15e0ba87488" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_right_to_request_riders_or_endorsements</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3213f233-8bb0-4769-958f-7da716bae2b2" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">can_be_requested_by_policy_owner</data>
