<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="8173134a-e29e-4aa3-9deb-7944def59471">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to determine the death benefit payment method operates independently of when interest starts accruing after the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="03cfef7f-f2a0-44bd-864f-0344e97bc6d0">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s power to select the death benefit settlement method depends on having a clearly designated beneficiary, as specified in the first sentence. Without an identified beneficiary, such choices would lack purpose.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="e6149469-d151-4d22-aff3-fb7f2901e4bd">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s power to choose the settlement method implies control over disbursement terms, which becomes relevant only after determining who qualifies to receive the benefit—such as under the rule stated in the first sentence regarding the policy owner being the recipient if no beneficiary survives.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="0c2f9120-31fb-43ab-81cd-fae794c65930">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has control over choosing how the death benefit is delivered to the beneficiary, reflecting flexibility in settlement options. This contrasts with the first sentence, which specifies what happens only when no eligible beneficiary remains alive at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="1c097ac1-210c-471f-87e7-62f4f7ca9887">
  <data key="d3">Selecting the method of death benefit payment depends on having an established beneficiary; thus, prior beneficiary designation allows for informed choices about settlement options.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">Selecting or modifying the death benefit payment method depends on having active authority over beneficiary designations, such as changing them after signing, ensuring alignment with current intent.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to select the settlement method for the death benefit. This right operates independently of whether a beneficiary change was previously submitted or its timing relative to the insured’s condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">Selecting or modifying the death benefit payment method depends on having active authority over beneficiary designations, such as changing them after signing, ensuring alignment with current intent.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="ea7568f9-97e8-481c-ba9d-673126fb9ca4">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to select the settlement method for the death benefit. This right operates independently of whether a beneficiary change was previously submitted or its timing relative to the insured’s condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="4ec4c4a4-c570-4478-be1c-c95a2d28b386">
  <data key="d3">Selecting the method of death benefit payment depends on having already identified a beneficiary, making it contingent on prior beneficiary designation.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="40cbb338-dde2-44ee-9830-c0c26916330c">
  <data key="d3">Choosing a settlement method determines how the death benefit is delivered after the insured’s passing, independent of whether the policy has been assigned earlier. Assignment does not automatically modify payment preferences.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="376c30b4-9340-49c7-86af-f148910aff82">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence grants the policy owner authority over payment methods for the death benefit, whereas the first clarifies the insurer’s non-liability for assignment validity. The topics are distinct and unrelated in terms of logical progression.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="89ec8af1-a187-47d1-be96-dd8563e25f71">
  <data key="d3">Choosing the method of death benefit payment is unrelated to the company’s disclaimers about tax consequences from assignments. One involves distribution mechanics; the other involves fiscal accountability.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">The existence of an assignment limits the scope of the policy owner’s rights, potentially restricting their ability to unilaterally alter how the death benefit is distributed to the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">Choosing a settlement method for the death benefit does not affect the policy owner’s ability to cancel the policy. The two actions operate independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">The option to select a death benefit payment method exists independently of whether the policy was canceled earlier; it applies only at time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s power to determine the death benefit payment method exists independently of whether the policy is later cancelled, though such control ceases upon cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">Choosing how the death benefit is paid does not affect whether unearned premiums are refunded; these are separate administrative actions governed by distinct provisions in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">Selecting the method for paying the death benefit requires knowledge of policy terms, making access to a policy copy essential for exercising this right effectively.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">Choosing the method for paying the death benefit involves strategic planning based on beneficiary needs; however, this choice is independent of accessing historical premium data.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">Choosing the method of death benefit payout depends on prior beneficiary designation, making it contingent on having established who the intended recipient(s) are.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Choosing how the death benefit is paid influences whether certain riders, such as those enabling early payouts, might be relevant, thus informing decisions about requesting specific endorsements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to determine how the death benefit is paid has no bearing on the company’s duty to deliver information within a reasonable timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">Choosing a death benefit settlement method has no bearing on the company’s responsibility to release information as required by law; they are separate administrative functions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the right to choose or alter the death benefit payment method, but this decision cannot be implemented without prior approval from the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09" target="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has the authority to choose or alter the payment method for the death benefit, but this decision is restricted by the specific settlement options defined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
