  <data key="d3">Electing a settlement option depends only on available plan provisions; it has no bearing on whether a beneficiary can be changed, which remains independently governed by submission of a written request.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="6903f2e1-fcf8-476e-af64-83ccd3093b64">
  <data key="d3">Settlement option elections are governed by the plan’s offered terms, while beneficiary changes become effective upon signing; neither process depends on the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="4f081890-55f2-4345-893f-c638987334c2">
  <data key="d3">Settlement options can only be modified according to the terms specified by the insurer. This restriction does not affect the timing or validity of beneficiary changes, which take effect regardless of the insured’s condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="f0a5245e-9eeb-422b-b2ca-4304e824a7be">
  <data key="d3">Settlement option elections are governed by the plan’s offered terms, while beneficiary changes become effective upon signing; neither process depends on the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
