  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="f292fa61-3d93-4115-9af6-3725ae88913a">
  <data key="d3">Changes to settlement options depend on available plan provisions, meaning such elections cannot override existing contract terms—even if those terms were established through earlier assignments affecting ownership rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="f36a1664-7f6f-4d19-a228-86f3f28f271d">
  <data key="d3">While the policy owner can elect a settlement option, such an action does not affect their existing right to cancel the policy entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="39685e64-b943-45f1-8db8-988a6da844bd">
  <data key="d3">Settlement option changes are bound by contract terms, even if coverage has been canceled; however, such changes may only apply when benefits are payable, which requires active coverage unless otherwise specified.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="2ff34d5f-b479-4e87-94c4-d2a540372601">
  <data key="d3">Settlement options are constrained by policy provisions, so changing them has no effect once coverage is cancelled and benefits cease entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="1241bca4-a181-4a4e-9fe3-1834756b497c">
  <data key="d3">Changing a settlement option depends on available terms but is independent of whether unearned premiums are refunded.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="5e7be213-5b9a-4b27-abe4-07034548f8e7">
  <data key="d3">Understanding settlement option terms requires access to policy details, so the ability to request a policy copy facilitates compliance with and awareness of settlement-related requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="1c612b00-c764-4d60-9e00-5642ec5e4c36">
  <data key="d3">Changing a settlement option depends solely on available terms and does not require or rely on accessing premium payment history, making it independent of such record requests.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="9a4ee5a5-54a6-4cfd-82d7-4f61d67a4610">
  <data key="d3">Changing a settlement option depends on available terms but does not impact the policy owner’s authority to designate or modify beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="70b7c267-94b3-4ca2-8b53-0f47120d88f4">
  <data key="d3">Changes to settlement options require adherence to existing terms, which may include eligibility tied to rider availability; thus, requesting eligible riders could enable future changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="7845d152-d637-47c0-a88e-9b66f96e5458">
  <data key="d3">Changes to settlement options depend on existing terms, even though the company commits to providing necessary information in a reasonable timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="c81dbb82-548f-41f6-8919-0493d10f9c59">
  <data key="d3">Rules about changing settlement options do not impact the company’s responsibility to release information as required by law.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="558f6754-63ec-4df4-bcd2-35ea7c37ab09">
  <data key="d3">The availability of settlement options limits the choices the policy owner can make regarding how the death benefit is distributed, ensuring compliance with predefined plan structures.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="911c8355-e674-438d-8970-674b61225d1c" target="925dc2ea-b455-4473-b4ed-51ff493dd9eb">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes that changes in settlement options must follow the terms of the offered options, meaning such changes cannot proceed without meeting those criteria—even if approved by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
