<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">While Sentinel Life Assurance Company is responsible for issuing the policy, its effectivity depends on payment of the initial premium, making the timing of that action critical regardless of the issuer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">Payment of the first premium is a prerequisite for the policy to take effect on the date specified in the Schedule of Benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium must be paid for the policy to become effective is unrelated to the specific policy form number assigned to it.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures policy validity but does not influence the availability or functionality of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures financial commitment, but does not influence whether the insured is alive at policy inception. This fact stands independently from survival status on the effective date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy's initial validity, while state-specific notices ensure legal compliance after issuance. These elements operate independently within different stages of policy lifecycle management.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy is active, but it does not directly affect whether the accelerated death benefit rider enables early payments.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for payment of the first premium ensures the policy is active, but it does not affect whether optional riders like the Accelerated Death Benefit are available. Riders are add-ons that exist independently of initial premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy is active, but it does not directly affect whether an individual qualifies for the accelerated benefit based on a terminal illness diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy's existence but does not influence the maximum benefit available under the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy is active, but this does not influence or relate to the medical criteria needed to qualify for accelerated benefits based on terminal illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for the first premium to be paid ensures the policy is active, but does not influence the medical certification process needed for life expectancy evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy is active, but it does not influence the maximum allowable payment under the rider, which is capped at 50% of the face amount regardless of policy status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid for the policy to become effective is unrelated to how administrative charges impact the reduced death benefit after an accelerated payout.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy is active, but does not influence the insurer’s ability to request a second medical opinion during a benefits claim process.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy is active, which is a prerequisite for any benefits, including accelerated ones. However, it does not directly influence the act of submitting a written request for such benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy is active, but does not directly affect how benefits impact the death benefit upon payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy is active, enabling any subsequent benefits like those from the accelerated death benefit rider. Without an active policy, even properly documented claims cannot proceed.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid for the policy to become effective is unrelated to how interest on an accelerated benefit reduces the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid for the policy to become effective is unrelated to how outstanding loans impact the adjusted death benefit after an accelerated payout.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium must be paid ensures the policy is active; however, even with an active policy, no accelerated benefit will be issued if the terminal illness resulted from a felony.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium must be paid for the policy to become effective sets a foundational precondition unrelated to the ability to revoke an accelerated benefit request later.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium must be paid for the policy to become effective is independent of information regarding the identity of the company's CEO.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid for policy activation does not influence or relate to the procedure for withdrawing a benefit request. They address separate administrative conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy is active, but it does not influence how liens are handled upon benefit acceleration. The presence of liens affects the final death benefit regardless of whether the policy was activated via premium payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy's general validity but does not influence whether the accelerated benefit is denied due to self-inflicted injury. The payment of premiums is unrelated to the cause-of-illness exclusions applied during claim evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid ensures the policy is active, making it possible for any benefit—including those subject to exclusions like war-related illnesses—to apply. Without policy activation, no claims, even excluding certain causes, could proceed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_PREQ</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid for the policy to become effective is independent of where the policy was physically executed. This statement pertains to financial activation criteria rather than procedural location.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium must be paid for the policy to become effective does not influence or relate to the legal consequences of submitting false information on an application or claim.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium must be paid for the policy to become effective does not influence or relate to the definition of fraudulent acts involving concealment of material facts.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid for the policy to become effective does not relate to the prohibition against providing false information to defraud insurers.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the first premium be paid does not influence or relate to the definition of fraudulent insurance acts. The two sentences pertain to different procedural and behavioral domains.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
