  <data key="d4">RIGHT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="bcd8710d-4871-4c06-b268-081a694c4805">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">LEGAL_NOTICE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">The policy contains optional riders, one of which might be the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider discussed; however, the issuing company, Sentinel Life, is unrelated to the structural feature of having optional riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">Optional riders may be added to the policy regardless of its effective date; they are separate features that exist alongside the core policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">Optional riders such as the Accelerated Death Benefit are enhancements to the base policy; however, their existence does not depend on the first premium being paid, though they become applicable once the policy is activated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">Optional riders, such as the Accelerated Death Benefit, exist independently of the policy’s initial activation condition. The presence of riders does not affect when the policy becomes effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of optional riders indicates additional coverage options available under the policy. The existence of such riders is independent of the policy’s specific form number.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">Optional riders such as the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider may necessitate additional state-specific legal notices depending on jurisdictional requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">The statement about optional riders creates a categorical framework that enables the specific mention of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider as an instance.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence establishes that the policy offers optional riders, setting the stage for the detailed explanation of one such rider in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">The presence of optional riders enables certain benefits, including the accelerated death benefit, which applies only under defined conditions such as a terminal illness diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">The existence of optional riders, including the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, sets the stage for conditions like a 12-month life expectancy requirement. This condition applies specifically to those seeking benefits under such riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">The mention of optional riders sets the stage for discussing the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, allowing explanation of its terms such as payment limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of optional riders in the policy creates the framework under which benefits like accelerated death benefits may be accessed, including requirements such as physician-certified life expectancy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of optional riders establishes the structural framework that makes accelerated benefits possible. This context supports the necessity of submitting a written request to activate such benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of optional riders in the policy creates the framework through which benefits like the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider can exist. This sets the stage for defining constraints such as the maximum pay-out allowed by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">The mention of optional riders sets the stage for specialized benefits like the accelerated death benefit, which involves medical verification processes including potential second opinions.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of optional riders in the policy creates the possibility for benefits like accelerated death payments, making it necessary for applicants to provide required medical documentation when requesting such benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of optional riders like the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider establishes the structural basis for receiving early payouts under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">The presence of optional riders enables certain benefits like accelerated payouts, creating the condition under which administrative charges may later impact the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">The presence of optional riders establishes the broader feature set available under the policy, including mechanisms such as accelerated benefits. This context enables understanding why certain financial adjustments—like loan deductions—are applied during benefit calculation.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">The presence of optional riders establishes the broader framework under which benefits like accelerated payments may apply. However, this general feature does not determine how liens impact the final death benefit calculation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">The presence of optional riders establishes the framework under which benefits like those described in fact_sentence_2 may apply. However, fact_sentence_2 specifically addresses how accrued interest impacts the remaining death benefit, independent of whether other riders exist.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of optional riders enables enhanced policy benefits such as accelerated death benefits, but specific exclusions apply—for instance, payments are denied if the illness stems from self-inflicted harm.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPT_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3">The mention of optional riders within the policy does not relate to the identity or role of the company's CEO. No contextual or causal link exists between the two statements.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">The presence of optional riders, including the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, sets the stage for conditions governing payouts. One such condition explicitly excludes payments if the terminal illness stems from criminal activity, ensuring risk mitigation for insurers.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">The presence of optional riders, including the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, sets the stage for eligibility conditions like those described in fact_sentence_2, where certain causes—including war—are explicitly excluded from benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPT_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">The presence of optional riders on the policy enables certain benefits such as accelerated death benefits. Revocation of a rider request requires formal written notification to the company, ensuring controlled termination of such provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of optional riders establishes the framework under which specific benefits, such as accelerated death benefits, become available. This enables the possibility of requesting early payouts, including the option to withdraw such a request before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The presence of optional riders is unrelated to the geographic location where the policy was formally executed.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">The existence of optional riders does not affect the definition or implications of fraudulent behavior during application or claims processes.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">The presence of optional riders in the policy provides additional benefits but does not directly affect the rules around fraudulent behavior.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">The existence of optional riders in the policy does not influence the definition or implications of fraudulent insurance acts. This statement stands independently regarding product design.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">The presence of optional riders in the policy is unrelated to the definition of committing a fraudulent insurance act. No causal or contextual link exists between them.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
