<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, available through Sentinel Life Assurance Company, permits partial pre-death payouts from the policy’s death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">OFFERED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">The ability to access an accelerated death benefit depends on policy terms being active, which starts from the effective date specified in the schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">The availability of early payments under the rider depends on eligibility criteria, independent of whether the initial premium has been paid.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">Eligibility for early payment via the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider is independent of whether the insured was alive on the policy's effective date; it hinges instead on health status and other specified criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">The accelerated death benefit provision describes a financial feature that applies across policies, including those identified by form numbers like SLAC-TL2025-20YR.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">The ability to make early payments under the rider could necessitate inclusion of state-mandated disclosures or procedural adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence describes a specific example of an optional rider available under the policy, illustrating how the broader category applies in practice.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">The ability to access a portion of the death benefit early depends on having the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider attached to the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">The ability to receive an accelerated death benefit depends on verifying the insured's life expectancy through documentation from a licensed physician.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">The ability to access an early portion of the death benefit hinges on being diagnosed with a terminal illness, making this eligibility criterion foundational to triggering the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">The ability to receive an accelerated death benefit depends on meeting specific medical criteria, including a prognosis of 12 months or less. Without such a diagnosis, the early payment provision cannot apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider permits early access to a portion of the death benefit, but the amount paid is capped at half the policy's face value.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to receive early payments under the rider is constrained by a cap determined by the insurance company, ensuring payouts remain within predefined limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">The ability to access an accelerated death benefit depends on providing medical evidence confirming eligibility. Without proper documentation, the initial claim cannot proceed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">The ability to receive an accelerated death benefit depends on submitting a formal written request, which initiates the claims process.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">The ability to access an accelerated death benefit depends on verifying the terminal diagnosis, which may trigger the insurer's right to request a second medical opinion to confirm eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_PREQ</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to receive an accelerated death benefit directly leads to a reduction in the final death benefit amount payable upon the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">The ability to receive an accelerated death benefit leads to reductions in the final death benefit, including accumulated interest on the paid-out amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">The rider enables early access to part of the death benefit, and any associated administrative charges further decrease the remaining death benefit upon payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">The rider enables early access to part of the death benefit, and any existing policy loans are subtracted from the available amount upon acceleration.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">The ability to receive an early portion of the death benefit triggers adjustments to the remaining payout, including deductions for existing liens on the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">The rider enables early access to benefits, but only if the terminal illness is not due to intentional self-injury, ensuring that fraudulent claims based on self-harm are prevented.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes the availability of early benefits under the rider, while fact_sentence_2 specifies that eligibility is voided if the terminal illness stems from a felony, thereby restricting when those benefits can be paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">The rider enables early access to a portion of the death benefit, creating a scenario where policyholders can choose to proceed or withdraw their request before funds are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">The rider enables early payout of benefits, but this provision does not apply when the terminal illness stems from war-related causes, thereby restricting its applicability under certain circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">The rider enables early access to benefits, and if the policyholder decides not to proceed, they may cancel their request through formal notification to the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">The accelerated death benefit enables early payouts under certain health conditions, but does not address fraudulent behavior during application processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">The accelerated death benefit enables early payouts under specific conditions, but such benefits are subject to anti-fraud provisions that penalize deceptive behavior during claim processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence explains how beneficiaries may access part of their death benefit early due to terminal illness. The second sentence outlines what constitutes insurance fraud but does not connect directly to the process or conditions of accelerated payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines how the rider enables early payouts under qualifying health conditions. Fact_sentence_2 warns that falsifying information to obtain such payments constitutes fraud, serving as a deterrent rather than a condition of the benefit itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, mentioned in the first statement, facilitates early disbursement of benefits, directly supporting the functionality described in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The Accelerated Death Benefit Rider functions as a provision that alters the standard treatment of the Death Benefit under specific circumstances, relying on the foundational existence and rules governing the Death Benefit outlined in the primary policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the foundational rule that all benefits—including those from riders like the Accelerated Death Benefit—are constrained by the policy’s terms and exceptions, ensuring consistency across coverage features.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b35fc4ed-5fda-42d4-a02d-52f331ae6482" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
