  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence defines the cap on benefits available through the rider, but it has no bearing on where the policy was signed. The location of policy execution is unrelated to the benefit calculation rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment limit ensures financial protection for insurers, supporting policies that prevent misuse through penalties like those outlined in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines the maximum financial benefit available under the rider, but does not influence or rely on whether misinformation was submitted during claims. It sets a structural boundary independent of ethical or procedural violations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence sets a financial ceiling on payouts, whereas the second explains what constitutes fraud, which may result in disqualification from receiving benefits. The two statements operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines the maximum financial benefit available under the rider, setting a clear cap at 50% of the face amount. Fact_sentence_2 warns that intentionally hiding information during the process may lead to criminal penalties, reinforcing ethical compliance without affecting the benefit's calculation.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">The presence of the rider allows partial pre-death payouts, which are restricted by the rule that no more than 50% of the face amount may be paid out, ensuring financial constraints align with policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The rule mandating written approval for policy changes supports the enforceability of the 50% cap on accelerated death benefits, confirming that such limitations are formally documented and binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Any change to the maximum allowable payout under the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider would require a signed amendment by an authorized company officer, consistent with the policy’s requirement for written approvals.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The 50% cap on the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider illustrates a pre-defined limitation that aligns with broader policy rules requiring written approval for changes, reinforcing compliance with established terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">The 50% limit on the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider reflects a pre-defined policy term that aligns with broader restrictions requiring written approval for changes, reinforcing compliance with established provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
