<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">The company's role as the policy issuer justifies its ability to impose a cap on benefits paid through the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment limit established by the company has no bearing on when the policy becomes effective. Financial caps are unrelated to the start date of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">The maximum benefit limit imposed by the company applies regardless of whether the initial premium has been paid, making it independent of policy activation conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a company-set maximum limit on payments under the rider does not affect whether the policyholder was alive on the effective date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment limit set by the company applies regardless of the specific policy form number, making it independent of that identifier.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">The company sets a maximum payment limit for the rider, independent of any state-level disclosures or notifications required by law.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a maximum limit on payments from the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider implies that not all riders operate without restrictions; thus, it reinforces the idea that some riders come with predefined conditions, supporting the broader claim about optional riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">Since the rider has a maximum payout determined by the insurer, the initial mention of its availability naturally leads into constraints governing how much can be received.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">The provision allowing early receipt of a portion of the death benefit operates only within the bounds established by the company's maximum allowable payment threshold.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">The maximum amount payable under the rider constrains the potential benefit available to individuals who meet the qualification criteria, such as being diagnosed with a terminal illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">While the 12-month life expectancy threshold sets who qualifies, the payment ceiling ensures that even qualified individuals cannot exceed a predefined dollar amount, regardless of need.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSTRAINS_ELIGIBILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a company-set maximum benefit influences the scope of what can be paid out, contingent upon proper documentation like a physician-certified life expectancy.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes a general principle—that the payment is capped by the company—which is made precise by fact_sentence_1 specifying that the cap equals 50% of the policy’s face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment allowed under the rider depends on the insurer's approval of qualifying medical documentation submitted with the request.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">The Company's right to require a second medical opinion ensures that claims for accelerated benefits align with established guidelines, including the maximum permissible payout. This oversight helps validate the legitimacy of the claim before any funds are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable payment under the rider determines how much the death benefit will be reduced when benefits are paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable benefit amount is determined by the insurance company, setting a ceiling on potential payouts. This financial constraint applies once the policyholder has initiated the claim process through a formal written request.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS PAYMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable payment under the rider constrains the total benefit available before any reductions. Administrative charges are deducted from this capped amount when calculating the final death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment allowed under the rider determines the initial principal amount from which interest is calculated, directly influencing how much the death benefit is reduced over time due to accrued interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment allowed under the rider is determined by company policy but does not override exclusions such as those related to self-inflicted injuries.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">The maximum benefit allowed by the company sets an upper bound on payments, but actual disbursement may be reduced due to pre-existing loans that diminish the adjusted death benefit upon acceleration.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment allowed by the company influences the total funds available after adjustments like liens. Outstanding liens reduce the adjusted death benefit, thereby affecting how much of the capped amount remains accessible.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment allowed under the rider is determined by company policy, but this does not affect whether benefits are paid if the illness stems from war-related causes.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment allowed under the rider is defined regardless of the reason for the terminal illness, including cases where it stems from criminal activity. This limitation does not override exclusions related to the cause of illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment limit imposed by the company sets an upper bound on benefits but does not affect the policyholder’s right to withdraw a request before payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment limit defined by the company governs how much can be accessed through the rider, but does not affect the ability to revoke a request once submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the upper limit imposed by the insurer on payouts from the accelerated death benefit. The second sentence identifies a corporate officer without referencing policies, benefits, or financial constraints.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">The payment limit imposed by the company does not affect whether fraudulent behavior occurs when filing applications or claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The maximum benefit amount under the rider is determined internally by the insurance company but has no connection to where the policy was signed.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment limit under the rider does not relate directly to definitions of fraudulent acts. It sets a financial boundary but does not influence or describe misconduct.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment limit imposed by the company does not influence whether concealing information qualifies as fraud. The financial ceiling is administrative, whereas fraud involves deliberate misconduct unrelated to benefit caps.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">The maximum payment limit imposed by the company ensures controlled disbursement of benefits, while the prohibition against fraudulent statements reinforces integrity in claim submission processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
