<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">A key condition for receiving benefits is providing medical documentation approved by the insurance company. Since Sentinel Life Assurance Company is the issuer, it holds the authority to determine what constitutes acceptable evidence.</data>
  <data key="d4">AUTHORIZES_REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">Providing medical documentation is necessary for initiating benefits, regardless of when the policy became effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">While medical documentation is necessary to validate a claim under the rider, it does not affect whether the policy itself is effective; that depends on payment of the initial premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTDATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">Providing medically acceptable documentation is essential for initiating a benefit claim, independent of whether the insured was alive on the effective date; however, without initial policy validity, such a request would be moot.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">Submitting medical documentation is required for claims processing; however, it is independent of the policy's form number designation.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">Providing medical documentation is a core part of initiating a claim under the rider; however, it does not depend on whether state-specific notices are present.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for medical documentation in support of a claim implies that the policy offers specific provisions—such as riders—that allow early payouts based on qualifying conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">Submitting medical documentation is required to activate the option of receiving benefits under the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">Submitting required medical documentation enables the policyholder to qualify for early payment under the rider provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">To qualify for the accelerated benefit based on a terminal illness diagnosis, applicants must submit medical documents deemed acceptable by the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">VALIDATES_ELIGIBILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Supporting medical documentation is required to substantiate a terminal illness diagnosis with a life expectancy of 12 months or less, ensuring compliance with the rider’s conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">To proceed with the claim, the policyholder must submit medical documentation approved by the company, which includes validation from a licensed physician regarding life expectancy.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">To qualify for the accelerated benefit capped at 50%, applicants must provide medical evidence accepted by the insurer. This condition enforces compliance with the financial cap defined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">To ensure compliance with the maximum payment limits, the insurer requires documented proof from a qualified healthcare provider confirming the diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Supporting medical documentation is essential for validating the request; without it, the written submission would not meet the criteria for processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">A written request for an accelerated benefit must include medical documentation approved by the company to initiate consideration. Without such validation, the subsequent reduction of the death benefit cannot occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the requirement for documented proof, which enables the insurer to assess eligibility. This necessity justifies the insurer's authority to seek additional confirmation via a second medical opinion.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">A valid medical documentation requirement ensures eligibility for the accelerated benefit, which subsequently leads to administrative charges being deducted from the remaining death benefit upon approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">A valid medical verification is required before any benefit can be issued, ensuring eligibility. Once approved, interest accrues on the advanced sum and reduces the remaining death benefit accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">A submitted request must include medical documentation verified by the company, ensuring legitimacy before any benefits are processed. After approval, outstanding loans are subtracted from the accelerated benefit to determine the net payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">A submitted request must include medical documentation approved by the company, ensuring legitimacy before processing. After approval, any existing liens on the policy are subtracted from the accelerated benefit to determine the net payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">A request for accelerated benefits must include medical documentation approved by the company. The policyholder retains the right to cancel that request anytime before receiving funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">A request for benefits must include medical documentation approved by the company, ensuring legitimacy of the diagnosis. However, even with proper documentation, payments are denied if the illness originated from war-related incidents.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a necessary step in initiating a benefit payment—submitting approved medical evidence. This detail has no bearing on the personal identity of the company's CEO.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">A submitted request must include medical proof confirming the diagnosis, which helps determine whether the illness resulted from intentional self-harm—a disqualifying factor under the rider's terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">VERIFIES CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">A written request for benefits must include medical documentation verified by the company to establish eligibility. After submitting such a request, the policyholder may revoke it at any time before payout by providing formal written notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 mandates supporting medical evidence for a claim, ensuring legitimacy; however, even with such documentation, payments are barred if the illness resulted from a felony, as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_EXCLUSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a procedural condition for submitting a claim—medical documentation must be provided. This has no bearing on the professional role of Eleanor B. Raynor at Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The need for medical documentation to validate a terminal illness claim is unrelated to where the policy was originally signed. The location of policy execution has no bearing on the evidentiary requirements for benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">A request for benefits requires verified medical evidence, and failing to provide truthful documentation could lead to accusations of fraud when filing claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
