  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">The insurer's right to request a second medical opinion ensures accurate assessment of terminal diagnosis, while the policyholder's ability to revoke a request maintains personal control over benefit access. Both provisions support fairness and transparency without affecting one another directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">The insurer may require a second medical opinion to verify terminal diagnosis, but this does not affect whether falsified information on forms constitutes fraud.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes the insurer's authority to verify medical diagnoses through an independent opinion. The second sentence specifies the physical location where the policy was signed but does not relate to any aspect of medical verification or claims processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">The insurer may require a second medical opinion to validate a claim, which helps prevent fraudulent submissions; concealing material facts to gain benefits would violate this safeguard.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS FRAUD</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">The insurer’s ability to require a second medical opinion helps ensure accurate assessments, thereby supporting mechanisms that deter intentional deception in claims processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">The insurer may require a second medical opinion to verify terminal diagnosis, helping prevent false claims. This safeguards against fraudulent submissions where individuals misrepresent health status.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The right to obtain a second medical opinion supports enforcement of the Death Benefit terms, ensuring accurate assessment of eligibility conditions related to terminal illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes a conditional procedure related to benefit claims, which operates under the umbrella of policy terms and exclusions stated in fact_sentence_1, particularly concerning claim validation and eligibility criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="df9797d7-629e-4917-bc56-582d8cf4fe9d">
  <data key="d3">The company's ability to require a second medical opinion (fact_sentence_1) serves as a mechanism to detect and prevent fraudulent claims like those referenced in fact_sentence_2, where dishonest activities undermine claim authenticity.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="9e3cd4f3-d236-4040-a6c4-c46f3a22a611">
  <data key="d3">The first statement outlines a standard administrative procedure regarding medical validation for benefit claims, while the second introduces a high-level executive linked to alleged fraudulent conduct; these topics operate independently within different operational contexts—claims processing versus internal integrity violations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="57fafae6-d83d-473d-a0a2-e4e4d1824c40">
  <data key="d3">The clause allowing a second medical opinion pertains to claim validation procedures, while Eleanor Raynor’s role involves corporate representation amid allegations of fraud—no direct interaction exists between these elements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="de0d67af-5b66-4374-8edd-cc82b199731b">
  <data key="d3">The clause about obtaining a second medical opinion relates to internal claims procedures, while the mention of the CEO involved in fraud concerns leadership accountability; these topics do not intersect meaningfully.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">A written amendment is required for any policy change; obtaining a second medical opinion might prompt such a change, making it subject to the written agreement rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to obtain a second medical opinion enables the company to verify eligibility for accelerated benefits, supporting the need for documented authorizations per fact_sentence_1 to ensure legitimacy and consistency in handling sensitive claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORDS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The company’s right to obtain a second medical opinion reinforces the need for formal procedures; it operates within the framework where only authorized personnel can act, consistent with the prohibition on unapproved policy alterations.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORDS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 grants the company discretion to verify medical claims via a second opinion, aligning with the broader principle in fact_sentence_1 that only officially authorized representatives can act on behalf of the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
