<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">When an accelerated benefit is paid, the death benefit is reduced accordingly. This outcome is independent of who issued the policy, though Sentinel Life Assurance Company administers the process under established rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">A reduction in the death benefit due to an accelerated payment depends on the claim being approved under the terms of the policy, regardless of when the policy became effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit leads to a reduction in the death benefit; however, this outcome depends on the policy already being effective due to premium payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit leads to a reduction in the death benefit; however, this outcome is independent of whether the policy was initially effective due to the insured's survival status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">The reduction of the death benefit after an accelerated payment is independent of the policy's form number.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">When an accelerated benefit is paid, it reduces the death benefit; this outcome remains unaffected by any state-specific legal notices.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit directly depends on having an applicable rider, such as the one referenced in the initial statement about optional riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit necessitates the use of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, which must be elected as an option on the policy. Without this rider, such payments cannot occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">A reduction in the death benefit occurs specifically because an accelerated benefit has been paid out earlier than normal.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit results from meeting the qualification criteria, including being diagnosed with a terminal illness and having a life expectancy of 12 months or less.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit reduces the final death benefit, directly resulting from the initial qualification based on a short life expectancy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit directly results in a lower death benefit, meaning the earlier approval based on medical certification leads to a permanent reduction in future payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">When a benefit is paid, the death benefit decreases accordingly, reflecting the financial obligation already fulfilled through early disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">A reduction in the death benefit occurs proportionally based on the amount paid from the accelerated benefit, which itself cannot exceed the company-set limit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit directly results in a reduction of the death benefit, reflecting the financial impact of early disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">When an accelerated benefit is paid, the death benefit is reduced accordingly, but only after proper medical documentation has been verified and accepted by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">When an accelerated benefit is issued, the total death benefit is decreased accordingly to reflect the early disbursement, maintaining financial balance within the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">When an accelerated benefit is paid, the death benefit decreases by the full amount disbursed. Administrative charges related to this payment further contribute to the reduction of the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">When an accelerated benefit is paid, the death benefit is reduced by the amount disbursed. This reduction includes not only the principal but also any accrued interest on the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">When an accelerated benefit is paid, the death benefit is reduced accordingly. Subsequently, any outstanding liens are deducted from this already-adjusted death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">When an accelerated benefit is paid, the death benefit is reduced accordingly; additionally, any existing loans on the policy are subtracted from the adjusted death benefit during this process.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">Payment of an accelerated benefit reduces the future death benefit. This reduction does not apply if the illness was due to war-related causes, which disqualify claims entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">Payment of an accelerated benefit reduces the death benefit, but only if the underlying cause of the terminal illness does not involve intentional self-injury, which would disqualify the claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_EXCLUSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit reduces the future death benefit. However, the policyholder retains the right to withdraw their request before payment, thereby avoiding that reduction.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">Payment of an accelerated benefit reduces the final death benefit. However, such payments are prohibited if the underlying illness resulted from criminal activity like a felony.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit triggers a reduction in the final death benefit. This outcome necessitates formal procedures like revocation via written notice if the policyholder wishes to cancel the request before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence explains how paying an accelerated benefit reduces the final death benefit. The second sentence provides organizational leadership information that has no bearing on the contractual terms described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how paying out an accelerated benefit reduces the final death benefit. It has no relation to Eleanor B. Raynor’s role as CEO of the insurance provider.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The payment of an accelerated benefit reduces the future death benefit, but this effect has no bearing on where the policy was executed.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit triggers a reduction in the death benefit, but such payments may be denied if material facts were concealed intentionally, potentially preventing the reduction from occurring.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit reduces the final death benefit payable; however, this does not directly connect to the definition of fraudulent acts involving false statements.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated benefit directly impacts the final death benefit payment, reducing its size accordingly. This reduction ensures alignment with the policyholder’s earlier withdrawal of funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_DIRECT_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes the financial adjustment to the death benefit upon receiving an accelerated payment. Fact_sentence_2 warns about criminal liability for providing false information during claims, but it does not relate directly to the effect of payments on benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The rule that the Death Benefit is adjusted downward upon payment of an accelerated benefit depends on its status as a component governed by the overall policy terms, including those defining benefits and conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes a specific benefit whose application is constrained by policy rules; fact_sentence_1 confirms these constraints apply universally, ensuring the accelerated benefit operates within established contractual boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">A reduction in the death benefit due to an accelerated payment necessitates formal procedures, reinforcing the importance of written agreements as mandated in the original policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">A reduction in the death benefit due to an accelerated benefit claim qualifies as a policy amendment needing documented authorization from an official company representative, aligning with the rule stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The rule prohibiting unauthorized policy changes does not prevent the application of the accelerated death benefit rider, which legally reduces the death benefit when triggered by qualifying circumstances and documented approval processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">PERMITTED_EXCEPTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces a scenario where the death benefit is adjusted due to a claim under a rider; such adjustments fall under the broader category of policy changes requiring official authorization, as stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9032bcb9-1234-463a-bddb-03fa887f677f" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">causes_reduction_in</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74912f80-19bb-4ec9-b61a-ac59c1f5f176" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
</edge>
<edge source="600cb288-ff29-43df-91fd-78045e50e1ad" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is reduced by</data>
</edge>
<edge source="87cb977a-8cda-4889-8353-c7941219ea0d" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">may be adjusted proportionally to</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6358c391-95b7-45f9-b9ed-6c3440f1b1ff" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">required to trigger</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="e47b4a81-b39c-48a0-bb1a-a135c1077abf">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="5456c4ce-e1a4-4d97-91a1-8334378a1cde">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="185897ae-39a5-4099-8e6a-0f393deb6006">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ROLE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="eda110a0-4894-46c1-9635-9dc3e5c661c1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="894c62d7-1161-4b6f-aa29-39d956442a2d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="86614b2e-d00e-4ae5-b162-d83c82291324">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="60e733ac-bc6e-45f7-8578-c5c1898b4c21">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">LOCATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="a79a085a-81f6-4cf7-864e-ed5555d17474">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="bcce726c-07a0-4d7f-8178-24288bed645e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL_CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="407fbbd0-2b62-4acc-b848-7034bc193e82">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ACTION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="ff6f2438-9df5-4cae-a17b-2cea5346ef5f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="9087bbd6-33e6-45f6-898b-7aa73805dd88">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="a270749d-a6a5-48fe-9d53-686df4f55770">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="d7755e17-0701-42fa-bf03-1be180f25da3">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="7c69bc82-4757-414a-ba3b-2e2cb99265f0">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="829778f0-e5a9-46de-9bbb-c3c25580df89">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">RIGHT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="36f500b5-429e-4965-9b42-2e19780577d1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">LEGAL_NOTICE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reduce the death benefit when benefits are paid early, independent of the specific insurance company issuing the policy, including Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reducing the death benefit occur only after a claim is processed; however, such reductions depend on the policy being active from its effective date onward.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">How administrative charges reduce the death benefit does not influence whether the policy becomes effective upon first premium payment.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reducing the death benefit occur after an accelerated payout and are unrelated to whether the insured was alive at policy inception.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">How administrative charges reduce the death benefit has no connection to the identification of the policy via its form number.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reducing the death benefit are part of the financial mechanism of the rider and are unrelated to any state-mandated disclosures.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reducing the death benefit only matter in policies where optional riders—such as the accelerated death benefit—are available.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges on the accelerated benefit reduce the final death benefit paid out. This applies only after the rider has been selected and activated.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">Since the rider permits early withdrawal of a portion of the death benefit, administrative charges are deducted from that amount, thereby reducing the overall payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reduce the death benefit only after the insured has qualified under the terms of the rider, such as being diagnosed with a terminal illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reduce the death benefit after an accelerated payment is made, but such deductions only apply once the policyholder qualifies under specific conditions—including a terminal illness prognosis of 12 months or less.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">After a policyholder receives an approved accelerated benefit payment, administrative charges are subtracted from the death benefit. This deduction occurs only after the initial condition—life expectancy certification—is met.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges decrease the overall death benefit after an accelerated payout, so they directly influence how much of the original 50% cap actually reaches beneficiaries. Since payments are limited to half the face amount, these charges operate within that constrained framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reduce the death benefit, meaning the effective payout cannot exceed the company-set maximum. This ensures that even after such deductions, the overall benefit remains within predefined limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reduce the death benefit only after a written request has been submitted and approved, making the initial action necessary for such reductions to occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reducing the death benefit occur only after a properly documented claim has been approved, making the presence of such documentation essential for any deduction to take place.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reduce the death benefit regardless of whether a second medical opinion was obtained; however, the need for such an opinion is independent of charge application.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of administrative charges in the death benefit reduction depends on the initial reduction triggered by the accelerated benefit payout, meaning such charges are subtracted after the primary disbursement occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges related to the accelerated benefit contribute to reducing the final death benefit, similar to how interest also reduces it. Both are cost factors deducted from the policy proceeds upon acceleration.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges are part of the total deductions applied to the death benefit after acceleration, alongside other financial obligations like outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMBINED_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges are one component reduced from the death benefit after acceleration; outstanding liens represent another such financial obligation that further diminishes the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains that administrative costs reduce the final death benefit after acceleration, but it does not relate directly to whether benefits are denied due to self-harm causes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reduce the death benefit after acceleration, but this does not affect whether benefits are denied due to criminal conduct.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reduce the death benefit after payment of the accelerated benefit, regardless of the cause of illness. This rule applies universally unless specific exclusion conditions like war-related causes prevent any payment at all.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reduce the death benefit after acceleration has been approved, but this does not impact the policyholder’s ability to revoke their request before payment occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reduce the death benefit when an accelerated benefit is paid out. This does not influence or depend on whether someone submitted false information during the application or claim process.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">Administrative charges reduce the death benefit when an accelerated benefit is paid, affecting the final payout. This financial adjustment operates independently of whether the policyholder chooses to revoke their request.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
