<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">Loan deductions from the adjusted death benefit occur only in policies with accelerated benefit provisions; thus, this detail relies on the existence of such riders, making it contingent upon the inclusion of optional riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the final death benefit upon accelerated payout, which only occurs if the rider is in place. The rider's availability makes such loan adjustments possible.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">When receiving an accelerated death benefit, the policyholder's outstanding loans are accounted for, reducing the net payout derived from the initial benefit provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">The presence of outstanding loans reduces the adjusted death benefit after acceleration, meaning such debts only impact the outcome once an insured has met the eligibility criteria set forth in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">When determining the adjusted death benefit after acceleration, any unpaid loans are accounted for. This step occurs only after confirming that the insured has a terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans are subtracted from the policy’s face amount when determining the reduced death benefit after acceleration, reflecting an accounting adjustment that follows initial eligibility confirmation via physician certification.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the adjusted death benefit after acceleration, which operates within the framework established by the 50% cap on payable amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the adjusted death benefit post-acceleration, meaning they constrain the effective amount that can be received even within the company-specified maximum limit.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the available death benefit after acceleration, meaning that even after submitting a written request, the actual payout may be lower due to pre-existing financial obligations tied to the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">Before payments are made, the insurer calculates the adjusted death benefit by deducting existing loans, which influences whether funds are available for distribution. This step follows the initial validation of medical evidence required to initiate the process.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances are deducted from the death benefit upon acceleration, regardless of whether a second medical opinion was obtained.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the adjusted death benefit after acceleration, which itself results in a lower overall death benefit due to prior payment of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans contribute to reducing the adjusted death benefit, just as administrative charges do, forming part of the cumulative impact on the remaining payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMBINED_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the adjusted death benefit, just as accumulated interest on the accelerated payment does, creating parallel reductions in the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_REDUCTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
