<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">Deductions for outstanding liens occur during the recalibration of the death benefit after acceleration, independent of the policy’s issuing entity, Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding liens are deducted from the death benefit after acceleration regardless of when the policy became effective; thus, the timing of policy inception has no bearing on lien adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding liens are subtracted from the death benefit after acceleration, independent of whether the first premium has been paid; thus, lien deductions do not depend on the policy's initiation status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">While the existence of liens reduces the adjusted death benefit after acceleration, this deduction is irrelevant to whether the policyholder was alive on the effective date—the timing of activation depends solely on survival at issuance, independent of future lien considerations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that liens impact the final death benefit adjustment; however, this detail is independent of the policy’s identifying form number mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">Liens are deducted from the adjusted death benefit upon acceleration, regardless of any state-specific notices that may appear in the policy documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding liens reducing the adjusted death benefit occur regardless of whether other riders exist, so the existence of optional riders has no bearing on lien deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">When determining eligibility and benefits under the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, it is important that any outstanding liens are accounted for during adjustments to the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSIDERED_IN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">Existing liens reduce the net amount available from the accelerated death benefit, meaning they directly impact the effective payout after early disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">After approval for accelerated benefits due to a terminal illness, any outstanding liens are accounted for in reducing the adjusted death benefit, reflecting the financial impact of pre-existing obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS_REMAINING_BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">When determining the reduced death benefit after acceleration, insurers deduct existing liens. This deduction only applies once the policyholder qualifies under the initial condition—that is, having a terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding liens are subtracted from the death benefit after acceleration, affecting the net payout. This deduction occurs independently of whether the life expectancy was medically verified.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">Liens decrease the adjusted death benefit after acceleration, meaning the portion of the 50% cap actually disbursed may be lower due to these deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">Deductions such as liens impact the actual payout, ensuring that even within the company-set maximum, the remaining balance reflects financial obligations tied to the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding liens impact the final benefit amount, but such calculations occur only after a written request has been submitted and processed.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">Before determining the actual payout, the insurer deducts outstanding liens from the adjusted death benefit. This deduction occurs only after verifying that required medical documentation has been received and accepted.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTPONED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">Liens are deducted from the death benefit after acceleration, regardless of whether a second medical opinion was obtained during the review process.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding liens affect the final death benefit after acceleration. This deduction occurs after the initial reduction caused by paying the accelerated benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding liens are deducted when adjusting the death benefit after acceleration, similar to how administrative charges are accounted for in reducing the total payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding liens are one of several deductions made from the death benefit after acceleration, just like accumulated interest on the paid-out amount, both reducing the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 notes that liens are deducted when adjusting the death benefit after acceleration. This mirrors fact sentence 1, where loans are similarly reduced, showing that both types of liabilities follow identical rules in benefit calculations.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">The presence of outstanding liens affects the final death benefit after acceleration but does not influence whether payment is denied due to the cause of illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">The presence of outstanding liens affects the final death benefit but does not influence whether payment is denied due to criminal activity causing the illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding liens affect the final death benefit after acceleration but do not influence whether benefits are paid due to the cause of illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains that liens reduce the available death benefit post-acceleration but does not relate directly to the revocation procedure.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains that liens impact the final death benefit after acceleration but does not influence the policyholder’s ability to revoke a request before payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3">The presence of outstanding liens affects the adjusted death benefit upon acceleration, but this detail has no bearing on the leadership of the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how outstanding liens affect the post-acceleration death benefit but does not relate directly to the issue of falsifying information on applications or claims.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The presence of liens affects the adjusted death benefit upon acceleration but does not relate to where the policy was signed.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">This statement explains how liens affect the post-acceleration death benefit but does not relate directly to the definition of fraud.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains how outstanding liens affect the post-acceleration death benefit, reflecting standard accounting practices. This does not directly connect to the concept of concealing information, which falls under separate regulatory and criminal considerations.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains how liens affect the post-acceleration death benefit, reflecting internal policy accounting rules. It does not directly connect to the concept of fraud or deceptive behavior described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces a specific modification to the death benefit involving liens, which aligns with the general principle in fact_sentence_1 that all policy changes must be documented in writing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Lien deductions during accelerated benefit payouts rely on procedural compliance, reinforcing the need for authorized personnel to validate and implement these changes per policy rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">Deductions for liens during accelerated benefit payouts rely on formal procedures; thus, adherence to the rule that only authorized agents can act prevents improper alterations affecting lien handling.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPRTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines how liens affect the adjusted death benefit under acceleration, but this detail is unrelated to whether agents can waive policy provisions, as stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdbd7b9a-9c9d-4906-83ec-2c1ae614c490" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">administers lien deduction procedure upon acceleration</data>
</edge>
<edge source="41eb3c74-5ec0-4635-b9cf-52b1ef66a0c5" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">triggers adjustment of Death Benefit including lien deduction</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5e35ed58-8e69-4ad2-a35a-a6138eb5fc57" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines timing of lien deduction in adjusted Death Benefit calculation</data>
</edge>
