  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="77b499e0-e59d-42cc-b6b7-830878ea7b6f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="184c1660-bc37-4f51-9c40-f22882e89d55">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="427ce68e-1a45-492c-a9e5-712e4b34569b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">LOCATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="b96b3dc8-73c1-4b7c-b6ef-90a8df0586c7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="86d5380f-ffe0-4318-b0f4-f43f85d6a7fc">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL_CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="c945613b-401b-40b3-a99a-4edbe29c39c5">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ACTION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="b83f3a15-e3cc-4520-9ff7-204eb63dbee5">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="3152b27e-a698-431d-b614-ab7ccf9b6afc">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="f4f0e49f-1d09-4c9b-9b11-978938b7927d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="986d3448-12bb-4b13-81fe-7e7542c85f98">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="c849c2f8-efb4-4535-aa22-e5ff7ea019be">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="02f16096-fe90-4945-83ec-86ed2a48536e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">RIGHT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="978fb954-216e-4e6c-8fa5-8286316f43df">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">LEGAL_NOTICE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises due to a felony, no accelerated benefit is payable. This exclusion applies regardless of Sentinel Life Assurance Company’s role as the policy issuer.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">A denial of benefits due to involvement in a felony does not depend on when the policy became effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">Even if the policyholder has fulfilled the initial payment requirement, they remain ineligible for accelerated benefits if the terminal illness was due to criminal activity such as a felony.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 prohibits payments if the terminal illness arises from a felony, reinforcing ethical and legal boundaries in claim processing. This rule operates independently of whether the insured was alive at the policy's effective date, which is governed by fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">A payment denial due to involvement in a felony is unrelated to the policy’s identifying form number.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of payments for illnesses resulting from felonies reflects a broader legal restriction that may necessitate inclusion of specific disclosures at the state level to ensure transparency and compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">LEGAL_CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">A key restriction on receiving accelerated benefits—that they won’t be paid if the illness arises from a felony—is part of the broader set of rules associated with optional riders, reinforcing how such provisions limit eligibility based on conduct.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder's terminal illness was due to involvement in a felony, they are ineligible for the Accelerated Death Benefit, despite having the rider attached.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">If an illness leading to a claim under the rider arises from a felony, the benefit cannot be paid; thus, the condition in fact_sentence_2 negates the possibility of receiving the early payment described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_LIMITATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness resulting from a felony disqualifies the individual from receiving the accelerated benefit, even if other criteria like life expectancy are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REJECTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Even if a policyholder meets the 12-month life expectancy requirement, benefits are not payable if the illness resulted from criminal conduct such as a felony.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness resulted from a felony, the claim is denied regardless of medical documentation supporting short life expectancy. Thus, the existence of a physician’s certification does not override this exclusionary rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness was due to a felony, no accelerated benefit will be issued regardless of whether it falls within the 50% cap defined by the rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness was due to a felony, no benefits are payable, even if the requested amount falls below the company's stated maximum limit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Even after submitting a written request, beneficiaries cannot receive accelerated benefits if the illness was caused by participating in a felony.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS_PAYMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises from a felony, no benefit will be issued regardless of submitted medical documents, making compliance with documentation requirements irrelevant in such cases.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREEMPTS_REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness was caused by a felony, the claim is ineligible regardless of whether a second medical opinion has been obtained.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises due to involvement in a felony, no accelerated benefit may be issued. This exclusion ensures that benefits are not payable in cases where the cause involves illegal conduct, preserving the integrity of the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">If the illness resulted from a felony, no benefit is paid regardless of any associated administrative charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">This clause prohibits payouts when a terminal illness arises due to involvement in a felony. It has no connection to how interest affects the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">This clause prohibits benefits if the terminal illness resulted from a felony, regardless of any existing loans or financial adjustments to the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness stems from a felony, no benefit is payable regardless of lien amounts affecting the adjusted death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 prohibits payments when an illness arises from felony involvement, complementing fact sentence 1, which bars claims due to self-inflicted injuries. Both clauses serve similar protective functions regarding intent-based misconduct.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a condition under which benefits are denied due to criminal activity. This has no bearing on the identity or role of the company's CEO, who is mentioned in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises due to a felony, the claim is ineligible regardless of timing. This does not affect the policyholder’s ability to cancel their application before funds are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 excludes benefits when the terminal illness stems from a felony, and fact_sentence_2 extends this principle to illnesses resulting from war-related activities. Both serve as independent grounds for denial, illustrating broad categorical exclusions tied to external causation.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES SIMILARLY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises due to a felony, the accelerated benefit cannot be paid. This restriction operates independently of whether a request has been revoked via written notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies a disqualifying condition related to criminal conduct affecting benefit eligibility. This does not relate to the geographical origin or execution site of the policy mentioned in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness stems from a felony, the accelerated benefit is denied; this aligns with broader rules prohibiting fraudulent behavior like falsifying claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises due to a felony, the rider does not pay benefits. This exclusion may intersect with broader fraud policies that penalize dishonesty in claims processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness stems from a felony, no benefit is payable under the rider. This restriction aligns with broader prohibitions against fraudulent behavior, such as intentionally hiding key details that could affect claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPT_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises from a felony, no accelerated benefit is payable. This aligns with broader prohibitions on dishonest acts that undermine policy integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">While the rider permits advance payments upon terminal diagnosis, it excludes cases where the illness resulted from participating in a felony, which adds a critical exception to the rider’s general provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION_CLAUSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The rule limiting accelerated benefits due to felony involvement directly constrains the scope of the Death Benefit described in the main policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces a specific limitation on accelerated benefits due to criminal conduct, which falls under the general scope of exclusions mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on accelerated benefits due to felony involvement reinforces the need for documented compliance, supporting the overarching rule that policy changes demand written approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES_REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes a restriction on accelerated benefits tied to criminal conduct, reinforcing the importance of formal procedures outlined in fact_sentence_1 to validate such limitations legally.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">The felony-related exclusion in the accelerated benefit provision reinforces the need for controlled, authorized handling of claims, consistent with the rule that no one except officials can change policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 restricts accelerated benefits when terminal illness arises from felony involvement, aligning with broader policy safeguards. These limitations reinforce the principle stated in fact_sentence_1—that deviations from rules require proper authorization, preventing misuse even during benefit claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45dc6ecc-80a4-4473-89d1-403fadf61614" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
</edge>
