  <data key="d4">LEGAL_NOTICE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises due to war-related activities, no accelerated benefit will be paid, even though the policy is issued by Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">A terminal illness resulting from war-related activities disqualifies the claim regardless of when the policy became effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises from war-related activities, no accelerated benefit is paid regardless of the policy's status. However, such a restriction does not override the need for the initial premium payment to activate coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION_DEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on paying benefits when the terminal illness stems from war-related activities does not depend on whether the insured was alive on the effective date, which governs initial policy activation rather than claim exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines an exception to payment based on cause of illness, which is unrelated to the policy form identifier mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion for war-related illnesses could be part of broader compliance frameworks, potentially including state-level mandates, though it stands independently as a defined exception.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSIONARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of payments when illnesses result from war-related activities depends on the availability of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, which is one of the optional riders offered by the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">Since the rider prohibits payment for illnesses due to war, its availability depends on excluding specific circumstances like those involving conflict, reinforcing the conditional nature of the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">While the rider permits early payments upon diagnosis of a terminal illness, such payments are withheld if the illness was caused by war-related incidents, thus limiting the scope of the initial benefit availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_LIMITATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">War-related origin disqualifies a terminal illness from qualifying for the accelerated benefit, even if other criteria like diagnosis and life expectancy are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Even if a policyholder meets the 12-month life expectancy threshold due to a terminal illness, they remain ineligible for benefits if the illness originated from war-related events.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness was caused by war-related activities, no accelerated benefit will be issued regardless of any medical certification confirming a short life expectancy. Thus, the existence of a physician’s certification cannot compensate for this specific exclusion.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT_APPLICABLE_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">If an illness is due to war-related activities, no benefit is paid at all—even if the claim would otherwise qualify under the 50% face amount limit established in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness was due to war-related activities, no benefit will be issued regardless of any pre-set payment caps.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT_APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Even if a written request has been submitted, no accelerated benefit will be issued if the terminal illness was caused by war-related activities.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises due to war-related activity, the claim is ineligible regardless of submitted medical documents. Thus, required medical proof cannot override this specific exclusion clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises from war-related activities, no accelerated benefit will be issued, irrespective of whether a second medical opinion was obtained or required. The presence of such an exclusion stands independently of the insurer’s verification procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">Claims are denied when the terminal illness arises from war-related activities. In such cases, no benefit is paid, so the death benefit remains unchanged.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness arises from war-related activities, no accelerated benefit is issued, meaning that related administrative charges would not apply since no payment occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises due to war-related activities, no accelerated benefit is payable regardless of any accumulated interest affecting future payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 sets a condition under which no payment occurs at all if the illness is war-related. This restriction exists irrespective of whether loans are present or not, meaning even without debt, such cases remain ineligible.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">If the terminal illness stems from war-related causes, no benefit is payable regardless of lien status or other financial factors.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 prohibits benefits if the illness originates from war-related incidents; likewise, fact_sentence_1 bars payouts due to intentionally inflicted injuries. Each represents a separate exception grounded in moral hazard or non-insurable risk factors.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSIONARY_PARALLEL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 prohibits payments if the illness arises from war-related actions, and fact_sentence_1 similarly blocks payouts due to involvement in a felony. Together, they represent complementary restrictions that prevent benefit access under morally or legally questionable circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES SIMILARLY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises from war-related causes, no accelerated benefit will be issued regardless of the policyholder’s intent. This exclusion stands irrespective of whether the policyholder later revokes their request.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a specific exclusion criterion related to the cause of terminal illness. This information does not relate to the administrative detail about where the policy was signed.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness stems from war, no accelerated benefit is payable regardless of any pending request. This exclusion does not affect the ability to revoke a previously submitted request through formal notification.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines a restriction on benefit payouts related to war causes, while the second provides information about a corporate leadership position. These statements address entirely different topics—eligibility criteria versus internal personnel—and do not influence each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a restriction on payment due to cause of illness, specifically excluding war-related causes. This detail is unrelated to the identity or role of the company's CEO mentioned in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises from war, the rider does not permit payment. This restriction complements broader anti-fraud measures, such as penalizing dishonest claims, ensuring integrity in benefit distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness stems from war, benefits are denied regardless of other conditions. This restriction reinforces the need for truthful disclosure, as hiding such information may constitute fraud.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPT_BY_FRAUD</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises due to war-related causes, the rider does not permit payment. This restriction aligns with broader prohibitions against fraudulent behavior in claims processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPT_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">If a terminal illness arises from war-related activities, no accelerated benefit is payable. This restriction operates independently of whether the claimant committed fraud; it pertains solely to the origin of the illness rather than intent or deception.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="b1aa54d6-2e04-4f72-a8ff-fe05054ce5b3">
  <data key="d3">While the policy includes an Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, it does not cover claims resulting from war-related terminal illnesses, thereby restricting the scope of the rider’s availability despite its general inclusion.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION_RESTRICTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of war-related terminal illnesses from accelerated benefits depends on the overarching policy terms governing the Death Benefit, making it contingent upon those foundational rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces a particular exclusion—war-related causes—for accelerated death benefits, which operates under the overarching condition described in fact_sentence_1 that all benefits are bound by policy-defined terms and exceptions.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces a specific exception to benefits, consistent with the requirement in fact_sentence_1 that all policy terms—including exceptions—be clearly stated and governed through formal procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIES_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces a specific exception to benefit eligibility tied to cause of illness, reinforcing the need for controlled modifications per fact_sentence_1 to maintain consistent application of such clauses.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPRESSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes limitations on accelerated death benefits tied to certain causes such as war, operating independently of who can change the policy; fact_sentence_1 ensures only authorized personnel can make changes, maintaining structural consistency regardless of benefit eligibility clauses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes a specific exclusion on accelerated benefits tied to war, consistent with broader policy constraints upheld by the requirement in fact_sentence_1 that only official representatives may enforce such clauses.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c611540d-125a-445d-a150-451581fd6bdc" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">may be ineligible for accelerated benefit if illness stems from war-related activities</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8513c964-d71a-4df6-b22a-9d5abd4bfad8" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is excluded from payment when terminal illness is caused by war-related activities</data>
</edge>
