</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder’s right to revoke an accelerated benefits request independently exists regardless of the issuing company; this autonomy is part of standard contractual terms rather than being contingent on the insurer’s identity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder can revoke a request for accelerated benefits at any time before payment, regardless of when the policy became effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">The right to revoke a request for accelerated benefits applies after the policy is active; it does not influence whether the policy itself became effective upon premium payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to revoke a request for accelerated benefits prior to payment exists independently of whether the insured was alive on the policy's effective date.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">The right to revoke a benefit request exists independently of the policy's form identifier.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">The policyholder’s ability to revoke a benefit request independently applies regardless of whether state-specific notices are present.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">The ability to revoke an acceleration request depends on the presence of an applicable rider, such as the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, which is made possible because the policy offers optional riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">Since the policyholder has the option to revoke a request for benefits, it implies they have access to the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, which enables such actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">The ability to revoke a request before payment depends on the existence of an early-payment mechanism established by the rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">Even after qualifying due to a terminal illness diagnosis, the policyholder retains control over the application process and can choose to cancel their request anytime before funds are disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">WITHDRAWABLE AFTER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">The ability to revoke a request for accelerated benefits at any time before payment gives the policyholder control over their decision after initiating an application. This right exists regardless of whether the individual meets the 12-month life expectancy threshold.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder's ability to revoke a request anytime before payment reflects flexibility in the application process. This right does not affect the necessity of physician-certified life expectancy, which remains a prerequisite regardless of withdrawal intent.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">This statement grants the policyholder the authority to cancel their application for early benefits anytime before funds are disbursed, providing control over the process regardless of the benefit ceiling defined elsewhere.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder’s ability to revoke a request before payment remains unaffected by the existence of a maximum benefit limit established by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder who has submitted a request retains the right to revoke it at any point before the benefit is disbursed, ensuring flexibility during the claims process.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">Before payment, the policyholder may withdraw their request for accelerated benefits. This revocation does not affect the need for proper medical documentation should they choose to reapply later.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder may choose to cancel their claim request at any point before receiving funds, independent of whether the company seeks an additional medical evaluation. This reflects individual agency unaffected by the insurer’s review procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder can revoke their request for accelerated benefits anytime before payout, preventing the subsequent reduction in the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder can withdraw their request for accelerated benefits anytime before payout, regardless of whether administrative charges later apply to the reduced death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder can withdraw their request for accelerated benefits anytime before payout, maintaining control over the process. This operational freedom exists regardless of how interest impacts the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder can choose to revoke their request for accelerated benefits at any point before payout, regardless of existing loans that would later affect the adjusted death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">This statement highlights the revocability of an acceleration request before payment, independent of how liens affect the resulting death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder may cancel their application for accelerated benefits anytime before disbursement, ensuring they retain autonomy even if certain exclusions like self-harm apply post-request.</data>
  <data key="d4">REVOKEABLE_BEFORE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder can withdraw their request anytime before payment, ensuring they retain control even if the illness was linked to a felony, though such cases remain ineligible under the terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder retains the ability to cancel their application for accelerated benefits at any point before disbursement. This right remains unaffected even if the underlying illness was due to war-related activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder has the right to cancel an accelerated benefit request before payment. This cancellation must be formally communicated via written notice to the insurance company.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">The ability to revoke a benefit request ensures procedural fairness but does not affect the legality of concealing information. Fraudulent behavior remains prohibited regardless of withdrawal rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_DIRECT_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">The option to revoke a benefit request ensures policyholder control before disbursement, but it does not affect the requirement that submitted information must be truthful when filing such requests.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes a withdrawal option available to the policyholder before receiving accelerated benefits. The second sentence provides information about the physical location where the policy was issued, which does not relate to the revocation process described earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">The policyholder can cancel an acceleration request before receiving funds, ensuring flexibility. This procedural right does not inherently connect to the definition of fraudulent acts involving deceit about material facts.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">The ability to revoke a benefits request ensures that applicants can avoid proceeding with potentially misleading information, thereby reducing risk of fraudulent submission.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS FRAUD</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="a95c37fd-7aad-43df-a80d-09cc336f0ae6">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder’s ability to revoke an accelerated benefits request depends on the Death Benefit being subject to policy terms, ensuring administrative consistency and legal enforceability within the framework established by the main policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="25f4cee7-d9c0-44f5-9b59-9dd48a31e12d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes a mechanism allowing withdrawal of an accelerated benefit request, which aligns with the general condition in fact_sentence_1 that all benefits are subject to policy-defined terms and limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="cd70f299-b66e-49aa-b3c6-69fcc2129242">
  <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 involves a reversible action under a rider, it indirectly reinforces the necessity of written communication for policy-related decisions, consistent with the broader rule stated in fact_sentence_1 about written waivers.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="2da9f77a-5318-41fa-9bdb-52b9728b043d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to revoke a request for accelerated benefits reflects a process consistent with the overarching principle that no policy alteration takes effect without proper documentation and approval, reinforcing the necessity of authorized sign-offs.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="cca9f6cf-6067-42df-94ad-2563bd3117d4">
  <data key="d3">While the ability to revoke an accelerated benefits request reflects policyowner autonomy, it operates under the broader framework where only authorized agents can alter policy terms, maintaining consistency in administrative oversight.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIES_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093" target="9f637f68-638b-4eec-9c72-453a879fc0d8">
  <data key="d3">While the ability to revoke an accelerated benefits request reflects internal flexibility in claim management, it operates under the overarching rule that no agent can unilaterally change policy terms without proper authorization, consistent with fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSISTENT_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c159c170-fd88-4875-924e-96d4e3192f68" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">administers</data>
</edge>
