  <data key="d4">LEGAL_NOTICE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">To revoke a benefit request, a written notice must be sent to Sentinel Life Assurance Company, the entity that issued the policy containing the rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">A written notice is required to revoke a benefit request, regardless of when the policy became effective.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">Requiring written notice to revoke a request is independent of whether the initial premium has been paid; one does not affect the validity or timing of the other.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">A written revocation notice terminates an ongoing request, independent of whether the policy was activated due to the insured being alive at the start.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines how a beneficiary may revoke a claim request, but it does not reference or rely on the policy form number mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the requirement for written revocation of a claim, which applies regardless of any state-specific rules mentioned in fact_sentence_1. The need for written notice is consistent across jurisdictions but unrelated to the presence of such notices themselves.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">A requirement for revoking a rider request involves submitting written notice to the company, reflecting the administrative framework governing optional policy enhancements introduced earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">A written notice to the company is required to revoke a request made under the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider, which is itself an optional rider offered by the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">A revocable request for accelerated benefits implies that such payments are optional and subject to withdrawal at any time before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">A formal withdrawal of a benefit request requires documented communication to the company. This action is only relevant once the individual has qualified under the terms of the rider, such as being diagnosed with a terminal illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines how a policyholder may revoke a claim request through formal notification. This action is independent of the diagnostic threshold specified in fact_sentence_1, which governs initial eligibility rather than post-submission actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">Written revocation of a request terminates the application process before payout. This action only applies once a request has been submitted; thus, it depends on the initial step requiring physician certification.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the formal method for withdrawing a claim request, preserving flexibility before payout. This procedural step operates independently of the monetary limit defined in fact_sentence_1, which governs only the size of any approved advance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">A revocable request allows the policyholder to cancel their application for benefits at any time before payout, independent of the payment ceiling established by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Before any benefits are paid, a policyholder may withdraw their application by providing written notice to the company, ensuring they retain control over the decision until disbursement occurs. This revocation capability depends on having previously submitted a written request.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder wishes to cancel an earlier request for accelerated benefits, they must submit written notice to the company. This revocation is only effective once the initial request has been made and documented with required medical evidence.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">A written notice is required to revoke a benefit request; however, this does not impact the insurer’s ability to independently obtain a second medical opinion when assessing eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder may revoke a request for an accelerated benefit by submitting written notice to the company. Such revocation prevents the associated reduction in the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder may revoke their request for an accelerated benefit by submitting written notice to the company. This action occurs regardless of any administrative charges already applied to the benefit calculation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written notice to revoke a claim ensures control over withdrawals. This procedure does not affect how interest impacts the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder may submit written notice to revoke their request for accelerated benefits before any payment is made. This action does not impact loan calculations already applied to the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">This statement outlines the requirement for written notice to revoke an acceleration request, independent of lien deductions from the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder may revoke a benefit request via written notice, but such revocation does not override pre-existing exclusions like those due to self-harm.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder may revoke a benefit request by submitting written notice to the company. This action does not override exclusions such as those related to felonies causing the illness.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder may submit a written revocation to cancel their request for benefits at any time before payout. This action remains effective even if the underlying cause of illness was war-related, though such cases were already ineligible anyway.</data>
  <data key="d4">PERMITS_REVOKE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">Written notice to the company is necessary to execute the revocation of an accelerated benefit request. Without such notice, the revocation cannot take effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written notice to revoke an accelerated death benefit request is unrelated to the identity of the company's CEO.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines procedural requirements for withdrawing a claim request under the rider. The second sentence identifies a corporate executive without any link to the withdrawal process or its conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">A requirement to provide written notice for revoking a claim does not directly relate to the definition of fraudulent behavior involving concealment of material facts.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written notice to revoke an accelerated death benefit request is independent of where the policy was originally executed. No connection exists between revocation procedures and the physical location of policy signing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">A policyholder may revoke a benefit request by submitting written notice to the company. This action does not relate directly to filing false information on applications or claims, which would constitute fraud.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">A requirement to revoke a claim via written notice does not directly influence or relate to the criminal implications of intentionally lying during claims processing.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">A revocation process requiring written notice ensures policyholder control over claims; however, such actions may still be subject to scrutiny under fraud regulations that penalize deceptive conduct regarding material information.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
