<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="44af3e5d-df42-4eb3-87f9-46f28167807c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="7dc9b898-8edf-4428-a8f0-8ce21ebdd2ff">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">RIGHT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="097cf66a-f771-4e30-82ba-64decd185d86">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">LEGAL_NOTICE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">Submitting falsified information on an application or claim has no bearing on the identity of the insurer, Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">Whether the policy became effective on a certain date does not influence the determination that providing false information during an application or claim is considered fraud.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">Submitting materially false information on an application or claim is a separate issue from whether the initial premium has been paid; it does not affect the policy's activation status.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">Submitting materially false information on an application or claim is considered fraud regardless of whether the insured was alive on the effective date; thus, it stands independently from the policy's activation condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">Rules prohibiting material misrepresentation apply universally across all policies, including those identified by form numbers like SLAC-TL2025-20YR.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">Providing materially false information on an application or claim is considered fraud, regardless of whether any state-specific notices were included in the policy documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">Providing false information on forms may lead to denial of benefits but has no bearing on whether riders are offered or available under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence addresses legal consequences of dishonesty in claims processes, whereas the first discusses access to accelerated benefits under specific conditions. No mutual influence exists between them.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">Providing false information on applications or claims is considered fraud, regardless of whether one qualifies for benefits like those from an accelerated death benefit rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">Providing false information on applications or claims may lead to denial of benefits, regardless of whether the individual meets clinical eligibility criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 highlights the risk of fraud when submitting inaccurate details, which could undermine the validity of a terminal illness diagnosis required by fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">Providing materially false information on an application or claim is considered fraud, regardless of whether it pertains to life expectancy documentation required by a licensed physician.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 warns about the legal implications of providing false information when applying for or claiming benefits, but it does not affect the calculation or cap of payments defined in fact_sentence_1, which remains fixed at 50% regardless of honesty.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">Providing false information on claims may lead to denial of benefits but does not alter the pre-established maximum payout allowed under the rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Providing false information on applications or claims is considered fraud regardless of whether a written request has been submitted, making it independent of the procedural step itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">Submitting fraudulent information invalidates any supporting documentation, undermining the legitimacy of a benefit request that depends on accurate medical proof.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">Providing false information on an application or claim is illegal regardless of whether a second medical opinion is requested.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false information on applications or claims violates policy integrity and may lead to denial or legal action. Such actions undermine the fairness of benefit distribution mechanisms like those described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_DIRECT_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">Submitting materially false information on an application or claim is considered fraud. This action may lead to denial of benefits but has no bearing on how administrative charges affect the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence highlights the legal risk of submitting misleading data when applying for benefits. This contrasts with the first sentence, which details how interest impacts the final payout amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">This statement warns about the criminal implications of dishonesty in applications or claims, independent of loan deductions from benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">This statement warns about the legal implications of submitting false information in claims, which is unrelated to the administrative adjustment of liens affecting the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false information on an application or claim is considered fraud. Such actions may lead to denial of benefits regardless of the underlying health condition, including cases where self-injury was involved.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false information on an application or claim is considered fraud, which undermines the integrity of the benefit system and may lead to denial—even beyond specific exclusions like those tied to felonies.</data>
  <data key="d4">POTENTIALLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">Providing false information on an application or claim is deemed fraud, reinforcing exclusions like those related to war-caused illnesses to prevent abuse of the accelerated benefit system.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">Submitting falsified information during an application or claim is considered fraud, regardless of whether a revocation occurs later; thus, revoking a request cannot excuse dishonesty earlier in the process.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">Submitting materially false information during an application or claim is considered fraud and carries legal consequences. This act is unrelated to the procedure for withdrawing a previously filed benefit request.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3">The statement about fraud does not relate to or provide any insight into the role or identity of the CEO at Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">Providing fraudulent information on an application or claim has no bearing on where the policy was originally executed. The act of fraud is independent of administrative geography.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes submitting false information as fraud, which aligns with the broader principle in fact_sentence_2 that intentionally concealing material facts also qualifies as fraudulent conduct.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines fraud broadly as filing applications or claims with materially false information. Fact_sentence_2 builds on this by specifying that such acts become legally recognized fraudulent insurance behaviors when done intentionally to deceive.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that providing false information on claims is fraud. Fact_sentence_2 explains that such acts require intentional deception about material facts, refining the legal standard for accountability.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="df9797d7-629e-4917-bc56-582d8cf4fe9d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 provides the legal standard defining insurance fraud, which directly applies to the event described in fact_sentence_2—a confirmed fraudulent insurance act.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="de0d67af-5b66-4374-8edd-cc82b199731b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines what constitutes insurance fraud, which provides a legal framework relevant to evaluating whether actions taken by individuals like Eleanor B. Raynor could qualify as fraudulent under company policies or regulations.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="9e3cd4f3-d236-4040-a6c4-c46f3a22a611">
  <data key="d3">The legal principle defining material falsehoods in insurance applications applies directly to cases like Eleanor B. Raynor's, whose authoritative role may involve overseeing claims processes vulnerable to fraudulent manipulation.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369" target="57fafae6-d83d-473d-a0a2-e4e4d1824c40">
  <data key="d3">The general prohibition against insurance fraud applies broadly to entities like Sentinel Life Assurance Company, where Eleanor B. Raynor holds leadership; however, no evidence links her directly to fraudulent behavior in this instance.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
