  <data key="d4">LEGAL_NOTICE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">The legal prohibition against fraudulent insurance acts applies regardless of the issuing company. Knowing this rule doesn't require knowledge of who issued the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against fraudulent statements applies regardless of when the policy became effective, so it is independent of the schedule date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">Prohibiting fraudulent statements does not affect the condition under which the policy becomes active upon premium payment.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false information with intent to defraud violates insurance law, but this has no direct connection to whether the insured was alive at policy inception.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">A statement about fraudulent acts in insurance does not pertain to or affect the designation of a specific policy form number.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the legal consequence of lying about one's condition when claiming benefits, but it does not relate directly to whether state-specific notices are required under law, which is addressed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent insurance acts, such as knowingly providing false information, are unrelated to whether a policy includes optional riders; it pertains to ethical and legal conduct during claim processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence defines a fraudulent act in insurance contexts. This definition applies broadly but is not specifically tied to the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider mentioned in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes that intentional deception in claiming benefits is illegal. This applies to situations like those covered by fact_sentence_1, where misrepresentation could lead to denial or penalties despite meeting clinical criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false information with intent to defraud is a separate legal issue that could disqualify someone from receiving benefits but is unrelated to whether a terminal illness has been medically confirmed.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 warns against intentional deception in claims processes, which directly impacts whether individuals meeting the 12-month life expectancy threshold (as stated in fact_sentence_1) can successfully access benefits without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false information about life expectancy—such as fabricating a diagnosis—is illegal and undermines the legitimacy of the physician-certified assessment required for benefit eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent behavior undermines the fairness of benefit limits, making it essential that such restrictions exist to deter dishonest claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNDERMINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent behavior undermines the legitimacy of claims, potentially triggering scrutiny that could affect whether a claimed benefit—even within the stated maximum—is approved.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">Providing false statements when requesting benefits may lead to criminal liability; therefore, accurate documentation is essential when making a formal request.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false claims undermines the validity of required medical documentation, making honesty essential for eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">Providing false statements to defraud insurers undermines the credibility of medical evaluations, potentially triggering the need for additional review such as a second medical opinion.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNDERMINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the legal implications of intentional misrepresentation in insurance claims. Fact_sentence_1 details how benefit payouts reduce the final death benefit, which is independent of fraud-related penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false statements to defraud insurers constitutes a fraudulent act under law. This rule stands independently of how administrative costs affect the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against knowingly providing false information relates to claim integrity and criminal liability, independent of how interest affects the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 warns that falsifying information to gain benefits constitutes fraud under law. This general legal principle does not influence or depend on the specific financial mechanism outlined in fact_sentence_1 about loan deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 defines fraudulent activity involving false statements in insurance claims, serving as a general warning. This legal principle may indirectly inform why certain verifications occur but does not logically depend on lien deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false statements to gain benefits constitutes fraud, which may include falsely claiming a terminal illness was non-self-inflicted when it actually was—a scenario covered by the self-harm exclusion.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false statements to obtain benefits is considered fraud, which justifies denying payments when linked to criminal acts such as felonies.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false information to obtain benefits constitutes fraud, reinforcing why certain cases like those involving war-related illnesses may be explicitly excluded to prevent misuse.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent behavior undermines the legitimacy of withdrawal rights, as intentionally deceptive actions could invalidate the entire claim even if withdrawn pre-payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNDERMINES REVOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">Submitting false statements with intent to defraud constitutes a serious offense but has no bearing on the administrative procedure for withdrawing a request.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3">The legal principle regarding fraudulent insurance acts does not relate to or depend on the identity of the CEO at Sentinel Life Assurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The legal warning about fraudulent insurance acts does not depend on or explain the physical location where the policy was executed.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies a specific type of fraudulent behavior—knowingly lying with intent to defraud—as a defined illegal act. This directly supports and clarifies the broader category of misconduct described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">SPECIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 highlights making false claims intentionally; fact_sentence_1 complements this by covering the omission of critical details, showing how both actions constitute fraudulent behavior under insurance law.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 identifies fraudulent insurance acts through intentional deception; fact_sentence_2 specifies that such acts require awareness of falsity or concealed material information, reinforcing the intent criterion.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="de0d67af-5b66-4374-8edd-cc82b199731b">
  <data key="d3">The general principle that knowingly providing false statements to an insurer constitutes fraud may apply to any individual in a leadership position like Eleanor B. Raynor, but no explicit link exists between her role and such behavior based on available information.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="df9797d7-629e-4917-bc56-582d8cf4fe9d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 provides a legal definition of fraudulent insurance acts, which helps contextualize the claim made in fact_sentence_2 that such an act occurred. It supports understanding the nature and potential implications of the reported fraud.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="9e3cd4f3-d236-4040-a6c4-c46f3a22a611">
  <data key="d3">The legal definition of fraudulent insurance acts provides a framework for evaluating whether Eleanor B. Raynor's conduct as an authorized representative may have violated ethical or legal standards during the handling of claims under the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd" target="57fafae6-d83d-473d-a0a2-e4e4d1824c40">
  <data key="d3">The definition of fraudulent insurance conduct provides a legal framework relevant to evaluating potential misconduct tied to Sentinel Life Assurance Company, where Eleanor B. Raynor holds leadership responsibility. Her position may imply accountability for ensuring adherence to anti-fraud policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
