<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="1f71e65a-9fb1-4dcf-bb24-91800bb3f3c7">
  <data key="d3">The definition of committing a fraudulent insurance act does not involve or rely on information about the issuing company.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="20fbfea1-87f5-44e4-993f-62b3ff2e28ee">
  <data key="d3">Defining fraudulent insurance acts does not provide information about when the policy becomes effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="05e6ea4e-3679-424b-a1ef-cd15cb0268c9">
  <data key="d3">Defining fraudulent insurance acts does not affect the condition under which the policy becomes effective upon premium payment. There is no causal or sequential connection between them.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="57f1482e-c194-4d7c-89bc-95a96701db5d">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent insurance acts involve deliberate deception about material facts, which is unrelated to whether the insured was alive at policy inception.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="d3c440cf-41e3-4d0b-a3f0-ad9eb7117fb9">
  <data key="d3">Defining fraudulent acts based on knowledge of falsity or concealment applies generally across policies but does not depend on or reference any particular policy form number like SLAC-TL2025-20YR.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="4be625d8-db33-4685-8ec1-310ef9190d46">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent actions involve deliberate deception about key facts, whereas state-specific provisions reflect jurisdictional legal mandates. These concepts intersect only indirectly through overarching policy legitimacy and enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="abd6a771-b2cc-4b47-8455-fa725fb92dac">
  <data key="d3">Defining fraudulent insurance acts based on knowledge of falsity or concealment does not relate to whether the policy includes optional riders. This is an independent concept regarding ethical conduct versus policy features.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="868545fb-b90c-4d86-aa47-b3fa5811f814">
  <data key="d3">The legal standard for fraudulent insurance acts does not influence or explain the availability or function of the Accelerated Death Benefit Rider.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="e7abe25a-548e-4854-99a9-005d2c7abd86">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence defines fraudulent acts involving intentional deception about key information in insurance claims. This concept is relevant to potential misuse of the rider but is not inherently tied to its operational mechanics described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="bb127988-dd0c-41ea-98d9-d68d41d35ba5">
  <data key="d3">Engaging in fraudulent activity, such as concealing material facts, could disqualify someone from receiving benefits even if they meet clinical criteria like a terminal illness diagnosis. Fraud undermines claim legitimacy regardless of health status.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="a82e95a0-cbf0-46a4-98e6-5b9250a0719c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines conduct that undermines claim legitimacy through deceit. This applies independently of whether the applicant meets the 12-month life expectancy criterion established in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="24953031-60ae-4e53-8878-b13b08a99bb6">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent actions include knowingly providing false details about one’s condition, which undermines the credibility of a physician’s life expectancy certification used to qualify for benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNDERMINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="9c8ab001-f2e6-4dce-9c28-676af9b34008">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent acts, such as concealing material information, can invalidate claims regardless of eligibility criteria like the 50% payout cap established in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="8c21a23d-34f1-400e-8692-3b5af49dbb3d">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent acts involve deception about material facts, which could potentially lead to improper claims—but this concept is independent of the predefined payment ceiling established by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="07aa45e3-df8b-4fdc-a2d7-4ebdc9b4974f">
  <data key="d3">A fraudulent insurance act—such as knowingly providing false information—can nullify a written request for benefits, even if it was formally submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">INVALIDATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="221c721d-0cca-43e4-9fde-c98c985d9e46">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent acts—such as concealing material facts—are relevant because they could invalidate the medical documentation submitted to support a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="c49d35db-1e22-49cf-aff0-80eed3363f59">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent acts involve deliberate falsehoods about key facts, such as falsely claiming terminal illness. Such actions could trigger scrutiny leading insurers to request additional medical evaluations like a second opinion.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="c24c3db2-61fe-4fe8-b84c-a66c833de08e">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent insurance acts involve knowingly providing false information about material facts, but such behavior has no inherent connection to how benefits affect the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="5959382c-3da3-4378-9d27-70eeead2dc9c">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent insurance acts involve knowingly concealing or falsifying material information, which could impact eligibility for benefits like the accelerated death benefit. However, this concept is separate from how administrative charges affect the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="8690a7f5-82be-413d-a92b-8be70122f5aa">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent acts involve deliberate falsehoods or omissions regarding key information when applying for benefits. Such actions could potentially trigger denial of an accelerated payment but do not directly affect how interest impacts the remaining death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="fa4bdb40-ec63-4909-8c9d-03d63650997f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the criteria for committing fraud in an insurance context. Fact_sentence_1 details how loan balances impact the final death benefit payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="74ab917d-fe31-437b-954d-cb3c8c3a0cc2">
  <data key="d3">This statement defines what constitutes fraudulent activity in insurance claims but does not connect to the calculation of liens or benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="3d180056-1ee5-45c0-95de-957558f0d6c0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that committing fraud requires knowledge of falsehoods or omissions regarding key information. This concept applies broadly but isn't triggered specifically by self-harm cases unless deception is involved.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="147ebded-c5e9-4ee9-a600-a0613a4ac44b">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent insurance acts involve knowingly concealing material information, which may include false claims tied to terminal diagnoses—but such actions do not directly trigger the felony-based exclusion unless explicitly linked.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="097f621e-9ee5-4ea1-bb84-d692f67b9f5b">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent acts involve knowingly providing false information about material facts during a claim process. Such behavior would disqualify a beneficiary regardless of the illness's cause, including cases where the illness stems from non-war causes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="cf34ad84-8215-4856-9bd3-153061d00093">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent insurance acts involve knowingly providing false information about key details. Such misconduct could potentially invalidate a withdrawal request but is not directly tied to the revocation mechanism itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="42959f78-4be8-4477-9f82-ca39bf16f6b5">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent acts involving deception about material facts could undermine the legitimacy of any withdrawal request, including those made via formal revocation notices.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="d40a8a1d-b256-47c5-bcc2-7c565e18e4a6">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="70e7fe46-b6c6-4910-8fcf-5836a44a1382">
  <data key="d3">The legal definition of a fraudulent insurance act does not reference or depend on any specific corporate leadership roles such as that held by Eleanor B. Raynor.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="4dda5c60-5f9a-445b-896e-afcf680b072f">
  <data key="d3">The concept of committing fraud through misrepresentation does not relate to where the policy was executed at the company's home office.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="7baa8b25-9b01-472b-86a7-c55acdb29369">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the necessary element of intent—knowing falsity or concealment—for committing fraud. This builds upon fact_sentence_1's assertion that false submissions constitute fraud, adding the requirement of awareness.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="f2b2eda1-ace9-416b-a284-68313b16efe9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that knowingly concealing material facts qualifies as a fraudulent act. Fact_sentence_1 clarifies that intentional concealment of material information constitutes fraud under insurance law.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="4842aa86-8d77-49f2-8517-35dcccfe1dcd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that committing fraud necessitates knowledge of falsity or concealment; fact_sentence_1 exemplifies this by describing deliberate submission of lies intended to deceive insurers.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXAMPLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="df9797d7-629e-4917-bc56-582d8cf4fe9d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the legal criteria for a fraudulent insurance act, which helps define and validate the claim made in fact_sentence_2 about its occurrence.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="de0d67af-5b66-4374-8edd-cc82b199731b">
  <data key="d3">The first statement outlines the legal basis for insurance fraud, while the second introduces a high-level executive involved in a suspected fraudulent incident; however, no explicit linkage exists between the individual's actions and the defined elements of fraud.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="9e3cd4f3-d236-4040-a6c4-c46f3a22a611">
  <data key="d3">The definition of fraudulent insurance acts provides a legal framework that may apply to potential misconduct by Eleanor B. Raynor, who holds an authoritative role in an organization under scrutiny for fraud.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee" target="57fafae6-d83d-473d-a0a2-e4e4d1824c40">
  <data key="d3">The concept of committing fraudulent insurance acts applies broadly to scenarios like those potentially involving Eleanor B. Raynor, whose position at Sentinel Life Assurance Company places her in a role where awareness of material misrepresentations could constitute actionable fraud.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38e4fbc9-9af6-4701-aa16-ea3f4c4f8f1d" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces rules against</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa802538-d9c3-4196-84eb-d0a410f4da04" target="cfcb3d69-6bc4-465d-b7ca-f58645d5d6ee">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
